s Club retail warehouses. [14] [15] As of 2026, Walmart is the second-largest company by revenue globally &#91; f &#93; and the largest private employer in the world, &#91; g &#93; with 2.1 million employees. &#91; a &#93; The company is ranked one in the Fortune 500 [16] and Fortune Global 500 . [17] In February 2026, Walmart became the first traditional retailer [18] to be valued at over $1 trillion [19] [20] and is known for product innovation . [21] It is a publicly traded family-owned business (th', '["clm_wiki_walmart_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
