VALUES
  ('cs_berkshire-hathaway_operations', 'org_berkshire-hathaway', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Greg Abel Era Berkshire Hathaway agreed to buy home builder Taylor Morrison Home Corporation for $6.8 billion in cash in May 2026. The transaction is expected to close in the second half of 2026, after which Taylor Morrison will become a private company. [1] The deal was the first major acquisition since Greg Abel succeeded Warren Buffett as CEO. [2] On June 1, 2026, Berkshire Hathaway agreed to invest $10 billion in Alphabet through a private placement. [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Berkshire Hathaway to Acquire Taylor Morrison Home Corporation for $8.5 Billion" . Taylor Morrison . Taylor Morrison . Retrieved June 1, 2026 . ^ Li, Yun (June 1, 2026). "Berkshire buys Taylor Morrison for $6.8 billion. Buffett touts Abel''s dealmaking" . CNBC . Retrieved June 1, 2026 . ^ "Berkshire Hathaway to invest $10 Billion in Alphabet in a private placement" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved June 2, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_berkshire-hathaway_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
