  ('cs_elevance-health_operations', 'org_elevance-health', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Blue Cross of California Blue Cross of California was the predecessor of WellPoint Health Network Inc . In 1982, Blue Cross of California was founded with the consolidation of Blue Cross of Northern California (established in 1936) and Blue Cross of Southern California (established in 1937). [1] In 1992, WellPoint was formed to operate Blue Cross of California''s managed care business. [2] In January 1993, Blue Cross of California spun off its managed care business into a publicly traded entity, WellPoint Health Networks Inc. Blue Cross of California retained an 80% interest and voting control. [3] [4] In 1996, Blue Cross of California restructured to a for-profit corporation , designating WellPoint Health Networks Inc. as the parent organization. [5] In April 1996, WellPoint completed its acquisition of Massachusetts Mutual Life Insurance Company ''s group life and health insurance subsidiaries for approximately $380 million, making it the second largest publicly held managed health company in the U.S. with 4 million policyholders. [6] In March 1997, WellPoint acquired the group health and life businesses of John Hancock Financial for $86.7 million. With this acquisition, WellPoint expanded its presence into Michigan , Texas , and the mid-Atlantic, and gained a unit that concentrated on serving the needs of large employers. [7] In 2000, WellPoint acquired PrecisionRx, a mail service pharmacy fulfillment center in Texas. [8] In March 2000, WellPoint acquired Rush Prudential Health Plans, a Chicago provider, for $204 million. [9] In March 2001, WellPoint acquired Cerulean Companies, the parent company of Blue Cross Blue Shield of Georgia . [10] In 2001, WellPoint offered to acquire CareFirst BlueCross BlueShield for $1.37 billion, including $119 million in bonuses to Carefirst executives. [11] In 2003, the offer was rejected by the Maryland insurance commissioner. [12] In 2002, WellPoint acquired RightChoice Managed Care, a Missouri-based company that ran Blue Cross an', '["clm_wiki_elevance-health_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
