VALUES
  ('cs_comcast_operations', 'org_comcast', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Comcast Comcast''s first logo from 1969 to 2000 The company was re-incorporated in Pennsylvania on March 5, 1969, under the new name Comcast Corporation . [1] Comcast''s initial public offering occurred on June 29, 1972, on the National Association of Securities Dealers Automated Quotation System (NASDAQ), a then-recently established stock exchange, with a market capitalization of U.S. $3,010,000. [1] [2] In 1977, HBO was first launched on a Comcast system with 20,000 customers in western Pennsylvania with a five-night free preview getting a 15% sign up rate. [1] [3] In 1986, Comcast bought 26% of Group W Cable , a broadcast company, doubling its number of subscribers to 1 million. [4] [5] Also that year, Comcast made a founding investment of $380 million in QVC . [1] In 1988, Comcast was able to buy a 50% share of SCI Holdings in a joint deal with Tele-Communications Inc. [6] Comcast also acquired American Cellular Network Corporation in 1988 for $230 million, marking the first time it became a mobile phone operator . [7] ^ a b c d Cite error: The named reference mcn was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) Littleton, Cynthia (June 19, 2015). "Ralph Roberts, Comcast Founder and Cable Pioneer, Dies at 95" . Variety . Archived from the original on October 23, 2018 . Retrieved October 23, 2018 . ^ Abratt, Russell; Bendixen, Michael (July 4, 2018). Strategic Marketing: Concepts and Cases . Routledge. ISBN 9780429951558 . ^ "Comcast, Form 425, Filing Date Feb 11, 2004" . Securities and Exchange Commission. Archived from the original on May 21, 2013 . Retrieved March 27, 2013 . ^ Fabrikant, Geraldine (December 25, 1985). "GROUP W CABLE SOLD TO 5 BUYERS" . The New York Times . Archived from the original on June 5, 2023 . Retrieved October 23, 2018 . ^ GERALDINE FABRIKANT (April 25, 1988). "2 Cable TV Companies To Buy SCI" . The New York Times . Archived from the original on October 19, 2021 . Retrieved February 15, 2014 . ^ "COMPANY NEWS; Ame', '["clm_wiki_comcast_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
