VALUES
  ('cs_johnson-johnson_history', 'org_johnson-johnson', 'overview', 'History',
   'American multinational pharmaceutical and medical device company Not to be confused with S. C. Johnson &amp; Son . "J&amp;J" and "JNJ" redirect here. For other uses, see J &amp; J (disambiguation) and JNJ (disambiguation) . Johnson &amp; Johnson Headquarters at One Johnson and Johnson Plaza in New Brunswick, New Jersey , U.S. Type Public Traded as NYSE : JNJ DJIA component S&amp;P 100 component S&amp;P 500 component ISIN US4781601046 Industry Pharmaceutical Medical Technology Founded January 1886 &#59;&#32;140 years ago ( 1886-01 ) in New Brunswick, New Jersey , U.S. Founders Robert Wood Johnson I James Wood Johnson Edward Mead Johnson Headquarters Johnson and Johnson Plaza , New Brunswick, New Jersey , U.S. 40°29′55″N 74°26′37″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 40.49861°N 74.44361°W &#xfeff; / 40.49861; -74.44361 Area served Worldwide Key people Joaquin Duato ( chairman &amp; CEO ) John C. Reed ( EVP ) Products List of Johnson &amp; Johnson products and services Revenue US$ 94.19 billion (2025) Operating income US$25.29 billion (2025) Net income US$26.80 billion (2025) Total assets US$199.2 billion (2025) Total equity US$81.54 billion (2025) Number of employees 138,200 (2025) Subsidiaries List Johnson &amp; Johnson Innovative Medicine Actelion Pharmaceuticals Alza Cilag Janssen Pharmaceuticals Janssen Vaccines Johnson &amp; Johnson Pharmaceutical Research and Development MorphoSys Ortho-McNeil Pharmaceutical Ortho-McNeil-Janssen Ortho Pharmaceutical Tibotec Johnson &amp; Johnson MedTech Abiomed DePuy Synthes Ethicon Johnson &amp; Johnson Vision Mentor Synthes Website jnj Footnotes [1] Johnson &amp; Johnson ( J&amp;J ) is an American multinational pharmaceutical , biotechnology , and medical technologies corporation headquartered in New Brunswick, New Jersey . The company is ranked No. 48 on the 2025 Fortune 500 list of the largest United States corporations. [2] In 2025, the company was ranked 42nd in the Forbes Global 2000 . [3] Along with Microsoft , Johnson &amp; Johnson is one of only two U.S.-based companies that has a prime credit rating of AAA from S&amp;P Global . [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Johnson and Johnson 2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . United States Securities and Exchange Commission . February 11, 2026. ^ "Johnson &amp; Johnson" . Fortune . Retrieved March 26, 2025 . ^ SCHIFRIN", MATT; MURPHY, ANDREA. "Forbes'' 2025 Global 2000 List - The World''s Largest Companies Ranked" . Forbes . Retrieved January 13, 2026 . ^ Kranz, Matt (August 2, 2023). "2 Remaini', '["clm_wiki_johnson-johnson_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
