   'Finances For the fiscal year 2018, Procter &amp; Gamble reported earnings of US$9.750 billion, with an annual revenue of US$66.832 billion, an increase of 2.7% over the previous fiscal cycle. The company''s shares traded at over $86 per share in 2017, and its market capitalization was valued at over US$221.5 billion in October 2018. [1] The company ranked No. 42 on the 2018 Fortune 500 list of the largest United States corporations by total revenue. Year Revenue in million US$ Net income in million US$ Total assets in millions US$ Employees 2005 56,741 6,923 61,527 2006 68,222 8,684 135,695 2007 74,832 10,340 138,014 2008 79,257 12,075 143,992 2009 76,694 13,436 134,833 135,000 2010 78,938 12,517 128,172 127,000 2011 82,559 11,564 138,354 129,000 2012 83,680 10,500 132,244 126,000 2013 84,167 11,068 139,263 121,000 2014 83,062 11,390 144,266 118,000 2015 76,279 6,777 129,495 110,000 2016 65,299 10,508 127,136 105,000 2017 65,058 15,326 120,406 95,000 2018 66,832 9,750 118,310 92,000 2019 67,684 3,897 115,095 97,000 2020 70,950 12,764 120,700 99,000 2021 76,118 14,035 119,307 101,000 2022 81,286 15,306 117,914 103,000 2023 82,006 14,653 120,829 107,000 2024 84,039 14,879 122,370 108,000 ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Annual Reports | P&amp;G" . www . Archived from the original on November 7, 2018 . Retrieved November 7, 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_procter-gamble_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
