  ('cs_boeing_operations', 'org_boeing', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Sea Launch In 1995, Boeing partnered with Russian, Ukrainian, and Anglo-Norwegian organizations to create Sea Launch , a company providing commercial launch services sending satellites to geostationary orbit from floating platforms. [1] In 2000, Boeing acquired the satellite segment of Hughes Electronics . [2] [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "What Happened to Sea Launch" . Space Daily . Archived from the original on December 14, 2018 . Retrieved January 24, 2020 . ^ Weiss, Stanley I.; Amir, Amir R. "Boeing Company – Description, History, &amp; Aircraft" . Encyclopedia Britannica . Archived from the original on July 18, 2019. ^ Pollack, Andrew (January 13, 2000). "$3.75 Billion Boeing-Hughes Satellite Deal Expected" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Archived from the original on May 3, 2015 . Retrieved January 24, 2020 .', '["clm_wiki_boeing_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
