  ('cs_honeywell_leadership', 'org_honeywell', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1906 Honeywell Heating Specialty Company founded In 1906, Mark Honeywell founded the Honeywell Heating Specialty Company in Wabash , Indiana , to manufacture and market his invention, the mercury seal generator. [1] [2] The Honeywell 516 , later used as the Interface Message Processor ^ body:not( ):not( ) Reilly, Edwin D. (2003). Milestones in Computer Science and Information Technology . illustrated Publisher Greenwood Publishing Group. p. 122. ISBN 9781573565219 . ^ Holohan, Dan (June 18, 2014). "Honeywell Heat Generator" . HeatingHelp . Archived from the original on June 14, 2022 . Retrieved June 14, 2022 .', '["clm_wiki_honeywell_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
