VALUES
  ('cs_3m_operations', 'org_3m', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '21st century body >div:not( ) body >div:not( ) 3M wordmark used from 1961 to 1978 On April 8, 2002, 3M''s 100th anniversary, the company changed its legal name to "3M Company". [1] [2] On September 8, 2008, 3M announced an agreement to acquire Meguiar''s, a car-care products company that was family-owned for over a century. [3] In August 2010, 3M acquired Cogent Systems for $943 million, [4] and on October 13, 2010, 3M completed acquisition of Arizant Inc. [5] In December 2011, 3M completed the acquisition of the Winterthur Technology Group, a bonded abrasives company. In 2011, 3M created CloudLibrary as part of its library systems unit as a competitor to OverDrive, Inc. ; in 2015 3M sold the North American part of that unit to Bibliotheca Group GmbH , a company founded in 2011 that was funded by One Equity Partners Capital Advisors, a division of JP Morgan Chase . [6] [7] As of 2012, 3M was one of the 30 companies included in the Dow Jones Industrial Average , added on August 9, 1976, and was 97 on the 2011 Fortune 500 list. [8] On January 3, 2012, it was announced that the Office and Consumer Products Division of Avery Dennison was being bought by 3M for $550 million. [9] The transaction was canceled by 3M in September 2012 amid antitrust concerns. [10] In May 2013, 3M sold Scientific Anglers and Ross Reels to Orvis . Ross Reels had been acquired by 3M in 2010. [11] In March 2017, 3M purchased Johnson Controls International Plc''s safety gear business, Scott Safety, for $2 billion. [12] In 2017, 3M had net sales for the year of $31.657 billion, up from $30.109 billion the year before. [13] In 2018, it was reported that the company would pay $850 million to end the Minnesota water pollution case concerning perfluorochemicals . [14] On May 25, 2018, Michael F. Roman was appointed CEO by the board of directors. [15] On December 19, 2018, 3M announced it had entered into a definitive agreement to acquire the technology business of M*Modal, for a total enterprise value of', '["clm_wiki_3m_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
