  ('cs_tesla-energy_history', 'org_tesla-energy', 'overview', 'History',
   'American solar energy generation and battery energy storage company Tesla Energy Operations, Inc. Type Division Industry Renewable energy Predecessors SolarCity Zep Solar Founded April 30, 2015 &#59;&#32;11 years ago ( 2015-04-30 ) Products Solar panels Solar Roof Powerwall Megapack Production output 31.4 GWh battery energy storage systems (2024) 223 MW solar (2023) Revenue US$ 10.1 billion (2024) Net income US$2.6 billion (2024) Total assets US$4.9 billion (2024) Parent Tesla, Inc. Website tesla /energy Footnotes Financials as of December 31,&#32;2024 &#91;update&#93; . References: [1] [2] body body This article is part of a series about Elon Musk Personal Awards and honors Business career Views Family Musk Foundation International relations Legal affairs Public image Texas Institute of Technology and Science Wealth Companies Zip2 PayPal X SpaceX Starlink Starshield xAI X Corp. Twitter under Elon Musk acquisition SEC investigation Tesla, Inc. SolarCity OpenAI Neuralink The Boring Company Terafab Thud Politics Activities America PAC America Party Building America''s Future Dept. of Govt. Efficiency Salute controversy Trade unions Tesla Protests Tesla Takedown vandalism Trump feud In the arts and media Character Limit Elon Musk by Vance Elon Musk''s Crash Course Elon Musk by Isaacson Filmography Ludicrous Make America Wait Again " The Musk Who Fell to Earth " Musk (film) Power Play Return to Space Revenge of the Electric Car The Space Barons html v t e Tesla Energy Operations, Inc. is the sustainable energy division of Tesla, Inc. that develops, manufactures, sells and installs photovoltaic solar energy generation systems , battery energy storage products and other related products and services to residential, commercial and industrial customers. The division was founded on April 30, 2015, when Tesla CEO Elon Musk announced that the company would apply the battery technology it developed for electric cars to a home energy storage system called the Powerwall . In November 2016, Tesla acquired SolarCity , in a US$2.6 billion deal, and added solar energy generation to Tesla Energy''s business. This deal was controversial; at the time of the acquisition, SolarCity was facing liquidity issues. The company''s current power generation products include solar panels (manufactured by other companies for Tesla), the Tesla Solar Roof (a solar shingle system), and the Tesla Solar Inverter. The company also makes a large-scale energy storage system called the Megapack . Addi', '["clm_wiki_tesla-energy_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
