   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_tesla-energy_operations', 'org_tesla-energy', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Tesla buys SolarCity Brothers Peter and Lyndon Rive , the cousins of Tesla CEO Elon Musk, founded SolarCity in 2006 to sell and install solar energy generation systems as well as other related products and services to residential, commercial and industrial customers. [1] [2] Musk suggested the solar company idea to the Rive brothers and he later served as the chairman of SolarCity. [3] In June 2014, SolarCity committed to building a second factory, later called Giga New York , in Buffalo, New York , that would build photovoltaic cells and would be triple the size of the next largest photovoltaic manufacturing plant in the United States. [4] By 2016, SolarCity had installed solar energy systems for over 325,000 customers and was one of the largest solar installation companies in the United States. [5] On August 1, 2016, Tesla announced that it would be acquiring SolarCity in an all-stock $2.6 billion acquisition. [6] Tesla''s mission since its inception has been "to accelerate the world''s transition to sustainable energy ". [7] Musk said the purchase would advance Tesla''s mission by helping the world move from a mine-and-burn hydrocarbon economy towards a solar electric economy. [8] The announcement cited (as benefits of the acquisition) operational and cost synergies, as well as allowing for integrated sales of products from Tesla''s existing battery energy storage products division. [9] The announcement of the deal resulted in a more than 10% drop in Tesla''s stock price. [10] The proposal for acquisition was approved by antitrust regulators in August 2016. [11] [12] More than 85% of unaffiliated shareholders of Tesla and SolarCity voted to approve the acquisition on November 17, [13] [14] allowing the deal to close on November 21, 2016. ^ body:not( ):not( ) Walsh, Bryan (April 17, 2008). "Green Start-Up Companies: Solarcity" . Time Magazine . Archived from the original on May 11, 2021 . Retrieved May 11, 2021 . ^ Walsh, Bryan (April 17, 2008). "The Environment - Gree', '["clm_wiki_tesla-energy_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
