VALUES
  ('cs_paypal_leadership', 'org_paypal', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Early history The company was originally established by Max Levchin , Peter Thiel , and Luke Nosek in December 1998 as Fieldlink. Later it was renamed Confinity , [1] a company which developed security software for hand-held devices. [2] When it had no success with that business model, it switched its focus to a digital wallet. [3] The first version of the PayPal electronic payments system was launched in 1999. [4] In March 2000, Confinity merged with X , an online financial services company founded in March 1999 by Elon Musk , Harris Fricker, Christopher Payne, and Ed Ho. [5] Musk was optimistic about the future success of the money transfer business Confinity was developing. [6] Musk and Bill Harris, then-president and CEO of the combined X , disagreed about the potential future success of the money transfer business and Harris left the company in May 2000. [7] In October 2000, Musk decided that X would terminate its other internet banking operations and focus on payments. [8] In the same month, Elon Musk was replaced by Peter Thiel as CEO of X , [9] which was renamed PayPal in June 2001 and went public in 2002. [10] [11] [12] PayPal''s IPO listed on NASDAQ under the ticker PYPL at $13 per share and generated over $61 million. [13] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Forrest, Conner (June 30, 2014). "How the ''PayPal Mafia'' redefined success in Silicon Valley" . TechRepublic . Archived from the original on November 4, 2014 . Retrieved November 11, 2014 . ^ Odell, Mark (September 30, 2014). "Timeline: The rise of PayPal" . Financial Times . Retrieved October 10, 2023 . ^ Cohan, Peter S. (September 5, 2013). "What PayPal''s Rocky Beginnings Can Teach You About Startup Success" . Entrepreneur Magazine . Archived from the original on November 12, 2014 . Retrieved November 11, 2014 . ^ "History of PayPal Inc. – FundingUniverse" . Archived from the original on November 11, 2020 . Retrieved November 12, 2014 . ^ Penenberg, Adam L. (August 9, 2012). "Reid Hoffman On PayPal''s Pivoted Path T', '["clm_wiki_paypal_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
