  ('cs_paypal_operations', 'org_paypal', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Finances Sales by region (2023) [1] Region share United States 58.0% Other Countries 42.0% The fiscal year for PayPal is from January 1 to December 31. For fiscal year 2019, PayPal reported earnings of US$2.459 billion, with an annual revenue of $17.772 billion, an increase of 15% over the previous fiscal cycle. PayPal''s shares traded at over $108 per share, and its market capitalization was valued at over $127.58 billion in December 2019. [2] [3] Year Revenue in million $ Net income in million $ Total Assets in million $ Price per Share in $ [4] Employees 2012 5,662 778 2013 6,727 955 19,160 2014 8,025 419 21,917 2015 9,248 1,228 28,881 16,800 2016 10,842 1,401 33,103 39.47 18,100 2017 13,094 1,795 40,774 73.62 18,700 2018 15,451 2,057 43,332 84.09 21,800 2019 17,772 2,459 51,333 108.17 23,200 2020 21,454 4,202 70,379 234.20 26,500 2021 25,371 4,169 75,803 188.58 30,900 2022 27,518 2,419 78,717 71.22 29,900 2023 29,771 4,246 82,166 61.41 27,200 2024 31,797 4,147 81,611 24,400 The COVID-19 pandemic has accelerated the growth of digital payment platforms, including PayPal, at the expense of the traditional banking sector. [5] As a result, PayPal has seen an increase in its stock to up to 78% in 2020 as of October. In addition, total payment volume has increased 29% amounting to $220 billion increasing positive investor sentiment. [6] PayPal laid off hundreds of workers across US offices and moved jobs overseas during the 2020-2022 pandemic. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "PayPal Holdings, Inc.: Shareholders Board Members Managers and Company Profile | US70450Y1038" . MarketScreener . Retrieved March 24, 2024 . ^ "Combined 2019 Annual Report / 2020 Proxy Statement" . PayPal Investor Relations . April 8, 2020. Archived from the original on July 17, 2020 . Retrieved August 9, 2020 . ^ "PayPal Holdings – Stock Price History: PYPL" . Macrotrends . Archived from the original on September 8, 2020 . Retrieved August 9, 2020 . ^ "PayPal Holdings - 9 Year Stock Price History: PYPL" . Ma', '["clm_wiki_paypal_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
