VALUES
  ('cs_thermo-fisher-scientific_leadership', 'org_thermo-fisher-scientific', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisition history In 1990, Thermo Fisher Scientific (then known as Thermo Instrument Systems) acquired mass spectrometer manufacturer Finnigan Instrument Corporation. [1] In 2003, the company (then Fisher Scientific International) acquired Perbio Science, a transaction that included brands such as Pierce Biotechnology, HyClone and Endogen. [2] In April 2006, BioImage was acquired by Thermo Fisher Scientific. [3] The merger was complete in November 2006, and technology transfer to a US site was completed during 2007 and 2008. [4] [5] BioImage was established in 1993 as a drug discovery research unit led by Ole Thastrup within Novo Nordisk , from which it spun out of in 1999. It had specialized in developing and selling proprietary bioassays to biopharmaceutical companies and research institutions. It made broad patents covering Enhanced GFP (EGFP), GFP-based biosensors and any genetically encoded protein fusion to a luminophore , with subsequent monitoring of the protein ''s translocation within a cell as the primary readout for drug discovery assays. [6] In December 2010, Thermo Fisher Scientific announced its acquisition of Dionex for $2.1 billion. [7] In May 2011, Thermo Fisher Scientific Inc. bought Phadia to expand into the testing of allergies and autoimmune diseases for €2.47 billion ($3.5 billion) in cash. [8] In April 2013, after a competitive bidding with Hoffmann-La Roche , [9] Thermo Fisher acquired Life Technologies Corporation for US$ 13.6 billion in a deal, adding further service lines related to advanced DNA sequencing and genetic testing. [10] Life Technologies was originally formed in 2008 through a $6.7B merger of Invitrogen , a cell therapy, and Applied Biosystems . [11] The company also acquired GIBCO (Grand Island Biological Company) as part of the Life Technologies acquisition. [12] In February 2015, the company announced it would acquire Advanced Scientifics for $300 million in a cash-deal. ASI designs manufactures, and delivers technologies ', '["clm_wiki_thermo-fisher-scientific_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
