   'Initial public offering (1992) On May 19, 1992, Boston Scientific launched an initial public offering of 23.5 million shares, of which 18.8 million were offered in the U.S. and 4.7 million were offered outside the U.S. The initial offering amounted to 23% of Boston Scientific''s outstanding stock. [1] &#58;&#8202;38&#8202; Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co. (lead) and PaineWebber Inc. were the underwriters and Abbott Laboratories held a 20% stake (23.5 million shares). The market capitalization was about $1.6 billion. [2] &#91; a &#93; The U.S. shares were listed on the New York Stock Exchange . [3] ^ Cite error: The named reference :0 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) "4 Apr 1992, 32 - Chicago Tribune at Newspapers " . Newspapers . Archived from the original on July 6, 2022 . Retrieved July 18, 2025 . ^ Solo, Sally (April 5, 1993). "Boston Scientific". Fortune . p. 97. Cite error: There are &lt;ref group&#61;lower-alpha&gt; tags or &#123;&#123;efn&#125;&#125; templates on this page, but the references will not show without a &#123;&#123;reflist&#124;group&#61;lower-alpha&#125;&#125; template or &#123;&#123;notelist&#125;&#125; template (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_boston-scientific_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
