  ('cs_pioneer-natural-resources_leadership', 'org_pioneer-natural-resources', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Divestitures and acquisitions # Year Acquisition / Divestiture Buyer / Seller Price Description of Assets Ref(s). 1 May 2004 Acquisition Evergreen Resources Inc. $2.1 billion in cash and stock Natural gas assets in Colorado [1] [2] 2 April 2012 Acquisition Carmeuse Industrial Sands $297 million Producer of Hickory frac sand [3] 3 May 2013 Divestiture Sinochem Group $1.7 billion 40% interest in approximately 207,000 net acres (84,000 net hectares) leased in horizontal Wolfcamp Shale [4] 4 October 2013 Divestiture Caelus Energy Alaska $550 million Interests in Alaska . In 2002, Pioneer made discoveries in its offshore Oooguruk field, west of Prudhoe Bay, Alaska . In 2008, Pioneer became the first independent operator to produce oil on the Alaska North Slope . [5] [6] 5 August 2014 Divestiture Linn Energy $340 million Non-producing assets in the Hugoton Basin [7] 6 June 2015 Divestiture Enterprise Products Partners $2.15 billion Midstream joint venture with Reliance Industries for assets in the Eagle Ford Group . JV was formed in 2010. [8] [9] 7 September 2016 Acquisition Devon Energy $435 million 28,000 acres in the Midland Basin [10] 8 March 2017 Divestiture Undisclosed $266 million 2,000 acres in Martin County, Texas [11] 9 January 2021 Acquisition Parsley Energy $7 billion in stock Assets in the Permian Basin [12] 10 April 2021 Acquisition DoublePoint Energy $6.4 billion in cash and stock Assets in the Midland Basin [13] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Pioneer and Evergreen in $2.1 Billion Energy Merger" . TheStreet . May 4, 2004. ^ "Pioneer and Evergreen Announce $2.1 Billion Merger" (Press release). U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . May 4, 2004. ^ "Pioneer Natural Resources Acquires Carmeuse Industrial Sands" . Hart Energy . March 5, 2012. ^ "Pioneer Natural Resources Announces Closing of $1.7 Billion Horizontal Wolfcamp Shale Transaction with Sinochem" (Press release). Business Wire . May 31, 2013 &#8211; via Yahoo . ^ "Pioneer to sell Alaska subsidiary for $550 m', '["clm_wiki_pioneer-natural-resources_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
