VALUES
  ('cs_pioneer-natural-resources_operations', 'org_pioneer-natural-resources', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisition by ExxonMobil In May 2024, in the largest merger in the petroleum industry in 20 years, Pioneer was acquired by ExxonMobil, making ExxonMobil the largest producer of shale gas in the Permian Basin . [1] [2] [3] Approval for the transaction from the Federal Trade Commission (FTC) was accompanied by a consent decree alleging that former Pioneer CEO Scott D. Sheffield colluded with OPEC to raise oil prices and making the merger conditional on Sheffield''s being barred from joining ExxonMobil''s board of directors or serving as an advisor to Exxon after the merger. [4] [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "ExxonMobil Completes Acquisition of Pioneer Natural Resources" (Press release). Business Wire . May 3, 2024. ^ Kumar, Arunima (May 3, 2024). "Exxon Mobil completes $60 billion deal for Pioneer Natural" . Reuters . ^ Krauss, Clifford (2023-10-11). "Exxon Mobil Strikes $60 Billion Deal for Shale Giant" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Archived from the original on October 26, 2023 . Retrieved 2026-04-01 . ^ "FTC bars former Pioneer CEO in Exxon Mobil deal, saying he colluded with OPEC" . NPR . Associated Press . May 2, 2024. ^ Pequeño IV, Antonio (May 2, 2024). "FTC Will Approve Exxon''s $60 Billion Merger With Pioneer—With One Caveat" . Forbes .', '["clm_wiki_pioneer-natural-resources_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
