VALUES
  ('cs_southwest-airlines_leadership', 'org_southwest-airlines', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Destinations Main article: List of Southwest Airlines destinations A 737-700 of Southwest in their Canyon Blue livery Southwest uses a point-to-point system combined with a rolling-hub model in its base cities, in contrast to the hub-and-spoke system of other major airlines. As of June 2026 &#91;update&#93; , Southwest Airlines flew to over 100 destinations in 43 states, Puerto Rico , Mexico , Central America , and the Caribbean . [1] This system means that the airline has no real hubs, but rather some airports with more destinations than others. Interline agreements The 727 pictured along with others were leased from other airlines and were eventually retired in 2000. Southwest currently has interline agreements with the following airlines: Air Premia [2] All Nippon Airways [3] China Airlines [4] Condor [5] EVA Air [6] Icelandair [7] Philippine Airlines [8] Singapore Airlines [9] Turkish Airlines [10] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Southwest Airlines Route Map" . Southwest Airlines . Retrieved June 8, 2026 . ^ "Southwest Signs Interline Deal With Air Premia" . Airlinegeeks . July 8, 2026 . Retrieved July 8, 2026 . ^ "MSN" . Msn . Retrieved June 23, 2026 . ^ "Southwest Newsroom" . SWA Newsroom . Retrieved July 30, 2025 . ^ "Southwest Airlines Teams Up With Condor Bringing Additional Travel Options Across the Atlantic" . SWA Newsroom . Retrieved December 2, 2025 . ^ "EVA Air and Southwest Airlines Launch Interline Partnership to Expand Seamless Travel Between Asia and North America" . Evaair . ^ "Does Southwest Airlines interline with any other airlines?" . Support . Retrieved March 22, 2025 . ^ "Southwest Airlines and Philippine Airlines launch partnership" . Southwestairlinesinvestorrelations . November 4, 2025. ^ "Southwest Signs Interline Deal With Singapore Airlines" . Airlinegeeks . June 8, 2026 . Retrieved June 8, 2026 . ^ "Southwest Airlines and Turkish Airlines to partner in transatlantic travel beginning in January 2026" . Southwestairlinesinvestorrelations (Press r', '["clm_wiki_southwest-airlines_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
