VALUES
  ('cs_republic-services_leadership', 'org_republic-services', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisitions # Date Company Price Description of Assets Ref(s). 1 May 1996 Continental Waste Industries $240 million Solid waste services [1] 2 January 1997 Meyer Waste Systems Inc. of Chesterton, Ind.; Monarch Environmental Inc. of Bowling Green, Ky.; and Rainbow Industries Inc. of Chantilly, Va. $79 million in stock Waste management businesses [2] [3] 3 February 1997 Taormina Industries $250 million 1 million customers in Southern California . [4] 4 December 2008 Allied Waste Industries $6.1 billion in stock Company became the second largest waste management company in the United States [5] [6] 5 October 2014 Rainbow Disposal Waste disposal services in Southern California . [7] 6 December 2014 U.S. operations of Alberta-based Tervita [8] 7 October 2017 ReCommunity Largest independent recycler in U.S. [9] 8 May 2021 Santek Waste Services $450 million Recycling and waste services operations primarily in the Southeastern United States [10] 9 September 2021 ACV Enviro Environmental services; acquired from Kinderhook Industries [11] [12] 10 February 2022 River City Waste Services Waste pickup in Illinois [13] 11 May 2022 US Ecology $2.2 billion Waste management and emergency response services [14] [15] 12 February 2025 Shamrock Environmental industrial waste and wastewater services platform. [16] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Republic Industries Intends To Buy Continental Waste" . The Wall Street Journal . May 21, 1996 . Retrieved 2026-07-31 . ^ "Republic Industries Acquires Three Waste-Management Firms" . The Wall Street Journal . January 16, 1997 . Retrieved 2026-07-31 . ^ "Republic Industries completes $60 million purchase of ..." . American City Business Journals . June 2, 1997 . Retrieved 2026-07-31 . ^ "Republic Industries Will Buy Waste Hauler for $250 Million" . The Wall Street Journal . February 5, 1997 . Retrieved 2026-07-31 . ^ Malone, Scott; Hall, Jessica (June 23, 2008). "Republic to buy Allied in $6 billion waste deal" . Reuters . Retrieved 2026-07-31 . ^ Corkery', '["clm_wiki_republic-services_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
