VALUES
  ('cs_general-mills_history', 'org_general-mills', 'overview', 'History',
   'American multinational food corporation For other uses, see General Mills (disambiguation) . General Mills, Inc. Logo used since December 2017 &#91; a &#93; Formerly Minneapolis Milling Company (1856–1877) Washburn-Crosby Company (1877–1928) Type Public Traded as NYSE : GIS S&amp;P 500 component Industry Food processing Founded 1856 &#59;&#32;170 years ago ( 1856 ) (as Minneapolis Milling Company) 1877 &#59;&#32;149 years ago ( 1877 ) (as Washburn-Crosby Company) 1928 &#59;&#32;98 years ago ( 1928 ) (as General Mills) Minneapolis , Minnesota, US Founders Robert Smith Cadwallader C. Washburn John Crosby James Ford Bell Headquarters Golden Valley, Minnesota , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Jeffrey Harmening ( chairman and CEO ) Products Baking mixes , breakfast cereals , yogurt , refrigerated dough , soup , pizza , snack foods , ice cream , soy products, vegetables , flour , other food products [1] Revenue US$ 19.86 billion (2024) Operating income US$3.432 billion (2024) Net income US$2.497 billion (2024) Total assets US$31.47 billion (2024) Total equity US$9.397 billion (2024) Number of employees 34,000 (May 2024) Subsidiaries Cereal Partners Worldwide (50%) Website generalmills Footnotes Financials as of fiscal year ended&#32;May 26,&#32;2024 &#91;update&#93; . References: [2] General Mills, Inc. is an American multinational manufacturer and marketer of branded consumer foods sold through retail stores. Founded on the banks of the Mississippi River at Saint Anthony Falls in Minneapolis , the company originally gained fame for being a large flour miller . It is headquartered in Golden Valley, Minnesota , a suburb of Minneapolis. Today, the company markets many well-known North American brands, including Gold Medal flour, Annie''s Homegrown , Lärabar , Cascadian Farm, Betty Crocker , Nature Valley , Totino''s , Pillsbury , Old El Paso , Häagen-Dazs , as well as breakfast cereals under the General Mills name, including Cheerios , Wheaties , Chex , Lucky Charms , Trix , Cocoa Puffs , and the monster cereals . [3] Cite error: There are &lt;ref group&#61;lower-alpha&gt; tags or &#123;&#123;efn&#125;&#125; templates on this page, but the references will not show without a &#123;&#123;reflist&#124;group&#61;lower-alpha&#125;&#125; template or &#123;&#123;notelist&#125;&#125; template (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Our Brands" . ^ "General Mills, Inc. FY 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . sec . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . June 26, 202', '["clm_wiki_general-mills_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_general-mills_leadership', 'org_general-mills', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Washburn-Crosby Company The company can trace its history to the Minneapolis Milling Company , incorporated in 1856. [1] The company was founded by Illinois congressman Robert Smith , who leased power rights to flour mills operating along the west side of Saint Anthony Falls on the Mississippi River in Minneapolis, Minnesota . Cadwallader C. Washburn acquired the company shortly after its founding and hired his brother William D. Washburn to assist in the company''s development. In 1866 the Washburns got into the business themselves, building the Washburn "B" Mill at the falls. At the time, the building was considered to be so large and output so vast that it could not possibly sustain itself. However, the company succeeded, and in 1874 he built the even bigger Washburn "A" Mill . In 1877, the mill entered a partnership with John Crosby to form the Washburn-Crosby Company , producing winter wheat flour. That same year Washburn sent William Hood Dunwoody to England to open the market for spring wheat. [2] Dunwoody was successful and became a silent partner. In 1878, the "A" mill was destroyed in a flour dust explosion along with five nearby buildings, an event known as the Great Mill Disaster . The ensuing fire led to the death of 18 workers. [3] Construction of a new mill began immediately. Not only was the new mill safer but it also was able to produce a higher quality flour after the old grinding stones were replaced with automatic steel rollers, the first ever used. In 1880, Washburn-Crosby flour brands won gold, silver and bronze medals at the Millers'' International Exhibition in Cincinnati , causing them to launch the Gold Medal flour brand. [4] In 1924, the company acquired a failing Twin Cities radio station, WLAG, renaming it WCCO (from Washburn-Crosby Company). ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Mill City Timeline" . millcitymuseum . Archived from the original on April 1, 2018 . Retrieved September 13, 2014 . ^ "The Story of a Grain of Wheat" . Angelfire . ^ "Washburn ''A', '["clm_wiki_general-mills_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_general-mills_operations', 'org_general-mills', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Founding as General Mills General Mills itself was created on June 20, 1928, [1] when Washburn-Crosby President James Ford Bell merged Washburn-Crosby with three other mills. [2] In the same year, General Mills acquired the Wichita Mill and Elevator Company of the industrialist Frank Kell of Wichita Falls , Texas . With the sale, Kell acquired cash plus stock in the corporation. [3] Postcard image of the Gold Medal Flour factory in Minneapolis c. &#8201;1900 Shares of the new company''s stock were first sold on the New York Stock Exchange on November 30, 1928, at $65 per share. The newly merged company paid a dividend in 1928 and has continued the dividend uninterrupted ever since – one of only a few companies to pay a dividend every year since its founding. [1] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "General Mills 150 - Making Food People Love" . GeneralMills . Archived from the original on July 26, 2021 . Retrieved April 5, 2016 . ^ Staff report (May 8, 1961). James Bell Ford of General Mills; Founder of Concern Is Dead at 81 -- Was Philanthropist New York Times ^ "J. W. Williams, "Frank Kell" " . tshaonline . Retrieved April 16, 2013 .', '["clm_wiki_general-mills_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 102. Kraft Heinz (slug=kraft-heinz, wiki='Kraft Heinz')
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_kraft-heinz_overview', 'org_kraft-heinz', 'overview', 'Overview',
   'The Kraft Heinz Company, commonly known as Kraft Heinz, is an American multinational food company formed on July 2, 2015, through the merger of Kraft Foods Group and the H.J. Heinz Company. It is co-headquartered in Chicago and Pittsburgh and manufactures and markets packaged foods and beverages under brands including Kraft, Heinz, Oscar Mayer, Philadelphia, Lunchables, Velveeta, Maxwell House, and Jell-O. In fiscal 2025, the company reported net sales of US$24.9 billion and employed approximately 35,000 people in 40 countries.', '["clm_wiki_kraft-heinz_overview"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   10, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
