VALUES
  ('cs_tyson-foods_operations', 'org_tyson-foods', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Meat alternatives and clean meat In 2016, Tyson Foods bought a 5% stake in the meat alternative company Beyond Meat , becoming the first major meat producer to invest in a meat alternative company. [1] [2] Tyson made an additional investment in Beyond Meat in 2017. [3] In 2019, Tyson sold its stake in advance of Beyond Meat''s initial public offering , with CEO Noel White saying Tyson intended to develop its own meat alternatives. [4] The company also developed the "blended products" line called Raised and Rooted , which featured a combination of animal and plant based ingredients. [5] This line initially included vegetarian nuggets as well as burgers with a blend of beef and pea protein , [6] [7] then expanded to include tenders. In 2020, Tyson discontinued the burger and removed egg whites from the nuggets, announcing that the Raised &amp; Rooted brand would be free of animal products moving forward. [8] [9] In early 2018, Tyson, through its venture capital arm Tyson Ventures, funded clean meat (cultured meat) research with an investment in California-based Memphis Meats . [10] [11] [12] [13] The same year, Tyson Ventures also invested $2.2 million in Israel-based clean meat company Future Meat . [14] [15] Former CEO Tom Hayes said Tyson''s investments in clean meat and meat alternatives "might seem counterintuitive", but they are part of an effort to meet future consumer demand in a sustainable way. [16] [17] [18] The company also announced in July 2015 that it had reduced the use of human antibiotics in its chicken by more than 84% since 2011. [19] [20] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Strom, Stephanie (October 10, 2016). "Tyson Foods, a Meat Leader, Invests in Protein Alternatives (Published 2016)" . The New York Times . Retrieved January 31, 2021 . ^ "Tyson snags a stake in Beyond Meat" . Food Dive . Retrieved January 31, 2021 . ^ "Beyond Meat secures $55m from funding round including Tyson" . Retrieved January 31, 2021 . ^ "Tyson sells stake in plant-based meat maker Beyon', '["clm_wiki_tyson-foods_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 105. Mars (slug=mars, wiki='Mars')
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
