VALUES
  ('cs_h-e-b_history', 'org_h-e-b', 'overview', 'History',
   'American supermarket chain based in San Antonio, Texas For other uses, see HEB . H-E-B Grocery Company, LP Trade name H-E-B Formerly C.C. Butt Grocery Store (1905–1927) Type Private Industry Grocery retail Founded November 26, 1905 &#32;(120 years ago) ( 1905-11-26 ) as C.C. Butt Grocery Store in Kerrville, Texas , United States Founder Florence Butt Headquarters San Antonio , Texas , United States Number of locations Over 435 stores (United States and Mexico) Area served Texas Mexico Aguascalientes Coahuila Guanajuato Nuevo León Querétaro San Luis Potosí Tamaulipas Key people Charles Butt ( chairman ) Howard Butt III ( CEO ) [1] Craig Boyan ( president ) [2] Roxanne Orsak ( COO ) Products Bakery, dairy, deli, frozen foods, gasoline, general grocery, meat, pharmacy, produce, seafood, snacks, toys Services Auto, health, fuel, ticket sales, utilities, and licenses Revenue US$ 46.5 billion (2024) [3] Owners Butt family (90%) Employee-owned (10%) [4] Number of employees 154,000 [3] (2025) Subsidiaries Central Market Favor Delivery H-E-B Mexico Website www Footnotes [5] H-E-B Grocery Company, LP , is an American privately held supermarket chain based in San Antonio, Texas , with more than 435 stores [6] throughout Texas and Mexico . [7] [8] The company also operates Central Market , an upscale organic and fine foods retailer. [9] As of 2024, the company had a total revenue of US$ 46.5 billion. [10] H-E-B ranked number 6 on Forbes &#39; 2022 list of "America''s Largest Private Companies". [11] The company also ranked number 3 on Forbes'' 2024 list of "Customer Experience All-Stars." [12] H-E-B was named Retailer of the Year in 2010 by Progressive Grocer . [13] Supermarket News ranks H-E-B 13th on the list of "Top 75 North American Food Retailers" by sales. [14] Based on 2019 revenues, H-E-B is the 19th-largest retailer in the United States. [15] It donates 5% of pretax profits to charity. [16] The official mascot of H-E-B is named H-E-Buddy, an anthropomorphic brown grocery bag , with multiple grocery items emerging from the top. [17] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Grieder, Erica (May 18, 2024). "H-E-B is Texas''s favorite business. Here''s what to know about the grocer" . Houston Chronicle . ^ "H-E-B Names Boyan President, COO" . Supermarket News. February 1, 2010 . Retrieved April 23, 2024 . ^ a b Iszler, Madison (December 26, 2024). "H-E-B, SpaceX, Zachry back on list of America''s biggest private companies. See where they ranked" . San Antonio Express-News . Retrieved July', '["clm_wiki_h-e-b_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
