VALUES
  ('cs_h-e-b_operations', 'org_h-e-b', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History The company was founded on November 26, 1905, when Florence Butt opened the C.C. Butt Grocery Store on the ground floor of her family home in Kerrville, Texas . [1] In 1919, Howard Edward Butt Sr. , Florence''s youngest son, took over the store upon his return from World War I. Shortly after becoming owner of his mother''s small store, Howard tried four expansions into Central Texas, including one in Junction , all of which failed. Finally, in 1927, Howard launched a successful second store in Del Rio, Texas , followed by the purchase of three grocery stores in the Lower Rio Grande Valley . The initials of Howard E. Butt became the name of the store. [2] Charles , the younger son of Howard E. Butt, became president of H-E-B in 1971. As of 2019, Charles Butt is chairman and CEO of H-E-B, having grown the business from annual sales of $250 million in 1971 to $13 billion in 2006. In 2010, Craig Boyan was named H-E-B''s president and COO . [3] By 2018, Martin Otto, the former CFO and chief merchant, had become the COO. [4] In 2011, the company was #12 on Forbes''s list of "America''s Largest Private Companies". [5] H-E-B is the largest privately held company and largest private employer in Texas. [6] H-E-B acquired Favor Delivery as a wholly owned subsidiary in February 2018. The details of the merger were not disclosed. [7] In 2019, H-E-B invested millions of dollars to replace cashier stations with self-checkout kiosks or smartphone apps, following the trend of national supermarkets (such as Walmart and Target ) towards self-checkout technology. [8] In 2025, H-E-B named current chief operating officer Roxanne Orsak as president, effective January 2026. She will succeed Craig Boyan, who is transitioning to senior advisor. [9] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "History Timeline for HEB Grocery" . H-E-B. ^ Kleiner, Diana J. "H-E-B" . The Handbook of Texas Online . Texas State Historical Association . Retrieved November 8, 2010 . ^ "Craig Boyan to Lead H-E-B as New President and CO', '["clm_wiki_h-e-b_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
