VALUES
  ('cs_anheuser-busch_history', 'org_anheuser-busch', 'overview', 'History',
   'Belgian-owned American brewing company This article is about the St. Louis based company. For the parent company, see AB InBev . For the historic brewery, see Anheuser-Busch Brewery . Anheuser-Busch Companies, LLC Formerly Bavarian Brewery (1852-1860) E. Anheuser &amp; Company (1860-1875) E. Anheuser Company Brewing Association (1875-1879) Anheuser-Busch Brewing Association (1879-1919) Anheuser-Busch, Inc. (1919-1979) Anheuser-Busch Companies, Inc. (1979-2013) Type Subsidiary Industry beverages beverage packaging Founded 1852 &#59;&#32;174 years ago ( 1852 ) (as Bavarian Brewery) Founder Eberhard Anheuser [1] Adolphus Busch [1] Headquarters St. Louis, Missouri , U.S. Number of locations 12 breweries &amp; 9 can plants Area served North America Key people Brendan Whitworth [2] (president and CEO) Products beer malt beverages energy drinks bottled water Revenue US$15.588 billion (2018) [3] Net income US$9.811 billion (2018) [3] Parent AB InBev Website anheuser-busch Anheuser-Busch delivery Truck (1905) Anheuser-Busch Companies, LLC [4] ( / ˈ æ n h aɪ z ər ˈ b ʊ ʃ / AN -hy-zər BUUSH ) is a Belgian-American brewing company headquartered in St. Louis , Missouri. [5] Since 2008, following the hostile takeover by AB Inbev of Belgium, it has been wholly owned by Anheuser-Busch InBev SA/NV ( AB InBev ), the world''s largest brewing company, [6] [5] [7] [8] which owns global brands such as Budweiser , Michelob , Stella Artois , and Beck''s . [9] The company employs over 19,000 people, [10] operates 12 breweries and nine aluminum can plants in the United States, [11] and until December 2009, was one of the largest theme park operators in the United States, with ten theme parks through the company''s family entertainment division Busch Entertainment Corporation . [12] 38°35′57″N 90°12′52″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 38.59917°N 90.21444°W &#xfeff; / 38.59917; -90.21444 ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "Heritage &#124; Anheuser-Busch" . anheuser-busch . Archived from the original on May 8, 2023 . Retrieved May 8, 2023 . ^ "Our Leaders" . Archived from the original on August 16, 2018 . Retrieved August 15, 2018 . ^ a b revenue and gross profit for 2018 was reported by zone unit and therefore includes other North American subsidiaries of AB InBev, from pg. 58 of company annual report ^ "Company Overview of Anheuser-Busch Companies, LLC" . Bloomberg Research . Bloomberg. February 5, 2017. Archived from the original on March 3, 2018 . Retrieved February 5, 2017 . Anheuser-Busch Companies, LL', '["clm_wiki_anheuser-busch_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
