VALUES
  ('cs_constellation-brands_history', 'org_constellation-brands', 'overview', 'History',
   'Breweries Constellation Brands has two breweries in Mexico that produce Corona and Modelo beer for the US market. Those locations are in Nava, Coahuila , and Ciudad Obregón , Sonora . [1] A third Brewery in Mexicali Baja California was never finished due to environmental issues. [2] Instead, Constellation is building its third brewery in Veracruz , Mexico. [3] [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) INDUSTRY, MEXICO. "Constellation Brands starts its second expansion stage on its plant in Nava" . Invest In Mexico . Retrieved June 15, 2023 . ^ "Mexico: Constellation Brands to dismantle 10m hl brewery within two years" . www . February 26, 2021 . Retrieved June 15, 2023 . ^ Madry, Kylie (January 7, 2022). "Mexico says Constellation brewery to be built by river after water dispute" . Reuters . Retrieved June 15, 2023 . ^ "Mexico says Constellation brewery to be built by river after water dispute" . Yahoo Finance . January 7, 2022 . Retrieved June 15, 2023 .', '["clm_wiki_constellation-brands_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_constellation-brands_leadership', 'org_constellation-brands', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'History Early days The company was established in 1945 by Marvin Sands in the Finger Lakes region of New York as Canandaigua Industries, selling bulk wine to bottlers in the eastern United States. [1] In its first year, the company sold approximately 200,000 gallons of wine and had gross sales of $150,000. [2] The company was incorporated as Canandaigua Wine Company, Inc. in 1972 and went public in 1973. [3] Marvin''s son Richard Sands became president in 1993 and CEO in 1996. [1] In 1999, Marvin Sands died following a brief illness. [1] In 1987, the company purchased the Manischewitz winery in Canandaigua, New York , and continues to license the Manischewitz name from R.A.B. Foods. [4] Expansion In 2000, the company changed its name to Constellation Brands, Inc. to reflect the scope of the company and its range of brands. [2] In 2007, Rob Sands was named president and CEO. [5] During the 2000s, there were multiple acquisitions, with some divestments later in the decade. Acquisitions included BRL Hardy (Australia) [6] and Nobilo (New Zealand) in 2003; Robert Mondavi Corp. for $1 billion in 2004; [7] Vincor International, Canada''s largest wine company, for $1.44 billion in 2006; [8] Spirits Marque One (owner of Svedka Vodka) in 2007; [9] and Beam Wines Estates, the wine operations of Fortune Brands (which included several major brands such as Clos du Bois) for $885 million in 2008. [10] The company later moved to a more premium wine portfolio, divesting Almaden Vineyards , Inglenook Winery , and the Paul Masson winery in Madera, California , in 2008, [11] and its value spirits portfolio to the Sazerac Company in 2009. [12] They sold 30 low-cost wine labels in January 2021 to E. &amp; J. Gallo for $810 million including Clos du Bois . [13] In 2013, Constellation acquired Grupo Modelo''s US beer business from Anheuser-Busch InBev , who were required to divest the business as a part of an anti-trust settlement permitting Anheuser-Busch InBev to acquire Grupo Modelo. [14] ', '["clm_wiki_constellation-brands_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
