VALUES
  ('cs_constellation-brands_operations', 'org_constellation-brands', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Early days The company was established in 1945 by Marvin Sands in the Finger Lakes region of New York as Canandaigua Industries, selling bulk wine to bottlers in the eastern United States. [1] In its first year, the company sold approximately 200,000 gallons of wine and had gross sales of $150,000. [2] The company was incorporated as Canandaigua Wine Company, Inc. in 1972 and went public in 1973. [3] Marvin''s son Richard Sands became president in 1993 and CEO in 1996. [1] In 1999, Marvin Sands died following a brief illness. [1] In 1987, the company purchased the Manischewitz winery in Canandaigua, New York , and continues to license the Manischewitz name from R.A.B. Foods. [4] ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) Fisher, Lawrence (August 31, 1999). "Marvin Sands, Winery''s Chairman, Dies at 75" . The New York Times . Retrieved June 6, 2017 . ^ Constellation Brands. "Constellation Brands &#124; History and Heritage" . Archived from the original on June 19, 2017 . Retrieved April 16, 2018 . ^ Paulson, Lynn. "The birth of Canandaigua Industries" . mpnnow . Archived from the original on December 15, 2018 . Retrieved April 14, 2018 . ^ "Manischewitz wine - heritage - history" . Archived from the original on August 1, 2008 . Retrieved 2008-09-06 .', '["clm_wiki_constellation-brands_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
