VALUES
  ('cs_whirlpool_operations', 'org_whirlpool', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Saltstraumen Saltstraumen Main article: Saltstraumen Saltstraumen is a narrow strait located close to the Arctic Circle , [1] 33 km (20 mi) south-east of the city of Bodø , Norway . It has one of the strongest tidal currents in the world. [2] [1] Whirlpools up to 10 metres (33 ft) in diameter and 5 metres (16 ft) in depth are formed when the current is at its strongest. ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Doyle, James (1 March 2012). A Young Scientist''s Guide to Defying Disasters . Gibbs Smith. p. 15. ISBN 978-1-4236-2441-7 . ^ "Er Saltstraumen egentlig verdens sterkeste tidevannsstrøm?" (English: Is Saltstraumen really the worlds strongest tidal current?), from NRK (www .no), 7 May 2016, Accessed 17 January 2021', '["clm_wiki_whirlpool_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
