VALUES
  ('cs_mattel_operations', 'org_mattel', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisitions: International Games, Fisher-Price, American Girl, Bluebird Toys In 1992, Mattel created the first President Barbie. Barbie has run for president seven times since 1992, and an all-ticket was released in 2016. [1] On October 8, 1992, Mattel opened its first production factory in Indonesia at the Jababeka Industrial Park in Cikarang , West Java , as the west plant, and expanded by opening a new plant in 1997, as the east plant. The west plant is now the main factory of Hot Wheels 5-car pack edition, and the east plant is now the main factory of Barbie dolls. [2] Mattel entered the gaming business in 1992 with the purchase of International Games, creators of UNO and Skip-Bo . [3] [4] The company purchased Fisher-Price, Inc. on August 20, 1993, and Tyco Toys, Inc. (owners of the Matchbox and Dinky Toys brands) in 1997. [5] In 1998, Mattel acquired Pleasant Company (creators of the American Girl brand) [6] and Swindon , England-based toymaker Bluebird Toys (along with its most prized property, Polly Pocket ). In the same year, the first American Girl retail store opened for business in Chicago . [7] In 1997, the Fisher-Price Little People toys underwent a redesign to look more like real kids with different skin colors, added arms and hands, and greater detail on the face, hair, and clothes. [8] Also that year, Mattel acquired View-Master , [9] and Hot Wheels partnered with NASCAR drivers Kyle Petty and Jack Baldwin leading to the production of the first NASCAR-themed vehicles. [10] In 1998, Mattel donated $25 million to help rebuild UCLA''s children''s hospital, which was later renamed the UCLA Mattel Children''s Hospital . [11] Barbie was inducted into the National Toy Hall of Fame that year. [12] The same year, Mattel purchased Bluebird Toys . &#91; citation needed &#93; Mattel purchased The Learning Company (formerly SoftKey) in 1999 for $3.5 billion, but sold it the following year at a loss. The company had a $430.9 million net loss that year. [6] On July ', '["clm_wiki_mattel_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
