  ('cs_lowes_operations', 'org_lowes', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Historical data For the fiscal year 2019 (2/1/2019-1/31/2020), Lowe''s reported earnings of US$4.281 billion, with an annual revenue of US$72.148 billion, an increase of 1.17% over the previous fiscal cycle. [1] Lowe''s shares traded at over $116 per share, [2] and its market capitalization was valued at over US$90.32 billion in January 2020. [3] Lowe''s ranked No. 42 on the 2019 Fortune 500 list [4] . Lowes announced a $10 billion stock buyback [5] at the end of 2018 to begin in 2019, while trimming jobs. [6] For the fiscal year 2018, Lowe''s reported earnings of US$2.314 billion, with an annual revenue of US$71.309 billion, an increase of 3.92% over the previous fiscal cycle. Lowe''s shares traded at over $96 per share, and its market capitalization was valued at over US$75.8 billion in October 2018. [7] Lowe''s ranked No. 40 on the 2018 Fortune 500 list of the largest United States corporations by total revenue. [8] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Annual Reports &amp; Proxy Statements" . Lowe''s Corporate . Retrieved July 10, 2026 . ^ "Stock closing price, LOW" . finance . January 31, 2020 . Retrieved July 10, 2026 . ^ "Lowe''s Market Cap 2010-2023 &#124; LOW" . www . Retrieved July 10, 2026 . ^ "Lowe''s" . Fortune . Retrieved July 10, 2026 . ^ "Lowe''s shares rise as retailer announces $10 billion stock buyback, 2019 forecast" . finance . Retrieved July 10, 2026 . ^ "Lowes layoffs" . August 13, 2019 . Retrieved July 10, 2026 . ^ "Lowe''s Revenue 2006-2018" . Macrotrends . Retrieved October 30, 2018 . ^ "Fortune 500 Companies 2018: Who Made the List" . Fortune . Archived from the original on January 15, 2019 . Retrieved November 10, 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_lowes_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
