VALUES
  ('cs_ross-stores_history', 'org_ross-stores', 'overview', 'History',
   'American discount department store chain Not to be confused with Roses (store) . Ross Stores, Inc. Trade name Ross Dress for Less Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : ROST Nasdaq-100 component S&amp;P 500 component Industry Retail Founded 1950 &#59;&#32;76 years ago ( 1950 ) , in Pacifica, California , U.S. [1] Founder Morris Ross Bill Isackson Headquarters Dublin, California , U.S. Number of locations 1,795 (Ross Dress for Less) [2] 353 (DD''s Discounts) [3] Area served United States Guam Puerto Rico Key people James Conroy ( CEO ) K. Gunnar Bjorklund ( Executive Chairman ) Michael J. Hartshorn ( COO ) Karen Fleming ( CMO ) Products Clothing, footwear, bedding, bath, furniture, home decor, jewelry, beauty products, toys, appliances, housewares, and giftware. Revenue US$ 14.89 billion (2018) [4] Operating income US$1.61 billion (2015) Net income US$1.02 billion (2015) Total assets US$4.87 billion (2015) Total equity US$2.47 billion (2015) Number of employees 88,100 (2019) Subsidiaries dd''s Discounts Website rossstores ddsdiscounts Footnotes [5] Ross Stores, Inc. , operating under the brand name Ross Dress for Less , is an American chain of discount department stores headquartered in Dublin, California . [6] It is the largest off-price retailer in the U.S.; as of July 2024, Ross operates 1,795 stores in 43 U.S. states , Washington, D.C. Puerto Rico and Guam , [7] covering much of the country, but with no presence in Alaska . [8] The company also operates DD''s Discounts , a discount department store chain with over 353 locations across the United States, most of which are located in Sun Belt states. [9] &#91; why? &#93; ^ body:not( ):not( ) "OBITUARY -- Morris Ross" . December 5, 1997. ^ "Ross Stores adds 24 new locations in 2 months" . ^ "Number of dd''s DISCOUNTS stores in the United States in 2023 -" . scapehero . ^ Jain, Chelsi. "Revenue Updated" . Ross Stores . ^ "Fortune 500 - 209 Ross Stores" . Fortune . Retrieved August 26, 2019 . ^ "Ross Stores" . True Work . Retrieved August 26, 2019 . ^ "Ross Stores adds 24 new locations in 2 months" . Retail Dive . Retrieved July 25, 2024 . ^ rvl. "Ross locations &amp; hours" . storesinfo . ^ "Number of dd''s DISCOUNTS stores in the United States in 2023 -" . scapehero .', '["clm_wiki_ross-stores_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
