VALUES
  ('cs_vf_leadership', 'org_vf', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Spinoff In August 2018, it was announced that VF would split into two separate companies. The jeans and outlet stores would be spun off as Kontoor Brands . VF kept the sports apparel and footwear businesses, and moved its corporate headquarters (and around 800 employees) to Denver, Colorado. An 11-story office building at 1551 Wewatta Street near Denver Union Station became VF''s new corporate headquarters. [1] All brands which until 2018 had maintained separate divisional headquarters (e.g., Jansport) were consolidated into VF''s new Denver headquarters. Kontoor Brands Inc. became a separate company with the stock symbol KTB in May 2019. Kontoor includes Lee , Wrangler , Rock &amp; Republic and VF Outlets. That company had 17,000 employees. [2] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "VF Corporation, parent company of outdoor brands The North Face, Smartwool, will relocate headquarters, 800 workers to Denver" . August 13, 2018. ^ Craver, Richard (May 25, 2019). "Kontoor begins independent life with focus on jeans innovation, attracting new customers" . Winston-Salem Journal . Retrieved May 26, 2019 .', '["clm_wiki_vf_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
