   'Early career From 1962 to 1964, Lauren served in the United States Army . After his discharge, he worked briefly for Brooks Brothers as a sales assistant before becoming a salesman for Rivetz, a necktie company. [1] At age 28, working for tie manufacturer Beau Brummell, Lauren convinced the company president to let him start his own line. He launched The Ralph Lauren Corporation in 1967 with men''s ties. [2] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Oprah Interviews Ralph Lauren" . Oprah . Archived from the original on May 25, 2016 . Retrieved May 1, 2011 . ^ "Ralph Lauren Greatest Moments" . Vanity Fair . August 21, 2012 . Retrieved October 24, 2016 .', '["clm_wiki_ralph-lauren_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
