VALUES
  ('cs_hanesbrands_history', 'org_hanesbrands', 'overview', 'History',
   'American clothing company Hanesbrands Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : HBI Founded 1901 &#59;&#32;125 years ago ( 1901 ) Founder John Wesley Hanes (Shamrock Mills) Pleasant H. Hanes (P. H. Hanes Knitting Company) Headquarters Winston-Salem, North Carolina , U.S. Number of locations 423 outlet stores (2024) Key people Stephen B. Bratspies ( CEO ) [1] [2] Scott Lewis ( CFO ) [3] [4] Brands Hanes Playtex Bali L''eggs Just My Size Barely There Wonderbra Maidenform Berlei Bonds Revenue US$ 3.51 billion (2024) Operating income US$186 million (2024) Net income US$−320 million (2024) Total assets US$3.84 billion (2024) Total equity US$34 million (2024) Owner Gildan Number of employees 41,000 (2024) Website www /corporate Footnotes [5] A tag on the inside of a Hanes T-shirt Hanesbrands Inc. is an American multinational clothing company based in Winston-Salem, North Carolina . [6] Employing 65,300 people internationally, [7] it owns several clothing brands, including Hanes , Playtex , Bali , L''eggs , Just My Size, Barely There, Wonderbra , Maidenform , Berlei , and Bonds . The company was acquired by Gildan in 2025. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Board of Directors &#124; Hanesbrands Inc" . ir . ^ "HanesBrands Board of Directors Appoints Stephen B. Bratspies as Chief Executive Officer, Effective Aug. 3, 2020" . www . June 9, 2020. ^ Hardison, Kathryn (12 January 2023). "Hanesbrands CFO Michael Dastugue Resigns; Scott Lewis Named Interim CFO" . Wall Street Journal . ^ "HanesBrands Updates Fourth Quarter 2022 Financial Outlook; Announces Departure of Chief Financial Officer Michael Dastugue and Refinancing Plans" . www . 12 January 2023. ^ "2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. February 14, 2025. ^ " Contact us ". Hanesbrands. Retrieved on October 26, 2010. "Hanesbrands Inc. 1000 East Hanes Mill Road Winston Salem, NC 27105 United States." ^ "Hanesbrands Inc. :: Our Company" . www . Archived from the original on November 28, 2006.', '["clm_wiki_hanesbrands_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
