VALUES
  ('cs_levi-strauss_leadership', 'org_levi-strauss', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Business career Levi''s sister Fanny and her husband David Stern moved to St. Louis , Missouri, while Levi went to live in Louisville, Kentucky , and sold his brothers'' supplies there. [1] Levi became an American citizen in January 1853. [2] The family decided to open a West Coast branch of their dry goods business in San Francisco , which was the commercial hub of the California gold rush . [3] Levi was chosen to represent them, and he took steamships for San Francisco via Panama, [3] where he arrived in early March 1854 and joined his sister''s family. [4] Strauss opened his wholesale business as Levi Strauss &amp; Co. and imported fine dry goods from his brothers in New York, including clothing, bedding, combs, purses, and handkerchiefs. [3] He made tents and later jeans while he lived with Fanny''s growing family. [5] Tailor Jacob W. Davis of Reno, Nevada , was one of his customers; in 1871, having invented a way to strengthen work pants using rivets, he went into business with Strauss to mass-produce them. [6] The next year, Davis asked Strauss to help him apply for a patent, and the patent (one-half assigned to Levi Strauss &amp; Co.) was issued in 1873. [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Evans, Harold (2004). They made America . Little Brown. ISBN 978-0-316-27766-2 . Retrieved November 12, 2012 . ^ Feldberg, Michael (2002). Blessings of freedom: chapters in American Jewish history . KTAV Publishing. p. 172. ISBN 978-0-88125-755-7 . Retrieved November 12, 2012 . ^ a b c "150th anniversary: How Levi''s could have been called Jacob''s" . The Mercury News . May 22, 2023 . Retrieved February 14, 2024 . &#91; permanent dead link &#93; ^ Leiman, Sondra (1994). America: the Jewish experience . UAHC Press. p. 59. ISBN 978-0-8074-0500-0 . Retrieved November 12, 2012 . ^ Downe, Lynn (2007). Levi Strauss &amp; Co . Arcadia Publishers. p. 9. ISBN 978-0-7385-5553-9 . Retrieved November 12, 2012 . ^ Loverin, Jan (2006), "A Nevada Stylist: Your Denim Jeans Are a Nevada Invention" (PDF) , N', '["clm_wiki_levi-strauss_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
