   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_etsy_history', 'org_etsy', 'overview', 'History',
   'E-commerce website focused on handmade or vintage items html body This article contains promotional content . Please help improve it by removing promotional language and inappropriate external links , and by adding encyclopedic text written from a neutral point of view . See our advice if the article is about you and read our scam warning in case someone asks for money to edit this article. ( September 2025 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Etsy, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : ETSY S&amp;P 600 component Nasdaq : ETSY (2015–2025) Industry E-commerce Founded June 18, 2005 &#59;&#32;21 years ago ( 2005-06-18 ) Founders Robert Kalin Chris Maguire Haim Schoppik Jared Tarbell Headquarters Brooklyn , New York City , United States Key people Josh Silverman ( CEO ) Fred Wilson ( chairman ) Revenue US$ 2.81 billion (2024) Operating income US$380 million (2024) Net income US$303 million (2024) Total assets US$2.42 billion (2024) Total equity US$–759 million (2024) Number of employees 2,400 (2024) Subsidiaries Depop Reverb Website etsy Footnotes [1] Etsy, Inc. is an American e-commerce company focused on handmade or vintage items and craft supplies. Its marketplace includes categories such as jewelry, apparel, home decor, furniture, toys, and art. Items described as vintage must be at least 20 years old. [2] The platform provides sellers with individual storefronts where they list their goods for a fee of US$0.20 per item. [3] Since 2013, the company has allowed the sale of mass-manufactured items. [4] As of December 31,&#32;2024 &#91;update&#93; , Etsy''s marketplace contained more than 100 million active listings and connected 8 million sellers with 96 million buyers. [1] At the end of 2024, Etsy had 2,400 employees. [1] In 2024, Etsy had gross merchandise sales of US$12.6 billion, a revenue of $2.81 billion, and a net gain of $303 million. [1] The platform generates revenue from three streams. Marketplace revenue includes a 6.5% transaction fee on the final sale value [5] and a listing fee of $0.20 per item. Seller Services include fees for services such as "Promoted Listings," payment processing, and the purchase of shipping labels through the platform. Other revenue includes fees received from third-party payment processors . [6] ^ a b c d body:not( ):not( ) "Etsy, Inc. 2043 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . SEC . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 19, 2025. ^ Etsy. "Vintage Items on Etsy" . Etsy . Retrieved July 10, 2020 . ^ Walker, Ro', '["clm_wiki_etsy_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
