VALUES
  ('cs_etsy_operations', 'org_etsy', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '2016–present In November 2016, Etsy disclosed that it paid US$32.5 million to purchase Blackbird Technologies, a startup that developed AI software used for shopping context/search applications. [1] [2] After experiencing a first-quarter loss in May 2017, Etsy replaced its chief executive and cut 8% of its workforce. In May 2017, Board member Josh Silverman was appointed CEO over Chad Dickerson, [3] citing pressure from shareholders and poor profits. [4] In July 2019, Etsy acquired the music based marketplace Reverb for $275 million. [5] During the COVID-19 pandemic in 2020 , shares in Etsy more than quadrupled. Equity analyst at D.A. Davidson Tom Forte stated the pandemic gave customers incentive to return to the website multiple times, rather than the usual occasional purchase of a unique product. [6] Non-medical face masks accounted for around 11% of gross-merchandise sales in the third quarter, selling roughly 24 million. [7] [8] On June 2, 2021, Etsy announced that it had agreed to acquire shopping app Depop , the fashion resell marketplace for $1.63 billion. [9] Depop was later sold to eBay for $1.2 billion in 2026. [10] In most locations where Etsy Payments is not available, new shops are unable to on board to Etsy. As of April 26, 2021, most sellers opening new shops on Etsy are required to on board with Etsy Payments, which brings limitations on creating new shops in some countries. [11] In June 2022, Etsy announced the August launch of a purchase protection program for buyers and sellers. The company stated that an item that arrives damaged, does not arrive or does not match a description, will be refunded in full for the buyer. Etsy also reported it would invest $25 million to cover the refunds for cases where the seller is not at fault for item damage or loss. [12] In December 2023, Etsy laid off approximately 225 employees, or 11% of its workforce. [13] In January 2024, Etsy introduced "Gift Mode", powered by OpenAI GPT-4 , which allows users to generat', '["clm_wiki_etsy_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
