   'Cycle schemes Bilbaobizi is a cycle sharing system owned by Lyft. Lyft acquired Motivate , a bicycle-sharing system and the operator of Capital Bikeshare and Citi Bike , in November 2018. [1] [2] The company also announced plans to add 28,000 Citi Bikes and expand its service. [3] In April 2022, Lyft announced an agreement to acquire PBSC Urban Solutions , a Canadian bike-share equipment and technology supplier. [4] In 2026 Lyft acquired Serveo bikeshares in Spain. [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Ghose, Carrie (December 3, 2018). "Lyft completes acquisition of Portland''s bike-share program operator" . American City Business Journals . Archived from the original on January 17, 2020 . Retrieved April 13, 2019 . ^ Stampler, Laura (November 29, 2018). "Lyft Inks Deal With N.Y.C. and Becomes Largest Bike-Share Service in U.S." Fortune . Archived from the original on April 11, 2019 . Retrieved April 13, 2019 . ^ Berger, Paul (November 29, 2018). "Lyft to Add 28,000 Citi Bikes and Expand Service" . The Wall Street Journal . Archived from the original on November 30, 2018 . Retrieved November 30, 2018 . ^ Bellan, Rebecca (April 20, 2022). "Lyft doubles micromobility footprint with PBSC acquisition" . TechCrunch . ^ Micromobility https://micromobility.io/news/lyft-to-acquire-serveos-bikeshare-business-in-spain', '["clm_wiki_lyft_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
