   'American social media platform Pinterest, Inc. Logo used since 2017 Screenshot The default page shown to logged-out users (the background montage images are variable) Type of business Public Type of site Social media service Traded as NYSE : PINS (Class A) S&amp;P 400 component Founded December 2009 &#59;&#32;16 years ago ( 2009-12 ) Headquarters San Francisco , California, U.S. Founders Ben Silbermann Paul Sciarra Evan Sharp Key people Bill Ready ( CEO ) Ben Silbermann ( Executive chairman ) Industry Internet Revenue US$ 3.65 billion (2024) Operating income US$180 million (2024) Net income US$1.86 billion (2024) Total assets US$5.34 billion (2024) Total equity US$4.75 billion (2024) Employees 4,666 (2024) URL pinterest Users 553 million MAU (2024) [1] [2] &#91; ‡ 1 &#93; [3] Pinterest is an American social media service for publishing and discovery of information [4] in the form of digital pinboards . [5] This includes recipes, home, style, motivation, and inspiration on the Internet using image sharing . [6] Pinterest, Inc. was founded by Ben Silbermann , Paul Sciarra , and Evan Sharp , [7] and is headquartered in San Francisco . &#91; ‡ 2 &#93; ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Pinterest Office Tour \u2013 San Francisco Tech Headquarters" . Refinery29 . Archived from the original on August 10, 2015 . Retrieved August 13, 2015 . ^ Coombs, Casey; Stewart, Ashley (August 9, 2016). "Pinterest chooses Seattle for its first engineering office outside the Bay Area" . Puget Sound Business Journal . Archived from the original on February 18, 2017 . Retrieved February 18, 2017 . Pinterest employs more than 800 employees worldwide, including 350 engineers. ^ "Pinterest, Inc. 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 6, 2025 . Retrieved February 6, 2025 . ^ Gershgorn, Dave (March 23, 2019). "Pinterest is distancing itself from social networks as it goes public" . Quartz . Archived from the original on April 4, 2020 . Retrieved May 7, 2020 . ^ Social, C. M. S. "How Pinterest Is Different from Other Social Media Platforms – CMS Social Media Company Miami FL" . Archived from the original on August 6, 2020 . Retrieved May 7, 2020 . ^ "New Pinterest features encourage brands and creators to upload more videos" . TechCrunch . July 10, 2019. Archived from the original on January 22, 2023 . Retrieved August 3, 2019 . ^ Vanian, Jonathan (February 6, 2023). "Pinterest shares slip on fourth-quarter revenue miss and weak forecast" . CNBC. Archive', '["clm_wiki_pinterest_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
