VALUES
  ('cs_pinterest_operations', 'org_pinterest', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Exploring Design as of 2012 The home feed is a collection of Pins from the users, boards, and topics followed, as well as a few promoted pins and pins Pinterest has picked. &#91; ‡ 1 &#93; On the main Pinterest page, a "pin feed" appears, displaying the chronological activity from the Pinterest boards that a user follows. &#91; ‡ 2 &#93; In October 2013, Pinterest began displaying advertisements in the form of "Promoted Pins". [1] Promoted Pins are based on an individual user''s interests, things done on Pinterest, or a result of visiting an advertiser''s site or app. &#91; ‡ 3 &#93; In 2015, Pinterest implemented a feature that allows users to search with images instead of words. [2] In March 2020, Pinterest introduced the "Today" tab on the home feed which shows trending pins. [3] In October 2022, Pinterest announced that its video-focused "Idea Pins" feature has included the ability to add popular tracks from top artists from licensing deals with Warner Music Group , Warner Chappell Music , Merlin, and BMG. [4] Visual search In 2017, Pinterest introduced a " visual search " function that allows users to search for elements in images (existing pins, existing parts of a photo, or new photos) and guide users to suggested similar content within Pinterest''s database. [5] The tools powered by artificial intelligence are called Pinterest Lens, Shop the Look, and Instant Ideas. [6] [7] [8] [9] Cite error: There are &lt;ref group&#61;‡&gt; tags on this page, but the references will not show without a &#123;&#123;reflist&#124;group&#61;‡&#125;&#125; template (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) Perez, Sarah (October 9, 2013). "Pinterest''s Promoted Pins Are Now In The Wild, Here''s How They Look" . TechCrunch . Archived from the original on March 3, 2016 . Retrieved April 27, 2017 . ^ Condliffe, Jamie. "Pinterest Now Has Visual Search and It''s Kinda Smart" . Gizmodo . Archived from the original on March 2, 2017 . Retrieved March 2, 2017 . ^ "Pinterest''s new Today tabs of', '["clm_wiki_pinterest_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
