VALUES
  ('cs_palantir_leadership', 'org_palantir', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '2003–2008: Founding and early years Palantir founder and chairman Peter Thiel in 2009 Palantir was founded in 2003. [1] [2] [3] Thiel named the startup after the " seeing stone " in J. R. R. Tolkien ''s legendarium . Likewise, Palantir''s office locations have names from Tolkien: The Shire (Palo Alto, California), Rivendell (McLean, Virginia), and Grey Havens (London, U.K.). [4] [5] In 2013, Thiel said Palantir was a "mission-oriented company" that could apply software similar to PayPal ''s fraud recognition systems to "reduce terrorism while preserving civil liberties". [6] In 2004, Thiel bankrolled the creation of a prototype by PayPal engineer Nathan Gettings and Stanford University students Joe Lonsdale and Stephen Cohen . The same year, he hired Alex Karp , a former colleague of his from Stanford Law School , as chief executive officer . [7] There are at least four versions of the story of Palantir''s founding, [8] [9] [10] [11] [12] but they all say that Thiel and Karp produced software that others found applications for. According to The Wall Street Journal , when Palantir launched in 2004, there were three investors other than Thiel and Karp but little interest from venture capital firms, so Thiel and his venture fund largely bankrolled the initial $30 million cost. CIA -affiliated venture capital firm In-Q-Tel [13] invested about $2 million. [14] According to Techcrunch , Oakhouse Partners led Palantir''s $7.5 million Series A (June 2006) and REV led its $10.5 million Series B (November 2006). [15] In its early years, Palantir maintained founder control by declining to offer board seats to investors, including In-Q-Tel. This practice continued through subsequent funding rounds. [16] [17] The New Republic called Karp''s formation of Palantir an embrace of techno-militarism to advance American global supremacy through hard power and targeted violence. [18] [19] [20] The Wall Street Journal said Palantir had a "pro-America ethos" from its inception, highlighting a 2', '["clm_wiki_palantir_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
