VALUES
  ('cs_servicenow_leadership', 'org_servicenow', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisitions July 2013: Mirror42, an Amsterdam -based software developer [1] July 2014: Neebula Systems, an Israeli cloud computing tools company [2] February 2015: Intréis [3] June 2016: Brightpoint Security [4] January 2017: Machine learning startup DxContinuum [5] October 2017: San Diego human-centered design firm Telepathy; the acquisition doubled the size of ServiceNow''s internal design agency, the Design Experience Organization [6] October 2017: SkyGiraffe, an enterprise mobility company backed by Microsoft Ventures. SkyGiraffe formed the basis for ServiceNow''s Mobile Platform, released in March 2019. [7] April 2018: VendorHawk, a software-as-a-service management company [8] May 2018: AI startup Parlo [9] October 2018: Data analytics company, FriendlyData [10] May 2019: Appsee Ltd., an in-app mobile analytics startup [11] November 2019: Fairchild Resiliency Systems [12] January 2020: Loom Systems, Passage AI, and Attivio [13] [14] June 2020: Sweagle [15] November 2020: Element AI [16] March 2021: Intellibot [17] May 2021: Lightstep [18] August 2021: Swarm64 and Mapwize [19] [20] October 2021: Gekkobrain [21] June 2022: Hitch [22] October 2022: Era Software [23] July 2023: AI-powered platform G2K [24] December 2023: UltimateSuite [25] [26] March 2024: 4Industry [27] July 2024: Raytion GmbH [28] November 2024: Mission Secure [29] January 2025: Cuein AI [30] February 2025: Quality 360 ° [31] March 2025: Moveworks [32] April 2025: Logik [33] May 2025: Data.World [34] December 2025: Veza [35] [36] December 2025: Armis [37] February 2026: Pyramid Analytics [38] March 2025: Traceloop [39] April 2026: Armis [40] July 2026: Ai.Work [41] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Bigelow, Bruce (July 10, 2013). "ServiceNow Acquires Dutch Provider of Performance Analytics Software" . Xconomy . Archived from the original on August 22, 2019 . Retrieved August 22, 2019 . ^ Goldenberg, Roy (July 9, 2014). "ServiceNow acquires Neebula Systems for $100m" . Globes . Retrieved March 4, 2021 . ^ Cathe', '["clm_wiki_servicenow_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
