VALUES
  ('cs_atlassian_leadership', 'org_atlassian', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '2019 data leak Main article: DataSpii In July 2019, cybersecurity researcher Sam Jadali exposed a catastrophic data leak known as DataSpii involving clickstream data provider DDMR and marketing intelligence company Nacho Analytics (NA). [1] [2] Branding itself as the "God mode for the internet", NA granted its free and paid members the ability to access real-time Jira and Confluence data from Atlassian''s cloud and on-premises products, impacting thousands of Atlassian customers including Reddit , FireEye, NBC Digital, BuzzFeed , AlienVault, Cardinal Health , T-Mobile, and Under Armour . [3] [4] Ars Technica''s coverage of Jadali''s findings highlighted DataSpii''s ability to disseminate sensitive Atlassian Jira data, including Blue Origin staff''s competitor discussions and technical issues with sensors, equipment and manifolds. DataSpii circumvented the most effective security measures, enabling the unauthorised dissemination of Jira data from the internal corporate networks of leading cybersecurity firms. [3] This resulted in the real-time leakage of Jira tickets containing the cybersecurity issues of entities such as the Pentagon, Bank of America , AT&amp;T and others. [5] Jadali''s investigation revealed that DDMR facilitated rapid dissemination of the data to additional third parties, often within minutes of acquisition, endangering the privacy of the sensitive data collected. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Goodin, Dan (18 July 2019). "My browser, the spy: How extensions slurped up browsing histories from 4M users" . Ars Technica . Retrieved 5 March 2024 . ^ Fowler, Geoffrey A. (2019-07-19). " Perspective | I found your data. It''s for sale ". The Washington Post . ISSN 0190-8286. Retrieved 2024-03-04. ^ a b Jadali, Sam (18 July 2019). "DataSpii - A global catastrophic data leak via browser extensions" . Security with Sam . Retrieved 5 March 2024 . ^ "DataSpii Impacted Companies" . Security with Sam . Retrieved 5 March 2024 . ^ Sam Jadali [@sam_jadali] (December 5, 2019). ', '["clm_wiki_atlassian_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
