  ('cs_intuit_leadership', 'org_intuit', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Legal issues Intuit formerly offered a free online service called TurboTax Free File as well as a similarly named service called TurboTax Free Edition which is not free for most users. [1] [2] [3] [4] TurboTax Free File was developed as part of an agreement whereby members of the Free File Alliance would offer tax preparation for individuals below an income threshold for free in exchange for the IRS not providing taxpayers with free pre-filled forms. [1] [2] In 2019, investigations by ProPublica found that Intuit deliberately steered taxpayers from the free TurboTax Free File to the paid TurboTax Free Edition through deceptive practices, including search engine delisting and misleading discounts targeted at members of the military. [3] [4] Subsequent investigations by the Senate Committee on Homeland Security and Governmental Affairs and the New York State Department of Financial Services reached similar conclusions, the latter concluding that Intuit engaged in "unfair and abusive practices". [5] [6] [7] [8] As of 2022, Intuit is the subject of multiple lawsuits and is under investigation by the FTC and several state attorneys general . [9] [10] On May 4, 2022, Intuit agreed to pay a $141 million settlement over misleading advertisements. [11] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Justin Elliott, Lucas Waldron (April 22, 2019). "Here''s How TurboTax Just Tricked You Into Paying to File Your Taxes" . ProPublica . Retrieved April 22, 2019 . ^ a b Cite error: The named reference Justin Elliott was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b Cite error: The named reference propublica was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b Cite error: The named reference MD was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ New York State Department of Financial Services (2020). Report on Investigation of Free Tax Preparation and Filing Services (PDF) (Report). ^ Elliott, Justin (July 15, 2020). "New York Regulator Launches Investigation Into TurboTax Maker Intuit and H', '["clm_wiki_intuit_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
