VALUES
  ('cs_palo-alto-networks_operations', 'org_palo-alto-networks', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Threat research Unit 42 is the Palo Alto Networks threat intelligence and security consulting team. They are a group of cybersecurity researchers and industry experts who use data collected by the company''s security platform to discover new cyber threats, such as new forms of malware and malicious actors operating across the world. [1] The group runs a popular blog where they post technical reports analyzing active threats and adversaries. [2] Multiple Unit 42 researchers have been named in the MSRC Top 100, Microsoft''s annual ranking of top 100 security researchers. [3] In April 2020, the business unit consisting of Crypsis Group which provided digital forensics, incident response, risk assessment, and other consulting services merged with the Unit 42 threat intelligence team. [4] According to the FBI , Palo Alto Networks Unit 42 has helped solve multiple cybercrime cases, such as the Mirai Botnet and Clickfraud Botnet cases, [5] the LuminosityLink RAT case, [6] [7] and assisted with "Operation Wire-Wire". [8] In 2018, Unit 42 discovered Gorgon, a hacking group believed to be operating out of Pakistan and targeting government organizations in the United Kingdom, Spain, Russia, and the United States. The group was detected sending spear-phishing emails attached to infected Microsoft Word documents using an exploit commonly used by cybercriminals and cyber-espionage campaigns. [9] In September 2018, Unit 42 discovered Xbash, a ransomware that also performs cryptomining , believed to be tied to the Chinese threat actor "Iron". Xbash is able to propagate like a worm and deletes databases stored on victim hosts. [10] In October, Unit 42 warned of a new crypto mining malware, XMRig, that comes bundled with infected Adobe Flash updates. The malware uses the victim''s computer''s resources to mine Monero cryptocurrency. [11] In November 2018, Palo Alto Networks announced the discovery of "Cannon", a trojan being used to target United States and European government entities. ', '["clm_wiki_palo-alto-networks_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
