  ('cs_fortinet_operations', 'org_fortinet', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisitions In 2008, the company acquired the intellectual property of IPLocks, a database security and auditing company. [1] In August 2009, Fortinet acquired the intellectual property and other assets of Woven Systems, an Ethernet switching company. [2] In December 2012, Fortinet acquired app-hosting service XDN (formerly known as 3Crowd) [3] In 2013 Fortinet acquired Coyote Point , a developer of hardware load balancers . [4] In 2015 Fortinet acquired Wi-Fi hardware company Meru Networks . [5] In June 2016, Fortinet acquired IT security, monitoring, and analytics software vendor AccelOps. [6] In June 2018, Fortinet acquired Bradford Networks, a maker of access control and IoT security solutions. [7] In October 2018, Fortinet acquired ZoneFox, a threat analytics company. [8] In late 2019, Fortinet acquired enSilo and CyberSponse. [9] [10] In 2020, Fortinet acquired SASE cloud provider OPAQ Networks, [11] and automated incident management company Panopta. [12] In March 2021, Fortinet acquired cloud and network security firm ShieldX. [13] In July 2021, Fortinet acquired application security company Sken.Ai to offer continuous application security testing. [14] In June 2024, Fortinet acquired Lacework, a data-driven cloud security company for an undisclosed amount. [15] [16] In August 2024, Fortinet acquired Next DLP, a cloud based DLP provider company for an undisclosed amount. [17] In 2025, Fortinet acquired Everest, an Indian company focus in WIFI access points for high density environments. [18] ^ body:not( ):not( ) McMillan, Robert (June 17, 2008). "Fortinet buys assets of security vendor IPLocks" . IDG News Service . Retrieved March 14, 2015 . ^ Kotadia, Munir (August 20, 2009). "Woven Systems technology lives on with Fortinet" . IT News . Retrieved March 13, 2015 . ^ Davis, Jim (December 17, 2012). "Did Fortinet acquire XDN in a bid to add more cache to its portfolio?" . 451 Group . Retrieved March 14, 2015 . ^ King, Rachel (March 22, 2013). "Fortinet buying ', '["clm_wiki_fortinet_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
