  ('cs_zscaler_leadership', 'org_zscaler', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Zero Trust Exchange Zscaler''s Zero Trust Exchange platform features cyberthreat protection, data protection, zero trust connectivity, and business analytics. [1] It was first announced at Zenith Live in June 2023. [2] In January 2024, the company announced Zscaler Zero Trust SASE ( secure access service edge ), [3] enabling it to offer its first single-vendor SASE. [4] It is built on the company''s AI-powered SSE platform to securely connect users, locations, and cloud services through its Zero Trust Exchange. [5] It also offers a cloud-based cybersecurity platform, Zscaler Internet Access. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "The 4 pillars of the Zscaler Zero Trust Exchange" . cio . Retrieved August 15, 2024 . ^ "Cloud security leader Zscaler bets on generative AI as future of zero trust" . venturebeat . Retrieved August 15, 2024 . ^ "What Is Secure Access Service Edge (SASE)?" . www . Retrieved 2024-12-16 . ^ "Zscaler CEO: Palo Alto Networks'' New Bundling Strategy Will ''Unravel Over Time'' " . crn . Retrieved August 15, 2024 . ^ "Zscaler''s single-vendor zero-trust SASE brings a new approach to an old problem" . siliconangle . Retrieved August 15, 2024 . ^ "Zscaler Data Protection Frequently Replacing Symantec" . crn . Retrieved August 15, 2024 .', '["clm_wiki_zscaler_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
