VALUES
  ('cs_cloudflare_operations', 'org_cloudflare', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History Cloudflare was founded on July 26, 2009, by Matthew Prince , Lee Holloway, [1] and Michelle Zatlyn. [2] [3] [4] Prince and Holloway had previously collaborated on Project Honey Pot , a product of Unspam Technologies that partly inspired the basis of Cloudflare. [5] In 2009, the company was venture-capital funded. [6] On August 15, 2019, Cloudflare submitted its S-1 filing for an initial public offering on the New York Stock Exchange under the stock ticker NET. [7] It opened for public trading on September 13, 2019, at $15 per share. [8] According to the company, the name ''Cloudflare'' was chosen, over the initial ''WebWall'', because it best described what they were trying to do: build a "firewall in the cloud." [9] In 2020, Cloudflare co-founder and COO Michelle Zatlyn was named president. [10] Cloudflare has acquired web-services and security companies, including StopTheHacker (February 2014), [11] CryptoSeal (June 2014), [12] Eager Platform Co. (December 2016), [13] Neumob (November 2017), [14] S2 Systems (January 2020), [15] Linc (December 2020), [16] Zaraz (December 2021), [17] Vectrix (February 2022), [18] Area 1 Security (February 2022), [19] Nefeli Networks (March 2024), BastionZero (May 2024), [20] Kivera (October 2024), [21] Replicate (November 2025), [22] and Human Native (January 2026). [23] Lava Lamps in the Cloudflare office Since at least 2017, Cloudflare has used a wall of lava lamps at its San Francisco headquarters as a source of randomness for encryption keys, alongside double pendulums at its London offices and a Geiger counter at its Singapore offices. [24] The lava lamp installation implements the Lavarand method, where a camera transforms the unpredictable shapes of the "lava" blobs into a digital image. [25] [24] In Q4 2022, &#91;update&#93; Cloudflare provided paid services to 162,086 customers. [26] [27] In October 2024, Cloudflare won a lawsuit against patent troll Sable Networks. Sable paid Cloudflare $225,000, granted it a royalty-f', '["clm_wiki_cloudflare_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
