VALUES
  ('cs_robinhood-markets_leadership', 'org_robinhood-markets', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '2013-2019: Foundation, options and cryptocurrency trading Robinhood co-founder Baiju Bhatt (left) and moderator Josh Constine (right) speak onstage during Day 2 of TechCrunch Disrupt SF 2018 at the Moscone Center on September 6, 2018, in San Francisco, California . Robinhood was founded in April 2013 by Vladimir Tenev and Baiju Bhatt , two former Stanford classmates who had previously built high-frequency trading platforms for financial institutions in New York City. [1] The company is named after Robin Hood , based on its self-stated mission to "democratize finance for all". [2] [1] Tenev and Bhatt served as co-CEOs from 2013 to 2020, when Tenev became the sole CEO and Bhatt became chief creative officer . [3] [4] In December 2013, Robinhood closed its seed funding round, securing $3 million in an investment led by Index Ventures , with participation from Andreessen Horowitz , Rothenberg Ventures , Tim Draper , and Howard Lindzon . [5] The founders presented the mobile app at LA Hacks in April 2014 and launched a beta release in December on the Apple App Store . [6] That September, Robinhood raised $13 million in a Series A round, with returning investors Index Ventures and Howard Lindzon, as well as new investors Ribbit Capital , Aaron Levie , Dave Morin , Jared Leto , Snoop Dogg , and Nas . [7] [8] The mobile app was launched officially in March 2015. [2] [9] [10] In May 2015, the company raised $50 million in a Series B round led by New Enterprise Associates . [11] [12] [13] [14] Robinhood raised $110 million in a Series C round at a $1.3 billion valuation in April 2017, bringing its total funding raised to $176 million. Investors included Yuri Milner of DST Global , Greenoaks Capital, and Thrive Capital . [15] [16] [17] In December 2017, the company launched commission-free options trading. [18] In February 2018, the company announced that it would be moving its headquarters from Palo Alto to the former headquarters of Sunset magazine in Menlo Park . [19] That ', '["clm_wiki_robinhood-markets_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
