VALUES
  ('cs_rivian_history', 'org_rivian', 'overview', 'History',
   'American electric vehicle company This article is about the American electric vehicle manufacturer. For the joint venture with Volkswagen Group, see Rivian and Volkswagen Group Technologies . Rivian Automotive, Inc. Formerly Mainstream Motors Avera Automotive Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : RIVN (Class A) Russell 1000 component ISIN US76954A1034 Industry Automotive Energy storage Founded June 2009 &#59;&#32;17 years ago ( 2009-06 ) in Rockledge, Florida , U.S. Founder RJ Scaringe Headquarters Irvine, California , U.S. [1] Number of locations 100 service centers (2026) [2] Area served North America Key people RJ Scaringe ( CEO ) Products Electric vehicles Batteries Production output 42,284 vehicles (2025) [3] Services Electric vehicle charging [4] Vehicle insurance [5] Software and services [6] Revenue US$ 5.39 billion (2025) [7] Operating income US$−3.585 billion (2025) [7] Net income US$−3.585 billion (2025) [7] Total assets US$14.86 billion (2025) [8] Total equity US$6.56 billion (2024) Owner Volkswagen Group (15.9%) Amazon (12.28%) Oryx Global (8.6%) Vanguard (5.1%) [9] Number of employees 14,861 (2024) Website rivian Footnotes [10] [11] Rivian Automotive, Inc. , is an American electric vehicle manufacturer and automotive technology company founded in 2009. It produces an electric sport utility vehicle (SUV) and a pickup truck , both on a "skateboard" platform that can support future vehicles and be adopted by other companies. They also produce an electric delivery van , the Rivian EDV . [12] The EDV is sold to Amazon for its deliveries. It started deliveries of its R1T pickup truck in late 2021, R1S sport utility vehicle in 2023, and R2 midsize SUV in 2026. The company also operates the Rivian Adventure Network, an open DC fast charging network in the United States. [13] Rivian is based in Irvine, California , with its manufacturing plant in Normal, Illinois , and other facilities in Palo Alto, California ; Carson, California ; Plymouth, Michigan ; Vancouver, British Columbia ; Wittmann, Arizona ; Woking, England ; and Belgrade, Serbia . [14] [15] Rivian has plans to build another US$5 billion factory in Social Circle, Georgia . [16] The company raised over US$13.5 billion in financing following its initial public offering in November 2021. [17] [18] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Ludlow, Edward (September 14, 2021). "Rivian Gets U.S. Regulatory Go-Ahead to Deliver EVs to Customers" . Bloomberg News . Archived from the original on October 22, 2021 . Retrieved Oct', '["clm_wiki_rivian_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
