  ('cs_rivian_operations', 'org_rivian', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Beginnings (2009) The company was founded in Rockledge, Florida [1] in 2009 as Mainstream Motors by RJ Scaringe . [2] After being renamed as Avera Automotive [3] or Avera Motors, and finally Rivian Automotive in 2011 (a word play on the Indian River in Florida, where Scaringe grew up), [4] the company began focusing on autonomous and electric vehicles . [5] RJ Scaringe with the R1 sports car prototype Rivian''s first car model was intended to be a sports car. This vehicle, dubbed the R1, was prototyped as a mid-engine hybrid coupe for the U.S. market, designed by Peter Stevens . [6] However, it was shelved in late 2011 as Rivian looked to restart its business in an effort to have a larger impact on the automotive industry . [7] Rivian received a large investment and grew significantly in 2015, opening research facilities in Michigan and the San Francisco Bay Area . [8] Shortly thereafter, Rivian began working exclusively on electric autonomous vehicles, in an attempt to build a network of related products. [9] It also began gearing its prototypes toward the "ride-sharing and driverless car markets." [10] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Price, Wayne T. (November 3, 2011). "Avera Motors of Rockledge becomes Rivian Automotive" . Florida Today . US. Archived from the original on March 14, 2011. ^ "Rivian: The history and future of an up-and-coming EV automaker" . Electrek . November 9, 2021. Archived from the original on December 22, 2021 . Retrieved December 21, 2021 . ^ "Who Owns Rivian?" . MotorTrend . November 10, 2021. Archived from the original on March 29, 2022 . Retrieved March 9, 2022 . ^ Seabrook, John (January 31, 2022). "America''s Favorite Pickup Truck Goes Electric" . The New Yorker . Archived from the original on February 14, 2022 . Retrieved February 18, 2022 . ^ "This startup is building self-driving trucks and SUVs for futuristic off-road adventures" . The Verge . Archived from the original on August 21, 2018 . Retrieved August 21, 2018 . ^ "Rivian R1" . Pete