   'American spaceflight and AI company This article is about the rocket and spacecraft manufacturer. For the British art gallery, see Spacex (art gallery) . "Space Exploration Technologies" redirects here. For the general topics, see Space exploration and Space technology . Space Exploration Technologies Corp. Company headquarters, SpaceX Starbase in Starbase, Texas Trade name SpaceX Type Public company Traded as Nasdaq : SPCX (Class A) Nasdaq-100 component Industry Space Telecommunications Artificial intelligence Founded March 14, 2002 &#32;(24 years ago) ( 2002-03-14 ) in El Segundo, California , U.S. [1] Founder Elon Musk Headquarters SpaceX Starbase , Starbase, Texas , U.S. Key people Elon Musk (CEO, chairman &amp; CTO ) [2] Gwynne Shotwell (president &amp; COO) [3] Products Launch vehicles Dragon capsules Starshield Revenue US$ 18.7 billion (2025) Operating income US$−2.6 billion (2025) Net income US$−4.9 billion (2025) Total assets US$92.1 billion (2025) Total equity US$2.6 billion (2025) Owners Elon Musk (42% equity; 82% voting control ) [4] Alphabet Inc. (4.19% equity) [5] Number of employees 22,000 (2026) [6] Subsidiaries SpaceXAI Starlink Website spacex Footnotes Financials as of December 31,&#32;2025 &#91;update&#93; . References: [2] body body This article is part of a series about Elon Musk Personal Awards and honors Business career Views Family Musk Foundation International relations Legal affairs Public image Texas Institute of Technology and Science Wealth Companies Zip2 PayPal X SpaceX Starlink Starshield xAI X Corp. Twitter under Elon Musk acquisition SEC investigation Tesla, Inc. SolarCity OpenAI Neuralink The Boring Company Terafab Thud Politics Activities America PAC America Party Building America''s Future Dept. of Govt. Efficiency Salute controversy Trade unions Tesla Protests Tesla Takedown vandalism Trump feud In the arts and media Character Limit Elon Musk by Vance Elon Musk''s Crash Course Elon Musk by Isaacson Filmography Ludicrous Make America Wait Again " The Musk Who Fell to Earth " Musk (film) Power Play Return to Space Revenge of the Electric Car The Space Barons html v t e Space Exploration Technologies Corp. , doing business as SpaceX , is an American spaceflight , telecommunications , and artificial intelligence company headquartered at the Starbase development site in Starbase, Texas . [7] The company operates three divisions: " Space ", which conducts more orbital launches annually than any other launch provider, including ', '["clm_wiki_spacex_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
