VALUES
  ('cs_northrop-grumman_operations', 'org_northrop-grumman', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'American aerospace and defense company Northrop Grumman Corporation Type Public Traded as NYSE : NOC S&amp;P 500 component Industry Aerospace , defense Predecessors Northrop Corporation Grumman Corporation Founded 1994 &#59;&#32;32 years ago ( 1994 ) Headquarters West Falls Church, Virginia , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Kathy J. Warden ( President and CEO ) Revenue US$ 41.9 billion [1] &#58;&#8202;48&#8202; (2025) Operating income US$4.51 billion [1] &#58;&#8202;48&#8202; (2025) Net income US$4.18 billion [1] &#58;&#8202;48&#8202; (2025) Total assets US$51.4 billion [1] &#58;&#8202;49&#8202; (2025) Total equity US$16.7 billion [1] &#58;&#8202;49&#8202; (2025) Number of employees ~95,000 [1] &#58;&#8202;5&#8202; (2025) Website www Footnotes [1] Northrop Grumman Corporation , headquartered in West Falls Church, Virginia , is an American aerospace and defense company that designs and manufactures systems for aeronautics, defense, missions, and space. The company is the 5th largest contractor of the U.S. federal government ; it receives over 2% of all federal government spending at contractors. [2] [3] [4] The company is ranked 110th on the Fortune 500 list of America''s largest corporations. [5] In 2024, 87% of the company''s revenues came from the US federal government, while 12% was from international sources. [1] Northrop Grumman and its industry partners have won the Collier Trophy nine times, including for the development and production of the James Webb Space Telescope , launched in 2021. [1] The company was formed in 1994 through the merger of Northrop Corporation and Grumman Aerospace . ^ a b c d e f g h i body:not( ):not( ) Northrop Grumman Corporation 2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K) (Report). U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . January 27, 2026. ^ "Top 100 &#124; Defense News, News about defense programs, business, and technology" . people . ^ SIPRI Top 100 Arms-Producing and Military Services Companies SIPRI. Retrieved December 18, 2019. ^ "Nort', '["clm_wiki_northrop-grumman_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
