VALUES
  ('cs_quanta-services_history', 'org_quanta-services', 'overview', 'History',
   'American infrastructure services corporation This article is about the American infrastructure services corporation. For the Taiwanese hardware company, see Quanta Computer . For the airline, see Qantas . Quanta Services, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : PWR S&amp;P 500 Component Founded 1997 Headquarters Williams Tower Houston , Texas Key people Earl C. Austin Jr. (CEO) Revenue $29.94 billion USD (Feb 2024) [1] [2] $9.466 billion USD (2017) [3] Number of employees 62,000 Website quantaservices Footnotes [4] Quanta Services is a U.S. corporation that provides infrastructure services for the electric power, pipeline, industrial and communications industries. The company has grown organically since its founding, but it has also acquired over 200 companies in the electrical contracting and other construction industries. In the 2020s, it has been involved in the construction of data centers as a consequence of the rise of artificial intelligence and its need for electrical power. Quanta Services employs about 62,000 people. Its operating companies achieved combined revenues of about $29.9 billion (US) in 2025. It is headquartered in Houston , Texas . In 1998, Quanta went public on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker symbol PWR. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Quanta Services, Inc. (PWR)" . Feb 7, 2024. ^ Stock analysis Archived link ^ "Quanta Services 2016 Annual Report" (PDF) . December 31, 2017. Archived from the original (PDF) on September 12, 2018 . Retrieved September 11, 2018 . ^ "Quanta FY2023 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 23, 2023. Archived from the original on April 8, 2023 . Retrieved April 8, 2023 .', '["clm_wiki_quanta-services_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
