VALUES
  ('cs_lennar_leadership', 'org_lennar', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '20th century Lennar dates back to F&amp;R Builders, a company founded in 1954 by Gene Fisher and real estate developer Arnold P. Rosen. In 1956, Leonard M. Miller, who later became the namesake of the Miller School of Medicine at the University of Miami , a 23-year-old entrepreneur that owned 42 lots in Miami-Dade County, Florida , invested $10,000 and partnered with the company. [1] In 1969, Lennar reached an equity base of $1 million, and by 1971, Miller and Rosen changed the name to Lennar Corporation. [1] That year the firm became a public company via an initial public offering , [2] raising $8.7 million. It was listed on the New York Stock Exchange in 1972. [1] In 1973, the company acquired Mastercraft Homes, based in Phoenix, Arizona , for approximately $2 million, as well as the Womack Development Company. Shortly thereafter, the company established operations in the Midwestern United States , purchasing Bert L. Smokler &amp; Company, based in Detroit , Michigan, and Dreyfus Interstate Development Corp., based in Minneapolis–Saint Paul . [3] [4] Lennar acquired H. Miller &amp; Sons in 1984 for $24 million. [5] In January 1989, the company acquired Richmond American Homes of Florida for $18 million. [6] In February 1992, the company acquired Amerifirst''s $1 billion real estate portfolio in a joint venture with Morgan Stanley . [7] A Lennar master-planned luxury residential community in San Jose, California In October 1992, following Hurricane Andrew , the company faced several lawsuits from homeowners alleging careless building quality. [8] [9] [10] In July 1993, the company formed a joint venture with Westinghouse Electric Corporation and Lehman Brothers to acquire a $2 billion face-value loan portfolio from Westinghouse Electric Corporation for $1.1 billion. [11] In 1995, the company acquired Friendswood Development Company from Exxon , [12] and acquired California company Bramalea. [1] In 1996, the company acquired Winncrest Homes. The company also acquired', '["clm_wiki_lennar_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
