VALUES
  ('cs_lennar_operations', 'org_lennar', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '21st century In 2000, the company acquired U.S. Home Corporation for $476 million in cash and stock, [1] [2] [3] which resulted in the company doubling in size. [4] In 2001, the company acquired home building operations from Fortress Investment Group . [5] In 2002, the company acquired Patriot Homes based in Columbia, Maryland , [6] Barry Andrews Homes in Baltimore, Maryland, as well as Don Galloway Homes, The Genesee Company, Cambridge Homes, and Sunstar Communities. [4] It also acquired Concord Homes and Summit Homes, both based in Chicago . [7] The company then acquired 650 acres (2.6 km 2 ) on Mare Island , in a closed Navy base, for redevelopment. [8] In 2003, Lennar acquired Coleman Homes. [4] In 2004, the company acquired Newhall Land and Farming Company for $990 million. [9] [10] [11] The company also acquired the assets of Queens Properties for $33.8 million, [12] in addition to Connel-Barron Homes and Classic American Homes. [4] In 2005, Lennar acquired Barker Coleman Homes, [4] and the company acquired the 3,718-acre Marine Corps Air Station El Toro for redevelopment. [13] [14] In 2006, Lennar spun off its commercial servicing division, LNR Property Corporation, which was acquired by Starwood Capital Group in 2012. [15] In November 2006, Lennar chairman Robert J. Strudler died. [16] [17] In December 2007, during the subprime mortgage crisis , the company sold an 80% interest in 11,000 properties for 40% of their previously stated book value to Morgan Stanley . [18] In 2007, Lennar founded Rialto Capital Management, which was originated to acquire distressed real estate and mortgage debt. [19] In 2008 and 2009, former businessman and convicted felon Barry Minkow engaged in an extortion scheme, spreading false information about the company that resulted in its stock price falling 26% in one day. [20] Minkow was sentenced to 5 years in prison and was ordered to pay $584 million in restitution. [20] [21] San Diego real estate developer Nicolas Marsch III hire', '["clm_wiki_lennar_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
