VALUES
  ('cs_pultegroup_leadership', 'org_pultegroup', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Early history In 1950, at the age of 18 years, William J. Pulte , began building and selling houses. [1] In 1956, he formed the company, Pulte Homes, Inc which was based in Bloomfield Hills, Michigan . [1] [2] In 1972, the company became a public company via an initial public offering . [3] In 1998, the company acquired Divosta for an estimated $150 million, [4] and it also acquired Radnor Homes for an undisclosed amount. [5] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Szczesny, Joseph (February 16, 2010). "Founder of Pulte Homes resigns after 60 years" . The Oakland Press . ^ Cite error: The named reference 10K was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Downer, Blake (June 19, 2023). "PulteGroup Is Building Long-Term Shareholder Value (NYSE:PHM)" . seekingalpha . ^ "Pulte Expands Southeast Operations By Buying Divosta" . The New York Times . Bloomberg News . July 2, 1998. ^ "Radnor Homes sold" . American City Business Journals . May 27, 1998.', '["clm_wiki_pultegroup_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
