VALUES
  ('cs_pultegroup_operations', 'org_pultegroup', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Since 2020 In 2023 and 2024, PulteGroup and Centex Homes built and awarded homes to US veterans in Houston and North Carolina. This was a part of the company’s Operation Coming Home and the U.S. Veterans Corps. [1] [2] In 2025, the company expanded its Del Webb brand to introduce Del Webb Explore in California and Florida. [3] The company has also partnered with Fastbrick Robotics to build homes in Florida using a robotic construction technology. [4] In February 2025, PulteGroup expanded its Build Your Future SkillPointe Scholarship program, with a $100,000 investment to support individuals from diverse backgrounds who are pursuing careers in residential homebuilding and technologies. [5] In May 2025, the organization’s Built to Honor Program completed its 100th home. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Marek, Emily (November 22, 2023). "PulteGroup''s Built to Honor program awards 80th mortgage-free home to Houston Air Force veteran" . Houston Agent Magazine . ^ Rupinta, Amber (March 1, 2024). "Widow of U.S. Navy Petty Officer surprised by gift of new Hero Home in Wendell" . ABC11 Raleigh-Durham . ^ Salandro, Vincent (March 18, 2025). "Inside PulteGroup''s Del Webb Explore Brand" . Builder Magazine . ^ Cite error: The named reference 11K was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Staff (February 5, 2025). "PulteGroup Expands 2025 Build Your Future Scholarship for Future Homebuilding Leaders" . The Construction Data . ^ Strong, Symone (May 6, 2025). "PulteGroup''s Built to Honor Program Celebrates 100th Build" . Builder Magazine .', '["clm_wiki_pultegroup_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
