   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_marriott_operations', 'org_marriott', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Senior leadership From Marriott''s founding in 1927 to 2012, the company''s senior leadership was led by members of the Marriott family. In 2012, Arne Sorenson became the first non-Marriott family member to be appointed chief executive; this practice continued when Anthony Capuano was named his successor in 2021. The current practice is members of the Marriott family are named chairman while other company executives are named as chief executive. Chairmen J. Willard Marriott (1927–1985) Bill Marriott (1985–2022) David Marriott (since May 2022) Chief executives J. Willard Marriott (1927–1972) Bill Marriott (1972–2012) Arne Sorenson (2012–2021) Anthony Capuano (since February 2021)', '["clm_wiki_marriott_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 199. Hyatt Hotels (slug=hyatt-hotels, wiki='Hyatt Hotels')
