VALUES
  ('cs_caesars-entertainment_leadership', 'org_caesars-entertainment', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1973–2000 The company traces its history back to the development of the Eldorado Hotel in Reno, which was opened in May 1973, by a group of investors that included Don Carano and other members of the Carano family. [1] [2] [3] In July 1995, the Eldorado opened the adjacent Silver Legacy Resort Casino in partnership with Circus Circus Enterprises . [4] The Eldorado companies were reorganized in 1996 as Eldorado Resorts LLC in connection with a $100 million bond offering . [5] [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Form 10-K: Annual Report (Report). Eldorado Resorts. March 1, 2019. p. 1 &#8211; via EDGAR. ^ "Eldorado Hotel granted license" . Nevada State Journal . UPI. May 25, 1973 &#8211; via Newspapers . ^ "Planned for downtown location: $6.2 million Reno luxury hotel complex" . Reno Evening Gazette . July 17, 1972 &#8211; via Newspapers . ^ Don Cox (July 28, 1995). "It''s Legacy''s big day" . Reno Gazette-Journal &#8211; via Newspapers . ^ Form S-4: Registration of Securities (Report). Eldorado Resorts LLC. September 12, 1996. p. 4 &#8211; via EDGAR. ^ John Stearns (August 21, 1996). "Eldorado raises $100M" . Reno Gazette-Journal &#8211; via Newspapers .', '["clm_wiki_caesars-entertainment_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_caesars-entertainment_operations', 'org_caesars-entertainment', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '2000–2020 In 2005, the company took over the bankrupt Hollywood Casino Shreveport in Louisiana, buying a 76 percent stake in the property for $154 million. [1] It was then rebranded as the Eldorado Casino Shreveport. [2] In 2013, Eldorado agreed to combine with the publicly traded MTR Gaming Group in a reverse merger . [3] [4] The merger would add three racinos in Ohio, Pennsylvania, and West Virginia to Eldorado''s portfolio. [5] The transaction closed on September 19, 2014, creating Eldorado Resorts Inc. in its present form. [6] Eldorado''s existing owners held 50.2 percent of the combined company, and Gary Carano was appointed as its chairman and CEO. [6] In November 2015, Eldorado bought Circus Circus Reno and the 50% stake in the Silver Legacy that it did not already own from MGM Resorts International for $73 million. [7] [8] In May 2017, Eldorado acquired Isle of Capri Casinos for $1.7 billion in cash, stock, and assumed debt, adding twelve casinos to its holdings. [9] In August 2018, Eldorado bought the Grand Victoria Casino in Illinois for $328 million. [10] [11] Two months later, Eldorado acquired the operating business of Tropicana Entertainment for $640 million, adding seven casinos to its portfolio. Gaming and Leisure Properties simultaneously purchased the real estate of five of the casinos and leased them to Eldorado for a total of $88 million per year. [12] [13] [14] Additionally, Eldorado paid $246 million for the real estate underlying Tropicana''s Lumière Place casino in Missouri. [12] In early 2019, Eldorado sold Presque Isle Downs and the operations of Lady Luck Casino Nemacolin to Churchill Downs, Inc. for a total of $179 million. [15] [16] In March 2019, it was reported that Eldorado was discussing a merger with Caesars Entertainment . [17] In June 2019, Caesars accepted Eldorado''s offer to purchase Caesars for $18 billion in stock and cash. [18] Eldorado operated 26 assets compared to Caesars, which controlled 53. [19] Eldorado would change its n', '["clm_wiki_caesars-entertainment_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 202. MGM Resorts International (slug=mgm-resorts, wiki='MGM Resorts International')
