VALUES
  ('cs_wynn-resorts_leadership', 'org_wynn-resorts', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Economic performance In 2017 CNBC reported that Wynn''s stock was up 44% for the year and that Wynn''s Macau operations were the leading US-based resorts there. [1] Wynn resorts continued to operate during the pandemic while requiring employees who chose not to receive a COVID-19 vaccination to submit weekly test results for the virus; employees were paid during this time,with added commensurate compensation for tipped employees. [2] [3] The company temporarily suspended its dividend in response to liquidity issues during the pandemic; the divided was reinstated in May 2023. [4] [5] Following the lifting of pandemic-related restrictions being lifted in the US and in Macau, the company began increasing revenues and profits. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Steve Wynn doubles down on Macau with new $4B casino" . CNBC . 22 August 2016. Archived from the original on 2017-10-03 . Retrieved 2018-03-19 . ^ Cliffor, Tyler (8 April 2021). "Wynn Resorts CEO says 60% of employees have been vaccinated, despite company not mandating shots" . CNBC. Archived from the original on 12 April 2021 . Retrieved 13 April 2021 . ^ O''Halloran, Suzanne (March 18, 2020). "Coronavirus won''t stop Wynn Resorts CEO from paying workers despite closings" . Fox Business . ^ "Wynn Resorts, Limited Common stock (WYNN) Dividend History" . NASDAQ . Retrieved 28 February 2025 . ^ Wynn Resorts (14 February 2023). Wynn Resorts, INC (Report). SEC. Archived from the original on 2 October 2023 . Retrieved 1 October 2023 . ^ Yu, Elaine (2023-08-19). "Macau Reclaims Crown From Vegas as World''s Top Gambling Hub" . The Wall Street Journal . Retrieved 2026-04-16 .', '["clm_wiki_wynn-resorts_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
