VALUES
  ('cs_activision-blizzard_operations', 'org_activision-blizzard', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'New titles and sales records (2009–2012) In early 2010, the independent studio Bungie entered into a 10-year publishing agreement with Activision Blizzard. [1] [2] By the end of 2010, Activision Blizzard was the largest video games publisher in the world. [3] The 2011 release of Activision Blizzard''s Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 3 grossed $400 million in the US and UK alone in its first 24 hours, making it the biggest entertainment launch of all time. [4] It was also the third consecutive year the Call of Duty series broke the biggest launch record; 2010''s Call of Duty: Black Ops grossed $360 million on day one; and 2009''s Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2 brought in $310 million. [5] Call of Duty: Black Ops III grossed $550 million in worldwide sales during its opening weekend in 2015, making it the biggest entertainment launch of the year. [6] [7] In 2011, Activision Blizzard debuted its Skylanders franchise, [8] which led to the press crediting the company with inventing and popularizing a new toys-to-life category. [8] [9] [10] The first release Skylanders: Spyro''s Adventure was nominated for two Toy Industry Association awards in 2011: "Game of the Year" and "Innovative Toy of the Year". [11] Skylanders: Spyro''s Adventure and its sequels were released for major consoles and PC, and many were released on mobile devices as well. [8] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Klepek, Patrick (April 29, 2010). "Industry Shocker: Developer Bungie Signs Deal With Activision" . G4tv . Archived from the original on January 12, 2013 . Retrieved April 30, 2010 . ^ Kohler, Chris (April 29, 2010). "Bungie, Activision Sign 10-Year Publishing Deal" . Wired . Archived from the original on May 2, 2010 . Retrieved April 30, 2010 . ^ Palmer, Maija; Bradshaw, Tim (June 30, 2010). "Computer games industry hits at tax rethink" . Financial Times . Archived from the original on July 3, 2010 . Retrieved June 30, 2010 . ^ Crecente, Brian (November 11, 2011). "Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 3 Shatters All Sales R', '["clm_wiki_activision-blizzard_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
