VALUES
  ('cs_roblox_overview', 'org_roblox', 'overview', 'Overview',
   'Roblox is an online game platform and game creation system developed by Roblox Corporation that allows users to program and play games created by themselves or other users. It was developed by David Baszucki and Erik Cassel in 2004, and released to the public in 2006. As of February 2025, the platform has reported an average of 85.3 million daily active users. According to the company, its monthly player base includes half of all American children under the age of 16.', '["clm_wiki_roblox_overview"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   10, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_roblox_history', 'org_roblox', 'overview', 'History',
   'Communication and age estimations Roblox allows players to communicate with each other in a variety of ways, such as through in-game chat and direct messaging. [1] Voice chat is usable for players over the age of 13 that have their age verified. [2] Players can join communities, where users can send messages in an internet forum -like environment. [3] Players are able to add other users as friends. An additional tier of this system, known as "Trusted Friends", allows users to send unfiltered chat messages and personal information to each other. If one of the users is over the age of 18 while the other user is between 13 and 17, then both parties must prove that they know each other in real life. This is done through either mutual QR code scanning, or importing their phone contacts. [4] [5] Users can only communicate with each other after they perform an age check , which is done through either ID verification or having a video of themselves analyzed by age estimation software. [6] [7] Communication is further restricted to only allow users in similar age groups to communicate with each other. For example, a user who is twelve years old can only communicate with users aged 9 to 15. [6] Age verification and estimations are handled via Persona , a third-party provider of age verification software. While the age estimation features can result in inaccurate age group assignment, the user can provide their ID to correct their age manually. [8] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Peters, Jay (November 18, 2024). "Roblox will restrict kids under 13 from chatting outside of games" . The Verge . Archived from the original on December 10, 2024 . Retrieved July 18, 2025 . ^ Cite error: The named reference :25 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Bankhurst, Adam (September 6, 2024). "Roblox Developer''s Conference 2024: Everything Announced" . IGN . Retrieved July 18, 2025 . ^ Peters, Jay (July 17, 2025). "Roblox will require a facial scan or government ID to have unfiltered chats" . The Verge . Retrieved July 18, 2025 . ^ Maas, Jennifer (July 17, 2025). "Roblox Rebrands ''Friends'' Feature as Gaming Platform Launches New Age-Estimation Teen Safety Tools" . Variety . Retrieved July 18, 2025 . ^ a b Peters, Jay (January 7, 2026). "Roblox now requires an age check if you want to chat" . The Verge . Retrieved January 8, 2026 . ^ "Roblox, Where Kids Game and Chat, Will Analyze Users'' Faces to Verify Age" . The New York Times . November 21, 2025 . Retrieved November 28, 2025', '["clm_wiki_roblox_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_roblox_leadership', 'org_roblox', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Virtual economy Logo of the virtual currency "Robux" Roblox features a large virtual economy centered around its virtual currency Robux. [1] [2] The currency allows users to buy, sell and create virtual items. [3] Roblox has a service called Roblox Plus, a subscription that gives users discounts on Robux and in-game purchases, and allows members to upload user-created content on the market. [4] [5] Many items on Roblox are user-generated. [6] [1] While only Roblox developers were able to create avatar items early on, [6] the capabilities of user-generated content has expanded greatly over time. [7] Since 2019, select users have gained the ability to publish avatar accessories, animations, [6] bundles and more. [1] [8] [7] Some items on Roblox have a "limited" status, with only a few being available and the price of the item based on supply and demand rather than a fixed price. These items function similarly to non-fungible tokens . The prices of limited items range, with the most valuable ones costing millions of Robux. [9] After the original supply of that item runs out, players can resell them for a higher price. [10] Additionally, users with an active Roblox Plus subscription are able to trade limiteds amongst each other. [5] Limited items made by the community cannot be traded and this feature is restricted to official items. [11] Developers are able to create purchasable content through one-time purchases. [12] Through the Roblox Developer Exchange program, users are able to exchange their earned Robux for real-world money, [13] as long as they have at least 30,000 Robux. [14] In 2020, Roblox reported that roughly 345,000 game developers on the platform earned money through the program. [3] [15] Avatar item creators have also been able to generate profit with the platform, with some individuals designing items as a full-time job. It has been reported that the highest-earning creators have earned over $100,000 a year from item sales. [16] A sizeable amount of sc', '["clm_wiki_roblox_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_roblox_operations', 'org_roblox', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Roblox Studio and game design The Roblox Studio interface as of August 2024 Roblox Studio is the platform''s game engine [1] and game development software. [2] [3] The engine and all games made on Roblox predominantly uses Luau , [4] a dialect of the Lua 5.1 programming language . [5] Since November 2021, the programming language has been open sourced under the MIT License . [4] [6] Some aspects of the engine were created using C++ . [7] To assist in the creation of games, Roblox Studio features multiple pre-made templates that users can modify. [2] As of 2020, Roblox reported that more than 2 million developers used Roblox Studio to create more than 20 million games per year. They also reported that a majority of developers were minors. [8] [9] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Gould, Elie (November 14, 2022). "Roblox is using the metaverse and AI to make creating games accessible" . TechRadar . Archived from the original on August 2, 2024 . Retrieved February 4, 2025 . ^ a b Haskins, Heath (September 16, 2021). "Roblox 101: How to Make Your First Game" . PCMag . Archived from the original on August 4, 2024 . Retrieved August 4, 2024 . ^ Takahashi, Dean (January 18, 2023). "Roblox says 70 user-created games have crossed a billion plays" . VentureBeat . Archived from the original on July 21, 2024 . Retrieved February 4, 2025 . ^ a b Miller, Ron (July 24, 2022). "Roblox beefs up its developer tools as it looks to a future beyond games" . TechCrunch . Retrieved February 4, 2025 . ^ "Why Luau?" . Luau . Roblox Corporation . Archived from the original on January 30, 2025 . Retrieved February 4, 2025 . ^ "Luau Goes Open-Source" . Luau . Roblox Corporation . November 3, 2021. Archived from the original on August 3, 2024 . Retrieved August 3, 2024 . ^ Takahashi, Dean (July 21, 2021). "Roblox CEO podcasts about the rise of the metaverse" . VentureBeat . Archived from the original on May 10, 2025 . Retrieved February 4, 2025 . ^ Cite error: The named reference NYTimes was invoked but neve', '["clm_wiki_roblox_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 217. Liberty Media (slug=liberty-media, wiki='Liberty Media')
