VALUES
  ('cs_iheartmedia_operations', 'org_iheartmedia', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '21st century In 2000, Clear Channel acquired Robert F. X. Sillerman ''s SFX Entertainment, a concert promoter that had focused on consolidation of regional promoters under a national operation. [1] In 2005, Clear Channel spun off its entertainment and live events business as Live Nation . [2] On November 16, 2006, Clear Channel announced plans to go private, being bought out by two private-equity firms, Thomas H. Lee Partners and Bain Capital Partners for $26.7 billion, which included their assumption of $8 billion in Clear Channel debt. [3] This was just under a 10 percent premium above its closing price of $35.36 a share on November 16: the deal valued Clear Channel at $37.60 per share. [4] [3] In a separate transaction also announced on November 16, 2006, Clear Channel said it would seek buyers for all of its television stations and 539 of its smaller radio stations, because the private-equity buyers were not interested in owning television or small-market radio. Over a hundred stations were assigned to Aloha Station Trust, LLC upon the consummation of the merger. The television stations were sold to Newport Television , a broadcaster owned by Providence Equity Partners , on April 23, 2007. [5] [6] [7] Due to the credit market crunch of 2007, Clear Channel encountered difficulty selling some of its radio stations. Clear Channel''s attempt to sell off over 100 stations to GoodRadio.TV, LLC was rejected by the equity firm backing the deal. [8] The deal then shifted to Frequency License LLC, but took longer to resolve itself as the two parties were engaged in lawsuits. On top of that, the sale of Clear Channel''s television portfolio to Newport Television had also turned uncertain, as Providence considered other options, although this transaction was ultimately completed. [9] On December 4, 2007, Clear Channel announced that they had extended the termination date of the buyout from December 12, 2007, to June 12, 2008. [10] On July 24, 2008, Clear Channel held a special', '["clm_wiki_iheartmedia_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
