  ('cs_colgate-palmolive_history', 'org_colgate-palmolive', 'overview', 'History',
   'American multinational consumer products company Colgate-Palmolive Company Logo used since 2025 Headquarters in Midtown Manhattan , New York City Trade name Colgate-Palmolive Formerly Colgate-Palmolive-Peet Company (1928–1953) Type Public Traded as NYSE : CL S&amp;P 100 component S&amp;P 500 component Industry Consumer goods Predecessors Colgate Palmolive (pre-1953 merger ) Founded 1806 &#59;&#32;220 years ago ( 1806 ) Founders William Colgate (Colgate) Burdett J. Johnson (Palmolive) William J. Peet and Robert Peet (Peet Brothers) Headquarters 300 Park Avenue , New York City 10022, U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Noel Wallace (Chairman, President &amp; CEO ) Stanley J. Sutula III ( CFO ) Products Cleaning agents Personal care products Pet food Revenue US$ 20.1 billion (2024) Operating income US$4.27 billion (2024) Net income US$2.89 billion (2024) Total assets US$16.0 billion (2024) Total equity US$212 million (2024) Number of employees c. &#8201;34,000 (2024) Website colgatepalmolive Footnotes [1] The Colgate-Palmolive Company , commonly known as Colgate-Palmolive , is an American multinational consumer products company headquartered on Park Avenue in Midtown Manhattan , New York City. The company specializes in the production, distribution, and provision of household, health care, personal care, and veterinary products. [2] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Colgate-Palmolive Company 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . February 13, 2025 . Retrieved February 14, 2025 . ^ " Legal/Privacy Archived February 6, 2016, at the Wayback Machine ." Colgate-Palmolive. Retrieved June 26, 2010.', '["clm_wiki_colgate-palmolive_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
