  ('cs_ulta-beauty_history', 'org_ulta-beauty', 'overview', 'History',
   'American beauty store chain Ulta Beauty, Inc. Formerly Ulta Salon, Cosmetics &amp; Fragrance Inc. (1990–2017) Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : ULTA S&amp;P 500 component Founded 1990 &#59;&#32;36 years ago ( 1990 ) (as Ulta Salon, Cosmetics &amp; Fragrance, Inc.) Founders Terry Hanson Dick George Headquarters Bolingbrook, Illinois , U.S. Number of locations 1,445 (2025) Key people Kecia Steelman ( CEO ) Revenue US$11.3 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.6 billion (2024) Net income US$1.2 billion (2024) Total assets US$6.0 billion (2024) Total equity US$2.5 billion (2024) Number of employees 58,000 (2025) Subsidiaries Space NK Website ulta Footnotes Financials as of February 1,&#32;2025 &#91;update&#93; . [1] Ulta Beauty, Forestville, Maryland Ulta Beauty Logo Ulta Beauty, Inc. , formerly known as Ulta Salon, Cosmetics &amp; Fragrance Inc. and before 2000 as Ulta3 , is an American chain of cosmetic stores headquartered in Bolingbrook, Illinois . [2] Ulta Beauty carries both high- and low-end cosmetics , fragrances , nail products, bath and body products, beauty tools and haircare products. Each location has a beauty salon available to the public. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "FY 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. March 27, 2025. ^ "About Us" . Ulta .', '["clm_wiki_ulta-beauty_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
