VALUES
  ('cs_autozone_operations', 'org_autozone', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'AutoZone In 1986, Auto Shack was sued by Radio Shack for trademark infringement. [1] While a court initially ruled in favor of Auto Shack, Radio Shack ultimately won on appeal. In 1987 Auto Shack announced plans to change its name to AutoZone. [2] [3] [4] The first AutoZone store was in Enid, Oklahoma . The company introduced an electronic catalog used to look up parts, check warranties, and view inventory. [5] The total number of stores was 459 in 16 states. ^ Cite error: The named reference :3 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference fortune2 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) "AutoZone Founder And Board Director J.R. ''Pitt'' Hyde III To Retire In December" . aftermarketNews . October 22, 2018 . Retrieved June 12, 2025 . ^ Eng, Dinah (July 25, 2013). "How Pitt Hyde put AutoZone into overdrive" . Fortune . Retrieved June 12, 2025 . ^ Cite error: The named reference :02 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_autozone_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
