VALUES
  ('cs_carvana_operations', 'org_carvana', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Controversy Hindenburg Research report (2025) In January 2025, short-selling investment firm Hindenburg Research published a report titled "Carvana: A Father-Son Accounting Grift For The Ages," in which it disclosed a short position against the company. [1] [2] The report alleged that Carvana''s financial turnaround was a "mirage" propped up by accounting manipulation and lax loan underwriting. [3] The report focused on deals between Carvana and DriveTime , a private dealership owned by Ernest Garcia II , father of Carvana CEO Ernest Garcia III . It alleged these transactions were structured favorably to Carvana, allowing it to inflate revenue and profitability. A former director quoted in the report likened the relationship to "Fight Club," stating, "there''s certain things we don''t talk about, and we don''t talk about DriveTime". [4] [1] Hindenburg also alleged that Carvana sold $800 million in auto loans in 2024 to a "suspected undisclosed related party," later identified as likely a trust affiliated with Cerberus Capital Management , Cerberus''s Chairman of Global Investments, Dan Quayle , former vice president and a Carvana director. [5] The report also cited former employees who described virtually non-existent underwriting standards and claimed 60-day delinquency rates were more than four times the industry norm. [2] The report alleged accounting practices that inflated key metrics like gross profit per unit and allowed income to be shifted between quarters. It also noted that Ernest Garcia II sold over $3.6 billion in Carvana stock between 2020 and 2021, and another $1.4 billion following a 2023 stock rally. [6] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Wayland, Michael (January 2, 2025). "Hindenburg Research shorts Carvana, calling company''s turnaround a ''mirage'' " . CNBC . Retrieved December 1, 2025 . ^ a b "Carvana: A Father-Son Accounting Grift For The Ages – Hindenburg Research" . January 2, 2025 . Retrieved December 1, 2025 . ^ Cite error: The named reference :1 was invoke', '["clm_wiki_carvana_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 246. CarMax (slug=carmax, wiki='CarMax')
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
