VALUES
  ('cs_lithia-motors_history', 'org_lithia-motors', 'overview', 'History',
   'U.S. automotive retailer html body This article may have been created or edited in return for undisclosed payments , a violation of Wikipedia''s terms of use . It may require cleanup to comply with Wikipedia''s content policies , particularly neutral point of view . See our advice if the article is about you and read our scam warning in case someone asks for money to edit this article. ( July 2023 ) Lithia Motors, Inc. Lithia''s headquarters in Medford, Oregon Type Public Traded as NYSE : LAD S&amp;P 400 component Industry Automotive dealerships Founded 1946 &#59;&#32;80 years ago ( 1946 ) in Ashland, Oregon , U.S. Founder Walt DeBoer Sidney DeBoer Headquarters Medford, Oregon , U.S. Key people Bryan DeBoer (President &amp; CEO ) Sidney DeBoer ( chairman ) Revenue US$ 36.2 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.5 billion (2024) Net income US$0.8 billion (2024) Total assets US$23.5 billion (2024) Total equity US$6.7 billion (2024) Number of employees 30,000 (2024) Divisions Driveway Subsidiaries DCH Auto Group Carbone Auto Group Baierl Auto Group Downtown LA Auto Group [1] Day Auto Group [2] Prestige Auto Stores [3] Website lithiadriveway Footnotes [4] [5] [6] Lithia Motors, Inc. (doing business as Lithia &amp; Driveway ) is an American nationwide automotive dealership group headquartered in Medford, Oregon . [7] As of 2025, Lithia is the largest automotive retailer in the United States by revenue, ahead of competitors such as AutoNation and Penske Automotive Group . [8] As of December 31, 2024, Lithia operates 459 dealership locations across the United States, Canada, and the United Kingdom. [9] The company employs approximately 30,000 people worldwide. [10] In 2015, Lithia Motors entered the Fortune 500 list at #482, [11] making it one of only three Oregon-based companies to appear on the list. [12] This followed Lithia’s 2014 acquisition of the DCH Auto Group, then one of the ten largest dealer groups in the United States with 27 dealerships. [13] In 2016, Lithia rose to #346 on the Fortune 500 and was recognized among the companies with the largest year-over-year climb. [14] Lithia reached #294 in 2018, [15] and #158 in 2022. [16] As of the 2025 Fortune 500, Lithia ranks #124 overall and #1 in the Automotive Retail category. [17] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Lithia purchases LA auto group" . 8 August 2017. ^ "Day Automotive Group Joins Lithia" . 27 February 2018. ^ "Lithia buys New Jersey stores from Prestige" . March 2018. ^ "Lithia Motors, Inc. Financials" . Nasd', '["clm_wiki_lithia-motors_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
