  ('cs_williams-companies_history', 'org_williams-companies', 'overview', 'History',
   'American energy company For other companies with "Williams" in their name, see Williams (disambiguation) § Organizations and companies . "John H. Williams (American businessman)" redirects here. For the American businessman who worked in baseball, see John Henry Williams (baseball) . The Williams Companies, Inc. Type Public company Traded as NYSE : WMB S&amp;P 500 component Industry Petroleum Founded 1908 &#59;&#32;118 years ago ( 1908 ) Founders David Williams Miller Williams Headquarters BOK Tower Tulsa, Oklahoma , U.S. Area served North America Key people Chad Zamarin (president &amp; CEO ) Products Oil natural gas Revenue US$ 10.5 billion (2024) Operating income US$3.34 billion (2024) Net income US$2.23 billion (2024) Total assets US$54.5 billion (2024) Total equity US$12.4 billion (2024) Number of employees 5,829 (2025) Website williams Footnotes [1] The Williams Companies, Inc. is an American energy company based in Tulsa, Oklahoma . Its core business is natural gas processing and transportation, with additional petroleum and electricity generation assets. A Fortune 500 company, [2] its common stock is a component of the S&amp;P 500 . ^ body:not( ):not( ) "2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S Securities and Exchange Commission. February 25, 2025. ^ "Williams" . Fortune . Archived from the original on April 23, 2019 . Retrieved December 16, 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_williams-companies_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
