VALUES
  ('cs_consolidated-edison_history', 'org_consolidated-edison', 'overview', 'History',
   'American energy company "ConEd" redirects here; not to be confused with Continental Edison or Commonwealth Edison . Consolidated Edison, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : ED DJUA component S&amp;P 500 component Industry Energy Founded March 23, 1823 &#59;&#32;203 years ago ( 1823-03-23 ) &#8211; as New York Gas Light Company 1871 &#8211; Harlem Gas Light Company 1884 &#8211; Consolidated Gas Company Headquarters Consolidated Edison Building , New York City , U.S. Area served New York metropolitan area Key people Tim Cawley (CEO) [1] Services Electricity Gas Steam Revenue US$ 15.26 billion (2024) [2] Operating income US$2.67 billion (2024) [2] Net income US$1.82 billion (2024) [2] Total assets US$70.56 billion (2024) [2] Total equity US$21.96 billion (2024) [2] Number of employees 15,097 (2024) [2] Website coned Con Ed''s East River Generating Station in Manhattan , New York City Consolidated Edison, Inc. , commonly known as Con Edison (stylized as conEdison ) or ConEd , is an energy company based in New York City. It is one of the largest investor-owned energy companies in the United States, with approximately $15.26 billion in annual revenues as of 2024, and over $70 billion in assets. [2] The company provides a wide range of energy-related products and services to its customers through its subsidiaries: Consolidated Edison Company of New York, Inc. ( CECONY ), a regulated utility providing electric and gas service in New York City and Westchester County, New York , and steam service in the borough of Manhattan ; Orange and Rockland Utilities, Inc. , a regulated utility serving customers in a 1,300-square-mile (3,400 km 2 ) area in southeastern New York and northern New Jersey ; and, Con Edison Transmission, Inc. , which invests in electric and natural gas transmission projects. In 2015, electric revenues accounted for 70.35% of consolidated sales (70.55% in 2014); gas revenues 13.61% (14.96% in 2014); steam revenues 5.01% (4.86% in 2014); and non-utility revenues of 11.02% (9.63% in 2014). [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Con Edison Names Timothy Cawley Chief Executive Officer; Con Edison of New York Names Matthew Ketschke President" . Cision Distribution (Press release). PR Newswire. Consolidated Edison. September 17, 2020. ^ a b c d e f g "Consolidated Edison 2023 Form 10-K Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 20, 2025. ^ "Con Edison Reports 2014 Earnings" (Press release). conEdison. February 19, 2015. Archived from the original ', '["clm_wiki_consolidated-edison_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
