VALUES
  ('cs_ecolab_operations', 'org_ecolab', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '1986–2000 In 1986, the company changed its name from Economics Laboratory to Ecolab Inc. and was listed on the New York Stock Exchange . [1] In 1987, the company formed a textile care division. In 1987, Ecolab acquired ChemLawn, a lawncare servicer provider, for $376 million. In 1992, it was sold to ServiceMaster for $103 million after years of losses. [2] In July 1991, Ecolab and Henkel formed a 50-50 European joint venture to expand into European and Russian markets. Ecolab also acquired Henkel''s institutional cleaning and sanitizing businesses in 19 countries in Latin America and the Asia-Pacific . Henkel then owned a 24% stake in Ecolab. [3] In 2001, Ecolab acquired the 50% interest in the joint venture held by Henkel for $445 million. [4] [5] Henkel sold its stake in Ecolab in November 2008, as it needed to raise cash during the 2008 financial crisis . [6] [7] [8] In November 1994, the company acquired Kay Chemical for $94 million. [9] In August 1997, the company acquired 14.9% of Gibson Chemical Industries of Australia for $18.7 million. [10] ^ Cite error: The named reference bcc was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference fundingu was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Ecolab, Henkel of Germany form joint venture" . United Press International . July 11, 1991 . Retrieved 2026-07-30 . ^ "COMPANY NEWS; ECOLAB TO BUY REST OF JOINT VENTURE FOR $445 MILLION" . The New York Times . Bloomberg News . November 24, 2001 . Retrieved 2026-07-30 . ^ "Ecolab speeds up acquisition of joint venture" . American City Business Journals . September 24, 2001 . Retrieved 2026-07-30 . ^ "Henkel Lets Go Of Ecolab" . Forbes . November 14, 2008 . Retrieved 2026-07-30 . ^ Kuehnen, Eva; Zieminski, Nick (November 10, 2008). Wallace, John (ed.). "Henkel to sell its stake in Ecolab" . Reuters . Retrieved 2026-07-30 . ^ "Ecolab Announces Henkel Completed Its Sale of Ecolab Shares" (PDF) (Press release). Business Wir', '["clm_wiki_ecolab_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
