  ('cs_ppg_history', 'org_ppg', 'overview', 'History',
   'Global supplier of glass and chemical products PPG Industries, Inc. One PPG Place in Pittsburgh Formerly Pittsburgh Plate Glass Company (1883–1968) Type Public Traded as NYSE : PPG S&amp;P 500 component Industry Chemicals Founded 1883 &#59;&#32;143 years ago ( 1883 ) , in Creighton, Pennsylvania , U.S. Founders John Baptiste Ford John Pitcairn Jr. Headquarters One PPG Place , Pittsburgh , Pennsylvania , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Tim Knavish ( chairman &amp; CEO ) Products Chemicals Decorative paints Industrial finishing products Coatings Revenue US$ 15.8 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.91 billion (2024) Net income US$1.12 billion (2024) Total assets US$19.4 billion (2024) Total equity US$6.96 billion (2024) Number of employees 46,000 (2024) Website ppg Footnotes [1] PPG Industries, Inc. is an American supplier of paints , coatings , and specialty materials based in Pittsburgh , Pennsylvania. It operates in more than 70 countries globally. A member of the Fortune 500 , PPG is the second largest coatings company in the world by revenue, behind Sherwin-Williams . [2] It is headquartered in PPG Place , an office and retail complex in downtown Pittsburgh, and is known for its glass facade designed by Postmodern architect Philip Johnson . ^ body:not( ):not( ) "PPG Industries, Inc. 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. February 20, 2025. ^ "Top manufacturers of paints, coatings, adhesives, and sealants" . Retrieved August 6, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_ppg_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
