VALUES
  ('cs_ppg_leadership', 'org_ppg', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'In sports PPG-sponsored IndyCar at the 2024 Firestone Grand Prix of St. Petersburg PPG has been involved in sports for numerous years, including being the primary sponsor for the CART PPG Indy Car World Series from 1980 to 1997. The company has been a partner of Team Penske in CART, IndyCar Series and NASCAR Cup Series since 1984. [1] Since the race''s inception in 1994, PPG has sponsored the trophy for the Brickyard 400 . PPG also partners with Formula 1 racing teams; they have had a partnership with Williams F1 Team since 2017. [2] PPG is the prime sponsor of John Force Racing and makes all their cars'' paints and decals before each NHRA race. [3] On October 4, 2016, it was announced that The Consol Energy Center in Pittsburgh would be giving up its naming rights, and transferred to PPG, making the arena named the PPG Paints Arena . [4] PPG has been involved in snooker since 2024, starting with the title sponsorship agreement with WST for the Tour Championship . The title sponsorship deal was then extended to the Triple Crown ''s Masters event until 2027 with its Johnstone''s Paint brand. [5] GORI, one of its sub-brands in Scandinavian countries, also sponsors the German Masters from 2025. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "PPG expands sponsorship with Blaney, Penske" . Racer . Retrieved August 6, 2026 . ^ "PPG" . Archived from the original on January 28, 2021 . Retrieved September 21, 2020 . ^ "PPG Teams Up with John Force Racing" . Archived from the original on October 1, 2022 . Retrieved September 23, 2020 . ^ "PPG to acquire naming rights to Consol Energy Center" . Retrieved October 4, 2016 . ^ "World Snooker Tour extends Johnstone''s Paint deal to Masters title rights" . SportBusiness . June 19, 2024 . Retrieved May 20, 2025 .', '["clm_wiki_ppg_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
