VALUES
  ('cs_ppg_operations', 'org_ppg', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '2020s In 2020, PPG won an Adhesives and Sealants Council (ASC) Innovation Award for "High Strength, Highly Ductile Structural Adhesive PR 2930". [1] In May 2021, PPG completed the acquisition of Wörwag, a German coating manufacturer. [2] On October 17, 2024, PPG announced its intent to sell its architectural coatings business in the U.S. and Canada to American Industrial Partners (AIP) for $550 million. Brands included in the sale are Glidden , Dulux (in Canada), Liquid Nails, Homax, Pittsburgh Paints and Stains, Flood, Sico and Manor Hall. The sale also includes 750 company owned retail stores, 6,600 independent dealer stores, and shelf facings at 8,100 retail and home improvement store locations. [3] The sale to AIP was completed on December 2, 2024. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Innovation Awards - Adhesive and Sealant Council" . www . Retrieved August 10, 2023 . ^ "PPG completes Worwag acquisition" . The Business Journals . May 17, 2021 . Retrieved August 6, 2026 . ^ "PPG reaches agreement to sell architectural coatings U.S. and Canada business to American Industrial Partners; announces comprehensive cost reduction program" . Yahoo Finance . October 17, 2024 . Retrieved October 18, 2024 . ^ "American Industrial Partners Completes Acquisition of PPG''s U.S. and Canadian Architectural Coatings Business" . December 2, 2024 . Retrieved August 6, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_ppg_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 272. LyondellBasell (slug=lyondellbasell, wiki='LyondellBasell')
