VALUES
  ('cs_lyondellbasell_operations', 'org_lyondellbasell', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Expansion Facility in Houston LyondellBasell''s United States operations filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection in January 2009, and emerged from bankruptcy in April 2010. [1] Its former parent company, LyondellBasell Industries AF S.C.A. was replaced by LyondellBasell Industries N.V. [2] It was listed on the New York Stock Exchange on October 14, 2010. [3] In 2012, 1 Houston Center , the building housing LyondellBasell''s Houston headquarters since 1986, was renamed LyondellBasell Tower. [4] In 2014, LyondellBasell announced that it was installing two large cracking furnaces at its Channelview plant, and the following year the company announced it would double production capacity at the Bayport Underwood plant. [5] LyondellBasell acquired the compounding assets of Zylog Plastalloys, an India-based company, in November 2015. [6] The acquisition made LyondellBasell the third largest poly (propylene) materials producer in India. [7] [8] In June 2016, LyondellBasell announced a factory in Northern China. It was the third facility for LyondellBasell to open in China, following Guangzhou and Suzhou . [9] In September 2016, LyondellBasell announced that it would build a $700 million polyethylene plant at the La Porte manufacturing complex on the Houston Ship Channel that would produce 1.1 billion pounds of polyethylene annually. [10] [11] The company started construction on a La Porte plant in May 2017. [12] [13] [14] The company completed an expansion of its Corpus Christi ethylene plant in January 2017. The plant''s capacity was increased by 50 percent to produce 2.5 billion pounds annually. [15] That same year, Hurricane Harvey hit the United States and affected the company''s Texas Gulf Coast operations. The Houston Ship Channel was temporarily closed, which prevented crude tankers from reaching refineries. The La Porte facility was damaged but came back online in late October. [16] [17] [18] In December 2017, LyondellBasell partnered with Suez , a French water and wa', '["clm_wiki_lyondellbasell_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
