VALUES
  ('cs_cf_operations', 'org_cf', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'American agrochemical manufacturer CF Industries Holdings, Inc. Type Public company Traded as NYSE : CF S&amp;P 500 component Industry Chemicals Founded 1946 &#59;&#32;80 years ago ( 1946 ) Headquarters Northbrook, Illinois , US Area served North America Key people Chris Bohn(CEO) Products Fertilizer Revenue US$ 7.084 billion (2025) [1] Operating income US$2.300 billion (2025) [1] Net income US$1.455 billion (2025) [1] Total assets US$14.088 billion (2025) [1] Total equity US$7.775 billion (2025) [1] Number of employees 3,016 [2] (2020) Website www CF Industries Holdings, Inc. is an American manufacturer and distributor of agricultural fertilizers , including ammonia , urea , and ammonium nitrate products. The company is based in Northbrook, Illinois , a suburb of Chicago , [3] and was founded in 1946 as the Central Farmers Fertilizer Company. For its first 56 years, it was a federation of regional agricultural supply cooperatives . CF then demutualized , and became a publicly traded company. ^ a b c d e body:not( ):not( ) "CF Industries - CF Industries Holdings, Inc. Reports Full Year 2025 Net Earnings of $1.46 Billion, Adjusted EBITDA of $2.89 Billion" . Retrieved February 24, 2026 . ^ "CF 2020 Sustainability Report Data Supplement 5.18.21" (PDF) . CF Industries. ^ "CF Industries Inc - Company Profile and News" . Bloomberg . Retrieved July 4, 2022 .', '["clm_wiki_cf_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
