  ('cs_dell-technologies_leadership', 'org_dell-technologies', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'IPO On January 29, 2018, it was reported that Dell Technologies was considering a reverse merger with its VMware subsidiary to take the company public. [1] On December 28, 2018, Dell Technologies became a public company, bypassing the traditional IPO process by buying back shares that tracked the financial performance of VMware . [2] [3] In May 2026, OpenAI partnered with Dell Technologies to allow enterprise customers to deploy the AI coding assistant Codex in on-premises and hybrid environments, integrating directly with the Dell AI Data Platform. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "VMware Plunges on Report It May Acquire Dell in Reverse Merger" . Bloomberg L.P. January 29, 2018 . Retrieved January 29, 2018 . ^ "Dell returns to public markets after 6 years" . Reuters. Archived from the original on July 6, 2022 . Retrieved December 28, 2018 . ^ "Bread Financial''s credit sales fall 13% in cooling economy" . American Banker . July 27, 2023 . Retrieved November 4, 2024 . ^ "OpenAI and Dell Technologies partner to bring Codex to hybrid and on-premises enterprise environments" . OpenAI. May 18, 2026 . Retrieved May 25, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_dell-technologies_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
