VALUES
  ('cs_broadcom_operations', 'org_broadcom', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Formation of Avago Technologies Logo of Avago Technologies KKR and Silver Lake Partners acquired the Semiconductor Products Group of Agilent Technologies in 2005 for $2.6 billion and formed Avago Technologies. [1] Avago Technologies agreed to sell its I/O solutions unit to PMC-Sierra for $42.5 million in October 2005. [2] In August 2008, the company filed an initial public offering of $400 million. [3] [4] In October 2008, Avago Technologies acquired Infineon Technologies'' Munich-based bulk acoustic wave business for €21.5 million. [5] On 6 August 2009, Avago Technologies went public on NASDAQ with the ticker symbol AVGO. [6] [7] Avago chip inside an iPhone 5s Avago Technologies announced its agreement to acquire CyOptics, an optical chip and component supplier, for $400 million in April 2013. [8] [9] The acquisition aimed to expand Avago Technologies'' fiber optics product portfolio. [9] In October 2013, Avago Technologies invested $5 million in Amantys, a power electronics technology provider, as part of a strategic investment agreement between the two companies. [10] Avago Technologies announced its agreement to acquire LSI Corporation in December 2013 for $6.6 billion. [1] [11] [7] [12] [13] The acquisition helped move Avago Technologies away from specialized products and towards a more mainstream industry, which included chips, especially storage for data centers. [13] The company sold its SSD controller business to Seagate Technology in May 2014. [14] In August 2014, the company was the ninth-largest semiconductor company. [15] Avago Technologies agreed to sell LSI''s Axxia Networking business to Intel for $650 million. [6] [16] The company also agreed to buy PLX Technology , an integrated circuits designer, for $309 million. [17] In February 2015, it was announced that Avago Technologies Limited had reached an agreement to acquire Emulex Corporation for $8 per share in cash. ^ a b Cite error: The named reference register was invoked but never defined (see the h', '["clm_wiki_broadcom_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
