  ('cs_jabil_history', 'org_jabil', 'overview', 'History',
   'American manufacturing company Jabil Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : JBL S&amp;P 500 component Industry Electronics Manufacturing Services [1] Founded 1966 &#59;&#32;60 years ago ( 1966 ) in Detroit, Michigan , U.S. Founders William E. Morean James Golden Headquarters St. Petersburg, Florida , U.S. Number of locations 30 countries [2] Area served Worldwide Key people Mark Mondello (Chairman) [3] Mike Dastoor (CEO) Gregory Hebard (CFO) Revenue US$ 28.9 billion (2024) [3] Operating income US$2.01 billion (2024) [3] Net income US$1.39 billion (2024) [3] Total assets US$17.4 billion (2024) [3] Total equity US$1.74 billion (2024) [3] Number of employees 138,000 (2024) [3] Website jabil Footnotes [4] Jabil Inc. is an American multinational manufacturing company involved in the design, engineering, and manufacturing of electronic circuit board assemblies and systems, along with supply chain services, primarily serving original equipment manufacturers . [5] [6] It is headquartered in the Gateway area of St. Petersburg, Florida . It is one of the largest companies in the Tampa Bay area . [7] [8] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Jabil Yahoo! Finance information" . Yahoo Finance . Retrieved 25 June 2012 . ^ "Jabil Locations" . Jabil . Archived from the original on 10 July 2022 . Retrieved 20 November 2020 . ^ a b c d e f g "Jabil FY 2024 10K Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . 28 October 2024. ^ "Jabil Circuit, Inc. History" . hoovers . Retrieved 25 June 2012 . ^ Cite error: The named reference cengage2018 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ "Jabil–The Manufacturing Giant You''ve Never Heard Of–Steps Out of the Shadows" . Fast Company . 6 May 2015 . Retrieved 2026-08-08 . ^ "In Slower Economy, More Cautious Jail Circuit Still Expects Third Record Year" . Archived from the original on 2012-06-24 . Retrieved 25 June 2012 . ^ "Jabil, Fortune 500" . Fortune . Retrieved 21 November 2018 . &#91; dead link &#93;', '["clm_wiki_jabil_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
