VALUES
  ('cs_avnet_history', 'org_avnet', 'overview', 'History',
   'Electronic component distributor This article is about the company. For other uses, see Avnet (disambiguation) . Avnet, Inc. Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : AVT S&amp;P 400 component Industry Electronics Founded 1921 &#59;&#32;105 years ago ( 1921 ) New York City , New York , U.S. Founder Charles Avnet Headquarters Phoenix, Arizona , U.S. Key people Phil Gallagher ( CEO ) Rodney Adkins ( chairman ) Ken Jacobson ( CFO ) Revenue US$ 26.53 billion (2023) Operating income US$1.35 billion (2023) Net income US$1.18 billion (2023) Total assets US$12.47 billion (2023) Total equity US$4.75 billion (2023) Number of employees c. &#8201;14,500 (2021) Website www Footnotes [1] [2] Avnet, Inc. is a distributor of electronic components headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona , named after Charles Avnet , who founded the company in 1921. After its start on Manhattan''s Radio Row , the company was incorporated in 1955 and began trading on the New York Stock Exchange in 1961. On May 8, 2018, Avnet changed stock markets to Nasdaq, [3] trading under the same ticker AVT. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Avnet, Inc. 2021 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . August 13, 2021. ^ "Avnet Names Phil Gallagher as Interim Chief Executive Officer and Announces Preliminary Fourth Quarter Fiscal 2020 Results" (Press release). August 3, 2020. ^ "Avnet to switch markets, be listed on the Nasdaq" . bizjournals . Retrieved June 4, 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_avnet_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
