VALUES
  ('cs_avnet_leadership', 'org_avnet', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '2010–present In July 2010, the company purchased Bell Microelectronics for $631 million. [1] In July 2011, CEO Roy Vallee retired, and then-COO Richard Hamada was appointed CEO. In March 2012 Avnet, Inc. acquired Ascendant Technologies and in October 2012, BrightStar Partners, Inc. and BSP Software LLC. This expanded Avnet Technology Solutions. In September 2016, Tech Data announced that it had entered into an agreement to acquire the Technology Solutions operating group from Avnet, Inc. in a stock and cash transaction valued at approximately US$2.6 billion. Under the terms of the agreement, Avnet received at closing approximately $2.4 billion in cash and 2.785 million shares of Tech Data common stock, representing an approximate 7 percent ownership position in Tech Data. [2] In October 2016, the company purchased British components distributor Premier Farnell for £691M. [3] In March 2019, Avnet announced that it was working with blockchain payment provider BitPay to accept cryptocurrency as payment for products and services. [4] Avnet stated that it had already closed "several multi-million dollar cryptocurrency transactions" in the first month of accepting Bitcoin. [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Avnet buys Bell Microproducts for $631 million" . Arizona Business and Money. July 7, 2010 . Retrieved September 2, 2015 . ^ "Tech Data Completes Acquisition of Technology Solutions Business from Avnet" . ^ "Premier Farnell Acquisition" . Premier Farnell . Archived from the original on February 14, 2017 . Retrieved February 13, 2017 . ^ "Avnet Now Accepts Cryptocurrency Payments" . Avnet . Retrieved March 20, 2019 . ^ "Avnet Leads Industry by Accepting Cryptocurrency" . Avnet . Retrieved March 20, 2019 .', '["clm_wiki_avnet_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
