VALUES
  ('cs_lkq_history', 'org_lkq', 'overview', 'History',
   'Automotive Parts Supplier html body A major contributor to this article appears to have a close connection with its subject. It may require cleanup to comply with Wikipedia''s content policies, particularly neutral point of view . Please discuss further on the talk page . See our advice if the article is about you and read our scam warning in case someone asks for money to edit this article. ( May 2025 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) LKQ Corporation Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : LKQ S&amp;P 600 component Industry Auto parts Founded February 1998 &#59;&#32;28 years ago ( 1998-02 ) Founder Donald F. Flynn Headquarters Nashville , Tennessee , U.S. Key people Justin Jude ( president and CEO ) Revenue $ 13,866 million [1] (2023) Owner ValueAct Capital , 7.1% [2] Number of employees 44,000 (2022) Subsidiaries Keystone Automotive Website lkqcorp LKQ wrecking yard in Texas LKQ Corporation ( “Like, Kind and Quality” ) is an American provider of alternative and speciality parts to repair and accessorize automobiles and other vehicles. LKQ has operations in North America, Europe and Taiwan. LKQ sells replacement systems, components, equipment and parts to repair and accessorize automobiles, trucks, and recreational and performance vehicles. [3] In December 2018, it was #300 on the list Fortune 500 . [4] In March 2017, Dominick P. Zarcone was selected to become the new President and Chief Executive Officer. [5] In June 2024 Justin Jude was selected to become the new President and Chief Executive Officer. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "LKQ-2023.12.31_10K" (PDF) . investor . p. 40 . Retrieved 2024-06-28 . ^ 2021 Proxy Statement ^ "LKQ Corporation | About, Auto Parts" . www . Retrieved 2018-01-02 . ^ "LKQ" . Fortune . Archived from the original on 2019-02-08 . Retrieved 2018-12-01 . ^ "LKQ Corporation Announces Leadership Transition" . investor . Archived from the original on 2018-07-27 . Retrieved 2018-07-27 .', '["clm_wiki_lkq_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
