VALUES
  ('cs_archer-daniels-midland_operations', 'org_archer-daniels-midland', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Regenerative agriculture In September 2022, PepsiCo and ADM established a partnership on regenerative agriculture projects that would increase the practice across their North American supply chains and help the companies meet carbon reduction goals. [1] In July 2023, ADM launched an expansion of the program, which offers producers financial incentives and technical support to implement regenerative practices. [2] As of December 2023, the company had allocated nearly 2 million acres of land within its supply chain for the program. [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Doering, Christopher (September 15, 2022). "PepsiCo, ADM partner to cut carbon through regenerative agriculture" . Food Dive . Retrieved August 29, 2023 . ^ Donley, Arvin (July 19, 2023). "ADM regenerative ag program set to expand" . Food Business News . Retrieved August 29, 2023 . ^ Marston, Jennifer (December 14, 2023). "2 million acres and counting: unpacking ADM''s regenerative agriculture progress report for North America" . AgFunderNews . Retrieved January 29, 2024 .', '["clm_wiki_archer-daniels-midland_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
