VALUES
  ('cs_mcdonalds_operations', 'org_mcdonalds', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Changes In 1994, McDonald''s banned smoking at the 1,400 United States locations it wholly owned. [1] [2] An American McDonald''s in Franklin, North Carolina , in 2024; it is an example of the "new" look of American McDonald''s restaurants In 2006, McDonald''s introduced its "Forever Young" brand by redesigning all of its restaurants. The restaurants were turned into cafe-esque space, being mostly terracotta, grey, and olive. The redesigned restaurants were also primarily furnished with wood furniture. [3] [4] As a result of the COVID-19 pandemic , McDonald''s closed most seating and all play areas in its United States restaurants. [5] It transitioned to drive-through and curbside orders at locations and online food ordering delivery services. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Hilts, Philip (February 24, 1994). "McDonald''s Bans Smoking at All the Sites It Owns" . New York Times . Archived from the original on November 12, 2020 . Retrieved May 10, 2025 . ^ Member, Trends Newsweek Is A. Trust Project (December 8, 2021). "People Can''t Believe McDonald''s Once Had Branded Ashtrays to Smoke Inside" . Newsweek . Archived from the original on May 28, 2025 . Retrieved May 28, 2025 . ^ Dozier, Alfred (October 22, 2022). "Modernizing fast food restaurants is a step in the wrong direction" . North Texas Daily . Archived from the original on August 22, 2025 . Retrieved May 29, 2025 . ^ "One Big Mac with Wi-Fi and lounge, please" . Los Angeles Daily News . February 28, 2006 . Retrieved May 29, 2025 . ^ McLean, Rob. "McDonald''s closes seating at corporate-owned restaurants amid coronavirus outbreak" . CNN . Archived from the original on December 17, 2020 . Retrieved July 10, 2020 . ^ Saxena, Jaya (March 17, 2020). "Corporate-Owned McDonald''s Will Only Offer Drive-Thru, Takeout, and Delivery Amid Coronavirus Pandemic" . Eater . Archived from the original on November 12, 2020 . Retrieved November 12, 2020 .', '["clm_wiki_mcdonalds_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
