VALUES
  ('cs_starbucks_leadership', 'org_starbucks', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '20th century 1970s Starbucks originally opened in Seattle, Washington, on March 30, 1971. [1] By selling coffee beans and related equipment, Starbucks became a local coffee bean retailer for the first ten years in Seattle. [2] It was founded by business partners Jerry Baldwin , Zev Siegl and Gordon Bowker who first met as students at the University of San Francisco . [3] The trio were inspired to sell high-quality coffee beans and equipment by coffee roasting entrepreneur Alfred Peet . [4] Bowker recalls that a business partner of his, Terry Heckler, thought words beginning with the letters "st" were powerful, leading the founders to create a list of words beginning with "st", hoping to find a brand name. They chose "Starbo", a misreading of the mining town Storbo in the Cascade Range named after Peter Storbo, founder and president of the Mount Rainier Mining Company. [5] [6] From there, the group remembered "Starbuck", the name of the chief mate in the book Moby-Dick . [7] Bowker said, " Moby-Dick didn''t have anything to do with Starbucks directly; it was only coincidental that the sound seemed to make sense . " [7] [8] The first Starbucks store was located in Seattle, at 2000 Western Avenue, from 1971 to 1976. The café was later moved to 1912 Pike Place. [9] During this time, Starbucks stores sold just coffee beans and not drinks. [10] In its first two years of operation, Starbucks purchased green coffee beans from Peet''s Coffee &amp; Tea . In 1973, Alfred Peet stopped supplying Starbucks and helped train their new Roastmaster, Jim Reynolds. [11] 1980s In 1984, the original owners of Starbucks, led by Jerry Baldwin , purchased Peet''s Coffee . [12] By 1986, the company was operating six stores in Seattle and had begun to sell espresso coffee. [13] [14] In 1987, the original owners sold the Starbucks chain to their former director of marketing Howard Schultz , who rebranded his Il Giornale coffee outlets as Starbucks and began to expand the company. [15] [16] Also i', '["clm_wiki_starbucks_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
