VALUES
  ('cs_darden-restaurants_history', 'org_darden-restaurants', 'overview', 'History',
   'American restaurant company Darden Restaurants, Inc. Darden Restaurants logo (2009–present) Darden''s headquarters in Orlando Type Public Traded as NYSE : DRI S&amp;P 500 component Industry Restaurant Predecessor General Mills Restaurants (1970–1995) Founded 1995 &#59;&#32;31 years ago ( 1995 ) Founder William Darden Headquarters Orlando, Florida , U.S. Number of locations 2,181 (2024) Area served Brazil Canada Costa Rica El Salvador Mexico Panama United States Key people Cynthia T. Jamison ( chair ) Rick Cardenas ( president &amp; CEO ) Services Foodservice Revenue US$ 11.4 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.31 billion (2024) Net income US$1.03 billion (2024) Total assets US$11.3 billion (2024) Total equity US$2.24 billion (2024) Number of employees 191,105 (2024) Divisions Olive Garden LongHorn Steakhouse Cheddar''s Scratch Kitchen Yard House The Capital Grille Seasons 52 Bahama Breeze Eddie V''s Ruth''s Chris Steak House Chuy''s Subsidiaries Darden Concepts, Inc. Website darden Footnotes Financials as of May 26,&#32;2024 &#91;update&#93; . [1] Darden Restaurants, Inc. is an American multi-brand restaurant operator headquartered in Orlando, Florida . [1] Darden has more than 2,100 restaurant locations and more than 200,000 employees, making it the world''s largest full-service restaurant company. [2] The company began as an extension of Red Lobster , founded by William Darden and initially backed by General Mills . Red Lobster was later sold in July 2014. The firm owns three fine dining restaurant chains: Ruth''s Chris Steak House , Eddie V''s Prime Seafood , and The Capital Grille ; and seven casual dining restaurant chains: Olive Garden , LongHorn Steakhouse , Bahama Breeze , Seasons 52 , Yard House , Cheddar''s Scratch Kitchen , and Chuy''s . ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "Darden FY 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. July 19, 2024 . Retrieved July 22, 2024 . ^ "Darden Brand Book" (PDF) . www . 2020. p. 4. Archived (PDF) from the original on December 18, 2021.', '["clm_wiki_darden-restaurants_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
