VALUES
  ('cs_cracker-barrel_operations', 'org_cracker-barrel', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '1981–1996 Location in Burnsville, Minnesota Cracker Barrel became a publicly traded company in 1981 to raise funds for further expansion. [1] [2] It floated more than half a million shares, raising $10.6 million. [3] Following the initial public offering, Cracker Barrel grew at a rate of around 20 percent per year; [4] by 1987, the company had become a chain of more than 50 units in eight states, with annual net sales of almost $81 million. [1] The company grew consistently through the 1980s and 1990s, attaining a $1 billion market value by 1992. [2] [5] [6] In 1993, the chain''s revenue was nearly twice that of any other family restaurant. [3] In 1994, the chain tested a carry-out-only store, Cracker Barrel Old Country Store Corner Market, in suburban residential neighborhoods. &#91; where? &#93; [6] In addition, it expanded into new markets through the establishment of more traditional Cracker Barrel locations, the majority of them outside the South, and tested alterations to its menus to adapt to new regions. [7] The chain added regional dishes to its menus, including eggs and salsa in Texas and Reuben sandwiches in New York, but continued to offer its original menu items in all restaurants. [5] Cracker Barrel did not close any locations until 1995, when a location on American Way in Memphis, Tennessee was closed due to it no longer meeting the company''s standards. [8] ^ a b Cite error: The named reference Rhein was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b Cite error: The named reference Gutner was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b Cite error: The named reference Carlino was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference Strother was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Brooks, Steve (March 1, 1996). "A barrel full of questions" . Restaurant Business . p. 48. Archived from the original on November 27, 2014 . Retrieved January 21, 2012 . ^ a b Moritz, Gwen (April', '["clm_wiki_cracker-barrel_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
