VALUES
  ('cs_papa-johns_history', 'org_papa-johns', 'overview', 'History',
   'American pizza restaurant chain For the company''s eponymous founder, see John Schnatter . Papa John''s International, Inc. Headquarters in Cumberland, Georgia Trade name Papa Johns Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : PZZA S&amp;P 600 component Industry Restaurant Genre Pizzeria Fast food Founded October 2, 1984 &#59;&#32;41 years ago ( 1984-10-02 ) Founder John Schnatter Headquarters Jeffersontown, Kentucky , U.S. Cumberland, Georgia , U.S. Number of locations 5,400 (December 2020) [1] Key people Todd Penegor ( president &amp; CEO ) Max Wetzel [2] ( CMO ) Jim Norberg [3] ( COO ) Products , , , Pizza chicken wings dessert Revenue US$1.81 billion (FY December 29, 2020) [1] Operating income US$90.253 million (FY December 29, 2020) [1] Net income US$57.932 million (FY December 29, 2020) [1] Total assets US$872.770 million (FY December 29, 2020) [1] Total equity −US$266.939 million (FY December 29, 2020) [1] Number of employees ~16,700 (FY December 29, 2020) [1] Website papajohns Papa John''s International, Inc. , trading as Papa Johns , [4] [5] is an American pizza restaurant chain founded by John Schnatter in Jeffersonville, Indiana , in 1984. The company went public in 1993 and had expanded to 1,500 restaurants by 1997. As of 2023 &#91;update&#93; , it is the fourth largest pizza delivery restaurant chain in the United States, [6] with headquarters in the Louisville, Kentucky , and Atlanta , Georgia, metropolitan areas. As of March 2022, Papa John''s global presence reached over 5,500 locations in 49 countries and territories. [7] Schnatter stepped down as CEO in 2018 and later resigned as chairman. Robert M. Lynch became CEO in 2019 and Todd Penegor succeeded him in 2024. A Papa John''s restaurant in Asheville, North Carolina ^ a b c d e f g body:not( ):not( ) Papa John''s International, Inc. Form 10-K for 2019 . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (Report). Archived from the original on April 16, 2021 . Retrieved March 24, 2020 . ^ "Former Heinz executive joins Papa John''s in management changes" . Food Business News . November 2019. Archived from the original on September 16, 2022 . Retrieved November 6, 2019 . ^ "Papa John''s Appoints Industry Veteran Jim Norberg as SVP and Chief of Restaurant Operations" . Business Wire . July 8, 2019. Archived from the original on April 25, 2022 . Retrieved July 8, 2019 . ^ "Papa John''s is changing its name – sort of" . FOX 2 . November 17, 2021. Archived from the original on November 23, 2021 . Retrieved November 23, 2021 . ^', '["clm_wiki_papa-johns_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
