VALUES
  ('cs_brinker_history', 'org_brinker', 'overview', 'History',
   'American restaurant company Brinker International, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : EAT S&amp;P 600 component Industry Restaurant Predecessor Chili''s Grill &amp; Bar (1975-76) Chili''s, Inc. (1976-91) Founded 1991 &#59;&#32;35 years ago ( 1991 ) Founder Larry Lavine (Chili''s Grill &amp; Bar) Norman E. Brinker (Brinker International, Inc.) Headquarters Dallas, Texas , U.S. Number of locations 1,672 restaurants (2019) Area served Worldwide Key people Kevin Hochman ( president and CEO ) Services Foodservice Revenue US$2.905 billion (2015) [1] Operating income US$311.20 million (2015) [1] Net income US$196.69 million (2015) [1] Total assets US$2.688 billion (2020) [1] Total equity -US$78.46 million (2015) [1] Number of employees 62,200 (2020) Subsidiaries Chili''s Pomona''s Pingu Fries Maggiano''s Little Italy Website brinker Footnotes [2] [3] Brinker International, Inc. (or simply Brinker ) is an American multinational hospitality industry company that owns Chili''s and Maggiano''s Little Italy restaurant chains . Founded in 1975 and based in Dallas, Texas, Brinker currently owns, operates, or franchises 1,672 restaurants under the names Chili''s Grill &amp; Bar and Maggiano''s Little Italy worldwide. [4] [1] ^ a b c d e f body:not( ):not( ) "Brinker International, Form 10-K, Annual Report, 2015" (PDF) . secdatabase . Retrieved June 12, 2016 . ^ Brinker International, Inc. (June 29, 2011). "FY 2011 10-K" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved April 17, 2012 . ^ Brinker International, Inc. (June 29, 2011). "2011 Annual Report to Shareholders" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved April 17, 2012 . ^ "Brinker International, Form 8-K, Current Report, Filing Date Feb 8, 2013" (PDF) . secdatabase . Retrieved Feb 13, 2013 .', '["clm_wiki_brinker_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
