VALUES
  ('cs_brinker_leadership', 'org_brinker', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisitions &amp; sales Brinker acquired Maggiano''s from Lettuce Entertain You Enterprises in August 1995. [1] The company sold off the Corner Bakery Cafe brand in 2005. [2] In December 2008, Mac Acquisition LLC, an affiliate of Golden Gate Capital , purchased a majority interest in Romano''s Macaroni Grill for $131.5 million. [3] [4] [5] In June 2010, Brinker sold On the Border Mexican Grill &amp; Cantina to OTB Acquisition LLC, also an affiliate of Golden Gate Capital. [3] [6] In 2015, the company purchased 103 franchised Chili’s restaurants for a reported $106.5 million. [7] In 2019, Brinker acquired 116 Midwestern Chili''s restaurants and purchased 23 more in 2021. [8] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Our Story" . Maggiano''s Little Italy . Retrieved 2024-05-29 . ^ "Brinker Selling Corner Bakery Cafe Chain for $70M" . benefitspro . Retrieved 2024-05-29 . ^ a b Cite error: The named reference FY 2011 AR was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ "Brinker Sells Majority Interest in Macaroni Grill" . www . Retrieved 2024-06-21 . ^ "Brinker to sell majority stake in Macaroni Grill" . Nation''s Restaurant News . 2008-08-18 . Retrieved 2024-09-19 . ^ Staff (2010-04-01). "Brinker Sells On The Border Brand" . franchisetimes . Retrieved 2024-06-21 . ^ "Brinker International acquires Chili''s franchisee in $106.5M deal" . Restaurant Business . 25 June 2015 . Retrieved 2024-06-21 . ^ Ifasso, Plamedie (3 September 2021). "Brinker International completes acquisition of 23 franchised Chili''s restaurants" . Dallas Business Journal . Retrieved 2024-09-19 .', '["clm_wiki_brinker_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
