VALUES
  ('cs_cava_leadership', 'org_cava', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Restaurants and expansion Cava restaurant in Silver Spring, Maryland In November 2018, Cava Group bought Zoës Kitchen , a restaurant chain with more than 250 locations, in a deal worth $300 million, taking the company private and helping Cava expand further into the suburbs. [1] [2] [3] As of August 2021, there were 133 Cava locations. All Cava restaurants are company-owned, and none are franchised. [1] In 2020, Cava Group converted seven of its Zoës Kitchen locations to Cava-branded restaurants, with plans to convert 50 more in 2021. [4] [5] [3] It has additional off-premises and digital kitchens dedicated to preparing food for online orders. [3] As of April 2026, Cava operated 459 restaurant locations in the United States. [6] ^ a b Cite error: The named reference acquiring was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) Cooper, Rebecca (August 17, 2018). "Cava Group acquires a massive competitor" . Washington Business Journal . Retrieved January 7, 2020 . ^ a b c Lucas, Amelia (April 18, 2019). "Cava sets its sights on more extensive national presence after Zoes Kitchen acquisition" . CNBC . Retrieved January 7, 2020 . ^ Cite error: The named reference value was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference investment was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ CAVA Group (May 15, 2025). "Earnings Release 2025 Q1" (PDF) . Retrieved May 16, 2025 .', '["clm_wiki_cava_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
