VALUES
  ('cs_lululemon_leadership', 'org_lululemon', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'IPO and expansion The company made its initial public offering in July 2007, raising $327.6 million by selling 18.2 million shares on the American Nasdaq . [1] [2] Christine Day , a former co-president of Starbucks , assumed her role as the company''s chief executive officer in 2008. [1] In December 2010, Lululemon recalled some of the store''s reusable bags that were made from polypropylene , based on reports of high levels of lead. [3] In 2012, Lululemon filed a lawsuit against Calvin Klein and supplier G-III Apparel Group for infringement of three of its design patents for yoga pants. [4] The case was settled out of court the same year. [5] In 2013, the company made its third consecutive appearance on Fortune &#39; s Fastest-Growing Companies list. [1] In December 2013, founder Chip Wilson announced his resignation as chairman, and that the president of Toms Shoes , Laurent Potdevin, would become CEO. [6] In 2018, Calvin McDonald became CEO of Lululemon Athletica. [7] In Dec. 2025, it was announced that Calvin McDonald would be stepping down as CEO. [8] In 2014, Lululemon opened its first store in Europe, in Covent Garden , London. [9] In February 2015, Wilson announced that he was resigning from the board, [10] [11] and Michael Casey, former lead director of the board, would replace him. [12] In 2018, Laurent Potdevin resigned as CEO and from the company''s board due to misconduct related to a relationship he was having with a then-employee and later contractor. [13] [14] In 2013, some customers complained that the clothing was of poor quality, with some items being "too sheer", having holes appear, and falling apart after a few uses. [15] [16] The same year, Lululemon recalled its black yoga pants that were unintentionally transparent and "too thin"; [17] the recall, which amounted to approximately 17 percent of all women''s pants sold in its stores, impacted its financial results . [18] The resulting financial loss and damage to the brand led to the forced departu', '["clm_wiki_lululemon_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
