  ('cs_crocs_history', 'org_crocs', 'overview', 'History',
   'American shoe manufacturing company Crocs, Inc. Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : CROX S&amp;P 400 component Industry Wholesale trade Retail &amp; consumer services Clothing &amp; clothing accessories Founded 2002 &#59;&#32;24 years ago ( 2002 ) Founder Scott Seamans, Lyndon Hanson and George Boedecker Jr Headquarters Broomfield, Colorado , U.S. Key people Andrew Rees ( CEO , 2017–present) [1] Anne Mehlman ( president , 2024–present) [2] Steven Smith (Head of Creative Innovation (2025-Present) [3] Products Shoes Revenue US$ 4.102 billion (2024) Net income US$950 million (2024) Total assets US$4.81 billion (2024) Total equity US$1.84 billion (2024) Number of employees 7,910, including 4,560 in retail-related functions (2024) Website crocs Footnotes [4] [5] Crocs, Inc. is an American footwear company based in Broomfield, Colorado which manufactures and markets the Crocs brand of foam footwear. Crocs, Inc. terms these "clogs," but they do not contain wood like traditional clogs . In 2021, they acquired the Italian footwear brand HEYDUDE for $2.5 billion. [6] In 2025, Crocs revenue stood at $3.3 billion, an increase of 1.5% from the previous year. [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Crocs CEO Andrew Rees explains the recent success of its shoes | CNN Business" . CNN . May 18, 2023 . Retrieved July 26, 2023 . ^ "Crocs, Inc. - Corporate Governance - Management" . investors . Retrieved July 26, 2023 . ^ "Crocs Names Steven Smith as head of Creative Innovation" . Complex /sneakers . November 26, 2024 . Retrieved October 23, 2025 . ^ "Inline Viewer: CROCS, INC. 10-K" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Washington, D.C. December 31, 2024. pp. 4, 34, F-6. ^ "Crocs, Inc. Reports Record Annual Revenues of $3.6 Billion, Growing 54% Over 2021" . Archived from the original on September 18, 2024 . Retrieved September 18, 2024 . ^ "Crocs, Inc. to Acquire Casual Footwear Brand HEYDUDE™" . investors . Retrieved April 7, 2026 . ^ "Crocs, Inc. Reports Fourth Quarter and Full-Year 2025 Results; Issues First Quarter and Full-Year 2026 Outlook" . investors . Retrieved April 7, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_crocs_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
