  ('cs_gopro_overview', 'org_gopro', 'overview', 'Overview',
   'GoPro, Inc. is an American technology company founded in 2002 by Nick Woodman. It manufactures action cameras and develops its own mobile apps and video-editing software. GoPro cameras are widely used for adventure sports, travel recording, and outdoor activities. Founded as Woodman Labs, Inc, the company is based in San Mateo, California.', '["clm_wiki_gopro_overview"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
