VALUES
  ('cs_spirit-airlines_operations', 'org_spirit-airlines', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Attempted mergers and bankruptcy Since 2022, various competing low-cost airlines announced plans to acquire Spirit. In February 2022, Frontier Airlines announced its intention to acquire Spirit, pending regulatory approval, with Frontier Airlines stock as the surviving entity. [1] The deal would have made the combined airline the fifth-largest airline in the U.S. [2] [3] In July 2022, Spirit''s shareholders rejected Frontier''s offer. [4] In April 2022, JetBlue proposed to acquire Spirit for $33 per share in cash, equivalent to $3.6 billion. [5] [6] In May, Spirit said its board of directors had decided not to consider JetBlue''s proposal. According to Spirit Airlines, JetBlue''s proposed acquisition would be unlikely to be approved by the U.S. Department of Justice''s Antitrust Division , because it would likely believe that an ultra-low-cost carrier being purchased by a higher-fare airline would increase fares for consumers. Spirit noted that the Antitrust Division was looking into JetBlue''s strategic partnership with American Airlines for the same reason. [7] That July, JetBlue reached an agreement to purchase Spirit for $33.50 per share, with additional inducements for Spirit shareholders. [8] [9] The deal would have made the unified company the fifth-largest airline based in the United States. [9] Spirit shareholders voted to approve the deal [10] but the Department of Justice sued to block it, [11] alleging that the merger would result in "higher fares, fewer seats, and harm millions of consumers". [12] [13] The trial began in October 2023, [14] and at its conclusion, a federal judge blocked JetBlue''s acquisition of Spirit Airlines on January 16, 2024, stating that the deal was anticompetitive towards other airline corporations and would harm consumers. As a result, Spirit Airlines'' stock fell by approximately 47% and the airline expressed concern over its future. Speculators predicted that Spirit may have to file for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection, followed by a', '["clm_wiki_spirit-airlines_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
