VALUES
  ('cs_allegiant-air_operations', 'org_allegiant-air', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Corporate affairs See also: Allegiant Travel Company § Business trends Allegiant Air is a wholly owned subsidiary of Allegiant Travel Company , a publicly traded holding company . The corporate headquarters for both the airline and its holding company are in Summerlin, Nevada , a suburb of Las Vegas. [1] Business model Allegiant''s business model differs from most other U.S. ultra-low-cost carriers by focusing primarily on leisure travelers in small and medium-sized cities that it considers underserved by major airlines. The airline operates nonstop flights from these markets to warm-weather vacation destinations such as Florida, Las Vegas, and Phoenix, [2] avoiding the traditional hub-and-spoke model used by larger carriers. Because many of its routes face little or no direct competition, Allegiant has been able to maintain a niche network; as of early 2020, only 18% of its 518 routes were also served nonstop by another airline. [3] [4] Like other ULCCs, Allegiant offers low base fares with few included amenities while generating substantial ancillary revenue through additional fees for services such as checked and carry-on baggage, seat assignments, and onboard food and beverages. [5] [6] [7] The airline also aggressively markets hotel bookings, rental cars, and tourist attractions through its Allegiant Vacations platform, generating additional commission revenue beyond airfare sales. [8] In 2024, ancillary fees averaged $75.34 per passenger. [9] Operationally, Allegiant emphasizes simplicity and low overhead costs. [10] The airline sells only point-to-point nonstop itineraries and does not offer connecting service, reducing scheduling complexity and minimizing the need to re-accommodate passengers during disruptions. [6] It frequently serves secondary airports in major metropolitan areas where landing fees and operating costs are lower, and in some markets has rented ticket counters on an hourly basis while outsourcing ground handling and airport staffing to third', '["clm_wiki_allegiant-air_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
