VALUES
  ('cs_heartland-express_operations', 'org_heartland-express', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History Heartland Express was founded in 1978 by Russell A. Gerdin. [1] Heartland Express went public in 1986. By 1988, the company had a fleet of more than 300 tractors and a net income of more than $5 million. [1] Heartland Express acquired Illinois-based Munson Transportation in 1994, doubling the size of the company. By the end of the following year, the company reported a net income of more than $20.5 million. [1] In 2013, Heartland Express purchased Gordon Trucking for $300 million. The acquisition made the company the fifth-largest asset-based trucking company in the United States. [2] In 2017, the company acquired Interstate Distributor from Saltchuk for $113 million. [3] Heartland express acquired Millis Transfer in 2019 for $150 Million. [4] In 2022, Heartland Express acquired Smith Transport for $170 million. [5] The company acquired the trucking assets of Contract Freighters, Inc. (CFI) from TFI International for $525 million later the same year. [6] [7] ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) M. L. Cohen (1997). "Heartland Express, Inc." . In Jay P. Pederson (ed.). International Directory of Company Histories . Vol. 18. St. James Press . pp. 225– 227. ISBN 1-55862-352-3 &#8211; via Archive . ^ Garnick, Coral. "Heartland Express buys Pacific-based Gordon Trucking for $300M" . The Seattle Times . Retrieved November 17, 2025 . ^ Ashe, Ari (July 6, 2017). "Heartland Buys Interstate Distributor From Saltchuk for $113 Million" . Transport Topics . Retrieved November 17, 2025 . ^ Gilroy, Roger (August 27, 2019). "Heartland Acquires Millis Transfer for $150 Million" . Transport Topics . Retrieved November 17, 2025 . ^ Campbell, Colin (June 1, 2022). "Heartland Express buys Smith Transport for $170M" . Trucking Dive . Retrieved November 17, 2025 . ^ "Heartland Express buys CFI''s truckload operations for $525 million" . KCRG-TV . August 22, 2022 . Retrieved November 17, 2025 . ^ Maiden, Todd (August 22, 2022). "Heartland Express acquires CFI assets for $525 million" . Freight', '["clm_wiki_heartland-express_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
