  ('cs_landstar-system_operations', 'org_landstar-system', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History Landstar has been in business since 1968 [1] and was incorporated in 1991. [2] In January 2014, Landstar sold its National Logistics Management (NLM) subsidiary to XPO, Inc. for $87m. [3] Using proprietary web-based software to provide management services for customers and carriers, NLM became the largest web-based expediter in North America. [4] In January 2017, Landstar opened its Landstar U.S./Mexico Logistics Service Center in Laredo, Texas . [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Company Overview of Landstar System, Inc" . Bloomberg . Retrieved July 29, 2018 . ^ Cite error: The named reference 10K2017 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ "XPO Logistics Completes Acquisition of NLM" . marketwatch . December 30, 2013. ^ "XPO Logistics Agrees to Acquire NLM" . The Wall Street Journal. December 11, 2013. ^ "Landstar opens up new U.S.-Mexico cross-border facility" . www . Retrieved July 11, 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_landstar-system_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
