VALUES
  ('cs_illinois-tool-works_history', 'org_illinois-tool-works', 'overview', 'History',
   'Wynn''s Wynn''s International was begun by a 70-year-old retired attorney, Chestein Wynn, in a garage in San Gabriel, California, making a product to reduce friction in engines. [1] [2] [3] [4] On May 28, 1947 , Carl Wynn incorporated Wynn Oil Company at 1222 Duarte Road, San Gabriel, California [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Wynn''s International, Inc" . Encyclopedia . Retrieved October 18, 2025 . ^ "Wynn''s aboard" . Supercars . Retrieved October 18, 2025 . ^ "Our Story" . Wynns USA . Retrieved October 18, 2025 . ^ "SAN GABRIEL VALLEY SUPERFUND SITES - Unilateral Administrative Order" (PDF) . United States Environmental Protection Agency . 2002. Archived from the original (PDF) on October 18, 2025 . Retrieved October 18, 2025 . ^ "About Wynn''s" . Wynn''s Australia . Retrieved October 18, 2025 . On May 28, 1947 ... incorporated ... Wynn Oil Company at 1222 Duarte Road, San Gabriel, California. ; April 1, 1948, Fire destroyed the two car garage. Within a few short weeks ... resume operation ... at Azusa, California ; Wynn''s Belgium was established in 1958 ; In 2005 Wynn''s became part of the Performance Polymers division of Illinois Tool Works.', '["clm_wiki_illinois-tool-works_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
