  ('cs_roper-technologies_leadership', 'org_roper-technologies', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisitions # Year Company Price Description of Assets Ref(s). 1 July 2012 Sunquest Information Systems $1.42 billion Diagnostic and laboratory software [1] 2 October 2016 ConstructConnect $632 million Software for the commercial construction industry [2] 3 December 2016 Deltek $2.8 billion Enterprise software for project-based businesses [3] 4 August 2020 Vertafore $5.35 billion Software for the property and casualty insurance industry [4] 5 October 2022 Frontline Education $3.725 billion Administration software for educators in K-12 [5] 6 August 2023 Syntellis Performance Solutions $1.25 billion Business performance management software, data, and intelligence [6] 7 August 2024 Transact Campus $1.5 billion Technology services for improving campus life [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Rusli, Evelyn M. (July 30, 2012). "Roper Industries to Buy Sunquest Information Systems for $1.4 Billion" . The New York Times . ^ "Roper Technologies to Acquire ConstructConnect, Leading Provider of SaaS Solutions for the Commercial Construction Industry" (Press release). PR Newswire . October 31, 2016. ^ Bach, James (December 6, 2016). "Herndon-based Deltek to be acquired for $2.8B" . American City Business Journals . ^ Hussain, Noor Zainab; Rana, Akanksha (August 13, 2020). D''Silva, Anil (ed.). "Roper Technologies to buy Vertafore for $5.35 billion" . Reuters . ^ "Thoma Bravo Completes Sale of Frontline Education to Roper Technologies" (Press release). PR Newswire . October 4, 2022. ^ "Thoma Bravo and Madison Dearborn Partners Sell Syntellis Performance Solutions to Roper Technologies" (Press release). Thoma Bravo . August 8, 2023. ^ Kachwala, Zaheer (August 15, 2024). "Roper to buy Transact Campus for $1.5 bln to grow education business" . Reuters .', '["clm_wiki_roper-technologies_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
