  ('cs_trane-technologies_leadership', 'org_trane-technologies', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Brands and subsidiaries The company''s brands and subsidiaries [1] include: Trane – subsidiary brand manufacturing heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) equipment American Standard Heating &amp; Air Conditioning – HVAC equipment brand Ameristar – Value HVAC equipment brand of American Standard Oxbox – Value HVAC equipment brand RunTru – Value HVAC equipment brand Thermocold – European HVAC equipment brand AL-KO – European manufacturer of air handling units Thermo King – subsidiary brand manufacturing refrigeration units for transport industry, HVAC units for buses and trains Frigoblock – European refrigeration unit brand ICS Cool Energy – Refrigeration and HVAC equipment for European industrial customers MTA-IT – HVAC equipment for European customers Nuvolo – cloud-based connected workplace solutions for digital advancements in heating and cooling BrainBox AI – Driving artificial intelligence and innovation across the built environment, including the Trane Technologies AI Lab Life Science Solutions – Provide precision-temperature controlled solutions for health and life sciences customers Farrar Scientific – Life sciences refrigeration brand Helmer Scientific – Life sciences refrigeration brand Diversified Laboratory Repair (DLR) - maintenance and repair services of laboratory equipment Data Center Solutions – Advancing smarter data center cooling Trane - Provides thermal management strategy [2] for hyperscale data centers Stellar Energy – innovator of data center cooling solutions in modular data centers Liquid Stack – liquid cooling technology for high-density AI-scale workloads ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Our Brands | Sustainable Solutions" . www . Retrieved 23 March 2026 . ^ "Improving how data centers are developed, designed and operated" . www . Retrieved 23 March 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_trane-technologies_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
