  ('cs_trane-technologies_operations', 'org_trane-technologies', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Sustainability and Innovation Trane Technologies embeds sustainability across its products, operations and long-term strategy. The company has key sustainability related commitments, which include: Gigaton Challenge , their goal to reduce one billion metric tons, or a gigaton, of greenhouse gas emissions (CO2e) from customer''s carbon footprints by 2030. Leading by Example , their commitment to have a restorative impact on the environment through their own supply chain and operations with decarbonization strategies and the 2050 Net-Zero roadmap, as outlined in their Climate Transition Plan [1] . Opportunity for All , a component of the workforce culture at Trane Technologies [2] where their employees are part of an uplifting culture focused on broadening access to education and skill development, purpose-driven careers with growth opportunities and career pathways in the company. Trane Technologies has expanded its digital and AI-enabled solutions through strategic acquisitions focused on building automation, data-driven energy optimization and advanced thermal management technologies. Brainbox AI : Trane Technologies announced the acquisition of BrainBox AI [3] , a developer of autonomous building management and AI‑driven HVAC optimization technology, on December 18, 2024 , and completed the acquisition on January 3, 2025 . Stellar Energy: The company completed the acquisition of the digital business of Stellar Energy [4] Americas, Inc. on February 17, 2026 , expanding its capabilities in energy systems analytics and performance optimization. LiquidStack: Trane Technologies announced its acquisition of LiquidStack [5] , a leader in advanced liquid cooling technologies for data centers and electronics, on February 10, 2026 , and completed the transaction on March 3, 2026 . ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Trane Technologies Climate Transition Plan" (PDF) . ^ "Careers at Trane Technologies | Trane Technologies jobs" . Trane Technologies . Retrieved 23 March 2026 . ^ "Trane Techn', '["clm_wiki_trane-technologies_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
