   'Finance The key financial trends for IDEX Corporation are based on fiscal years ending December 31: [1] Year Revenue (USD billion) Gross Profit (USD billion) Net Income (USD billion) 1994 0.399 0.166 0.033 2000 0.704 0.303 0.063 2006 1.150 0.477 0.146 2012 1.950 0.803 0.037 2018 2.480 1.120 0.410 2021 2.760 1.220 0.449 2024 3.269 1.445 0.505 In Q1 2025, IDEX beat Wall Street earnings and revenue estimates, reporting revenue of US $814.3 million and adjusted EPS of $1.75, citing strong demand in its Health &amp; Science Technologies segment. [2] For Q2 2025, the company posted revenue of US $865.4 million (up 7.2% YoY) and EPS of $2.07, outperforming forecasts, though it lowered full-year adjusted EPS guidance to a range of $7.85–$7.95 due to softening demand trends. [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "IDEX Corporation Financial Overview" . Smartfin . Retrieved 2025-08-07 . ^ "IDEX tops quarterly estimates on demand for health and science products" . Reuters. 2025-05-01 . Retrieved 2025-08-07 . ^ "IDEX Corp slashes 2025 profit forecast on slow demand for industrial equipment" . Reuters. 2025-07-30 . Retrieved 2025-08-07 .', '["clm_wiki_idex_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
