VALUES
  ('cs_transdigm_operations', 'org_transdigm', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisitions TransDigm focuses largely on acquiring other aerospace component manufacturers for expansion and growth. [1] &#58;&#8202;492&#8202; The company acquired more than 60 businesses in its first 25 years of operations, [2] &#58;&#8202;228&#8202; 49 of which were completed after TransDigm''s initial public offering in 2006. [3] In 2010, TransDigm acquired competing aftermarket aerospace parts company McKechnie Aerospace Holdings for $1.27 billion. [4] In 2016, it bought Data Device Corp., a power, networking and electronics company, for $1 billion. [5] Two years later, TransDigm purchased a competing parts manufacturer, Esterline , for $4 billion. [6] This was the largest acquisition in TransDigm''s history. [3] In March 2022, TransDigm acquired the Montreal -based helicopter mission equipment company, DART Aerospace for approximately $360 million in cash. [7] In May 2023, TransDigm acquired aviation and transportation research company Calspan for $725 million. [8] [9] [10] In November 2023, TransDigm acquired Electron Device Business of Communications &amp; Power Industries for $1.39 billion. [11] In January 2026, TransDigm agreed to acquire Jet Parts Engineering and Victor Sierra Aviation Holdings from PE firm Vance Street Capital for $2.2 billion in cash. [12] ^ Cite error: The named reference international was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference lessons was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Banerjee, Arunima (October 10, 2018). "TransDigm dives deeper into aero spare parts market with Esterline buy" . Reuters. Archived from the original on October 10, 2018 . Retrieved October 7, 2020 . in its biggest-ever deal ^ "CORRECTED - CORRECTED-UPDATE 2-TransDigm to buy rival McKechnie for $1.27 bl" . U.S . Archived from the original on 2023-09-04 . Retrieved 2026-08-06 . ^ Stynes, Tess (2016-05-24). "TransDigm to Acquire Data Device Corp. for $1 Billion" . Wall Street Journal . ISSN', '["clm_wiki_transdigm_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
