VALUES
  ('cs_booz-allen-hamilton_history', 'org_booz-allen-hamilton', 'overview', 'History',
   'American management and consulting IT firm For other uses, see Booz Allen Hamilton (disambiguation) . Booz Allen Hamilton Holding Corporation Type Public Traded as NYSE : BAH (Class A) S&amp;P 400 component Industry Management consulting Technology consulting Founded June 18, 1914 &#59;&#32;112 years ago ( 1914-06-18 ) Founders Edwin G. Booz James L. Allen Carl L. Hamilton Headquarters McLean, Virginia , U.S. Key people Horacio D. Rozanski (Chairman, President &amp; CEO) Services Management and Technology Consulting Revenue US$ 10.7 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.01 billion (2024) Net income US$606 million (2024) Total assets US$6.56 billion (2024) Total equity US$1.05 billion (2024) Number of employees 34,200 (2024) Website boozallen Footnotes [1] [2] [3] Booz Allen Hamilton Holding Corporation (informally Booz Allen ) [4] is the parent of Booz Allen Hamilton Inc., an American government and military contractor specializing in intelligence , technology , and cybersecurity . [5] The company is headquartered in McLean, Virginia , [6] in the Washington metropolitan area , with 80 additional offices around the globe. Booz Allen''s stated core business is to provide consulting, analysis, and engineering services to public- and private-sector organizations and nonprofits. [7] [8] It is a major provider of cybersecurity services to the U.S. Security and Exchange Commission . [9] [10] Nearly all of the company''s revenue comes from U.S. government contracts. [11] [12] [13] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "U.S. SEC: Booz Allen Hamilton Holding Corporation Form 10-K" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . May 24, 2024. ^ "Booz Allen (BAH) Form 10-Q" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . January 28, 2022. ^ "Top 100 Federal Prime Contractors: 2007. 13: Booz Allen Hamilton Inc" . Archived from the original on June 26, 2007 . Retrieved November 21, 2007 . ^ "Booz Allen Hamilton website: About Booz Allen" . Booz Allen Hamilton . Retrieved June 25, 2013 . ^ Bach, James (June 15, 2017). "Booz Allen under DOJ investigation for government overhead charges" . Washington Business Journal . Retrieved June 17, 2017 . ^ "Office Locations" . www . Retrieved June 1, 2017 . ^ Heath, Thomas (July 12, 2015). "Booz Allen returning to its roots, with a twist" . The Washington Post . ^ "Core Expertise" . www . Retrieved September 15, 2018 . ^ "Booz Allen Gets $113M SEC Cybersecurity Support Contract; Mark Gamis Quoted" . GovCon Wire . February 21, 2020 . Retrieved July 31, 2025 . ^', '["clm_wiki_booz-allen-hamilton_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
