VALUES
  ('cs_booz-allen-hamilton_leadership', 'org_booz-allen-hamilton', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '20th century Founding partners (from left to right): George Fry, Edwin G. Booz , Carl L. Hamilton , and James L. Allen The company that was to become Booz Allen was founded in 1914, in Evanston, Illinois , when Northwestern University graduate Edwin G. Booz founded the Business Research Service. The service was based on Booz''s theory that companies would be more successful if they could call on someone outside their own organizations for expert, impartial advice. [1] Booz''s service attracted a number of clients, such as Goodyear Tire &amp; Rubber Company , Chicago''s Union Stockyards and Transit Company , and the Canadian Pacific Railway . [2] During the following three decades, the company went through a number of name changes and business models, eventually settling on Booz, Fry, Allen &amp; Hamilton , named after their partnership in 1936. Before George A. Fry''s departure in 1942, the company''s name was changed again to Booz Allen Hamilton. [3] The post- World War II era saw a shift in the company''s client pool, with many contracts coming from governmental institutions and different branches of the Armed Forces . [2] Edwin G. Booz died in 1951. The company received its first international contract two years later, in 1953, to help reorganize land-ownership records for the newly established Philippines government. [4] Booz Allen has been credited with developing several business concepts. In 1957, Sam Johnson, great grandson of the S.C. Johnson &amp; Son founder, and Booz Allen''s Conrad Jones published How to Organize for New Products [5] which discussed theories on product life-cycle management . [6] [7] In 1958, Gordon Pehrson, deputy director of U.S. Navy Special Projects Office, and Bill Pocock of Booz Allen Hamilton developed the Program Evaluation and Review Technique (PERT) . [8] [9] In 1982, Booz Allen''s Keith Oliver coined the term " supply chain management ". [10] The partnership was dissolved in 1962 and the company was registered as a private corporatio', '["clm_wiki_booz-allen-hamilton_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
