  ('cs_mantech_operations', 'org_mantech', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Notable contracts The firm supports critical and national security programs through more than 1,000 current contract vehicles, including IDIQs, fixed-price, cost-reimbursement, labor-hour, time-and-materials, and many others. [1] On October 30, 2018, MANTECH announced a 10-year contract with the U.S. Air Force Space Command (AFSPC) totaling $158 million to provide full-spectrum security services to protect mission-critical programs. [2] On September 5, 2018, MANTECH announced a $668 million GSA FEDSIM award to support the Department of Homeland Security ’s Continuous Diagnostics and Mitigation (CDM) Dynamic and Evolving Federal Enterprise Network Defense (DEFEND) program. [3] On July 12, 2018, MANTECH announced the award of a $959 million managed services contract to provide Enterprise IT solutions for a Department of Defense agency. [4] On January 30, 2018 MANTECH announced a $133 million award from the U.S. Army Intelligence &amp; Security Command to support INSCOM''s mission of counter-intelligence and counter-terrorism throughout the world. [5] On November 30, 2017, The U.S. Army has awarded MANTECH an $847 million task order for Vehicle Engineering Maintenance and Operations Support (VEMOS). This effort was awarded under the GSA OASIS MA-IDIQ and will be managed by FEDSIM. Under the 5-year agreement, MANTECH will provide a wide range of sustainment support services (operational engineering and logistics support) globally for some 25,000 vehicles including the Army''s Mine-Resistant Ambush Protected vehicles, or MRAPs. [6] On November 27, 2017, MANTECH announced an $816 million contract with the U.S. Department of State to provide wide-ranging electronic and physical security countermeasure programs that will safeguard personnel supporting State''s mission, both overseas and domestic. [7] On August 14, 2017, MANTECH was awarded a $180 million contract, with full potential value of $450 million including contract extensions over a 10-year term, to manage and 