  ('cs_parsons_history', 'org_parsons', 'overview', 'History',
   'American technology-focused engineering firm Parsons Corporation Parsons headquarters in Chantilly, Virginia Type Public Traded as NYSE : PSN S&amp;P 400 component Industry Security Defense Intelligence Technology Critical Infrastructure Founded 1944 &#59;&#32;82 years ago ( 1944 ) in California , United States (as Ralph M. Parsons Company) Founder Ralph M. Parsons Headquarters Chantilly, Virginia , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Carey Smith ( CEO , chair and president ) [1] Revenue US$ 6.4 billion (2025) Operating income US$418 million (2025) Net income US$241.1 million (2025) Total assets US$5.77 billion (2025) Total equity US$2.77 billion (2025) Number of employees 21,000 (2025) Website parsons Footnotes [2] Parsons Corporation is an American multinational technology-focused defense, intelligence, and infrastructure engineering firm. Founded in 1944, [3] Parsons is headquartered in Chantilly, Virginia , and serves both government and private sector organizations in more than 30 countries. [4] Parsons became a public company after its initial public offering (IPO) in 2019. It was included in the Fortune 1000 in 2020 and added to the S&amp;P 400 in 2024. [5] [6] As of late 2025, Parsons employs over 21,000 professionals worldwide. [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Parsons Corporation Board Unanimously Elects Carey Smith As Chairwoman" . www (Press release). January 24, 2022 . Retrieved May 20, 2024 . ^ "Parsons Corporation 2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. February 11, 2026 . Retrieved March 11, 2026 . ^ Brown, Heidi (November 10, 2007). "Rebuilding" . Forbes . Retrieved August 17, 2018 . ^ "Parsons Corporation 2022 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . ^ Lake, Sydney (May 18, 2020). "35 Virginia companies make 2020 Fortune 1000 list" . Virginia Business . Retrieved October 19, 2024 . ^ "Palantir Technologies, Dell Technologies, and Erie Indemnity Set to Join S&amp;P 500; Others to Join S&amp;P MidCap 400 and S&amp;P SmallCap 600" . News Release Archive . Retrieved October 19, 2024 . ^ "10-K: Annual report for year ending December 31, 2025" .', '["clm_wiki_parsons_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
