  ('cs_accenture_operations', 'org_accenture', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Reincorporation in Ireland, 2009 until present On 26 May 2009, Accenture announced that its board of directors had unanimously approved changing the company''s place of incorporation from Bermuda to Ireland. [1] Since 2013, Accenture has acquired over 200 companies . [2] Accenture has been a strategic partner of The Alan Turing Institute since 2017. [3] In January 2026, the company announced the acquisition of Faculty , a UK-based artificial intelligence company, in a deal that values the company at $1 billion. [4] In March 2026, Accenture agreed to acquire Ookla , a Seattle-based network intelligence company known for Speedtest , Downdetector , Ekahau, and RootMetrics from Ziff Davis for $1.2 billion. [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Accenture to move HQ to Ireland from Bermuda" . RTE . 27 May 2009 . Retrieved 21 July 2026 . ^ "Accenture Mergers and Acquisitions Summary" . mergr . Mergr. n.d. Archived from the original on 11 August 2023 . Retrieved 28 August 2025 . ^ "Accenture" . Turing Institute . n.d. Archived from the original on 5 September 2025 . Retrieved 28 August 2025 . ^ "Accenture buys UK AI start-up Faculty in $1bn deal" . www.ft . Archived from the original on 12 January 2026 . Retrieved 13 January 2026 . ^ "Accenture announces deal to acquire Ookla" . Staffing Industry Analysts . 10 March 2026 . Retrieved 21 July 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_accenture_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
