VALUES
  ('cs_amgen_leadership', 'org_amgen', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '2000–2014 Binder was succeeded as CEO by Kevin W. Sharer in 2000. [1] Robert A. Bradway became Amgen''s president and chief executive officer in May 2012, following Sharer''s retirement. [2] In June 2010, Amgen received approval by the Food and Drug Administration for Prolia, a protein drug for the treatment of post-menopausal osteoporosis. [3] In clinical trials, Prolia reduced the rate of vertebral fractures by 61% and the risk of hip fractures by 40%. [4] In November 2010, the FDA approved Xgeva for the prevention of complications of bone metastases in patients with solid tumors. [5] The clinical trials primarily enrolled patients with breast or prostate cancer. In March 2011, Amgen acquired a manufacturing facility near Dublin, Ireland. [6] Amgen opened an affiliate in China in 2013. [7] [8] In November 2014, the company halted all trials of rilotumumab in advanced gastric cancer patients after one of the trials found more deaths in those who took the compound with chemotherapy, than those without. [9] Also in November 2014, the company, in conjunction with AstraZeneca , reported positive results for brodalumab in a Phase III trial comparing the compound with ustekinumab and a placebo in treating psoriasis . [10] In the same month, construction was completed on Amgen''s next-generation biomanufacturing facility in Singapore. [11] Blincyto ( blinatumomab ) was approved by the FDA in December of that year. [12] [13] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Amgen names new CEO" . CNN . May 11, 2000. Archived from the original on December 20, 2002. ^ "Kevin Sharer, Amgen Chairman and CEO, Announces Plan to Retire With Robert Bradway to Become CEO on May 23, 2012; Sharer Will Continue as Chairman of the Board Until End of 2012" (Press release). PR Newswire . December 15, 2011. ^ "Drug Approval Package" . Food and Drug Administration . ^ "HIGHLIGHTS OF PRESCRIBING INFORMATION – Prolia (denosumab)" (PDF) . Food and Drug Administration . June 2010. ^ "FDA Approves Xgeva to Help Prevent Cance', '["clm_wiki_amgen_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
