VALUES
  ('cs_amgen_operations', 'org_amgen', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Philanthropy In October 2017, the Amgen Foundation pledged $3 million to Khan Academy to support the development of free online biology lessons. [1] [2] In July 2020, Amgen granted an additional $3 million Khan Academy to support educational equity and science learning. [3] [4] In January 2020, the Amgen Foundation and Harvard University debuted LabXchange, a free online science education platform. [5] [6] Amgen and the Amgen Foundation announced a commitment of up to $12.5 million to support COVID-19 relief efforts in March. [7] In November 2021, Amgen awarded a $2 million grant to the CDC Foundation to launch the latter''s EmPOWERED Health Program, promoting patient engagement in decision making for cancer treatments. [8] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Vuocolo, Alex (June 23, 2020). "Khan Academy Founder Says $3M Grant Will Help Tackle Inequities in Virtual Education" . Cheddar . ^ D''Angelo, Alexa (October 29, 2017). "Amgen Foundation awards Khan Academy $3 million to support development of biology" . Ventura County Star . ^ "Amgen Foundation awards $3 million to Khan Academy" . Candid . July 24, 2020. ^ Molina, Brett (July 30, 2020). "Q&amp;A: Khan Academy CEO Sal Khan on the new school year and virtual learning" . USA Today . ^ Kelly, Rhea (January 24, 2020). "Amgen and Harvard Launch Free Online Science Ed Platform -- Campus Technology" . Campus Technology . ^ Kahn, Natalie L.; Wang, Andy Z. (April 8, 2020). "Harvard''s LabXChange Provides Platform for Remote Scientific Learning During Pandemic" . The Harvard Crimson . ^ "Amgen, AT&amp;T, Others Announce Commitments for COVID-19 Response" . Candid . March 25, 2020. ^ "CDC Foundation Active Programs October 1, 2020 – September 30, 2021" . CDC Foundation . December 9, 2021. Archived from the original on January 15, 2022.', '["clm_wiki_amgen_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
