  ('cs_amphenol_history', 'org_amphenol', 'overview', 'History',
   'American manufacturer of electrical connectors Amphenol Corporation Type Public Traded as NYSE : APH (Class A) S&amp;P 500 component Industry Electronics Founded 1932 &#59;&#32;94 years ago ( 1932 ) Founder Arthur J. Schmitt Headquarters Wallingford , Connecticut , United States Key people R. Adam Norwitt, President and CEO Products Coaxial cables Connectors Revenue US$ 15.2 billion (2024) Operating income US$3.16 billion (2024) Net income US$2.42 billion (2024) Total assets US$21.4 billion (2024) Total equity US$9.79 billion (2024) Number of employees c. &#8201;125,000 (2024) Website amphenol Footnotes [1] [2] html body This article needs more citations . Please help improve this article by adding citations to reliable sources . Unsourced material may be challenged and removed . Find sources: "Amphenol" – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR ( April 2026 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Amphenol Corporation is an American producer of electronic and fiber optic connectors, cable and interconnect systems such as coaxial cables . [3] Amphenol is a portmanteau from the corporation''s original name, American Phenolic Corp. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Amphenol Corporation 2024 Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. February 7, 2025. ^ "Amphenol Corp-CL A (APH:US)" . Archived from the original on 2010-12-20 . Retrieved 2011-01-19 . ^ Pace, Stan (2018-05-20). "Amphenol (NYSE:APH) versus Methode Electronics (MEI) Critical Comparison" . StockNewsTimes . Retrieved 2018-05-23 . ^ "Amphenol" . Amphenol Global Interconnect Systems . Retrieved 2019-01-25 .', '["clm_wiki_amphenol_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
