  ('cs_analog-devices_operations', 'org_analog-devices', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'American semiconductor manufacturer This article is about the semiconductor company. For the general concept, see Analog device . Analog Devices, Inc. Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : ADI Nasdaq-100 component S&amp;P 500 component Industry Semiconductors Founded 1965 &#59;&#32;61 years ago ( 1965 ) in Cambridge, Massachusetts , U.S. Founders Ray Stata Matthew Lorber Headquarters Wilmington, Massachusetts , U.S. Key people Vincent Roche ( chairman and CEO ) Products Semiconductors Revenue US$ 11.02 billion (2025) Operating income US$2.932 billion (2025) Net income US$2.267 billion (2025) Total assets US$47.99 billion (2025) Total equity US$33.82 billion (2025) Number of employees 24,500 (2025) Website analog Footnotes Financials as of November 1,&#32;2025 &#91;update&#93; . [1] Analog Devices, Inc. ( ADI ), also known simply as Analog , is an American multinational semiconductor company specializing in data conversion , signal processing , and power management technology, headquartered in Wilmington, Massachusetts . [2] [3] The company manufactures analog, mixed-signal and digital signal processing (DSP) integrated circuits (ICs) used in electronic equipment. [4] [5] These technologies are used to convert, condition and process real-world phenomena, such as light, sound, temperature, motion, and pressure into electrical signals. [6] Analog Devices has approximately 100,000 customers [7] in the following industries: communications, computer, instrumentation, military/aerospace, automotive, and consumer electronics applications. [8] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "FY 2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . 25 November 2025. ^ Hoovers. " Analog Devices, Inc. ." Retrieved January 4, 2011. ^ "Contact Us | Analog Devices" . www . Retrieved 26 January 2021 . ^ Reuters. " Analog Devices, Inc. ." Retrieved January 4, 2011. ^ Cite error: The named reference doris was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ ECE lab. " Digital Signal Processors ', '["clm_wiki_analog-devices_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
