   'American asset management company Ares Management Corporation Ares Management''s global headquarters Type Public Traded as NYSE : ARES (Class A) S&amp;P 500 component Industry Asset Management Founded 1997 &#59;&#32;29 years ago ( 1997 ) Founders Antony Ressler , John Kissick, Michael Arougheti, David Kaplan, and Bennett Rosenthal Headquarters Los Angeles , California, U.S. Revenue US$ 3.885 billion (2024) Operating income US$946 million (2024) [1] Net income US$441 million (2024) AUM $596 billion (2025) [2] Total assets US$24.884 billion (2024) Total equity US$6.824 billion (2024) Number of employees approx. 4,200 (November 2025) Website www www www www Footnotes [3] Ares Management Corporation is a global alternative investment manager operating in the credit , private equity and real estate markets. The company was founded in 1997, with additional offices across North America, Europe, and Asia. As of June 30, 2026, Ares Management Corporation''s global platform had approximately $671.3 billion in assets under management and 4,400 employees operating across North America, Europe, Asia Pacific and the Middle East. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Ares Management Operating Income 2012-2025" . ^ "About Ares Management Corporation" . Ares Management Corporation . Retrieved November 20, 2025 . ^ "Ares Management Corporation (Financials)" . Yahoo! Finance . Retrieved June 23, 2020 . ^ "Ares Management Q2 Earnings Meet Estimates, AUM Rises Y/Y" . Yahoo Finance .', '["clm_wiki_ares-management_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
