VALUES
  ('cs_arista-networks_operations', 'org_arista-networks', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Corporate history Arista Networks was founded and incorporated in 2008, evolving from its roots in Arastra, [1] established in 2004. Arista went public as ANET in 2014 and entered the S&amp;P 500 in 2018 and was recognized on the 2026 Fortune 500 list of the largest United States corporations by revenue. [2] It provides cloud and AI high performance networking. Members of Arista’s leadership team have experience in networking and innovation. [3] In June 2014, Arista Networks had its initial public offering on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol ANET. [4] In December 2014, Cisco filed two lawsuits against Arista alleging intellectual property infringement., [5] and the United States International Trade Commission issued limited exclusion and cease-and-desist orders concerning two of the features patented by Cisco [6] and upheld an import ban on infringing products. [7] In 2016, on appeal, the ban was reversed following product changes and two overturned Cisco patents, and Cisco''s claim was dismissed. [8] [9] In August 2018, Arista agreed to pay Cisco US$ 400 million as part of a settlement that included a release for all claims of infringement by Cisco , dismissal of Arista''s antitrust claims against Cisco , and a 5-year stand-down between the companies. [10] In August 2018, Arista Networks acquired Mojo Networks. [11] In September 2018, Arista Networks acquired Metamako and integrated its low-latency product line as the 7130 series. [12] In February 2020, Arista acquired Big Switch Networks. [13] In October 2020, Arista acquired Awake Security. [14] Arista''s CEO, Jayshree Ullal, was named to Barron''s list of World''s Best CEOs in 2018 and 2019. [15] In August 2022, Arista Networks acquired Pluribus Networks, a unified cloud network company, for an undisclosed sum. [16] In July 2025, Arista expanded its AI-driven campus and branch networking offerings and acquired the VeloCloud SD-WAN portfolio from Broadcom. This combination of innovations has the potential ', '["clm_wiki_arista-networks_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
