VALUES
  ('cs_assurant_history', 'org_assurant', 'overview', 'History',
   'American specialized insurance company Not to be confused with Asurion . Assurant, Inc. Trade name Assurant [1] Formerly Fortis, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : AIZ S&amp;P 500 component Industry Insurance Founded 1892 &#59;&#32;134 years ago ( 1892 ) Headquarters Atlanta , Georgia , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Keith W. Demmings ( president &amp; CEO ) [2] Products Home insurance renters'' insurance manufactured housing flood insurance credit insurance extended service contracts Services Risk management Revenue US$ 11.9 billion (2024) Operating income US$927 million (2024) Net income US$760 million (2024) Total assets US$35.0 billion (2024) Total equity US$5.11 billion (2024) Number of employees 14,200 (2024) Website assurant Footnotes [3] Assurant, Inc. [1] is a global provider of risk management products and services [4] with headquarters in Atlanta . [3] Its businesses provide a diverse set of specialty, niche-market insurance products in the property, casualty, extended device protection, and preneed insurance sectors. The company''s main operating segments are Global Housing and Global Lifestyle. [3] The company, formerly known as Fortis, Inc., was spun off from Dutch and Belgian financial-services company Fortis Insurance N.V. in 2004. The company''s initial public offering on Feb. 5, 2004 at $1.76 billion was the fourth largest that year. In connection with the public offering, the company changed its name to Assurant, Inc. [5] [6] Assurant is 325 on the Fortune 500 list of the largest companies in the United States by revenue as of 2022. [7] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "ASSURANT - Trademark Details" . Justia Trademarks . Retrieved February 17, 2026 . ^ "Management Committee, President and CEO Keith Demmings" . Archived from the original on 2022-01-04 . Retrieved 2022-01-04 . ^ a b c "Assurant, Inc. 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 20, 2025 . Retrieved March 4, 2025 . ^ Frankel, Daniel. "Comcast chooses Assurant for mobile phone protection plans | FierceCable" . www . Archived from the original on 18 July 2017 . Retrieved 26 July 2017 . ^ "Dutch insurer Amev is buying VSB Groep NV bank for..." tribunedigital-chicagotribune . Retrieved 2017-07-12 . ^ Gelsi, Steve. "Assurant''s debut leads IPO quintet" . MarketWatch . Retrieved 2017-07-12 . ^ "Assurant" . Fortune . Archived from the original on 2019-08-07 . Retrieved 2022-06-04 .', '["clm_wiki_assurant_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
