VALUES
  ('cs_atmos-energy_history', 'org_atmos-energy', 'overview', 'History',
   'American energy company Atmos Energy Corporation Type Public Traded as NYSE : ATO DJUA component S&amp;P 500 component Industry Energy Founded 1906 &#59;&#32;120 years ago ( 1906 ) Headquarters Dallas, Texas , U.S. Key people J. Kevin Akers (President and CEO) Kim R Cocklin (Executive Chairman of the Board) Charles K Vaughan (Founder) Products Natural gas Revenue US$ 2.82 billion (2020) [1] Operating income US$824.1 million (2020) [2] Net income US$601.4 million (2020) [2] Total assets US$15.36 billion (2020) [2] Total equity US$6.79 billion (2020) [2] Number of employees 5,019 (September 2023) Website atmosenergy Atmos Energy Corporation , headquartered in Dallas, Texas , is one of the United States'' largest natural-gas-only distributors, [3] serving about three million natural gas distribution customers in over 1,400 communities in nine states [4] from the Blue Ridge Mountains in the East to the Rocky Mountains in the West. &#91; citation needed &#93; Atmos Energy also manages company-owned natural gas pipeline and storage assets, including one of the largest intrastate natural gas pipeline systems in Texas. [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Atmos Energy Corporation 10K" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved September 25, 2015 . ^ a b c d "Atmos Energy Corporation 10K" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved September 25, 2015 . ^ "Atmos Energy | Best Southwest Partnership, TX" . www . Retrieved 2018-02-14 . ^ "Atmos Energy, Form 8-K, Current Report, Filing Date Jan 3, 2013" . secdatabase . Retrieved Jan 16, 2013 . ^ "Advises Atmos Energy Corporation" . Shearman &amp; Sterling . Archived from the original on 2023-12-25 . Retrieved 2018-02-14 .', '["clm_wiki_atmos-energy_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
