VALUES
  ('cs_atmos-energy_leadership', 'org_atmos-energy', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Utility Operations Colorado-Kansas Division Formerly Greeley Gas, acquired 1993; [1] added Kansas units of United Cities Gas in 1999 [2] Kentucky/Mid-States Division Western Kentucky Gas Company acquired 1989 from Texas American Energy; [3] United Cities Gas acquired 1997 [4] Louisiana Division Trans Louisiana Gas acquired 1988, Louisiana Gas Service acquired 2001 from Citizens Utilities [5] Mid-Tex Division Formerly Lone Star Gas and TXU Gas, acquired 2004 [6] Mississippi Division Formerly Mississippi Valley Gas, acquired 2001 [7] West Texas Division Formerly Amarillo Gas, Pioneer Natural Gas, and Energas ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Atmos to acquire Greeley. (Atmos Energy; Greeley Gas)" . The Oil Daily . 1993-03-30. Archived from the original on 2015-03-29 . Retrieved 2015-02-27 . ^ United Cities gets new name ^ "Texas firm purchases Western Kentucky Gas" . Kentucky New Era . 1987-06-30. pp. 13– . Retrieved 2015-02-27 . ^ Atmos Energy completes merger with United Cities Gas ^ Atmos Picks Up Citizens'' Louisiana Distribution Assets ^ Turner, Tyya N. (2005). "TXU Corp.". Vault Guide to the Top Energy &amp; Oil/gas Employers . Vault Inc. pp. 173– 179. ISBN 9781581313185 . ^ Atmos Energy to buy Mississippi Valley Gas for $150 million', '["clm_wiki_atmos-energy_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
