VALUES
  ('cs_biogen_leadership', 'org_biogen', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '2000s In 2003, Biogen merged with San Diego, California -based IDEC Pharmaceuticals (formed in 1985 by University of California-San Diego ''s physicians and immunologists Ivor Royston and Robert E. Sobol, San Diego bio entrepreneur Howard Birndorf , and Stanford University cancer researchers Ron Levy and Richard Miller) and adopted the name Biogen Idec. [1] [2] After the merger, Biogen Idec became the 3rd largest Biotechnology company in the world. [3] Following shifts in research core areas, the company has since shortened its name, reverting to simply Biogen. [4] In May 2006, the company announced it would acquire cancer specialist, Conforma Therapeutics for $250 million. [5] Later in the same month, the company announced its intention to acquire Fumapharm AG, consolidating ownership of Fumaderm and BG-12 , an oral fumarate , which was being studied for the treatment of multiple sclerosis and psoriasis . [6] In January 2007, the company announced it would acquire Syntonix Pharmaceuticals for up to $120 million, gaining Syntonix''s lead product for hemophilia B as well as the technology for developing inhalable treatments. [7] [8] [9] In 2008, two new brain infection cases from Tysabri users surfaced in Europe that raised international concern about Tysabri and its effects with the progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML) brain condition. Biogen is one of the drug''s producers. [10] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "The San Diego Technology Archive" . Libraries . Retrieved 2026-07-30 . ^ "Biogen and IDEC Pharmaceuticals Announce Merger To Create a New Biotechnology Industry Leader" . Exhibit 99.1 . Retrieved 1 December 2018 . IDEC — Founded in 1985 to develop monoclonal antibodies. Founders include Ivor Royston, Howard Birndorf, Richard Miller and Brook Byers ^ Pollack, Andrew (2003-06-24). "Idec to Merge With Biogen in $6.8 Billion Deal" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Retrieved 2026-07-30 . ^ Dulaney, Chelsey (2015-03-23). "Biogen Drops Idec From Name" . Wall St', '["clm_wiki_biogen_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
