  ('cs_brown-brown_operations', 'org_brown-brown', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History Brown &amp; Brown was founded in 1939 as a small insurance agency in Daytona Beach, Florida, by J. Adrian Brown, partnering with his cousin Charles "Cov" Owen. [1] Originally named Brown &amp; Owen , the firm quickly expanded its customer base in central Florida. [2] J. Adrian''s son, J. Hyatt Brown , joined the agency in 1959, bought the company and became CEO in 1961, and played a key role in its growth and modernization. [3] [1] In 1980, Brown &amp; Brown restructured to adopt a decentralized model, aiming to boost revenue and profit margins by giving more authority to local teams. This approach encouraged an entrepreneurial culture across the company. [4] In 1983, the firm changed its name to Brown &amp; Brown, Inc. to reflect its focus on national expansion. In 1993, the company merged with Poe &amp; Associates. [1] Also in 1993, the company went public, listing on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker symbol BRO. [5] The use of public stock for acquisitions enabled a deliberate expansion strategy focused on acquiring middle-market insurance brokers nationwide. [1] J. Hyatt Brown retired as CEO in 2009, but remains with the company as chairman. He was succeeded as CEO by his son J. Powell Brown. [1] Subsequently, the company has pursued aggressive acquisition strategies and organic growth. It surpassed $1 billion in revenue in 2012. [1] It joined the S&amp;P 500 index in 2021. [6] In 2021, new headquarters were completed at Daytona Beach, Florida, featuring an 11-story building on 13 acres facing the Halifax River. [7] In 2021, Brown &amp; Brown was added to the S&amp;P 500 index following an announcement by S&amp;P Dow Jones Indices , effective September 20, 2021. [8] In 2022, Brown &amp; Brown was added to the S&amp;P 500 Dividend Aristocrats Index, which includes S&amp;P 500 companies that have increased their dividend payments for at least 25 consecutive years. [9] In 2023, Brown &amp; Brown received the Platinum Bell Seal for Workplace Mental', '["clm_wiki_brown-brown_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
