VALUES
  ('cs_builders-firstsource_operations', 'org_builders-firstsource', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History In 1998, private investment firm JLL Partners acquired Builders'' Supply and Lumber Company from the Pulte Corporation, forming Builders FirstSource. Over the next five years the company acquired 23 companies and grew revenue to $2 billion. The company was taken public in 2005 and began trading on the NYSE. [1] [2] In 2015, Builders FirstSource acquired ProBuild . [3] This acquisition resulted in a combined entity with $6.1 billion in combined 2014 revenue and over 430 locations across 40 states. In 2018, the revenue of the combined company was $7.7 Billion. [4] In December 2019, Builders FirstSource acquired Raney Components, LLC and Raney Construction, Inc, [5] located in Groveland, Florida .This business unit now operates under the name Florida Construction Services. [6] In January 2020, Builders FirstSource acquired Bianchi &amp; Company, Inc, [7] a millwork supplier and install company located in Charlotte, North Carolina , and TW Perry, a Maryland-Based Building Materials Distributor. [8] In August 2020, Builders FirstSource announced a merger with BMC Stock Holdings in an all-stock deal valued at approximately $2.5 billion. [9] [10] The merger combined two of the largest U.S. building materials distributors and created a company with more than $11 billion in annual sales, approximately 26,000 employees, and a network of about 550 distribution and manufacturing locations across more than 40 U.S. states. [11] The deal was completed in January 2021, at which point it was announced that former BMC president and CEO Dave Flitman would be appointed CEO following a 90-day transition period. Following the closing, the combined company retained the Builders FirstSource branding. [12] In April 2021, Flitman became CEO, succeeding Chad Crow who had served in that role from 2017 until his retirement that year. [9] Also in 2021, Builders FirstSource acquired the parent company of Alliance Lumber, the largest independently operated supplier of building materials in ', '["clm_wiki_builders-firstsource_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
