VALUES
  ('cs_cadence-design-systems_leadership', 'org_cadence-design-systems', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1983–1999 Founded in 1983 in San Jose, California , [1] Cadence Design Systems began as an electronic design automation (EDA) company named Solomon Design Automation (SDA). [2] SDA''s cofounders included James Solomon , Richard Newton , [2] and Alberto Sangiovanni-Vincentelli . [2] [3] Cadence was formed by the merger of SDA and ECAD . A public company, [2] ECAD had been co-founded by Ping Chao, Glen Antle, and Paul Huang in 1982. [2] &#91; failed verification &#93; Cadence Design Systems was officially formed through the 1988 merger of SDA and ECAD, [2] with Joseph Costello appointed both CEO and president of the newly combined company. After the merger, Cadence began trading on the New York Stock Exchange and Costello oversaw further mergers and acquisitions. [2] In 1989, the company acquired Gateway Design Automation for $72 million. [4] In 1990 it acquired Automated Systems Inc., and in doing so added "board design to its existing line of chip design software." [5] In 1991, Cadence acquired its rival Valid Logic Systems for around $200 million, its biggest acquisition yet. The revenues of the combined company were $390 million, according to the New York Times. [2] In 1996, Cadence acquired High Level Design Systems, [6] at which point Cadence had 3,300 employees and $742 million in annual revenue. Following the resignation of Cadence''s original CEO Joe Costello in 1997, Jack Harding was appointed CEO. [7] Ray Bingham was named CEO in 1999. [8] Cadence purchased Ambit Design Systems for $260 million, which made tools for system-on-a-chip technology, in 1998, [9] and OrCAD Systems in 1999. [10] Cadence acquired Quickturn Design Systems in 1999, preventing a hostile takeover attempt by Mentor Graphics . [11] ^ Cite error: The named reference OriginalRef_Sorkin_nytim was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b c d e f g h NYTimes A Fun Chief at Cadence Is Serious Merger Man Retrieved October 4, 1991 ^ body:not( ):not( ) Bailey, Brian (December 20, 2017)', '["clm_wiki_cadence-design-systems_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
