  ('cs_carnival_history', 'org_carnival', 'overview', 'History',
   'Anglo-American global cruise operating company Carnival Corporation Ltd. Carnival Place, Doral, Florida Type Public Traded as NYSE : CCL ISIN BMG2004J1036 Industry Hospitality , tourism Predecessors Carnival Cruise Line (an existing subsidiary; Carnival Corporation) P&amp;O Princess Cruises (Carnival plc) Incorporated Bermuda Founded 1972 &#59;&#32;54 years ago ( 1972 ) (as Carnival Cruise Line, now a subsidiary) 1993 &#59;&#32;33 years ago ( 1993 ) (as Carnival Corporation) 2003 &#59;&#32;23 years ago ( 2003 ) (as Carnival Corporation &amp; plc) May 7, 2026 &#59;&#32;3 months ago ( 2026-05-07 ) (as Carnival Corporation Ltd.) Founder Ted Arison (for the Carnival Cruise Line) Headquarters Carnival Place, Doral, Florida , United States Area served Worldwide Key people Micky Arison (Chairman) Josh Weinstein (President and CEO) Brands AIDA Cruises Carnival Cruise Line Costa Cruises Cunard Line Holland America Line P&amp;O Cruises Princess Cruises Seabourn Services Cruise line Revenue US$26.622 billion (2025) Operating income US$4.483 billion (2025) Net income US$2.760 billion (2025) Total assets US$51.687 billion (2025) Total equity US$12.284 billion (2025) Number of employees 101,000 (2025) Website www Footnotes [1] [2] [3] [4] [5] Carnival Corporation Ltd. is a Bermuda-domiciled American cruise line operator that owns more than 90 vessels across eight brands. [5] [6] Carnival is listed on the New York Stock Exchange , [7] and is a component of the S&amp;P 500 index. [8] From 2003 to May 7, 2026, Carnival was a dual-listed company , consisting of U.S.-based and British corporations collectively known as Carnival Corporation &amp; plc . Carnival Corporation''s operational headquarters are in Doral, Florida . [9] Carnival also has significant UK operations, with regional headquarters in Southampton , England. [10] [11] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Mission &amp; History" . Carnival Corporation &amp; PLC. Archived from the original on August 29, 2018 . Retrieved July 21, 2015 . ^ Cite error: The named reference P&amp;Odeal was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ "Corporate Timeline" . Carnival Corporation &amp; plc. Archived from the original on December 4, 2015 . Retrieved July 21, 2015 . ^ "Form 10-K 2024/25" (PDF) . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved January 27, 2026 . ^ a b "Our Brands" . Carnival Corporation &amp; plc . Retrieved March 14, 2023 . ^ Cite error: The named reference unification-complete-pr was invoked but never defined (s', '["clm_wiki_carnival_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
