VALUES
  ('cs_caseys_history', 'org_caseys', 'overview', 'History',
   'American convenience store chain This article is about the American convenience store chain. For other uses, see Casey (disambiguation) . html body This article relies excessively on references to primary sources . Please improve this article by adding secondary or tertiary sources . Find sources: "Casey''s" – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR ( February 2018 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Casey''s General Stores, Inc. Casey''s current logo since October 2020 Trade name Casey''s Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : CASY S&amp;P 500 component Industry Retail Founded 1968 &#59;&#32;58 years ago ( 1968 ) in Boone, Iowa , U.S. Founder Donald Lamberti Headquarters Ankeny, Iowa , U.S. Number of locations 2,920 (FY April 2026) Area served Midwestern and Southern United States Key people Darren Rebelez ( Chairman ) Darren Rebelez ( President &amp; CEO ) Steven Bramlage ( CFO ) Products Pizza Coffee Wings Prepared foods Gasoline Beverages Snacks Dairy products Salads Services Convenience store Gas station Fast food Revenue US$ 15.94 billion (FY APR 30 2025) Operating income US$ 712.44 million (FY APR 30 2019) Net income US$ 546.52 million (FY APR 30 2025) Total assets US$ 8.21 billion (FY APR 30 2025) Total equity US$ 3.50 billion (FY APR 30 2025) Number of employees 23,338 (full-time) 25,934 (part-time) 49,272 (total) (FY APR 30 2025) Website www Footnotes [1] Casey''s General Stores, Inc. ( doing business as Casey''s ) is a chain of convenience stores in the Midwestern and Southern United States . The company is headquartered in Ankeny, Iowa , a suburb of Des Moines . [2] As of May 1, 2026, Casey''s has 2,950 stores in 19 states. Following 7-Eleven ''s purchase of Speedway , Casey''s is the third-largest convenience store chain in the United States (after 7-Eleven and Circle K / Couche-Tard ) and the largest that is wholly American-owned. [3] It is one of two Iowa-based Fortune 500 companies. [4] Casey''s is famous for their pizza , including a breakfast pizza and a taco pizza, resulting in Casey''s being the fifth largest pizza chain in the U.S. [5] [6] Exterior of a Casey''s in Farragut, Tennessee ^ body:not( ):not( ) "US SEC: Form 10-K Casey''s General Stores, Inc" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved August 5, 2019 . ^ "Casey''s General Stores" . Fortune . Archived from the original on March 21, 2019 . Retrieved December 28, 2018 . ^ "Top 202 Convenience Stores 2024" . CSP Daily News . Retrieved July 30, 2024 . ^ "Visualize the Fortune', '["clm_wiki_caseys_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
