VALUES
  ('cs_baxter_operations', 'org_baxter', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Philanthropy In 2008, Baxter launched Science@Work: Expanding Minds with Real-World Science, which supports teacher training and student development in healthcare and biotechnology in Chicago Public Schools. [1] &#58;&#8202;17&#8202; In 2013, the company was included in The Civic 50, a list of the most community-minded companies in America from The National Conference on Citizenship and Points of Light, published by Bloomberg. [2] In 2014, roughly 6,300 Baxter employees volunteered in their communities through The Baxter International Foundation''s Dollars for Doers program, addressing local concerns such as healthcare, the environment and education. [3] &#58;&#8202;104&#8202; In 2014, Baxter and The Baxter International Foundation gave over $50 million. [4] Baxter was included for the 13th year in Corporate Responsibility magazine''s 100 Best Corporate Citizens list in 2014 for its social responsibility performance. [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Education and Critical Community Needs" (PDF) , Baxter , Baxter sustainability report, 2015, archived from the original (PDF) on September 11, 2015 , retrieved October 18, 2015 ^ "The Civic 50 website, 2013 results" . Civic50 . Archived from the original on July 6, 2014 . Retrieved July 16, 2017 . ^ "Employee Involvement" (PDF) , Baxter , Baxter sustainability report, 2015, archived from the original (PDF) on September 11, 2015 , retrieved October 18, 2015 ^ "Community Support" (PDF) , Baxter , Baxter sustainability report, 2015, archived from the original (PDF) on September 11, 2015 , retrieved October 18, 2015 ^ "Press Room: Press Releases – Baxter" . www.Baxter . June 2014. Archived from the original on June 3, 2015 . Retrieved July 16, 2017 .', '["clm_wiki_baxter_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 504. Cboe Global Markets (slug=cboe-global-markets, wiki='Cboe Global Markets')
