VALUES
  ('cs_ciena_operations', 'org_ciena', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisitions Company acquired Year AstraCom Inc. 1997 ATI Telecom International Ltd. 1998 Terabit Technology Inc. 1998 Lightera Networks Inc. 1999 Omnia Communications Inc. 1999 Cyras Corp. 2001 ONI Systems 2002 WaveSmith Networks Inc. 2003 Akara Corp. 2003 Catena Networks 2004 Internet Photonics 2004 World Wide Packets Inc. 2008 Nortel Metro Ethernet Networks 2010 Cyan 2015 TeraXion Inc. 2016 Packet Design 2016 DonRiver 2018 Centina Systems 2019 Nubis Communications 2025 Ciena acquired the telecommunications company AstraCom Inc. in 1997 for $13.1 million. Fourteen of AstraCom''s engineers signed four-year contracts with Ciena, and joined the company''s new research and development team in Alpharetta, Georgia . [1] In early 1998, the company acquired Norcross, Georgia –based ATI Telecom International Ltd. and its subsidiary Alta Telecom in a transaction worth $52.5 million. Alta''s engineering and installation products were used by service providers for switching, transport, and wireless communications; the company continued to operate as a subsidiary of Ciena. [2] [3] [4] Ciena purchased Terabit Technology Inc., a producer of detectors for data transmission based in Santa Barbara, California , [5] for $11.7 million in April 1998. [6] The company acquired Cupertino, California –based Lightera Networks Inc. and Marlborough, Massachusetts –based Omnia Communications Inc. for $980 million in stock in 1999. [7] [8] The company purchased Cyras Corp. of Fremont, California , during 2000 to 2001 for $2 billion in stock. [9] [10] ONI Systems, a San Jose, California –based producer of phone and computer data equipment, was acquired by Ciena for $900 million in stock in June 2002. [11] [12] [13] The acquisitions of Cyras, which produced optical switch systems, and ONI, which made transport equipment for data transfer, allowed Ciena to focus on networks in metropolitan areas. [14] Ciena purchased WaveSmith Networks Inc., an optical-networking equipment manufacturer based in Acto', '["clm_wiki_ciena_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
