VALUES
  ('cs_expedia_history', 'org_expedia', 'overview', 'History',
   'American travel technology company Expedia Group, Inc. Former headquarters of Expedia Group in Bellevue, Washington . Formerly Expedia, Inc. Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : EXPE S&amp;P 500 component ISIN US65248E2037 Industry Travel technology Predecessor Liberty Expedia Holdings Founded October 22, 1996 &#59;&#32;29 years ago ( 1996-10-22 ) Founder Rich Barton Headquarters Seattle, Washington , United States Key people Barry Diller ( chairman and senior executive ) Ariane Gorin ( vice chairman and CEO ) Products Expedia Hotels Vrbo Travelocity Hotwire Orbitz Ebookers CheapTickets CarRentals Expedia Cruises Wotif Trivago Expedia Group Media Solutions Expedia Group Partner Solutions Revenue US$ 13.69 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.319 billion (2024) Net income US$1.234 billion (2024) Total assets US$22.39 billion (2024) Total equity US$2.799 billion (2024) Number of employees 16,500 (2024) Parent Microsoft (1996–1999) Website expediagroup Footnotes [1] Expedia Group, Inc. is an American travel technology company that owns and operates travel fare aggregators and travel metasearch engines , including Expedia , Hotels , Vrbo , Travelocity , Hotwire , Orbitz , Ebookers, CheapTickets , CarRentals , Expedia Cruises , Wotif , and Trivago . [1] Over 3.5 million lodging facilities and flights on over 500 airlines are bookable on the company''s websites. [1] It has 16,500 employees, and its headquarters are located in Seattle , Washington . The word "Expedia" is derived from a combination of "exploration" and "speed". [2] The company is listed on Nasdaq under the ticker symbol EXPE. ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) "Expedia Group, Inc. 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 7, 2025. ^ Staff, KOMO News (October 7, 2019). "New Expedia Seattle HQ welcomes first new employees" . KOMO . Retrieved January 8, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_expedia_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
