  ('cs_lennox_history', 'org_lennox', 'overview', 'History',
   'American climate control product manufacturer Lennox International Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : LII S&amp;P 500 component Industry HVAC Founded 1895 &#59;&#32;131 years ago ( 1895 ) Founder Dave Lennox Headquarters Richardson, Texas , U.S. Key people Alok Maskara (CEO) Revenue US$ 5.34 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.03 billion (2024) Net income US$807 million (2024) Total assets US$3.47 billion (2024) Total equity US$850 million (2024) Owner John W. Norris, III (9.8%) Number of employees 14,200 (2024) Website lennox Footnotes [1] A Lennox air conditioner Lennox International Inc. is an American provider of climate control products for the heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) and refrigeration markets. [1] Based in Richardson, Texas , the company is 9.8% owned by John W. Norris, III, a descendant of DW Norris , who acquired the company in 1904. The company''s largest production facilities are in Saltillo, Mexico , Marshalltown, Iowa , and Orangeburg, South Carolina . [1] ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) "Lennox International Inc. 2024 Form 10-K Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 11, 2025.', '["clm_wiki_lennox_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
