  ('cs_lennox_leadership', 'org_lennox', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisitions and divestitures In 1971, the company sold its low pressure gas cylinder business to Worthington Industries . [1] In 1973, Lennox acquired Heatcraft, including the Larkin, Bohn, Chandler, and Climate Control brands. [2] In 1998, the company acquired Pyro Industries, a manufacturer of pellet stoves . [3] In December 2010, the company acquired Kysor/Warren from The Manitowoc Company for $138 million. [4] In September 2023, the company sold its European commercial HVAC and refrigeration businesses to funds managed by Syntagma Capital. [5] In October 2023, the company acquired AES. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Gearino, Dan (17 May 2013). "Worthington Industries expands with oil, gas boom" . The Columbus Dispatch . ^ "Lennox International Acquires Heatcraft" . Mergr . ^ Wilhelm, Steve (August 16, 1998). "Pellet-stove pioneer is bought by Texas giant" . American City Business Journals . ^ "Lennox Acquires Kysor/Warrenfrom Manitowoc" . Endeavor Business Media . December 15, 2010. ^ "Lennox Announces Agreement to Sell European Commercial HVAC and Refrigeration Businesses" (Press release). PR Newswire . September 21, 2023. ^ "Lennox Acquires AES to Expand Commercial HVAC Services" (Press release). PR Newswire . October 25, 2023.', '["clm_wiki_lennox_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
