  ('cs_mccormick_operations', 'org_mccormick', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Research and development In February 2019, McCormick announced that it worked with IBM to build an artificial intelligence (AI) system to analyze decades of data to develop new flavor combinations and seasoning mixes. [1] The company brought its first AI-developed line of seasoning mixes to market in 2019, which were called "One" for making one-dish meals. ^ body:not( ):not( ) Metz, Rachel (February 5, 2019). "The world''s biggest spice company is using AI to find new flavors" . CNN . Retrieved February 5, 2019 .', '["clm_wiki_mccormick_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 521. Motorola Solutions (slug=motorola-solutions, wiki='Motorola Solutions')
