VALUES
  ('cs_motorola-solutions_leadership', 'org_motorola-solutions', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisitions In January 2014, the company announced its acquisition of Twisted Pair Solutions, a provider of push-to-talk over broadband applications for secure, real-time communication on any device. [1] Twisted Pair created an integrated communications system that allows different devices (smartphones, tablets, and PCs) to talk to each other in business, public safety, and military applications. [1] In February 2015, the company acquired Emergency CallWorks, a provider of Next-Generation 9-1-1 ( NG9-1-1 ) call-taking software for public safety. The company developed technology that consolidates information from multiple 911 calls reporting the same emergency into a single source that can be shared with emergency professionals. [2] In April of that year, it acquired PublicEngines, a crime analysis firm. [3] [4] The company is based in Utah and provides cloud-based solutions for data analytics of crime, predictive policing strategies, and citizen engagement. [3] In February 2016, the company completed its acquisition of Airwave Solutions , the UK-based operator of the British public safety radio network responsible for providing mission-critical voice and data communications to more than 300 emergency and public service agencies comprising police, fire, rescue and ambulance services across England, Scotland, and Wales. [5] In November 2016, the company completed acquisition of Spillman Technologies, which produces law enforcement and public safety software solutions for computer-aided dispatch (CAD) and records management systems (RMS). [6] In March, 2017, Motorola Solutions acquired Interexport SA. [7] In August 2017, Motorola Solutions announced it completed the acquisition of Kodiak Networks, a privately held provider of broadband push-to-talk (PTT) for commercial customers. [8] Its clients included AT&amp;T , Vodafone , KPN , Verizon , Telefónica , Bell Canada , and Vivo . [9] In March 2018, Motorola Solutions acquired Avigilon , a Canadian manufacturer of video', '["clm_wiki_motorola-solutions_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
