VALUES
  ('cs_supermicro_leadership', 'org_supermicro', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Corporate affairs Board of directors As of March 2026, Supermicro''s board of directors consists of co-founder Charles Liang, co-founder Sara Liu, Tally Liu, Sherman Tuan, Judy Lin, Robert Blair, Susie Giordano, and Scott Angel. [1] Giordano joined the board in August 2024 and served as the only member of Supermicro''s special committee to oversee an internal audit of concerns raised by EY. [2] In April 2025, the company''s former senior vice president of corporate development, Yitai Hu, became its chief legal officer, serving as Supermicro''s general counsel. [2] In March 2026, DeAnna Luna was promoted to the role of chief compliance officer at the company. [3] Financials On March 8, 2007, Supermicro raised $64 million in an initial public offering , selling 8 million shares at $8 a share. [4] Supermicro''s stock trades under the ticker symbol SMCI [5] on the Nasdaq exchange. In 2009, Supermicro sold about $720 million worth of computer servers and related products and employed almost 1,100 people. [6] By the end of 2023, the company had reported a fiscal year 2023 revenue of $7.1 billion and employed over 5,000 workers globally. [7] Supermicro replaced Whirlpool in the S&amp;P 500 after a large rally in the company''s stock lifted its market cap from $4.5B at the end of 2022 to $60B in March 2024. [8] [9] [10] In June 2024, Supermicro made its debut on the Fortune 500 list, reaching number 498. [11] By 2025, the company had climbed 206 spots, earning the 292nd position on the list. [12] On July 22, 2024, Supermicro became a Nasdaq-100 company, replacing Walgreens Boots Alliance in the index. [13] Supermicro was removed from the index in December 2024. [14] In June 2026, Supermicro raised $7 billion "through a series of equity and equity-linked financing transactions" to fund the purchasing of components related to demand for its AI servers. The components used will fulfill orders worth $39 billion. [15] Additionally, in Supermicro''s fiscal third quarter of 2026, the com', '["clm_wiki_supermicro_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
