VALUES
  ('cs_wabtec_leadership', 'org_wabtec', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Mergers and acquisitions Examples of notable mergers and acquisitions by Wabtec include: April 1998 - RFS Industries for $10 million, rebranding it to Wabtec Rail UK. [1] [2] March 2010 - Xorail, railway signaling design and construction company, for $40 million [3] [4] July 2010 - G&amp;B Specialties, track products manufacturer, for $31.8 million [5] August 2010 - Bach-Simpson Corporation, locomotive component supplier for $12.0 million [6] November 2010 - Swiger Coil Systems, Cleveland -based manufacturer of traction motors and electric coils, for approximately $43.0 million [7] February 2011 - Brush Traction , English locomotive builder and maintainer, for $31 million [8] [9] November 2011 - Bearward Engineering, English industrial radiator manufacturer [10] June 2012 - Mors Smitt Holding for $88.4 million [11] October 2012 - LH Group, diesel engine, transmission and bogie overhaul and industrial locomotive supplier for $48 million June 2014 - Fandstan Electric Group, rail and industrial equipment manufacturer, comprising the Brecknell Willis, Stemmann Technik and TransTech brands for $199.4 million [12] June 2015 - Metalocaucho (MTC), producer of suspension and anti-vibration systems for $23.4 million [13] December 2016 - acquired 51% of Faiveley Transport ''s shares in a cash-and-stock deal valued at $1.7 billion, including debt [14] [15] [16] August 2014 - Dia-Frag, manufacturer of friction products including motorcycle braking, for $70.6 million. [12] October 2015 - Track IQ , lineside sensor manufacturer [17] February 2019 - GE Transportation for $11 billion January 2022 - Masu, New Delhi-based railway friction company, for $34 million [18] [19] April 2022 - Trimble’s Beena Vision business [20] June 2022 - Collins Aerospace ARINC rail solutions [21] June 2023 - L&amp;M Radiator, heat exchanger manufacturer in Hibbing, Minnesota [22] July 2025 - Evident''s Inspection Technologies for $1.78 billion [23] [24] December 2025 - Frauscher Sensor Technology Group, Sc', '["clm_wiki_wabtec_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
