   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_wabtec_operations', 'org_wabtec', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Merger with GE Transportation On April 20, 2018, it was reported that General Electric (GE), undergoing a strategic review, was in talks to sell its century-old locomotive business, GE Transportation , to Wabtec, according to people familiar with the matter. [1] On May 21, 2018, GE and Wabtec confirmed the merger of GE Transportation with Wabtec in an $11 billion deal, completed on February 25, 2019, which saw Wabtec shareholders take a 50.8% shareholding in the merged company, with GE shareholders owning 24.3% and GE itself 24.9%. [2] [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "GE Is in Talks to Unload Rail Business in Deal With Wabtec" . Bloomberg Business. April 20, 2018 . Retrieved April 21, 2018 . ^ "GE to Merge Rail Division With Wabtec in $11 Billion Deal" . Wall Street Journal . May 21, 2018 . Retrieved May 21, 2018 . ^ Wabtec and GE Transportation complete merger Archived August 1, 2020, at the Wayback Machine Railway Gazette International February 25, 2019', '["clm_wiki_wabtec_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
