VALUES
  ('cs_zimmer-biomet_operations', 'org_zimmer-biomet', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History Exton, Pennsylvania office EMEA-Office in Winterthur , Switzerland Zimmer Biomet was established in 1927 by Justin O. Zimmer (1884–1951) [1] in Warsaw, Indiana. [2] [3] On April 24, 2014, it was announced that Zimmer had agreed to purchase Biomet Inc. for $13.4 billion. [4] In October 2014, however, it was announced that the EU''s antitrust regulators had opened an extensive investigation into Zimmer''s bid for Biomet due to concern that it would substantially lessen competition in certain markets. [5] In March 2016, European Commission (“EC”) conditionally cleared Zimmer''s proposed acquisition of Biomet, Inc. [6] [7] and on June 24, 2015, Zimmer completed its acquisition of Biomet forming Zimmer Biomet Holdings. [8] In October 2014, the company announced it would acquire ETEX Holdings, Inc. [9] [10] In March 2016, Zimmer Biomet announced it would acquire Ortho Transmission, LLC. [11] The company also announced it would acquire sports medicine company, Cayenne Medical, Inc. [12] [13] Later in the same year the company acquired medical device manufacturer, LDR Holding Corporation for $37 per share ($1 billion in total), [14] merging it into their Spine division. [15] [16] In July, the company acquired French surgical robotics company Medtech. [17] In August, the company announced it was acquiring Delaware-based CD Diagnostics, [18] a diagnostics company developing immunoassays and biomarker testing. [19] In September, Zimmer announced the acquisition of Clinical Graphics, B.V. [20] The Justin Zimmer House in Warsaw is listed on the National Register of Historic Places . [21] In January 2023, the company announced its intention to acquire Embody, Inc. for $155 million (plus a potential $120 million in milestones). [22] In August 2024, Zimmer Biomet announced plans to acquire OrthoGrid Systems , an AI surgical guidance company, in order to expand its market share in hip replacement procedures. [23] [24] In 2026, Zimmer Biomet acquired the iovera pain therapy busi', '["clm_wiki_zimmer-biomet_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 531. UBS (slug=ubs, wiki='UBS')
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_ubs_overview', 'org_ubs', 'overview', 'Overview',
   'UBS Group AG is a Swiss multinational investment bank and financial services firm founded and based in Switzerland, with headquarters in both Zurich and Basel. It holds a strong foothold in all major financial centres as the largest Swiss banking institution and the world''s largest private bank. UBS manages the largest amount of private wealth in the world, counting approximately half of The World''s Billionaires among its clients, with over US$7 trillion in assets as of December 2025 (AUM). Based on international deal flow and political influence, the firm is considered one of the "biggest, most powerful financial institutions in the world". UBS is also a leading market maker and one of the eight global ''bulge bracket'' investment banks. Due to its large presence across the Americas, EMEA and Asia–Pacific markets, the Financial Stability Board considers it a global systemically important bank and UBS is widely considered to be the largest and most sophisticated "truly global investment bank" in the world, given its market-leading positions in every major financial centre globally.', '["clm_wiki_ubs_overview"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   10, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_ubs_history', 'org_ubs', 'overview', 'History',
   'Competition UBS and Credit Suisse branches next to each other in Zurich On a global scale, UBS competes with the largest global investment banks , [1] [2] particularly within the Bulge Bracket . [1] [3] and until acquiring Credit Suisse in 2023 was regularly compared against it. [4] [5] According to a 2018 study published by Coalition Research Institute, UBS was among the top 10 of the world''s investment banks. [6] In Switzerland: UBS competes with a number of cantonal banks , such as Zürcher Kantonalbank , Banque cantonale vaudoise and other cantonal banks, as well as Raiffeisen , PostFinance , and the Migros Bank . &#91; citation needed &#93; In Europe: UBS competes with several larger banks, such as Deutsche Bank , HSBC , Crédit agricole , BNP Paribas , Natixis , Royal Bank of Scotland , Santander and UniCredit . &#91; citation needed &#93; In the United States: UBS competes with the largest American banks, such as Citigroup , Bank of America , Goldman Sachs , JPMorgan Chase and Morgan Stanley . &#91; citation needed &#93; ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Morgan, Stephen (3 October 2016). "The Battle of the Bulge Bracket" . whartonmagazine . Archived from the original on 3 November 2018 . Retrieved 11 November 2013 . ^ Investopedia Staff (25 November 2003). "Bulge Bracket" . Investopedia . Archived from the original on 27 February 2021 . Retrieved 10 August 2018 . ^ Cite error: The named reference Divestopedia-2021 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ "FINMA details TBTF decrees" . FINMA . finma.ch. 7 May 2014. Archived from the original on 3 January 2021 . Retrieved 4 February 2018 . ^ "These Are the Best-Paying Investment Banks" . Institutional Investor . 11 August 2017. Archived from the original on 20 August 2020 . Retrieved 31 October 2018 . ^ "Investment Banking: UBS and CS Remain Among Top 10 – Just" . finews . Archived from the original on 24 February 2021 . Retrieved 4 February 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_ubs_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
