  ('cs_east-west-bank_operations', 'org_east-west-bank', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '2025 wildfire relief After the January 2025 Southern California wildfires , East West donated $250,000 to the Pasadena Community Foundation’s Eaton Fire Relief and Recovery Fund. [1] The bank contributed an additional $100,000 to the YMCA of Metropolitan Los Angeles, while the bank’s employees created their own relief fund with the company matching contributions. [2] East West’s donations to first responders and nonprofit organizations exceeded $1 million, as of August 2025. [3] For customers, East West activated a “Skip-a-Pay” program, allowing affected homeowners to delay mortgage payments. [4] The bank also partnered with major museums, foundations, and philanthropists to help launch the “LA Arts Community Fire Relief Fund,” which raised an initial $12 million to support artists and arts workers impacted by the fires. [5] [6] [7] East West has participated in United Way ’s WalkUnited LA. In July 2025, more than 500 East West-affiliated participants joined the walk, raising over $40,000. The bank pledged an additional $100,000 matching grant. East West’s other nonprofit partners include Gold House Foundation, Grameen America, Junior Achievement, Operation Hope, and San Gabriel Habitat for Humanity. [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Lenders Ready Funds, Make Large Donations | Los Angeles Business Journal" . 2025-01-20 . Retrieved 2025-06-25 . ^ "SoCal''s Top Banks and Credit Unions Focus on Community in Wake of Wildfires" . Los Angeles Times . 2025-03-23 . Retrieved 2025-06-25 . ^ a b Cite error: The named reference Turner was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ "Compiled Resources Available For Impacted Angelenos | Mayor Karen Bass" . mayor . 2025-01-10 . Retrieved 2025-06-25 . ^ Pogrebin, Robin (2025-01-15). "Arts Groups and Donors Create Fire Relief Fund for Los Angeles Artists" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Retrieved 2025-06-29 . ^ "Getty and other arts organisations launch $12m relief fund for victims of Los Angeles wildfires" . www . 2025-