  ('cs_atlantic-union-bank_history', 'org_atlantic-union-bank', 'overview', 'History',
   'American financial institution Atlantic Union Bankshares Corporation The bank''s logo Formerly Union Bank and Trust Company (1902–2010) First Market Bank (1997–2010) Union First Market Bank (2010–2015) Union Bank &amp; Trust (2015–2019) Type Public company Traded as NYSE : AUB Industry Financial services Predecessors Union Bank and Trust Company First Market Bank, FSB Founded 1902 &#59;&#32;124 years ago ( 1902 ) (as Union Bank And Trust Company) [1] November 4, 1997 &#59;&#32;28 years ago ( 1997-11-04 ) (as First Market Bank) [2] March 20, 2010 &#59;&#32;16 years ago ( 2010-03-20 ) (as Union First Market Bank) Headquarters Bowling Green, Virginia (1902–2010) Richmond, Virginia (1997–Present) Number of locations 190 branches (2026) Areas served Virginia Maryland North Carolina Key people Ronald L. Tillett ( chairperson ) John C. Asbury ( CEO ) Maria Tedesco ( President and COO ) Products Checking accounts , saving accounts , credit cards , loans Revenue US$ 1.345 billion (2024) Net income US$2.89 billion (2024) Total assets US$24.585 billion (2024) Total equity US$3.142 billion (2024) Number of employees 2,125 (2024) Website www Footnotes [3] Atlantic Union Bankshares Corporation is a bank holding company based in Richmond, Virginia and is the parent company of Atlantic Union Bank, a regional bank . It operates 190 branches in Virginia , Maryland , and North Carolina and is the largest bank headquartered in Virginia. [3] It is on the list of largest banks in the United States . It offers loans for automobiles, commercial real estate, construction, and housing as well as equipment financing and insurance products. [3] [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Union Bank and Trust Company (11579) - History" . Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation - BankFind Suite . Retrieved June 3, 2026 . ^ "Atlantic Union Bank (34589) - History" . Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation - BankFind Suite . Retrieved June 3, 2026 . ^ a b c "Atlantic Union Bankshares Corporation 2024 Form 10-K Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 27, 2025. ^ Ress, Dave (October 19, 2023). "Rising interest a boost for Atlantic Union bank depositors" . Richmond Times-Dispatch .', '["clm_wiki_atlantic-union-bank_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
