  ('cs_atlantic-union-bank_leadership', 'org_atlantic-union-bank', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Naming rights and sponsorships Atlantic Union Bank has naming rights for the Atlantic Union Bank Center , a multi-purpose arena on the James Madison University campus in Harrisonburg, Virginia as part of a ten-year name sponsorship agreement worth $2.25 million. [1] [2] The bank also has naming rights for the Atlantic Union Bank Pavilion in Portsmouth . [3] The bank has sponsored Drumstick Dash, a 5K run in Roanoke. [4] [5] as well as the 10K Mini run for children in Richmond. [6] [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "JMU Rebrands Arena After Sponsor Name Change" . Daily News-Record . May 22, 2019. ^ Mettlen, Shane (September 13, 2020). "JMU Bracing For Limited Debut In New Arena" . Daily News-Record . ^ "Portsmouth amphitheater undergoes name change" . WVEC . Hampton, Virginia . May 21, 2019. ^ Woods, Megan (November 19, 2019). "Atlantic Union Bank donates thousands to Drumstick Dash cause" . WSLS-TV . ^ Roshetko, Katey (November 25, 2019). "Race coordinators in Roanoke prepare for 14th annual Drumstick Dash" . WDBJ . ^ "Sports Backers Atlantic Union Bank 10K Mini Kids Run" . WTVR-TV . March 23, 2022. ^ "The 2023 Sports Backers Atlantic Union Bank 10K Mini Kids Run" . WTVR-TV . February 27, 2023.', '["clm_wiki_atlantic-union-bank_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
