VALUES
  ('cs_ww_history', 'org_ww', 'overview', 'History',
   'American health and weight loss firm This article is about the company. For the diet, see Weight Watchers (diet) . WW International, Inc. Formerly Weight Watchers (1963–2018) Type Public Traded as OTC Pink : WGHTQ Nasdaq : WW Founded May 15, 1963 &#59;&#32;63 years ago ( 1963-05-15 ) Queens , New York , U.S. Headquarters 675 Avenue of the Americas , 6th Floor New York , NY 10010 Key people Tara Comonte , President &amp; CEO Products Weight loss , Packaged foods , Exercise products Revenue $1.5 billion ( 2018 ) [1] Operating income $267.305 million ( 2017 ) [2] Net income $163.514 million ( 2017 ) [2] Total assets 1.246 billion ( 2017 ) [2] Total equity -1.015 billion ( 2017 ) [2] Number of employees 18,000 (as of 2017 &#91;update&#93; ) [2] Website weightwatchers WW International, Inc. , formerly Weight Watchers International, Inc. , is a global company headquartered in the U.S. that offers weight loss and maintenance, fitness, and mindset services such as the Weight Watchers comprehensive diet program . [3] Founded in 1963 by Queens , New York City homemaker Jean Nidetch , WW''s program has three options as of 2019: online via its mobile app and website, coaching online or by phone, or in-person meetings. [3] In 2018, the company rebranded to "WW" to reflect "its development from focusing on weight loss to overall health and wellness." [4] [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Treffis Team Staff. "Time to Sell Weight Watchers Stock?" . Forbes . Retrieved November 5, 2019 . ^ a b c d e Cite error: The named reference 10K2017 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b "What is Weight Watchers Diet?" . U.S. News &amp; World Report . Retrieved May 21, 2018. ^ Hope, Katie. "Weight Watchers drops ''weight'' from name" . BBC News . September 24, 2018. ^ Wahba, Phil (September 24, 2018). "What''s in a Name? Weight Watchers Changes Name to ''WW'' " . Fortune . ( registration required )', '["clm_wiki_ww_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_ww_leadership', 'org_ww', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Reception As of July 2018, Weight Watchers was the most widely used commercial diet in the world. [1] [2] In addition to the U.S., as of 2018 it had operations in countries including Canada, the UK, Germany, Switzerland, France, Belgium, the Netherlands, Sweden, Australia, New Zealand, and Brazil. [3] Its main long-term competitors in the commercial weight-loss company genre are Jenny Craig and Nutrisystem. [4] [2] [5] Weight Watchers has been included in U.S. News &amp; World Report &#39; s rankings for 40 most popular diets and has also been listed as No.1 for weight loss and best commercial diets. [6] For Weight Watchers customers who choose to attend meetings, in addition to supplying information and lifestyle tips, meetings operate as support groups that provide empathy, rapport, and mutual understanding, as well as positive reinforcement . [7] [8] [9] Some therapists have said that focusing on counting calories or points, as promoted by WW, can lead to a disordered relationship with food and hunger. [10] [11] Previously the company''s prepared foods had been criticized as containing preservatives and other additives; [12] [13] as of late 2018 Weight Watchers has removed all artificial sweeteners, flavors, colors, and preservatives from products carrying the company''s name, and dropped or reformulated most of the food products it once produced. [14] [15] [16] [17] In August 2019, WW released Kurbo by WW , a weight management and health app directed at children and teenagers. It has been criticized by some experts on nutrition and eating disorders for encouraging dieting in children as young as 8. [18] Christy Harrison, a registered dietician, wrote in the New York Times , "programs like this are fertile ground for disordered eating" and that efforts to lose weight "are especially troubling when imposed on children who aren''t in a position to make their own choices and who haven''t had the opportunity to develop a peaceful relationship with food and their bodies."', '["clm_wiki_ww_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_ww_operations', 'org_ww', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Decline and bankruptcy On April 9, 2025, it was reported that WW was preparing to file for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection within the coming months, blaming financial challenges and increased competition from weight loss drugs such as Ozempic . The company planned to eliminate most of its debt and sell itself to creditors. [1] On May 6, 2025, WW filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy in Delaware , with plans to eliminate most of its $1.5 billion debt in an effort to put itself in a better financial position. The company expected to emerge from bankruptcy within no more than 40 days, or around June 15, 2025, with operations expected to be running normally throughout the procedure. [2] [3] WW was delisted from Nasdaq on May 16, and commenced trading over-the-counter . [4] In early July 2025, WW emerged from bankruptcy and was relisted on the NASDAQ. [5] [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Gladstone, Alexander (April 9, 2025). "WeightWatchers Prepares for Bankruptcy" . Wall Street Journal . Retrieved April 10, 2025 . ^ Valinsky, Jordan (May 6, 2025). "WeightWatchers files for bankruptcy" . CNN . Retrieved May 6, 2025 . ^ "Weightwatchers files for bankruptcy as Ozempic and Mounjaro surge in popularity" . www . May 7, 2025 . Retrieved May 8, 2025 . ^ "Can Weight Watchers be saved? As the company files for bankruptcy, we take a closer look" . May 19, 2025. ^ https://finance /news/weightwatchers-emerges-bankruptcy-slimming-down-072911233 ^ https://www /story/weightwatchers-emerges-from-bankruptcy-and-is-taking-aim-at-menopause-96661116', '["clm_wiki_ww_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
