VALUES
  ('cs_konecranes_operations', 'org_konecranes', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Konecranes (2022- ) In October 2022, Anders Svensson was appointed as the new CEO of Konecranes. He joined Konecranes from Sandvik . [1] In April 2024, it was announced that Konecranes had acquired the German crane and service supplier, Kocks Kranbau for an undisclosed amount. [2] In December 2024, Konecranes acquired the Dutch Peinemann Port Services BV and Peinemann Container Handling BV, based in Rotterdam . [3] On May 15, 2025, Marko Tulokas, then leading Konecranes'' Industrial Equipment business area, was named as the new CEO of Konecranes. [4] The company had announced in January 2025 that then-CEO Anders Svensson would leave the company. [5] Svensson started as CEO at Sweden''s Hexagon AB on July 21, 2025. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Konecranes appoints new CEO" . vertikal . Retrieved 2023-08-22 . ^ Writer, Staff (2024-04-08). "Konecranes acquires German Kocks Kranbau - Hoist" . Hoist . Archived from the original on 2025-11-10 . Retrieved 2026-07-26 . ^ Karamalegkos, Antonis (2024-12-04). "Konecranes completes acquisition of Peinemann Port Services and Container Handling businesses" . Container News . Retrieved 2024-12-07 . ^ "Inside information: Marko Tulokas appointed President and CEO of Konecranes | Stock exchange releases" . Konecranes . Archived from the original on 2025-06-14 . Retrieved 2026-07-26 . ^ "Inside Information: President and CEO Anders Svensson will leave Konecranes | Stock exchange releases | Konecranes" . www . Retrieved 2025-07-30 . ^ "Hexagon welcomes new President and CEO, Anders Svensson" . Hexagon . Retrieved 2026-07-26 .', '["clm_wiki_konecranes_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
