VALUES
  ('cs_uipath_history', 'org_uipath', 'overview', 'History',
   'Romanian-American software company UiPath Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : PATH (Class A) S&amp;P 400 component Industry Software Founded 2005 &#59;&#32;21 years ago ( 2005 ) in Bucharest, Romania Founders Daniel Dines Marius Tîrcă Adrian Dorache Andra Ciorici Lavinia Cojocaru Headquarters One Vanderbilt , New York City , U.S. Number of locations 31 countries Area served Worldwide Key people Daniel Dines ( chairman and CEO ) Ashim Gupta ( CFO ) Michael Atalla ( CMO ) Products Agentic AI software RPA tools Revenue US$ 1.43 billion (2025) Operating income US$&#8722;163 million (2025) Net income US$&#8722;74 million (2025) Total assets US$2.87 billion (2025) Total equity US$1.85 billion (2025) Number of employees 3,868 (2025) Website uipath Footnotes Financials as of January 31,&#32;2025 &#91;update&#93; . [1] UiPath Inc. is a Romanian-American multinational software company that develops artificial intelligence (AI) and agentic automation and orchestration software. The company''s software enables the building and orchestration of AI agents to automate complex processes and workflows. Founded in 2005 in Bucharest , Romania, by Daniel Dines and Marius Tîrcă, the company is headquartered in New York City . The company became public on April 21, 2021, which at the time was reportedly one of the largest US software IPOs in history. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "UiPath Inc. Full Year Ended 31 January 2025 Form 10-K Report" . SEC . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . March 24, 2025.', '["clm_wiki_uipath_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_uipath_leadership', 'org_uipath', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Products UiPath develops agentic automation software that combines robots, AI agents and people to automate workflows and processes. [1] Agentic automation integrates traditional robotic process automation (RPA), artificial intelligence, and human decision-making capabilities to allow for larger, more complex automations. [2] UiPath''s main product is the UiPath Platform for Agentic Automation. [3] The platform combines a family of low-code visual integrated development environment (IDE) products called UiPath Studio for process creation, with client-side agents called Robots that execute those processes. [4] An important part of the platform is UiPath Maestro, an orchestration engine designed to automate, model and optimize complex business processes, and monitor the performance of agents and robots. [5] Its earlier RPA products simplified tasks performed using other business software such as CRM or ERP systems, in internal and back-office areas like accounting, human resources paperwork, and claims processing. [6] [7] [8] [9] UiPath also hosts the UiPath Academy, to provide job training and certification in the fields of agentic automation and robotic process automation. [10] [11] ^ https://venturebeat /ai/uipaths-new-orchestrator-guides-ai-agents-to-follow-your-enterprises-rules ^ https://venturebeat /ai/uipaths-new-orchestrator-guides-ai-agents-to-follow-your-enterprises-rules/ ^ https://venturebeat /ai/uipaths-new-orchestrator-guides-ai-agents-to-follow-your-enterprises-rules ^ https://venturebeat /ai/robotic-process-automation-company-uipath-raises-568-million-at-7-billion-valuation ^ https://venturebeat /ai/uipaths-new-orchestrator-guides-ai-agents-to-follow-your-enterprises-rules ^ body:not( ):not( ) "UiPath: RPA and AI will be commoditized productivity tools within 5 years" . Venturebeat . June 22, 2019 . Retrieved March 3, 2021 . ^ "UiPath nabs $568M at a $7B valuation to bring robotic process automation to the front office" . TechCrunch . April 30, 2019 . ', '["clm_wiki_uipath_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_uipath_operations', 'org_uipath', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History UiPath was founded in 2005 in Bucharest, Romania as DeskOver, by Romanian entrepreneurs Daniel Dines and Marius Tîrcă. [1] In 2013, the company released the first UiPath Desktop Automation product line, which gave companies RPA tools to automate manual and repetitive back office tasks. [1] In 2015, the company changed its name to UiPath. [1] Also in 2015, after receiving seed funding from Accel Partners and earlier investors, the company also opened offices in London , New York City , Bangalore , Paris , Singapore , Washington, D.C. , and Tokyo . [2] [1] By April 2016, the company had released its Front Office and Back Office Server suites, and also released its Studio Community Edition. Within six months, the company had 10,000 active members, and more than 250 enterprise customers. [1] In 2017, UiPath reported 590 employees and moved its headquarters to New York to be closer to its international customer base. [3] In October 2019, UiPath announced the acquisition of Ukrainian process documentation company StepShot and Dutch process mining company ProcessGold. [4] Also in October, the company announced several updates to its technology platform, including UiPath Explorer, an automation identification and planning tool developed using technology from the acquired companies; a robot communication tool called UiPath Apps; a low code robot programming tool called UiPath StudioX; an embedded analytics tool called UiPath Insights; and UiPath Connect, a tool that allowed every employee to find new processes to automate. [4] [5] In November of the same year, the company reported it had 5,000 customers worldwide, and a developer community of more than 500,000 people. [6] In November, the company was ranked first in the Deloitte Technology Fast 500. [7] In March 2021, UiPath acquired Cloud Elements , an interconnectivity platform to advance API-based automation capabilities. [8] [9] In April 2021, UiPath raised $1.3 billion in an initial public offering on the New Yo', '["clm_wiki_uipath_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
