VALUES
  ('cs_american-international_leadership', 'org_american-international', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1919–1945: early years AIG was founded December 19, 1919 [1] when American Cornelius Vander Starr (1892–1968) established a general insurance agency, American Asiatic Underwriters (AAU), in Shanghai, China . [2] Business grew rapidly, and two years later, Starr formed a life insurance operation. [3] By the late 1920s, AAU had branches throughout China and Southeast Asia, including the Philippines , Dutch East Indies , and Malaya . [4] In 1926, Starr opened his first office in the United States, American International Underwriters Corporation (AIU). [5] He also focused on opportunities in Latin America and, in the late 1930s, AIU entered Havana , Cuba. [6] The steady growth of the Latin American agencies proved significant as it would offset the decline in business from Asia due to the impending World War II. [2] In 1939, Starr moved his headquarters from Shanghai to New York City. [7] [8] ^ Cite error: The named reference loc was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Laing, Jonathan R. (July 8, 1991). "Are the Glory Years Over? – Much Slower Growth Seems in the Offing for AIG". Barron''s . ^ Tracer, Zachary (December 18, 2012). "Benmosche Exits Greenberg Jewel Linked to AIG Founding" . Bloomberg Businessweek . Archived from the original on January 21, 2016 . Retrieved February 21, 2013 . ^ "AIG Europe – History". Marketline . February 18, 2004. ^ Bandler, James (October 7, 2008). "Hank''s Last Stand" . Fortune . Archived from the original on September 29, 2008 . Retrieved February 21, 2013 . ^ "American International Group Inc (New York Stock Exchange)" . Company profile . New York: Thomson Reuters . Archived from the original on February 20, 2009 . Retrieved March 18, 2009 . ^ "AIG: What does this US giant do?" . BBC . September 17, 2008. Archived from the original on March 20, 2009 . Retrieved March 18, 2009 . ^ "Foreign Office Files for China, 1949–1976" . Part 1: Complete Files for 1949: Publisher''s Note . Adam Matthew Publicatio', '["clm_wiki_american-international_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
