  ('cs_cms-energy_history', 'org_cms-energy', 'overview', 'History',
   'Electric and gas company in Jackson, Michigan, US CMS Energy Corporation Headquarters in downtown Jackson Type Public Traded as NYSE : CMS S&amp;P 500 component Industry Energy Founded 1886 &#59;&#32;140 years ago ( 1886 ) Headquarters Jackson, Michigan , U.S. Area served United States Key people Garrick Rochow ( President &amp; CEO ) Rejji Hayes ( CFO ) [1] Products Electricity Natural gas Revenue US$ 7.52 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.49 billion (2024) Net income US$1.00 billion (2024) Total assets US$35.9 billion (2024) Total equity US$8.23 billion (2024) Number of employees 8,324 (2024) Subsidiaries Consumers Energy , NorthStar Clean Energy Website www Footnotes [2] One Energy Plaza (Jackson, Michigan) CMS Energy Corporation is an American energy company based in Jackson, Michigan , that is focused principally on utility operations in Michigan . [3] Its principal business is Consumers Energy , a public utility that provides electricity and natural gas to more than 6 million of Michigan''s 10 million residents. [4] [5] Its non-utility businesses are focused primarily on domestic independent power production. Consumers Energy has operated since 1886. [6] NorthStar Clean Energy''s primary businesses are independent power production and natural gas transmission. [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Leadership" . Archived from the original on 10 July 2015 . Retrieved 9 July 2015 . ^ "CMS Energy 2024 Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. 11 February 2025 . Retrieved 12 February 2025 . ^ Bruce Corning (30 June 2015). "SunTrust Robinson Humphrey Rating Update on CMS Energy Corporation (NYSE:CMS)" . Retrieved 9 July 2015 . ^ "Ally Financial Larger Than S&amp;P 500 Component CMS Energy" . Forbes . Retrieved 9 July 2015 . ^ Tarryl Jackson (7 May 2012). "CMS Energy brought in $6.5 billion in revenue in 2011, making this year''s Fortune 500 list" . Mlive . Retrieved 9 July 2015 . ^ "The world''s 10 longest running energy utility companies" . 29 April 2015 . Retrieved 9 July 2015 . ^ "CMS Energy Corp (CMS)" . Reuters . Retrieved 9 July 2015 .', '["clm_wiki_cms-energy_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
