  ('cs_cms-energy_leadership', 'org_cms-energy', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Sustainability and Environment In 2015, 9 percent of CMS Energy''s power comes from renewable energy sources. [1] Primary CMS Energy subsidiary Consumers Energy joined the Wildlife Habitat Council as an active member. [2] By 2007, all power facilities received the Clean Corporate Citizen award from the Michigan Department of Environmental Quality. [3] [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "CEO expects Michigan to expand renewable standard in 2015" . 28 April 2014 . Retrieved 9 July 2015 . ^ "Two Consumers Energy Generating Facilities Receive International Recognition from Wildlife Habitat Council" . 15 December 2014 . Retrieved 9 July 2015 . ^ "ENVIRONMENT" . Archived from the original on 10 July 2015 . Retrieved 9 July 2015 . ^ "CMS Energy Hikes Dividend" . Nasdaq . Retrieved 9 July 2015 .', '["clm_wiki_cms-energy_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
