   '1970–1980s: formation and listings CRH (Cement Roadstone Holdings) was established in 1970 through the merger of Cement Ltd (est. 1936) and Roadstone Ltd (est. 1949). [1] The company listed on the Irish Stock Exchange in 1973. [2] CRH entered the United States market in 1978 by acquiring Amcor, a Utah-based concrete products group, which became Oldcastle Inc. The company expanded its U.S. presence in 1985 with the acquisition of Callanan Industries, a New York State aggregates producer. [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "CRH History Overview" . crh . Retrieved 15 March 2015 . ^ "CRH plc" . Irish Stock Exchange . Retrieved 20 March 2016 . ^ Cite error: The named reference Callanan was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_crh-plc_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
