  ('cs_kimco-realty_history', 'org_kimco-realty', 'overview', 'History',
   'Overview As of December 31, 2025, the company owned interests in 565 U.S. shopping centers and mixed-use assets comprising 100 million square feet of gross leasable space. [1] Kimco was the first public vertically integrated REIT designed to be internally managed and advised, providing its own property and asset management. [2] ^ Cite error: The named reference 10K was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) Brueggeman, William (2016). Real estate finance and investments . New York, NY: McGraw-Hill Education. ISBN 978-0-07-337735-3 . OCLC 908192655 .', '["clm_wiki_kimco-realty_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
