VALUES
  ('cs_kimco-realty_leadership', 'org_kimco-realty', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'History The Kimco Corporation, the predecessor of the company, was founded in 1966 by a group of real estate investors, including Martin Kimmel and Milton Cooper, who merged their retail assets. This asset merger led to the new company being named Kim - co . The company was incorporated in 1973. [1] In 1988, the company acquired Gold Circle for $325 million. [2] In November 1991, the company became a public company via an initial public offering , raising $120 million. [1] [3] In 1998, the company acquired Price REIT for $535 million in stock. [4] In October 2003, the company acquired Mid-Atlantic Realty Trust for $441 million. [5] [6] A few years later, in 2007, Kimco acquired The Birchwood Organization – another Long Island -based company – for $92 million. [7] In August 2021, the company acquired Weingarten Realty . [8] In November 2022, the company acquired a portfolio of eight Long Island, NY shopping centers for $375.8 million. [9] In January 2024, Kimco acquired RPT Realty , making the company the largest shopping center REIT. [10] In October 2024, the company acquired Waterford Lakes Town Center for $322 million. [11] ^ a b Cite error: The named reference 10K was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) Barmash, Isadore (September 8, 1988). "Kimco Buys Campeau''s Gold Circle" . The New York Times . ^ Pomerantz, Dorothy (March 10, 2008). "Beyond The Big Box" . Forbes . ^ Kirkpatrick, David D. (January 14, 1998). "Kimco to Announce Pact to Acquire Price REIT for $535 Million in Stock" . The Wall Street Journal . ^ "Kimco to Buy Mid-Atlantic Realty Trust for $444 Million" . The New York Times . Bloomberg news . June 19, 2003. ^ Trainor, Tim (June 20, 2003). "Kimco To Buy Mid-Atlantic in $680M Deal" . CoStar Group . ^ "Kimco Realty Corporation announces third quarter transaction activity" (Press release). Business Wire . October 8, 2007. ^ "Kimco Realty and Weingarten Realty Investors Announce Closing of Merger" (Press release). Busine', '["clm_wiki_kimco-realty_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
