VALUES
  ('cs_sba-communications_history', 'org_sba-communications', 'overview', 'History',
   'Operations The company develops wireless infrastructures, including small cells, indoor/outdoor distributed antenna systems, and traditional cell sites that support antennas used for wireless communication by mobile carriers and wireless broadband providers. [1] [2] SBA Communications operates in two segments: Site Leasing and Site Development. [3] It leases antenna space to wireless service providers on towers that it owns or operates, [4] and manages rooftop and tower sites for property owners under various contractual arrangements. As of 2020, it owned 30,000 towers around North and South America . Its biggest market is Brazil, where the company owns over 10,000 towers. [4] The company also managed or leased approximately 4,800 actual or potential towers. [5] In addition, it provides various site development services comprising network pre-design; site audits; identification of potential locations for towers and antennas; support in buying or leasing of the location; assistance in obtaining zoning approvals and permits; tower structure construction; antenna installation; and radio equipment installation, commissioning, and maintenance. [2] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "SBA Communications Pulls Loan Repricing Amid Market Volatility" . Bloomberg . 2024-08-05 . Retrieved 2024-11-21 . ^ a b "SBA Communications Corp: Overview" . Global Data . Retrieved November 21, 2024 . ^ "SBA Communications Corp (NASDAQ:SBAC)" . CNN Business . Archived from the original on September 13, 2015 . Retrieved October 21, 2020 . ^ a b "Sba Communications Corp" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved October 21, 2020 . ^ "Form 10-K" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved October 21, 2020 .', '["clm_wiki_sba-communications_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
