VALUES
  ('cs_verizon_history', 'org_verizon', 'overview', 'History',
   'American telecommunications company Not to be confused with Vierzon . Verizon Communications Inc. Logo used since 2024 &#91; a &#93; Headquarters in New York Formerly Bell Atlantic Corporation (1983–2000) Type Public Traded as NYSE : VZ S&amp;P 100 component S&amp;P 500 component ISIN US92343V1044 Industry Telecommunications Predecessors NYNEX Corporation GTE Corporation Frontier Communications Founded October 7, 1983 &#59;&#32;42 years ago ( 1983-10-07 ) Headquarters 1095 Avenue of the Americas , New York City , U.S. Area served United States (consumer services) Worldwide (business services) Key people Mark Bertolini ( chairman ) Dan Schulman ( CEO ) Tony Skiadas ( CFO / EVP [1] ) Products Fixed telephony Mobile telephony Broadband Digital television Internet television IPTV IoT Revenue US$ 138.2 billion (2025) Operating income US$29.26 billion (2025) Net income US$17.61 billion (2025) Total assets US$404.3 billion (2025) Total equity US$105.7 billion (2025) Number of employees 89,900 (2025) Divisions Verizon Consumer Verizon Business Subsidiaries Verizon Fios Verizon Value Visible by Verizon Yahoo (10%) Website verizon Footnotes [2] [3] [4] [5] [6] [7] [8] [9] [10] Verizon Communications Inc. ( / v ə ˈ r aɪ z ən / &#32; ⓘ və- RY -zən ) is an American telecommunications company headquartered in New York City . [4] It is the world''s second-largest telecommunications company by revenue and its mobile network is the largest wireless carrier in the United States , with 146.8 million subscribers as of March 31, 2026. [11] The company was formed in 1983 as Bell Atlantic as a result of the breakup of the Bell System into seven companies, each a Regional Bell Operating Company (RBOC), commonly referred to as "Baby Bells." [12] The company was originally headquartered in Philadelphia and operated in the states of Pennsylvania, New Jersey, Delaware, Maryland, Virginia, and West Virginia. In 1997, Bell Atlantic expanded into New York and the New England states by merging with fellow Baby Bell NYNEX . While Bell Atlantic was the surviving company, the merged company moved its headquarters from Philadelphia to NYNEX''s old headquarters in New York City. In 2000, Bell Atlantic acquired GTE , which operated telecommunications companies across most of the rest of the country not already in Bell Atlantic''s footprint. Bell Atlantic, the surviving entity, changed its name to Verizon, a portmanteau of veritas (Latin for "truth") and horizon . [13] In 2015, Verizon expanded in', '["clm_wiki_verizon_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
