VALUES
  ('cs_mizuho-americas_history', 'org_mizuho-americas', 'overview', 'History',
   'Operations Mizuho Americas is a holding firm for a variety of financing, securities, treasury services, and aggregating segments in corporate and investment banking. [1] Departments include loan markets, corporate and investment banking, [2] equity, [1] high yield sales &amp; trading, fixed income sales and trading, and leveraged capital markets, which oversees the origination of investment grade and non-investment grade debt products. [3] As of December 31, 2022, its total assets were approximately $2 trillion and total revenues were 605 billion yen. [4] Mizuho Financial Group’s U.S. operations also include Mizuho Bank USA; [5] Mizuho Securities USA LLC, a U.S. broker dealer engaged in securities; [5] and Mizuho Trust &amp; Banking Co. (USA). [5] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "Mizuho Adds Darlene Pasquill as Equity Division Head &#124; Finance Magnates" . Financial and Business News &#124; Finance Magnates . October 24, 2018. ^ Haunss, Kristen (November 2017). "LPC: Mizuho eyes US leveraged finance expansion" . Reuters . Retrieved 2024-02-08 . ^ Adler, Lynn (10 May 2018). "Mizuho Americas makes 5 senior high-yield sales, trading hires" . Reuters . Retrieved 2024-02-08 . ^ "Bank Holding Company Performance Report December 31, 2022-FR BHCPR" . Retrieved 2024-02-08 . ^ a b c "ANNUAL REPORT" . www . Retrieved 2024-02-08 .', '["clm_wiki_mizuho-americas_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
