VALUES
  ('cs_juniper-networks_leadership', 'org_juniper-networks', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Origins and funding Juniper founder Pradeep Sindhu Pradeep Sindhu , [1] a scientist with Xerox ''s Palo Alto Research Center (PARC), [2] conceived the idea for Juniper Networks while on vacation in 1995 [3] and founded the company in February 1996. [4] Sindhu wanted to create data packet -based routers that were optimized for Internet traffic ( packet switching ), [3] [5] whereby the routing and transferring of data occurs "by means of addressed packets so that a channel is occupied during the transmission of the packet only, and upon completion of the transmission the channel is made available for the transfer of other traffic ." [6] [7] He was joined by engineers Bjorn Liencres from Sun Microsystems and Dennis Ferguson from MCI Communications . [8] Sindhu started Juniper Networks with $2 million in seed funding , which was followed by $12 million in funding in the company''s first year of operations. [9] About seven months after the company''s founding, Scott Kriens was appointed CEO to manage the business, while founder Sindhu became the Chief Technology Officer . [2] [10] By February 1997, Juniper had raised $8 million in venture funding . [11] Later that year, Juniper Networks raised an additional $40 million in investments [12] from a round that included four out of five of the largest telecommunications equipment manufacturers: Siemens , Ericsson , Nortel and 3Com . [13] [14] [15] [16] Juniper also received $2.5 million from Qwest and other investments from AT&amp;T . [17] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Business: Spot the difference; Juniper Networks" . The Economist . September 1, 2001. ^ a b Cite error: The named reference five was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b Votteler, Ed (2002). International Directory of Company Histories: Juniper Networks, Inc . Vol. 43. St. James Press. pp. 251– 255. ^ Guy, Sandra (September 2, 1997). "Startup sprouts with lofty goals". Telephony . ^ Cite error: The named reference twelve was invoked but never defined (see', '["clm_wiki_juniper-networks_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
