VALUES
  ('cs_juniper-networks_operations', 'org_juniper-networks', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisitions and investments Main article: List of acquisitions by Juniper Networks By 2001, Juniper had made only a few acquisitions of smaller companies, due to the leadership''s preference for organic growth. [1] The pace of acquisition picked up in 2001 and 2002 with the purchases of Pacific Broadband and Unisphere Networks . [2] In 2004 Juniper made a $4 billion acquisition of network security company NetScreen Technologies . [3] Juniper revised NetScreen''s channel program that year and used its reseller network to bring other products to market. [4] Juniper made five acquisitions in 2005, mostly of startups with deal values ranging from $8.7 to $337 million. It acquired application-acceleration vendor Redline Networks , VOIP company Kagoor Networks , as well as wide area network (WAN) company Peribit Networks . [5] Peribit and Redline were incorporated into a new application products group and their technology was integrated into Juniper''s infranet framework. [6] [7] Afterwards, Juniper did not make any additional acquisitions until 2010. [8] From 2010 to September 2011, Juniper made six acquisitions and invested in eight companies. Often Juniper acquired early-stage startups, developing their technology, then selling it to pre-existing Juniper clients. [9] Juniper acquired two digital video companies, Ankeena Networks and Blackwave Inc., as well as wireless LAN software company Trapeze Networks . [9] [10] In 2012, Juniper acquired Mykonos Software, which develops security software intended to deceive hackers already within the network perimeter. [11] and a developer of software-defined network controllers, Contrail Systems. [12] In 2014, Juniper acquired the software-defined networking (SDN) company WANDL. [13] In April 2016, Juniper closed its acquisition of BTI, a provider of cloud and metro network technology, in an effort to beef up its data center interconnect and metro packet optical transport technology and services. [14] Juniper acquired cloud operatio', '["clm_wiki_juniper-networks_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 596. Parametric Technology Corporation (slug=parametric-technology, wiki='Parametric Technology Corporation')
