  ('cs_dexcom_operations', 'org_dexcom', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Partnerships Dexcom entered into a partnership in 2015 with Google Life Sciences (which subsequently became Verily ) to develop the Dexcom G7 [1] [2] [3] Dexcom entered a non-exclusive agreement with Tandem Diabetes Care , Inc. in 2015 to allow the integration of its new G5 and G6 continuous glucose monitoring systems into Tandem''s insulin pumps. [4] [5] Tandem Diabetes Care received FDA approval in December 2019 for Control-IQ, a closed-loop technology that uses Tandem''s t:slim X2 insulin pump and the Dexcom G6 "to automatically increase, decrease, or stop the delivery of insulin in response to the glucose levels of people with Type 1 diabetes." [6] In June 2019, Dexcom announced a collaboration with Companion Medical to enable the exchange of CGM data from Dexcom with insulin data from InPen into both companies'' software applications. [7] Dexcom entered into a partnership with Livongo , a digital chronic care management company, in January 2020 to share CGM data from the Dexcom G6 with Livongo''s platform. This integration allowed Livongo to incorporate the CGM data along with other patient data. [8] In February 2020, Dexcom and Insulet Corporation signed a non-exclusive, global agreement to combine current and future Dexcom continuous glucose monitoring systems with Insulet''s tubeless insulin delivery Pod into the Omnipod Horizon System for automated insulin delivery. [9] This allowed the ability to adjust insulin doses based on Insulet''s algorithm or through their smartphone. [10] The company also announced in March 2020 a partnership with Welldoc to integrate G6 CGM data with BlueStar, a digital platform for diabetes management . [11] In November 2024, Dexcom announced a "strategic partnership" and data exchange with Oura . [12] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Fierce Biotech" . fiercebiotech . Retrieved 2015-08-11 . ^ "Verily Life Sciences" . verily . Retrieved 2017-02-15 . ^ "Dexcom G7 CGM - Powerfully simple diabetes management" . Dexcom . Retrieved 2023-06-28 . ^ "FDA ', '["clm_wiki_dexcom_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
