VALUES
  ('cs_gartner_leadership', 'org_gartner', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'History 1980s Gideon Gartner and David Stein founded Gartner, Inc. in 1979 [1] to provide IT industry research and analysis to businesses buying and selling computer hardware. [2] Gideon Gartner had previously worked at IBM, and his new firm specialized in information about IBM and its products. [3] Gartner''s reports were often delivered as a one-pager containing only high-level insights. [4] [5] Gartner analysts developed the Magic Quadrant visual framework of placing companies within defined market quadrants during the early 1980s [6] and began to integrate the methodology into their presentations and later reports. [7] By 1983, the firm employed 80 research analysts and generated $8 million in revenue. [8] In 1985, Gartner''s brokerage and investment division separated from the firm to become a wholly owned subsidiary called Gartner Securities. [9] Two years later, the name was changed to SoundView Financial Group, [10] which eventually operated as SoundView Technology Group . [11] In July 1986, Gartner rebranded as Gartner Group and became a publicly traded company. [12] [13] In January 1987, Gartner Group acquired another technology research firm, the Cupertino-based Infocorp. [14] That same year Gartner reported $25 million in sales and $1.9 million in earnings. [15] The U.K.-based Saatchi &amp; Saatchi acquired Gartner Group in 1988. [15] [16] 1990s In 1990, Gartner Group was taken private by Gideon Gartner and other executives [17] in an acquisition deal backed by funding from Bain Capital and Dun &amp; Bradstreet , then a Bain client. [18] [19] Under Bain ownership, Gartner refocused on IT industry pricing data and expanded its profit margins from 10 percent to 30 percent. [20] Dun &amp; Bradstreet acquired a majority share in Gartner in 1993. [21] Gartner went public again in October 1993, with Dun &amp; Bradstreet maintaining a 50 percent stake. [22] Over the next eight years, Gartner acquired or made substantial investments in 30 companies, [23] including', '["clm_wiki_gartner_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
