   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_hca-healthcare_operations', 'org_hca-healthcare', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'United Kingdom HCA International , the UK arm of Hospital Corporation of America , "caters for around half of all private patients in London." [1] The main hospital sites within the United Kingdom it operates include: The Christie Private Care, Manchester The Wilmslow Hospital [2] The Harley Street Clinic HCA at The Shard The Lister Hospital London Bridge Hospital The Portland Hospital for Women and Children The Princess Grace Hospital The Wellington Hospital Leaders in Oncology Care It opened urgent care walk-in centres at London Bridge Hospital and the Portland Hospital in March 2018. It claims that patients, on average, wait just seven minutes to see a nurse and 17 minutes to see a doctor. [3] In February 2022, [4] outsourced cleaning staff at London Bridge Hospital reported a lack of PPE, no access to sick pay, a lack of training and no prior warning about which rooms may be contaminated with the virus through the COVID-19 pandemic . The Princess Grace Hospital specializes in breast cancer and surgery, aided by Kefah Mokbel and Nick Perry who, in 2005, founded The London Breast Institute. The company opened The Harborne Hospital, a newly built private hospital located close to the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, Birmingham , in February 2024. [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Paul Gallagher (June 14, 2013). "World''s largest private healthcare company HCA plans expansion into NHS" . The Independent . ^ 52 Alderly Road ^ "HCA expands network of urgent care centres" . LaingBuisson. March 12, 2018 . Retrieved May 11, 2018 . ^ "HCA: Promoting US style for-profit healthcare in the UK" . April 14, 2022. ^ "The Harborne Hospital - Private Healthcare &#124; HCA UK" . www .co.uk . February 7, 2024.', '["clm_wiki_hca-healthcare_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
