  ('cs_incyte_operations', 'org_incyte', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisition history Incyte has made a total of 3 acquisitions. Maxia Pharmaceuticals (2003): An early acquisition in Incyte''s history, the company purchased Maxia in 2003 for $42 million. [1] Villaris Therapeutics (2022): This acquisition was valued at approximately $1.4 billion and included an upfront payment along with milestones. It added new assets to Incyte''s portfolio for treating vitiligo and other autoimmune conditions. [2] Escient Pharmaceuticals (2024): In May 2024, Incyte acquired this San Diego-based, clinical-stage company for $750 million. The acquisition provided Incyte with two oral drug candidates for inflammatory diseases, EP262 and EP547. [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Incyte Acquires Maxia Pharmaceuticals; Acquisition Expands Drug Discovery &amp; Development Programs | Incyte" . February 19, 2003. : CS1 maint: url-status ( link ) ^ "Incyte Announces Agreement to Acquire Medicxi-backed Villaris Therapeutics and Auremolimab (VM6) | Incyte" . October 3, 2022. : CS1 maint: url-status ( link ) ^ "Incyte Completes Acquisition of Escient Pharmaceuticals | Incyte" . : CS1 maint: url-status ( link )', '["clm_wiki_incyte_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
