VALUES
  ('cs_loews_leadership', 'org_loews', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Subsidiaries Loews Corporation''s principal subsidiaries are: CNA Financial Corporation (89% owned) — one of the largest commercial property and casualty insurance companies in the United States. CNA reported record core income of $1.3 billion in 2024. [1] Boardwalk Pipelines (100% owned) — operates approximately 14,000 miles of natural gas and natural gas liquids pipelines. Loews Hotels &amp; Co (100% owned) — operates luxury hotels across the United States. In 2024, Loews Hotels opened the Loews Arlington Hotel and Convention Center, a 888-room property representing a $550 million investment. [2] Altium Packaging (53% owned) — rigid plastic packaging manufacturer operating more than 60 facilities in the United States and Canada. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "CNA Financial Announces Q4 2024 Results" . PR Newswire . February 10, 2025 . Retrieved February 26, 2026 . ^ "Loews Hotels pursues $435 million expansion in Texas and Florida" . Skift . February 5, 2024 . Retrieved February 26, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_loews_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
