VALUES
  ('cs_rockwell-automation_operations', 'org_rockwell-automation', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '21st century Previous logo In 2001, Rockwell International split into two companies. The industrial automation division became Rockwell Automation, while the avionics division became Rockwell Collins . [1] The split was structured so that Rockwell Automation was the legal successor of Rockwell International, while Rockwell Collins was the spin-off. Rockwell Automation retains Rockwell International''s stock price history and continues to trade on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol "ROK". In 2007, Reliance Electric Drives and Dodge Bearings were spun off from the company. In February 2019, Rockwell Automation and Schlumberger entered a joint venture to create Sensia, the oil and gas industry''s first fully integrated automation solutions provider. [2] Rockwell was later announced as a founding member of the ISA Global Cybersecurity Alliance to help advance readiness and awareness in manufacturing. [3] Another partnership was formed in November 2019 with Accenture ''s Industry X to help deliver greater industrial supply chain optimization. [4] Simulation software provider Ansys and Rockwell Automation also allied to help customers design simulation-based digital twins of products, processes, and manufacturing. [5] In May 2023, The Wall Street Journal reported that Rockwell Automation was under a U.S. federal investigation regarding potential access to its software by the Chinese government through company employees in Dalian . [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Rockwell to Change Name to Rockwell Automation after Rockwell Collins spinoff" . 20 February 2001. Archived from the original on 2018-03-21 . Retrieved 2016-02-06 . ^ "Rockwell Automation and Schlumberger announce Sensia joint venture" . Automation . 2019-02-20 . Retrieved 2022-02-27 . ^ "Rockwell Automation joins ISA Global Cybersecurity Alliance as a founding member" . Automation . 2019-08-14 . Retrieved 2022-02-27 . ^ "Rockwell Automation partners with Accenture to create digital solutions for industrial clien', '["clm_wiki_rockwell-automation_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
