VALUES
  ('cs_zoetis_leadership', 'org_zoetis', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1950s to 2000s Zoetis building in Exton, PA In the 1950s, Pfizer began research on several drugs, including oxytetracycline , which was found to be effective in livestock. [1] In 1952, the Pfizer Agriculture Division opened a 732-acre research and development facility in Terre Haute, Indiana , called Vigo . [1] [2] By 1988 the division was renamed Pfizer Animal Health . [1] The 1995 acquisition of Norden Laboratories from GlaxoSmithKline expanded Pfizer''s animal health division into small animal care, including domestic pets . [1] Secondary research and development centres were opened in Kalamazoo, Michigan , in 2003. [1] In the same year, Pfizer acquired Pharmacia Corporation for US$ 60 billion in stock options . [3] Between 2007 and 2011, the company acquired Embrex Inc, Catapult Genetics, Bovigen, Wyeth , Fort Dodge Animal Health, Vetnex Animal Health Ltd, Synbiotics Corporation, Microtek, King Pharmaceuticals , and Alpharma . [1] ^ a b c d e f body:not( ):not( ) "Form S-1" . WASHINGTON, D.C: U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . 10 August 2012 . Retrieved 2 February 2013 . ^ "Pfizer Buys 732 Acre Vigo Chemical Plant" . Chicago Daily Tribune . 17 July 1958. p. 1. Archived from the original on 16 February 2013 . Retrieved 2 February 2013 . : CS1 maint: deprecated archival service ( link ) ^ Frank, Robert; Scott, Hensley (16 July 2002). "Pfizer to Buy Pharmacia For $60 Billion in Stock - WSJ" . Wall Street Journal . ISSN 0099-9660 . Retrieved 8 August 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_zoetis_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_zoetis_operations', 'org_zoetis', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisitions In November 2015, the company announced it would acquire a developer of aquaculture treatments and diseases, Pharmaq, for $765 million. [1] [2] In 2017, Zoetis acquired Ireland-based Nexvet, a company with a biologics focused technology and product candidate pipeline. [3] In the same year, the company also acquired KL Automation, a robotics company. [4] In May 2018, the company announced its intention to acquire Abaxis for $1.9 billion in cash. [5] [6] [7] In August 2021, Zoetis announced it would buy Jurox, increasing the business'' presence in New Zealand, the US, Canada and the UK. [8] In June 2022, Zoetis acquired Basepaws, a privately held genetics company. [9] In September 2023, Zoetis acquired Petmedix, a privately held Cambridge, UK-based company, to bring the benefits of species-specific antibody therapies to pet owners. [10] [11] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Zoetis Inc. Form 8-K Current Report Filed 2015-11-02" . edgar . Archived from the original on 23 January 2025 . Retrieved 8 August 2026 . ^ Staff, G. E. N. (3 November 2015). "Zoetis Purchasing PHARMAQ for $765M" . GEN - Genetic Engineering and Biotechnology News . Retrieved 8 August 2026 . ^ Vinluan, Frank (13 April 2017). "Zoetis Builds on Biologics Pipeline with $85M Nexvet Acquisition" . Xconomy . New York, NY, USA . Retrieved 9 April 2018 . ^ Cite error: The named reference :2 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Mathias, Tamara. "Zoetis to buy veterinary diagnostics firm Abaxis for $1.9 billion" . U.K . Archived from the original on 3 June 2019 . Retrieved 8 August 2026 . ^ Hart, Simon (7 August 2026). "Jalalive" . Retrieved 8 August 2026 . ^ Dunn, Louise S. (1 August 2018). "Zoetis concludes $2 billion acquisition of Abaxis" . Today''s Veterinary Business . Retrieved 8 August 2026 . ^ "Zoetis to Acquire Jurox, a Leading Provider and Manufacturer of Livestock and Companion Animal Products" . ^ "Zoetis Completes Acquisition of Basepaws, an Innovative Leader in Petcare Genetics', '["clm_wiki_zoetis_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 629. KeyBank (slug=keybank, wiki='KeyBank')
