VALUES
  ('cs_banc-of-california_leadership', 'org_banc-of-california', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Merger with PacWest Bancorp In July 2023, a few months after bank runs in regional banks caused a banking crisis , Banc of California agreed to rescue and acquire Pacific Western Bank in an all-stock deal valued at $1.1 billion, aimed at restoring confidence in the bank. [1] As part of the deal, Warburg Pincus and Centerbridge Partners would invest $400 million in the combined company. [2] Wolff was credited with orchestrating the deal, which closed in November 2023, having previously served in several executive roles at Pacific Western Bank from 2002 to 2014. [3] [4] In 2025, Wolff became President, Chairman and CEO of Banc of California, Inc. [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Nishant, Niket; Saini, Manya (July 26, 2023). "PacWest stock soars on $1.1 billion buyout deal with Banc of California" . Reuters . ^ Dickson, Steve (July 25, 2023). "PacWest to be sold to Banc of California in rescue deal" . Los Angeles Times . ^ "Jared M. Wolff" . Los Angeles Times . Retrieved October 3, 2025 . ^ "Jared Michael Wolff - BANC | Banc of California Inc. - Wall Street Journal" . www . Retrieved October 3, 2025 . ^ "Banc of California - Jared Wolff" . BancofCal . Retrieved October 3, 2025 .', '["clm_wiki_banc-of-california_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
