VALUES
  ('cs_banc-of-california_operations', 'org_banc-of-california', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Philanthropy &amp; Sponsorships Banc of California has previously been an official sponsor of the USC Trojans and the athletic program of the University of Southern California . [1] The bank was also a major sponsor of Los Angeles FC , a Major League Soccer franchise, including and a 15-year, $100 million deal with the club for the naming rights to their stadium Banc of California Stadium in Los Angeles, which opened in 2018. [2] [3] The naming rights were restructured in 2020. [4] Banc of California supported the recovery from the January 2025 Southern California Wildfires. A week after the fires began, the bank created the Wildfire Relief &amp; Recovery Fund with a $1 million donation to aid wildfire recovery and rebuilding efforts. [5] In August, these funds were allocated to Steadfast LA, a nonprofit created by Rick Caruso , which supports small businesses in Altadena , Malibu and Pacific Palisades . [6] The bank also contributed $250,000 to the L.A. Area Chamber''s Small Business Disaster Relief Fund, assisting small businesses impacted by crises throughout the region. [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Banc of California Focuses on Financial Literacy as Part of USC Athletic Sponsorship" (Press release). Banc of California. June 24, 2014 . Retrieved August 23, 2016 &#8211; via Business Wire . ^ Koren, James Rufus (August 23, 2016). "Banc of California snags naming rights for L.A. Football Club soccer stadium" . Los Angeles Times . Retrieved August 23, 2016 . ^ Novy-Williams, Eben (August 23, 2016). "Bank Run by 41-Year-Old Signs $100 Million Stadium-Name Deal" . Bloomberg News . Retrieved August 25, 2016 . ^ Novy-Williams, Eben (May 27, 2020). "Banc of California Paid $20 Million to End L.A. Soccer Stadium Name Agreement" . Variety . Archived from the original on June 7, 2020 . Retrieved May 30, 2020 . ^ "Banc of California Creates Charitable Fund and Commits $1 Million to Support Southern California Communities Affected by Wildfires" . Los Angeles Times . January 14, 20', '["clm_wiki_banc-of-california_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
