VALUES
  ('cs_sprint_operations', 'org_sprint', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Brown Telephone Company Brown Telephone Company was founded in 1899 by Cleyson Brown , to deploy the first telephone service to the rural area around Abilene, Kansas . [1] In 1911, C. L. Brown consolidated the Brown Telephone Company with three other independents to form the United Telephone Company . [2] C. L. Brown formed United Telephone and Electric (UT&amp;E) in 1925. In 1939, at the end of the Great Depression , UT&amp;E reorganized to form United Utilities . [2] United Telephone System logo, used from 1981 into the 1990s In 1964, Paul H. Henson became president of United Utilities; two years later, he was named chairman. [3] When Henson began working at the company in 1959, it had 575,000 telephones in 15 states and revenues of $65 million. [4] [5] [3] Henson is credited with creating the first major fiber optic network, having recognized it as a way to handle more calls and provide better quality sound. [3] In 1972, United Utilities changed its name to United Telecommunications . [2] In 1980, United Telecommunications began working on a 23,000 mile fiber optic network for long-distance calls. [3] In 1989, this long-distance business became profitable for the company for the first time. [3] In 1990, Henson retired from United Telecommunications; by this time the company''s revenues had grown to $8 billion. [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Inside the Plan to Pull Sprint Out of Its Death Spiral" . Bloomberg Businessweek . January 26, 2016 . Retrieved October 15, 2018 . ^ a b c Glashauser, Georgia (2007). Bicycle from Sea to Shining Sea . British Columbia: Trafford Publishing. p. 76. ^ a b c d e f Johnston, David Cay (April 15, 1997). "Paul Henson, 71, Pioneer In Fiber Optic Phones at Sprint" . The New York Times . Retrieved October 15, 2018 . ^ "Sprint Says Former Chief Paul H. Henson Has Died" . Wall Street Journal . April 14, 1997 . Retrieved October 15, 2018 . ^ "Independent Phone Group Elects" . The New York Times . October 23, 1964 . Retrieved October 15, 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_sprint_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
