VALUES
  ('cs_kbr_operations', 'org_kbr', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Growth In May 2019, the company introduced new branding. [1] At the end of 2023, KBR released KCap, a decarbonization technology offered in partnership with Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Ltd (HPCL), India. [2] As of 2024, the company supports various NASA programs, educational institutions, international partner space agencies, and commercial partners. [3] In September 2025, KBR’s board of directors approved the spin-off of the company’s government services segment, Mission Technology Solutions (MTS). [4] MTS is set to become a new, independent publicly-traded company by mid-to-late 2026. After the spinoff, KBR will still operate its sustainable technology business. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Chapa, Sergio (May 3, 2019). "KBR rolls out new look as company evolves from blue collar past" . Chron . Retrieved November 4, 2020 . ^ "KBR LAUNCHES KCAP℠ — A NEXT-GENERATION DECARBONIZATION SOLUTION" . Oil Gas Technology . February 7, 2024 . Retrieved May 28, 2025 . ^ Cite error: The named reference :12 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b Wilkers, Ross (September 24, 2025). "KBR plans spinoff of government business" . Washington Technology . Retrieved October 10, 2025 .', '["clm_wiki_kbr_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 639. Kraft Foods Group (slug=kraft-foods, wiki='Kraft Foods Group')
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
