   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_orbital-sciences_operations', 'org_orbital-sciences', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Merger On April 29, 2014, Orbital Sciences announced that it had entered into a definitive agreement with Alliant Techsystems to combine Orbital and ATK''s Aerospace and Defense (A&amp;D) Groups to create a US$4.5 billion (combined calendar year 2013 annual revenue), 13000-person company. The new company was called Orbital ATK, Inc . [1] On September 18, 2017, Northrop Grumman announced plans to purchase Orbital ATK for US$7.8 billion in cash plus assumption of US$1.4 billion in debt. [2] Orbital ATK shareholders approved the buyout on November 29, 2017. [3] The Federal Trade Commission (FTC) approved the acquisition with conditions on June 5, 2018, and one day later, Orbital ATK were absorbed and became Northrop Grumman Innovation Systems . [4] [5] ^ Cite error: The named reference orbitalatk was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference auto was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference Northrop Grumman Corporation was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference Federal Trade Commission was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference Erwin was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_orbital-sciences_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 649. Bentley Systems (slug=bentley-systems, wiki='Bentley Systems')
