VALUES
  ('cs_bentley-systems_history', 'org_bentley-systems', 'overview', 'History',
   'American software development Not to be confused with Bentley Motors . html body Some of this article''s listed sources may not be reliable . Please help improve this article by looking for better, more reliable sources. Unreliable citations may be challenged and removed. ( February 2023 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Bentley Systems, Incorporated Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : BSY (Class B) S&amp;P 400 component Industry Computer software [1] Founded 1984 &#59;&#32;42 years ago ( 1984 ) Founders Keith A. Bentley Barry J. Bentley Raymond B. Bentley Headquarters Exton, Pennsylvania , U.S. Key people Nicholas Cumins ( CEO ) [2] Products Software Revenue US$ 1.5 billion (2025) Number of employees 5,800 (2025) Website bentley Bentley Systems, Incorporated is a US-based software development company that develops, manufactures, licenses, sells and supports computer software and services for the design , construction , and operation of infrastructure globally. The company''s software serves the building, plant, civil, and geospatial markets in the areas of architecture , engineering , construction (AEC) and operations. Their software products are used to design, engineer, build, and operate large constructed assets such as roadways , railways , bridges , buildings , industrial plants , power plants , and utility networks. Bentley Systems is headquartered in Exton, Pennsylvania , United States, but reports development, sales and other departments in 45 countries. In 2025, the company reported revenue of $1.5 billion in 189 countries. ^ Company Profile from Hoover’s: Bentley Systems, Incorporated | Company Profile from Hoover’s , Retrieved September 12, 2016 ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Bentley Systems CEO plans to grow Philadelphia presence after ''game-changer'' acquisition" . Philadelphia Business Journal . December 3, 2024.', '["clm_wiki_bentley-systems_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
