  ('cs_bentley-systems_operations', 'org_bentley-systems', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History body >div:not( ) body >div:not( ) Retired logo and wordmark Keith A. Bentley and Barry J. Bentley founded Bentley Systems in 1984. [1] In an interview with trade publication Geo Week News, Keith Bentley recounted how he had previously developed CAD software while working as a programmer at DuPont. [2] After retaining rights to this software, he joined his brother Barry''s chemistry software startup, and they later pivoted to the CAD software market. [2] Their brothers Greg, Scott, and Ray later joined the company, which relocated to Pennsylvania. [3] They introduced the commercial version of PseudoStation in 1985, which allowed users of Intergraph ''s VAX systems to use low-cost graphics terminals to view and modify the designs on their Intergraph IGDS (Interactive Graphics Design System) installations. [4] An MS-DOS version of MicroStation was introduced in 1986. [5] In April 2002, Bentley filed for an initial public offering , [6] but it was withdrawn before taking effect. [7] In November 2016, German-based Siemens announced it would pay about $76 million for a minority stake in Bentley, as well as invest in developing joint software with it. [8] In September 2020, Bentley Systems set terms of its IPO valuing the company at about $4.96 billion. The company would offer 10.75 million shares priced between $17 and $19 per share. [9] [10] In 2023, the company reported that its annual 2022 revenue exceeded $1 billion. [11] Also in 2023, Keith Bentley retired from his Chief Technology role, [12] and Greg Bentley retired in March 2024. [13] In July 2024, Chief Operating Officer Nicholas Cumins became the first non-family member to lead the company as CEO. [12] ^ Section 10: CAD/CAM/CAE/CADD: Section 10: CAD/CAM/CAE/CADD Archived April 4, 2016, at the Wayback Machine , accessdate: September 14, 2016 ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "A conversation with Bentley Systems co-founder Keith Bentley &#124; Geo Week News" . www . ^ "Bentley Goes Public- Finally" . October 5, 2020. ', '["clm_wiki_bentley-systems_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
