  ('cs_adtran_history', 'org_adtran', 'overview', 'History',
   'American telecommunications equipment company Adtran, Inc. Headquarters – Huntsville, Alabama, United States Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : ADTN FWB : QH9 SDAX component ISIN US00486H1059 Industry Telecommunications Fiber Networking Voice and Data Equipment Founded 1985 &#59;&#32;41 years ago ( 1985 ) [1] Headquarters Huntsville , Alabama , [2] US Key people Tom Stanton ( CEO ) Revenue US$ 1.08 Billion ( FY 2025 ) [3] Operating income US$ -15.6 Million (up from -$427.6 Million in FY 2024) ( FY 2025 ) [3] Net income US$ -45.7 Million (up from -US$459.9 Million in FY 2024) ( FY 2025 ) [3] Total assets US$ 1.2 Billion ( FY 2025 ) [3] Total equity US$ 145.8 Million (up from $126.9 Million in FY 2024) ( FY 2025 ) [3] Number of employees 3,338 [4] Parent ADTRAN Holding Website adtran Adtran, Inc. is an American fiber networking and telecommunications company headquartered in Huntsville , Alabama . It is a vendor of both residential and enterprise networking equipment, along with administrative software for network management and deployment. Its customers include communications service providers, governments, enterprises and utilities. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "ADTRAN, Inc. (ADTN) Company Profile &amp; Facts – Yahoo Finance" . ^ About Us ; TBE website; retrieved April 25, 2007 ^ a b c d e "ADTRAN Holdings, Inc. 2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" (PDF) . ADTRAN Holdings, Inc. February 26, 2026 . Retrieved 2026-07-08 . ^ "ADTRAN Holdings, Inc. 2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" (PDF) . ADTRAN Holdings, Inc. February 26, 2026. p. 19 . Retrieved 2026-07-08 .', '["clm_wiki_adtran_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
