  ('cs_ziprecruiter_history', 'org_ziprecruiter', 'overview', 'History',
   'Online employment marketplace ZipRecruiter, Inc. Type of site Public Traded as NYSE : ZIP Founded March 14, 2010 &#59;&#32;16 years ago ( March 14, 2010 ) Headquarters Santa Monica, California Founder(s) Ian Siegel Joe Edmonds Ward Poulos Will Redd Key people Ian Siegel ( CEO ) Industry Employment websites Revenue US$ 418.1 million (2020) [1] Employees 1,000 [2] URL ziprecruiter ZipRecruiter headquarters in Santa Monica ZipRecruiter, Inc. is an American employment marketplace for job seekers and employers. [3] [4] [5] [6] [7] [8] The company is headquartered in Santa Monica, California , [9] with offices in Tempe, Arizona ; [10] London, UK, and Tel Aviv , Israel. [11] [12] [13] [14] ^ ZipRecruiter files for direct listing on NYSE: 2020 saw profitability despite 3% decrease in revenue - AIM Group ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Forbes Companies" . Forbes . Retrieved 17 May 2019 . ^ "Growth spurt pushes ZipRecruiter into bigger digs" . American City Business Journals . 13 June 2018 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ Bonn, Tess (2018-09-20). "ZipRecruiter CEO downplays threat of artificial intelligence on job market" . The Hill . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ Libassi, Matthew (2016-08-23). "ZipRecruiter: From the Kitchen Table to the Big Time" . FOXBusiness . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "For job seekers, search is out, ''curation'' is in" . USA TODAY . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter announces AI tool that matches businesses with ideal job candidates" . VentureBeat . 2018-06-14. Archived from the original on 2020-12-04 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ King, Peter (February 10, 2019). "These apps can aid in your job search" . Newsday . Archived from the original on October 16, 2019 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ Schleifer, Theodore (2018-02-06). "ZipRecruiter is raising money for the first time in almost four years" . Recode . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter hiring more than 200 in Tempe" . American City Business Journals . 30 January 2017 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ Danney, Micah. "Israel tech team grows as it drives US jobs site expansion" . The Times of Israel . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter expands in Tempe, continues hiring" . USA TODAY . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "Northern Virginia Media Services partners with ZipRecruiter" . INSIDENOVA.COM . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ Orbach, Meir (2018-05-29). "ZipRecruiter Expands Israeli Research and Development Center" . CTECH - www . Retrieved 2019-03-05 .', '["clm_wiki_ziprecruiter_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
