VALUES
  ('cs_ziprecruiter_leadership', 'org_ziprecruiter', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Funding ZipRecruiter delayed raising venture capital until 2014, when the company''s first round of financing of $63 million was led by IVP. [1] In October 2018, the company raised $156 million for its online employment marketplace, which brought its total funding to $219 million. [2] [3] Blake Irving , Cipora Herman, and Emilie Choi were added as new members to its board. [4] The October 2018 raise was at a valuation of $1 billion. [5] [6] [7] [8] [9] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Gage, Deborah (2014-08-26). "ZipRecruiter Raises $63M To Make Jobs Easier to Find and Fill" . The Wall Street Journal . ISSN 0099-9660 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter now valued at $1.5 billion" . bizjournals . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter picks up $156M, now at a $1B valuation, for its AI-based job-finding marketplace" . TechCrunch . 4 October 2018 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter adds ex-Facebook, LinkedIn, GoDaddy execs to board" . The Business Journals . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ Dignan, Larry. "ZipRecruiter raises $156 million in VC funding and here''s where AI fits" . ZDNet . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter Is Valued at $1.5 Billion in a Bet on AI Hiring" . Bloomberg . 2018-10-04 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter Raises $156 Million | Los Angeles Business Journal" . Los Angeles Business Journal . 4 October 2018 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ "ZipRecruiter raises $156 million to match job candidates with employers" . VentureBeat . 2018-10-04. Archived from the original on 2019-02-06 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 . ^ Geron, Tomio (2018-10-04). "ZipRecruiter Raises $156 Million at Valuation Above $1 Billion" . The Wall Street Journal . ISSN 0099-9660 . Retrieved 2019-03-05 .', '["clm_wiki_ziprecruiter_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
