VALUES
  ('cs_american-water-works_leadership', 'org_american-water-works', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisitions and mergers American Water Works In July 2025, the company announced an agreement to acquire certain assets from Nexus Water Group, which operates in eight states and has about 87,000 customer connections under agreement. [1] In October 2025, the company agreed to acquire Essential Utilities in an all-stock merger. Upon completion of the deal, expected in early 2027, [2] [3] Current American Water shareholders would own about 69% of the combined company, with former Essential shareholders owning the remainder. [4] California American Water In July 2017, California American Water acquired the Oxbow Marina Mutual Water Company in Sacramento. [5] In February 2020, the company acquired the operating assets of Fruitridge Vista Water Company, becoming the water provider for approximately 4,800 customers. [6] In September 2021, the company acquired East Pasadena Water Co., a family-owned utility serving homes and businesses in Pasadena . [7] In September 2022, the company acquired Warring Water Services, Inc., a privately owned water utility in Piru, California, for $4.6 million. [8] In February 2025, the company completed its acquisition of the West San Martin Water Works system assets for $1.6 million. [9] In May 2025, the company acquired the Mesa Del Sol water system in the Corral de Tierra area of Salinas . [10] In August 2025, the company completed its acquisition of the Bass Lake Water Company system. [11] Illinois American Water In July 2017, Illinois American Water acquired the Forest Homes–Maple Park Public Water District. [12] In September 2017, the company acquired the Piasa Township Sanitary District. [13] In November 2019, the company acquired the Village of Godfrey ''s wastewater system, adding approximately 6,200 wastewater customers to its Southern Illinois service area. [14] In October 2020, the company acquired the City of Jerseyville ''s water and wastewater systems for $43.25 million. [15] In December 2022, the company acquired the water dis', '["clm_wiki_american-water-works_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
