  ('cs_american-water-works_operations', 'org_american-water-works', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'American Water Works In July 2025, the company announced an agreement to acquire certain assets from Nexus Water Group, which operates in eight states and has about 87,000 customer connections under agreement. [1] In October 2025, the company agreed to acquire Essential Utilities in an all-stock merger. Upon completion of the deal, expected in early 2027, [2] [3] Current American Water shareholders would own about 69% of the combined company, with former Essential shareholders owning the remainder. [4] ^ Cite error: The named reference :02 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) Cone, Alan (27 October 2025). "American Water, Essential to merge as utility worth $40B" . UPI . Retrieved 19 November 2025 . ^ Litvak, Anya (October 27, 2025). "American Water and Essential Utilities to combine, leaving fate of Peoples Natural Gas uncertain" . Pittsburgh Post-Gazette . Retrieved 19 November 2025 . ^ "American Water to fortify US presence with Essential Utilities deal" . Reuters. October 27, 2025.', '["clm_wiki_american-water-works_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
