VALUES
  ('cs_equinix_operations', 'org_equinix', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Environmental impacts In 2015, Equinix announced a long-term commitment to power its data centers with clean, renewable energy . [1] The announcement followed criticism from the environmental group Greenpeace in 2014, which said in a report on internet companies’ environmental practices that Equinix was not doing enough to address renewable energy use or carbon emissions . [2] In response, the company signed agreements with wind farms in Texas and Oklahoma to purchase renewable energy to offset electricity use at its North American data centers. [3] In September 2020, Equinix issued $1.35 billion in green bonds to help fund environmental projects. [4] At the same time, the company introduced a Green Finance Framework to describe how it reports on and tracks projects funded through green debt. [5] [6] In January 2021, Equinix joined the Climate Neutral Data Centre Pact , committing to make their data centers climate neutral by 2030. [7] In 2024, the company expanded a heat export program that redirects excess heat from its data centers to nearby buildings. [8] [9] That year, Equinix vice president Christopher Wellise said that rising energy use from AI was increasing strain on electrical grids . and that AI development needed to be considered with sustainability in mind. [10] Equinix’s environmental efforts have been recognized by external organizations. The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) named the company a Green Power Partner in 2019 and 2020. [11] [12] [13] [14] In May 2026, Equinix faced challenges from social movement the Housing Assembly (HA) and UK non-profit Foxglove regarding the company''s plans to build two data centers in Cape Town , South Africa. A formal objection from city planners said the plans should not be approved without Equinix disclosing its water, power, and environmental impacts. [15] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Ian Murphy (December 2015). "Equinix makes climate pledge" . Enterprise Times. Archived from the original on August 19, 2022 . R', '["clm_wiki_equinix_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 664. Evergy (slug=evergy, wiki='Evergy')
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
