VALUES
  ('cs_fiserv_history', 'org_fiserv', 'overview', 'History',
   'Provider of financial services technology to banks html body This article may contain excessive or inappropriate references to self-published sources . Please help improve it by removing references to unreliable sources where they are used inappropriately. ( April 2014 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Fiserv, Inc. Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : FISV S&amp;P 500 component Founded 1984 &#59;&#32;42 years ago ( 1984 ) Headquarters Milwaukee , Wisconsin, U.S. Key people Takis Georgakopoulos ( president and CEO ) Paul Todd ( CFO and Treasurer) Revenue US$ 20.5 billion (2024) Operating income US$5.88 billion (2024) Net income US$3.13 billion (2024) Total assets US$77.2 billion (2024) Total equity US$27.1 billion (2024) Owner KKR &amp; Co. (12%) Number of employees c. &#8201;38,000 (2024) Website www Footnotes [1] [2] Fiserv, Inc. ( / f aɪ ˈ s ɜːr v / fy- SURV ) is an American multinational financial technology company headquartered in Milwaukee , Wisconsin. [3] The company processes debit and credit card transactions, loyalty programs, loans, electronic bill pay, wires and ACH transfers, check deposits, and ATM transactions on behalf of banking institutions. [1] The company also produces debit and credit cards and point of sale terminals. [1] [4] Customers primarily include companies in the financial services sector, including banks, savings and loan associations , credit unions , securities broker dealers, mortgage , insurance, leasing and finance companies, and retailers. [1] In 2024, 85% of the company''s revenues were from the U.S. and Canada, while 15% of revenues were from other countries. [1] Processing represented 81% of revenues and products, including software, hardware, and physical cards, represented 19% of revenue. [1] The company is ranked 208th on the Fortune 500 [5] and 269th on the Forbes Global 2000 . [6] ^ a b c d e f body:not( ):not( ) "Fiserv, Inc. 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . United States Securities and Exchange Commission . February 20, 2025. ^ "SEC FORM 13-D Information Table" . sec . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . ^ McLaughlin, Kaylie (April 22, 2025). "Fiserv, Milwaukee-based financial firm, could get incentives to open office at OP''s Aspiria" . Johnson County Post . ^ Pandey, Maia (September 3, 2025). "Which Wisconsin companies rely the most on H-1B visas? What to know amid Trump''s new order" . Journal Sentinel . ^ "Fiserv" . Fortune . ^ "Fiserv" . Forbes .', '["clm_wiki_fiserv_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
