VALUES
  ('cs_fiserv_leadership', 'org_fiserv', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1980s and 1990s Fiserv was founded in 1984, and within two years, it was listed on NASDAQ . The company experienced rapid growth mainly due to a series of acquisitions, including Citicorp Information Resources, a subsidiary of Citicorp , which was the largest acquisition in its early years. This acquisition put Fiserv into the commercial banking , internal and credit union core account processing market space. [1] In 1995, Fiserv acquired Information Technology, Inc., (ITI) of Lincoln, Nebraska. Thus, Fiserv acquired Premier, which at that time was the most widely implemented account processing platform in the US, and represented an increase in Fiserv''s account processing clients. [1] Fiserv also launched its website in 1995, and introduced fully electronic bill payment (branded as E-bills) in 1997, reaching $1 billion in revenue. [2] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Fiserv, Inc. (July 31, 2009). "Fiserv Celebrates 25th Anniversary by Remembering Founders and Serving Clients" . Fiserv (Press release) . Retrieved March 23, 2016 . ^ Fiserv, Inc. (n.d.). "About Fiserv" . Fiserv . Archived from the original on January 10, 2019 . Retrieved March 23, 2016 .', '["clm_wiki_fiserv_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
