VALUES
  ('cs_bnp-paribas_operations', 'org_bnp-paribas', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Creation of BNP Paribas Group In 1999, BNP and Société Générale fought a complex battle on the stock market, [1] with Société Générale bidding for Paribas and BNP bidding for Société Générale and counter-bidding for Paribas. BNP''s bid for Société Générale failed, while its bid for Paribas succeeded, which led to a merger of BNP and Paribas one year later on 23 May 2000. In 2006, BNP Paribas purchased Banca Nazionale del Lavoro (BNL) , Italy''s sixth-largest bank. On 9 August 2007, BNP Paribas became the first major financial group to acknowledge the impact of the sub-prime crisis by closing two funds exposed to it. This day is now generally seen as the start of the 2008 financial crisis and the bank''s quick reaction saved it from the fate of other large European banks such as UBS . [2] [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "La bataille boursière entre la BNP et SG Paribas s''achève aujourd''hui" . lesechos.fr . 6 August 1999. ^ Harry Wilson (3 August 2010). "BNP Paribas makes first asset write back since 2007" . The Telegraph . London. Archived from the original on 21 November 2011 . Retrieved 6 April 2011 . ^ Morning Zhou (9 August 2007). "Asian stocks may fall on credit woes, global sell-off" . Market Watch. Archived from the original on 7 June 2011 . Retrieved 6 April 2011 .', '["clm_wiki_bnp-paribas_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
