  ('cs_first-citizens-bancshares_history', 'org_first-citizens-bancshares', 'overview', 'History',
   '"First Citizens Bank" redirects here. For the bank in Trinidad and Tobago, see First Citizens Bank (Trinidad and Tobago) . American financial services company First Citizens BancShares, Inc. First Citizens Bank branch in Murphy, North Carolina Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : FCNCA (Class A) Russell 1000 component Industry Banking Founded 1898 &#59;&#32;128 years ago ( 1898 ) Headquarters Raleigh, North Carolina , U.S. Area served United States Key people Frank B. Holding Jr. ( CEO &amp; chairperson ) Products Commercial bank Investment bank Revenue US$ 5.55 billion (2022) Net income US$1.05 billion (2022) Total assets US$209 billion (Q2 2023) Total equity US$19.771 billion (Q2 2023) Owner Holding family Number of employees 10,375 (2022) Divisions First Citizens Bank Silicon Valley Bank Subsidiaries SVB Global Services India LLP Website firstcitizens Footnotes [1] First Citizens Bancshares, Inc. is a bank holding company based in Raleigh, North Carolina , and one of the largest banks in the United States . Its primary subsidiary is First Citizens Bank , which operates over 500 branches in 23 states. A second subsidiary is Silicon Valley Bank , which operates 39 offices in 15 states. For three generations, the bank has been led by the family of Robert Powell Holding, who joined the bank in 1918 and served as president from 1935 to 1957. [2] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "First Citizens BancShares, Inc. Second Quarter 2023 Form 10-Q Quarterly Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . August 4, 2023. ^ Cite error: The named reference Holding was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_first-citizens-bancshares_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
