   'American fintech, mortgage lending, and real estate parent company For the aerospace manufacturer, see Rocket Lab . Rocket Companies, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : RKT (Class A) Russell 1000 component Industry Financial technology Mortgage lending Real estate Founder Dan Gilbert Headquarters One Campus Martius , Detroit , Michigan , U.S. Areas served United States Canada Key people Dan Gilbert ( chairman ) Varun Krishna ( CEO ) Bill Emerson ( president ) Jonathan Mildenhall ( CMO ) Brian Brown (CFO) Heather Lovier (COO) Revenue US$5.10 billion (2024) Operating income US$255 million (2024) Net income US$29.4 million (2024) Total assets US$24.5 billion (2024) Total equity US$9.04 billion (2024) Owner Rock Holdings (93%) Number of employees 14,200 (2024) Website rocketcompanies Footnotes [1] [2] [3] [4] Rocket Companies, Inc. , is an American fintech and homeownership services company. Founded by Dan Gilbert [5] and based in Downtown Detroit , Michigan, the company is one of the largest mortgage lenders in the United States through its flagship subsidiary Rocket Mortgage (formerly known as Quicken Loans). [6] Its subsidiaries include Redfin , Forsalebyowner , and Rocket Money. [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. March 3, 2025. ^ Lambert, Lance (April 8, 2025). "Look Out, Zillow: A New Real Estate Juggernaut is Forming" . Fast Company . ^ Graham, Megan (January 4, 2024). "Rocket Cos. Hires Former Airbnb CMO Jonathan Mildenhall as Its CMO" . Wall Street Journal . ^ "Our Leadership" . Rocket Companies . Retrieved 11 October 2025 . ^ Whitman, Victor (March 11, 2025). "Seattle-based Redfin''s Sale to Rocket Could Shift Online Homebuying Market" . The Detroit News . ^ Neubauer, Kelsey (May 20, 2025). "The 10 Largest Mortgage Lenders in the U.S." CNBC . ^ Reindl, J. C. "Dan Gilbert''s deposition in lawsuit reveals reasons for $500M stock sale" . Detroit Free Press . Retrieved 2025-12-30 .', '["clm_wiki_rocket-companies_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
