  ('cs_herbalife_leadership', 'org_herbalife', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'J.H. Whitney &amp; Company and Golden Gate Capital In 2002, the company was acquired for US$685 million by J.H. Whitney &amp; Company and Golden Gate Capital . [1] Concurrently, plant sources of ephedrine were removed from Herbalife products in 2002 after several U.S. states banned supplements containing such herbs. [2] &#58;&#8202;15&#8202; [3] In April 2003, Michael O. Johnson joined Herbalife as CEO following a 17-year career with The Walt Disney Company . [4] On December 16, 2004, the company had an initial public offering on the NYSE of 14.5 million common shares at $14 per share, [5] netting the owners $1.3 billion. [6] On May 7, 2014, the company announced that it entered into a deal with Bank of America Merrill Lynch to repurchase $266 million of its stock. [7] The company announced in November 2016 that Chief Operating Officer Richard Goudis would take over the position of CEO in June 2017 and Johnson would transition to Executive Chairman. [8] In August 2017, the company announced that it would repurchase up to $600 million of its stock. [9] On April 25, 2018, Herbalife announced that it had changed its name from Herbalife Ltd. to Herbalife Nutrition Ltd. The company also announced that its shareholders had approved a two-for-one stock split. [10] [11] In January 2019, Herbalife announced that it was replacing Goudis after learning of comments he had made before taking over as CEO that were "contrary to the company’s expense-related policies and business practices” and inconsistent with the company''s standards and culture". Former CEO Johnson subsequently took over the role on an interim basis. [12] In March 2020, John Agwunobi was appointed Chief Executive Officer. [13] Agwunobi departed from Herbalife in October 2022 and Michael O. Johnson was appointed Chairman and interim Chief Executive Officer. [14] In May 2025, Stephan Gratziani was appointed Chief Executive Officer, becoming the first distributor since founder Mark Hughes to lead the company. Micha', '["clm_wiki_herbalife_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
