  ('cs_people_history', 'org_people', 'overview', 'History',
   'American media and internet company Not to be confused with the subsidiary People Inc. . For the non-profit in Western New York providing services to seniors, see People Inc. (Western New York) . People Incorporated IAC Building in New York City Formerly Silver King Broadcasting Company, Inc. HSN Inc. (1996–1998) USA Networks Inc. (1998–2002) USA Interactive (2002–2003) InterActiveCorp (2003–2004) IAC/InterActiveCorp (2004–2022) IAC Inc. (2022–2026) Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : PPLI Russell 1000 component S&amp;P 600 component ISIN US44891N2080 [1] Industry Conglomerate Predecessors Silver King Communications Founded July 28, 1986 &#59;&#32;40 years ago ( 1986-07-28 ) Headquarters IAC Building , New York City , United States Area served Worldwide Key people Barry Diller ( chairman ) Products Mass media Casinos Resorts Car rental Revenue US$ 2.39 billion (2025) Operating income − US$97 million (2025) Net income − US$104 million (2025) Total assets US$7.13 billion (2025) Total equity US$4.73 billion (2025) Number of employees 5,156 (2025) Subsidiaries People Inc. MGM Resorts International (26.1%) Turo Inc. (33%) Website people-incorporated Footnotes [2] People Incorporated [3] is an American conglomerate that owns People Inc. , Vivian Health, The Daily Beast , IAC Films, 26.1% of MGM Resorts International (with a proposal of a complete acquisition), and 31% of Turo . [2] The company was founded in 1986 as Silver King Broadcasting Company and in 1996 became HSN Inc., the holding company of Home Shopping Network . In 1998, the company acquired USA Network and changed its name to USA Networks, Inc. It sold its television assets to Vivendi in 2002 and changed its name to USA Interactive . The company changed its name to InterActiveCorp , and later to IAC/InterActiveCorp in 2004. In 2012, the company acquired About and changed its name to IAC Inc. In June 2026, the company changed its name to People Incorporated. The company is organized in Delaware with principal executive offices in New York City. [2] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Deutsche Börse Xetra - XFRA : ISIN Change" . Retrieved April 12, 2025 . ^ a b c "IAC: 2025 Form 10-K Annual Report" . United States Securities and Exchange Commission . February 20, 2026. ^ Cite error: The named reference people was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_people_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
