  ('cs_people_operations', 'org_people', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '2000s In May 2001, Univision Communications acquired USA Broadcasting , a division of USA Networks including 13 local stations. [1] The next year, Vivendi bought the rest of USA''s television entertainment businesses, including the USA Network and Sci-Fi Channel. [2] This led to the creation of a new company named Vivendi Universal Entertainment , led by Diller. [3] In July 2001, the company entered the online travel business with its acquisition of Expedia , [4] followed the next year by the acquisition of Interval International . [5] In May 2002, following the shift in focus to online assets, the company changed its name to USA Interactive ( USAI ). [6] It was renamed InterActiveCorp in June 2003. [7] It was renamed IAC/InterActiveCorp in July 2004. [8] In August 2003, IAC acquired LendingTree for $734 million in stock. [9] In September 2003, the company acquired Hotwire for $685 million. [10] [11] In October 2003, IAC agreed to buy French travel site Anyway from Transat A.T. for $62.7 million. [12] [13] In March 2004, the company acquired Tripadvisor for $212 million. [14] [15] In August 2004, the company acquired ServiceMagic . [16] In March 2005, it acquired Ask Jeeves for $1.85 billion in stock. [17] [18] [19] Also in March 2005, it launched Gifts . [20] In August 2005, the company bundled together its travel-related sites and spun them off as a new public company, Expedia, Inc. [21] In January 2006, the company acquired ShoeBuy for an undisclosed sum, [22] which the company sold to Jet for $70 million in January 2017. [23] In August 2006, the company acquired a controlling stake in Connected Ventures, owner of CollegeHumor and Vimeo , for $21 million. [24] In September 2007, IAC acquired a majority stake in GarageGames . [25] In May 2008, IAC and Ask acquired Lexico , the owner of Dictionary , Thesaurus , and Reference , for approximately $100 million in cash. [26] In August 2008, IAC spun off several of its businesses, including: Tree (formerly LendingTree), ', '["clm_wiki_people_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
