  ('cs_janus-capital_history', 'org_janus-capital', 'overview', 'History',
   'Former American publicly owned investment firm headquartered in Denver, Colorado Janus Capital Group Inc. Type Public company Traded as NYSE : JHG (formerly) Industry Financial Founded 1969 &#59;&#32;57 years ago ( 1969 ) Founder Thomas H. Bailey Fate merged with Henderson Group , forming Janus Henderson in 2017 Headquarters Denver , Colorado , United States Revenue $1,076 million (2015) [1] AUM $190.9 billion (2016) [1] Number of employees 1,272 (2016) [1] Website www Janus Capital Group, Inc. was an American publicly owned investment firm headquartered in Denver, Colorado . It was founded by Thomas H. Bailey as Stilwell Financial Incorporated in 1969. Outside the U.S., Janus had offices in Sydney , Paris , Zürich , Frankfurt , Dubai , Taipei , London , Milan , Tokyo , Hong Kong , Melbourne , and Singapore . It was a constituent of the S&amp;P MidCap 400 Index. [2] It merged with Henderson Group in May 2017 to create Janus Henderson . ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) "Annual Report, Format 10-K, 2015" . Janus Capital Group Inc. Archived from the original on 20 October 2016 . Retrieved 19 October 2016 . ^ CNBC (3 October 2016). "S&amp;P Indices Announces Changes to U.S. Indices" . Prnewswire . Retrieved 2016-10-25 .', '["clm_wiki_janus-capital_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
