  ('cs_albemarle-inc_operations', 'org_albemarle-inc', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History In February 1994, Ethyl Corporation completed the corporate spin-off of its chemical businesses to form Albemarle Corporation. [1] Albemarle was headquartered in Richmond, Virginia , until 2008 when it announced plans to move its corporate headquarters to Baton Rouge, Louisiana . [2] In July 1994, the company acquired the Asano Corporation, a sales and marketing company headquartered in Tokyo, Japan . [1] In 1998, the company bought a custom manufacturing and oilfield chemicals plant in Teesport , England . Also in 1998, a joint venture was signed by the company, Jordan Dead Sea Industries Company, and Arab Potash . [3] In January 2000, the company acquired Ferro Corporation ''s PYRO-CHEK flame retardant business. [4] In June 2000, the company formed a joint venture with Jinhai Chemical and Industry Company, based in China . [5] In August 2000, the company launched PolymerAdditives , a business-to-business internet joint venture with Cytec Industries and General Electric to provide materials faster and more efficiently directly from trusted suppliers. [5] [6] In 2001, it acquired Martinswerk GmbH, which it sold in 2016. [7] It also acquired the custom and fine chemicals businesses of ChemFirst Inc. for $74 million. [8] In 2003, it acquired the fuel and lubricant antioxidants business of Ethyl Corporation. [9] It also acquired the phosphorus-based polyurethane flame retardants businesses of Rhodia. [10] It also acquired the bromine fine chemicals business of Atofina S.A. [11] In January 2004, the company acquired Asian flame retardants distributor Taerim International based in Seoul , South Korea . [12] In July 2004, Albemarle acquired the refinery catalysts platform from AkzoNobel , with sites and/or joint ventures in the Netherlands, Houston , France, Brazil , Japan and Singapore , for €615.7 million. [2] [13] [14] In 2006, in partnership with UOP, a subsidiary of Honeywell , Albemarle created the Hydroprocessing Alliance to deliver integrated refinery solut', '["clm_wiki_albemarle-inc_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
