   'American information technology company "CTSH" redirects here. For the gene, see Cathepsin H . Cognizant Technology Solutions Corporation Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : CTSH (Class A) S&amp;P 500 component ISIN US1924461023 Industry Information technology Consulting Outsourcing Predecessor Dun &amp; Bradstreet Founded 26 January 1994 &#59;&#32;32 years ago ( 1994-01-26 ) in Chennai , Tamil Nadu , India [1] Founders Kumar Mahadeva [2] [3] Headquarters Teaneck, New Jersey , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Ravi Kumar Singisetti ( CEO ) Revenue US$ 21.108 billion (2025) [4] Operating income US$3.389 billion (2025) [4] Net income US$2.230 billion (2025) [4] Total assets US$20.692 billion (2025) [4] Total equity US$15.015 billion (2025) [4] Number of employees 349,800 (September 2025) [4] Website cognizant Cognizant Technology Solutions Corporation is an American domiciled Indian multinational information technology services and outsourcing company, headquartered in Teaneck, New Jersey . It was originally founded in Chennai , India, as an in-house technology unit of Dun &amp; Bradstreet in 1994. [5] After a series of corporate restructurings, the company went public in 1998. [6] Ravi Kumar Singisetti has been the CEO of the company since January 2023, replacing Brian Humphries . [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Cognizant opens new facility in Chennai for hybrid work" . The Economic Times . Archived from the original on August 28, 2022 . Retrieved August 28, 2022 . ^ "Cognizant founder Mahadeva to retire" . Economic Times . December 22, 2003. Archived from the original on June 13, 2018 . Retrieved June 4, 2018 . ^ "Cognizant''s co-founder to step down from board" . Livemint. February 6, 2020. Archived from the original on July 29, 2020 . Retrieved July 29, 2020 . ^ a b c d e f "2025 Annual Report" (PDF) . Cognizant Technology Solutions Corporation . Retrieved March 6, 2025 . ^ Mishra, Pankaj (March 21, 2013). "Cognizant''s Francisco D''Souza: The horizon chaser" . Archived from the original on August 15, 2022 . Retrieved July 30, 2013 . ^ Newswires, Dow Jones (June 20, 1998). "Cognizant, Interplay IPOs Meet With Weak Demand" . The Wall Street Journal . ISSN 0099-9660 . Archived from the original on August 15, 2022 . Retrieved January 2, 2020 . ^ Chennai, BL (January 12, 2023). "Cognizant appoints former Infosys president Prayag P as CEO, succeeds Brian Humphries" . BusinessLine . Retrieved November 3, 2023 .', '["clm_wiki_cognizant_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
