VALUES
  ('cs_coherent_leadership', 'org_coherent', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'History Coherent was founded as II-VI Incorporated in 1971 by Carl Johnson and James Hawkey. [1] [2] The name "II-VI" is a reference to the groups II and VI in the periodic table , since the company started its business by producing cadmium telluride ( cadmium belongs to group II and tellurium belongs to group VI ). [3] The company''s first products included lenses, windows, and mirrors for CO 2 lasers . [1] The company held its initial public offering in 1987. [1] According to Carl Johnson, the funds raised by the IPO allowed II-VI to expand its zinc selenide manufacturing capacity. [1] In the 1990s, the company began to grow both on its own and through acquisitions. [1] It purchased Litton Systems'' silicon carbide group from Northrop Grumman in the 1990s, [1] Virgo Optics in 1995, [4] and Lightning Optical Corporation in 1996, [4] among others. The combination of Virgo and Lightning created II-VI''s VLOC division for developing one-micron solid-state lasers. [4] Acquisitions in the 2000s have included Laser Power Optics in 2000; Marlow Industries in 2004; [5] HIGHYAG (75% in 2007 [6] and the remaining 25% in 2013); Photop Technologies in 2010; [7] Oclaro''s Santa Rosa, California, optics coating facility in 2012; Anadigics and EpiWorks in 2016; [8] and Integrated Photonics in 2017. [9] [4] The acquisition of Avalon Photonics, Anadigics, and EpiWorks allowed II-VI to increase its production of vertical-cavity surface-emitting lasers (VCSELs), [4] important to 3D sensing technology; and the acquisition of Finisar Corporation in 2019 brought to II-VI Finisar''s high volume 3DS VCSELs indium phosphide (InP) platform and its experience in integrating InP lasers with optics and electronics in transceivers. [4] Acquisitions of INNOViON, Ascatron, and some of GE''s patents have expanded its business in silicon carbide substrates. [4] In 2022, II-VI acquired laser manufacturer Coherent, Inc. . [10] and took the name Coherent Corp. Carl Johnson served as II-VI''s first CEO from 1', '["clm_wiki_coherent_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
