  ('cs_coherent_operations', 'org_coherent', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Locations and facilities Coherent Corp. is headquartered in Saxonburg, Pennsylvania , [1] located north of Pittsburgh in Butler County . The company has R&amp;D, manufacturing, sales, service, and distribution facilities in 130 locations worldwide. [2] The Saxonburg headquarters site was once the property of KDKA , the world''s first commercially licensed radio station, and some of the original structures are still there. [3] In the 1940s, the site was expanded by the Carnegie Institute of Technology and the U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission to become a 400 MeV synchrocyclotron research facility. [4] II-VI acquired the property around 1978 and has further expanded the facility over the years. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Local laser optics company introduces new systems" . www . June 4, 2019 . Retrieved 2019-09-12 . ^ "Form 10-K Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. August 18, 2023. ^ "II-VI: Milestones of its first leader" . Retrieved March 22, 2022 . ^ a b "II-VI: Milestones of its first leader" .', '["clm_wiki_coherent_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
