  ('cs_corteva_history', 'org_corteva', 'overview', 'History',
   'American agriculture company Corteva, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : CTVA S&amp;P 500 component ISIN US22052L1044 Industry Agricultural chemicals Predecessors Dow AgroSciences E. I. du Pont de Nemours and Company (legal) Founded March 2018 &#59;&#32;8 years ago ( 2018-03 ) Headquarters Indianapolis, Indiana , U.S. Key people Chuck Magro ( CEO ) Revenue US$ 17.401 billion (2025) Operating income US$1.204 billion (2025) Net income US$1.105 billion (2025) Total assets US$42.845 billion (2025) Total equity US$24.144 billion (2025) Number of employees 21,500 (2025) Parent DowDuPont (2018–2019) Subsidiaries Pioneer Hi-Bred International Website corteva Footnotes [1] Corteva, Inc. (also known as Corteva Agriscience ) is an American company devoted to products for seeds and crop protection, [1] including herbicides , insecticides , fungicides , and biologicals (natural herbicides) that are sold in 110 countries. [1] The company''s name combines "cor" (Latin for "heart") with "teva" (the Hebrew word for nature). [2] It is headquartered in Indianapolis, Indiana . Its primary brand is Pioneer Hi-Bred International . ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) "2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . United States Securities and Exchange Commission . February 12, 2026. ^ "Brand Positioning &amp; Purpose" . Presciant . Retrieved August 6, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_corteva_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
