  ('cs_deckers-brands_history', 'org_deckers-brands', 'overview', 'History',
   'American consumer retail company "DECK" redirects here. For other uses, see Deck . Deckers Outdoor Corporation Headquarters in Goleta, California Type Public Traded as NYSE : DECK S&amp;P 500 component Founded 1973 &#59;&#32;53 years ago ( 1973 ) Founders Karl F. Lopker Doug Otto Headquarters Goleta, California , U.S. 34°25′47″N 119°51′43″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 34.4296°N 119.86202°W &#xfeff; / 34.4296; -119.86202 Number of locations 179 (2025) Area served Worldwide Key people Michael Devine III (Chairman) Stefano Caroti (CEO) Products Footwear, apparel, and accessories Revenue US$ 4.99 billion (2025) Operating income US$1.18 billion (2025) Net income US$966 million (2025) Total assets US$3.57 billion (2025) Total equity US$2.51 billion (2025) Number of employees 5,500 (2025) Subsidiaries Hoka Koolaburra Teva UGG Website deckers Footnotes Financials as of March 31,&#32;2025 &#91;update&#93; . [1] Deckers Outdoor Corporation , doing business as Deckers Brands , is an American footwear designer and distributor founded in 1973 and based in Goleta, California . The company''s portfolio of brands includes UGG , Teva, and Hoka . It was founded by Doug Otto and Karl F. Lopker . [2] [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "FY 2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. May 23, 2025. ^ Leff, Lisa (February 16, 1997). "Money, Fame And Family" . The Los Angeles Times . Retrieved October 14, 2014 . ^ Olsen, Patricia R. (January 23, 2010). "The Joy of a Family Shop" . The New York Times . Retrieved October 14, 2014 .', '["clm_wiki_deckers-brands_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
