VALUES
  ('cs_edwards-lifesciences_operations', 'org_edwards-lifesciences', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History The Starr-Edwards caged ball valve. Edwards Lifesciences was originally founded by electrical engineer Miles "Lowell" Edwards in 1958, a graduate of Oregon State University . [1] Edwards invented the first medically proven and adopted artificial heart valve . Dr. Albert Starr , a surgeon at the Oregon Health and Sciences University , is credited as the first to successfully implant the Starr-Edwards mitral valve in a patient in 1960. [2] As a result of the successful heart implant, Edwards established manufacturing in Santa Ana, California the same year to continue his research in pulmonary devices. [3] Edwards'' valves are still in operation today. An early patient lived a record 48 years with the implant before requiring a replacement. [4] Edwards was acquired by Baxter in 1985. It was spun off from Baxter in 2000. [5] In 2017, Edwards completed the acquisition of Valtech Cardio for $340 million. [6] Also in 2017, Edwards acquired Harpoon Medical of Baltimore , Maryland for $100 million. Harpoon, founded in 2013, developed a minimally invasive heart surgery product for mitral valve repair [7] to treat degenerative mitral regurgitation . At the time of the acquisition, the product was not available on any market. [8] On April 18, 2019, Edwards completed the acquisition of CAS Medical Systems of Branford , Connecticut for ~$100 million. [9] Edwards Sapien 3 and Sapien 3 Ultra Transcatheter Heart Valve systems were FDA -approved for the treatment of patients at low risk for death or major complications associated with open-heart surgery on August 16, 2019. [10] These products are used to treat patients with severe aortic stenosis without utilizing open-heart surgery . [11] In 2020, Edwards co-sponsored the Virtual ISPOR - FDA Summit centered on patient preference information in medical device regulatory decisions. [12] In December 2021, the FDA approved the SAPIEN 3 transcatheter valve in combination with the Alterra adaptive prestent for the treatment of seve', '["clm_wiki_edwards-lifesciences_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 763. Equifax (slug=equifax, wiki='Equifax')
