VALUES
  ('cs_firstenergy_history', 'org_firstenergy', 'overview', 'History',
   'American electric utility FirstEnergy Corp. The FirstEnergy Building, the company’s former headquarters in Akron, Ohio Type Public Traded as NYSE : FE DJUA component S&amp;P 500 component Industry Electric Utility Predecessors Ohio Edison Centerior Energy Founded November 7, 1997 &#59;&#32;28 years ago ( 1997-11-07 ) Headquarters Akron, Ohio , United States Area served 6 million customers within 65,000 square miles (170,000 km 2 ) of Ohio , Pennsylvania , West Virginia , Maryland , and New Jersey (as of June, 2012) Key people Brian X. Tierney ( CEO ) Products Electricity generation, transmission and distribution, energy management, other energy-related services Revenue US$ 13.472 billion (2024) Operating income US$2.375 billion (2024) Net income US$1.127 billion (2024) Total assets US$52.044 billion (2024) Total equity US$13.72 billion (2024) Number of employees 12,294 (2024) Divisions GPU Inc. Allegheny Energy Website firstenergycorp Footnotes [1] [2] FirstEnergy Corp. is an electric utility headquartered in Akron, Ohio . It was established when Ohio Edison merged with Centerior Energy in 1997. Its subsidiaries and affiliates are involved in distributing, transmitting, and generating electricity, energy management, and other energy-related services. Its ten electric utility operating companies comprise one of the United States'' largest investor-owned utilities , based on serving 6 million customers within a 65,000-square-mile (170,000 km 2 ) area of Ohio , Pennsylvania , West Virginia , Virginia , Maryland , New Jersey , and New York . [3] In 2018, FirstEnergy ranked 219 on the Fortune 500 list of the largest public corporations in the United States by revenue. [4] FirstEnergy has 3599.15 MW of energy generation capacity, including coal, hydropower, and solar. [5] In 2020, FirstEnergy Corp. completed the separation of its competitive, commodity-exposed generation business—later organized as Energy Harbor (later acquired by Vistra Corp. [6] )—to concentrate on its regulated utility operations. The move followed several years of restructuring, including the 2018 bankruptcy of its generation subsidiary. [7] ^ Cite error: The named reference firstenergycorp was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) "2024 10-K/A" (PDF) . sec . February 27, 2025 . Retrieved March 10, 2025 . ^ Kulkarni, Vineet (December 22, 2015). "FirstEnergy Relies Heavily on Coal for Power Generation - Market Realist" . Market Realist . Retrieved April 12, 2016 ', '["clm_wiki_firstenergy_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
