  ('cs_generac_history', 'org_generac', 'overview', 'History',
   'American industrial company For the communes in France , see Générac (disambiguation) . Generac Holdings Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : GNRC S&amp;P 500 component Industry Manufacturing Founded 1959 &#59;&#32;67 years ago ( 1959 ) [1] Founder Robert Kern [2] Headquarters Waukesha, Wisconsin , U.S. [3] [4] Key people Aaron Jagdfeld (CEO) [3] Products Generators Revenue US$4.29 billion (2024) [5] Operating income US$537 million (2024) [5] Net income US$316 million (2024) [5] Total assets US$5.11 billion (2024) [5] Total equity US$2.50 billion (2024) [5] Number of employees 9,239 (2024) [5] Website generac Generac Holdings Inc. , commonly referred to as Generac (derived from a combination of generating and AC ), is an American manufacturer of backup power generation products for residential, light commercial, and industrial markets. [6] Generac''s power systems range in output from 800 watts to 9 megawatts [7] and are available through independent dealers, retailers, and wholesalers. [6] Generac has headquarters in Waukesha, Wisconsin , [3] [4] and manufacturing facilities in Berlin , Oshkosh , Jefferson , Eagle , and Whitewater , all in Wisconsin. [7] ^ Generac Power Systems – About Us ^ Generac workers get a holiday surprise – JSOnline ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) Tom Daykin (November 7, 2011), "Generac to add over 400 jobs at Wisconsin plants" , Milwaukee Journal Sentinel , JSOnline ^ a b HQ may now be based in Genesee, Wisconsin according to more recent publication: Jeff Engel (October 29, 2012), "Hurricane Sandy puts Wisconsin generator makers into overdrive" , Milwaukee Business Journal , bizjournals , retrieved October 30, 2012 ^ a b c d e f "2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. February 19, 2025. ^ a b "Generac Holdings Inc (GNRC.N) Company Profile – Reuters " . Reuters . &#91; dead link &#93; ^ a b 2010 Generac Holdings Annual report', '["clm_wiki_generac_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
