   'Independent aerospace manufacturer and defense contractor Honeywell Aerospace Inc. Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : HONA Nasdaq-100 component S&amp;P 100 component S&amp;P 500 component Industry Aerospace Founded 1936 &#59;&#32;90 years ago ( 1936 ) Headquarters Phoenix, Arizona , United States Key people Jim Currier ( President &amp; CEO ) Josh Jepsen ( CFO ) Products Aircraft engines , Avionics , satellites , spacecraft , black boxes Revenue US$15 billion (2024) Number of employees c. &#8201;40,000 Parent Honeywell (until June 29, 2026) Website www Honeywell Aerospace Inc. is an independent American manufacturer of aircraft engines , avionics , [1] auxiliary power units (APUs), and other aviation systems. Headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona , it operates as one of the world''s largest standalone tier-1 aerospace and defense suppliers. The company generates approximately $15 billion in annual revenue from a balanced portfolio of commercial and military defense contracts. [2] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Slaton, Hunter R., "Vault Guide to the Top Manufacturing Employers", Vault Inc. (2nd Edition) ^ "Honeywell Announces Intent to Separate Automation and Aerospace, Enabling the Creation of Three Industry-leading Companies" . Honeywell. February 6, 2025.', '["clm_wiki_honeywell-aerospace_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
