VALUES
  ('cs_hormel-foods_operations', 'org_hormel-foods', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '1920–1950 The Hormel plant circa 1920 In 1921, when George''s son Jay Hormel returned from service in World War I, he discovered that assistant controller Cy Thomson had embezzled $1,187,000 from the company over the previous ten years. [1] The scandal provided George Hormel with additional incentive to professionalize his company. He did so by arranging for more reliable capital management, by dismissing unproductive employees, and by continuing to develop new products, [2] &#58;&#8202;90–103&#8202; reportedly with the mantra "Originate, don''t imitate". [3] In 1926, the company introduced Hormel Flavor-Sealed Ham, America''s first canned ham, [4] and added a canned chicken product line in 1928. [1] Throughout the 1930s, Hormel ads were featured on the radio program The George Burns and Gracie Allen Show . [5] In 1933, workers, led by itinerant butcher Frank Ellis, formed the Independent Union of All Workers and conducted one of the nation''s first successful sit-down strikes ; the union would later join the Congress of Industrial Organizations (CIO, later AFL-CIO). [6] [7] [8] Hormel Chili and Spam were introduced in 1936 and 1937 respectively. [9] [1] In 1938, Jay C. Hormel introduced the "Joint Savings Plan" which allowed employees to share in the profits of the company. [10] By 1942, George and Jay established the Hormel Foundation to act as trustees of the family trusts. [11] The Foundation funded the Hormel Institute at the University of Minnesota , initially started with a study of the food value of soybeans. [12] The institute''s scope later grew towards studying nutrition, animal diseases and food technology. Hormel''s production increased to aid in World War II and 65% of its products were purchased by the U.S. government by 1945. [13] &#58;&#8202;77–78&#8202; Founder George Hormel died in March 1946 at age 85. ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) Frances Levinson (1946). Hormel: The Spam Man . Time Life Inc. p. 63. Archived from the original on July 20, 2023 . Retrieved', '["clm_wiki_hormel-foods_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
