VALUES
  ('cs_huntington-inc_operations', 'org_huntington-inc', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '21st century In 2002, the company sold its branches in Florida to SunTrust Banks for $705 million. [1] [2] [3] [4] In 2006, it acquired Unizan Financial. [5] [6] [7] In 2007, the company acquired Sky Financial Group Inc. , based in Bowling Green, Ohio , which increased its presence in Indiana and Ohio and expanded it into Western Pennsylvania for the first time. [8] [9] [10] [11] [12] In 2008, the United States Department of the Treasury invested $1.4 billion in the company as part of the Troubled Asset Relief Program , and in 2010, the company repaid the Treasury. The U.S. government made a profit of over $144 million from its investment in the company. [13] [14] [15] [16] In 2009, the bank''s board of directors named Steve Steinour as president, CEO, and chairman, succeeding Thomas Hoaglan, who retired after eight years in those positions. [17] [18] Huntington bid against Fifth Third Bank to acquire National City Corp. branches in the Pittsburgh region from PNC Financial Services . The United States Department of Justice ordered PNC to sell the branches to comply with United States antitrust law after the National City acquisition by PNC . [19] PNC sold the overlapping branches to First Niagara Bank . [20] On October 3, 2009, the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation named Huntington as receiver of a $400 million deposit portfolio from the bank failure of Warren Bank in Warren, Michigan . [21] [22] [23] On December 18, 2009, Huntington signed a 45-day lease with the FDIC to run a bridge bank for the failed Citizens State Bank in New Baltimore, Michigan . [24] [25] [26] In 2011, three word marks and two icons were placed atop the 200 Public Square building in Cleveland . The building was constructed in 1985 as the headquarters for formerly the headquarters for Standard Oil of Ohio (Sohio) and in the early 1990s became BP Building or BP America Building when the company unified its North American operations under one brand. [27] In March 2012, the bank acquired Dearb', '["clm_wiki_huntington-inc_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
