VALUES
  ('cs_international-flavors-fragrances_leadership', 'org_international-flavors-fragrances', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Research and innovation In 1968, in conjunction with the Monell Foundation, IFF established the Monell Chemical Senses Center , dedicated to the research of taste and smell. [1] In 1985, Dr. Braja D. Mookherjee, a scientist at IFF, pioneered Living Flower technology, which changed the way perfumes are created. The technology allows for the most accurate transmission of the scent of real flowers through perfume ingredients [2] . In 1990, IFF broke ground in their R&amp;D facility located in Union Beach, NJ , to develop its 5,000-square-foot greenhouse and botanical garden, which can maintain tropical and subtropical temperature zones for more than 1,300 varieties of exotic plants. [3] It is home to a miniature rose called "Overnight Scentsation" (also known as the "Space Rose") which was cultivated for experiments in space and left the Earth during a 10-day flight on board the shuttle Discovery (STS-95) in 1998. Low gravity critically altered the fragrance of the rose, which was later commercialized by IFF and Shiseido. [4] [5] [6] [7] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Pat Kind Tribute" . Monell Chemical Senses Center . Archived from the original on October 19, 2017 . Retrieved August 1, 2018 . ^ "Всё о компании IFF (International Flavors &amp; Fragrances)" . internationalff.ru . Retrieved February 5, 2026 . ^ "Living Flower Technology Makes Rose Perfume Actually Smell Like a Rose" . Lawrence Journal-World . Retrieved August 1, 2018 . ^ "IFF V.P., Global Director Dr. Braja Mookherjee Dies. (Industry News)" . Thefreelibrary . Retrieved August 1, 2018 . ^ "NASA - Space Scents" . Nasa . Archived from the original on April 1, 2017 . Retrieved August 1, 2018 . ^ Oakes, Kelly. "Happy Valentine''s Day! Here''s a Space Rose" . Blogs . Retrieved August 1, 2018 . ^ "5 Strange Items Developed from NASA Technology" . Science . March 3, 2011 . Retrieved August 1, 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_international-flavors-fragrances_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
