  ('cs_intuitive-surgical_leadership', 'org_intuitive-surgical', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Finances For the fiscal year 2017, Intuitive Surgical reported earnings of US$660 million, with an annual revenue of US$3.129 billion, an increase of 15.7% over the previous fiscal cycle. Intuitive Surgical''s shares traded at over $307 per share, and its market capitalization was valued at over US$58 billion in November 2018. [1] Year Revenue in mil. US$ Net income in mil. US$ Total assets in mil. US$ Price per share in US$ Employees Stock split 2005 227 94 502 21.24 2006 373 72 672 35.65 2007 601 145 1,040 61.82 2008 875 204 1,475 85.48 2009 1,052 233 1,810 61.58 2010 1,413 382 2,390 104.33 2011 1,757 495 3,063 122.21 2012 2,179 657 4,059 172.93 2013 2,265 671 3,950 149.97 2,792 2014 2,132 419 3,959 147.55 2,978 2015 2,384 589 4,907 169.00 3,211 2016 2,704 736 6,487 212.10 3,755 2017 3,129 660 5,758 307.18 4,444 October 6, 2017: A 3-for-1 stock split, providing shareholders with two additional shares for each share held. 2018 [2] 3,724 1,125 7,847 5,527 2019 [3] 4,479 1,379 9,733 7,326 2020 4,360 1,600 11,000 8,000 2021 5,710 1,800 12,500 9,500 October 5, 2021: A 3-for-1 stock split, providing shareholders with two additional shares for each share held. 2022 6,220 2,000 14,000 11,000 2023 7,120 2,200 15,500 13,676 2024 8,350 2,600 17,000 521.96 15,000 ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Intuitive Surgical Revenue 2006-2018 | ISRG" . www . Retrieved 2018-11-06 . ^ "Annual Report 2018" (PDF) . annualreports . Retrieved 1 April 2022 . ^ "Annual Report 2019" . gcs-web . Retrieved 1 April 2022 .', '["clm_wiki_intuitive-surgical_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
