VALUES
  ('cs_kenvue_leadership', 'org_kenvue', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Spin-off and IPO On November 12, 2021, Johnson &amp; Johnson announced that it would spin off its consumer health division as a separate company in an effort to streamline operations. [1] The new company would assume well-known consumer brands such as Aveeno , Band-Aid , Neutrogena , and Tylenol , while Johnson &amp; Johnson would focus on the pharmaceutical and medical device sectors. [1] CEO Alex Gorsky said that the split was in response to "a significant evolution in these markets, particularly on the consumer side", [1] and would enable faster expansion for both businesses. [2] Other pharmaceutical companies that made similar moves around this time included Merck &amp; Co. , which sold its consumer health business to Bayer in 2014, &#91; note 1 &#93; [1] and Pfizer , which merged its consumer health division with that of GSK plc in 2019. &#91; note 2 &#93; [2] The November 2021 announcement also occurred the same week that General Electric and Toshiba each announced that they would split into multiple entities. [2] The New York Times noted that Johnson &amp; Johnson had long benefited from a "halo effect," namely a lingering positive connotation ascribed to the company name stemming from its popular household brands such as Johnson''s Baby , but that its reputation had declined as a result of various controversies in recent years; [2] Johnson &amp; Johnson was the subject of litigation over its role in the opioid epidemic in the United States , as well as over allegations that its talc -based baby powder contained asbestos and caused ovarian cancer for some consumers. [2] The spin-off was seen as an effort to move past these controversies and assuage shareholder apprehension. [2] The Times also pointed out that, while the consumer health business operates many well-known brands, it was not nearly as lucrative as the pharmaceutical and medical device sectors, taking $15 billion in revenue in 2021 compared to the latter''s combined $77 billion, and commented that t', '["clm_wiki_kenvue_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
