VALUES
  ('cs_labcorp_operations', 'org_labcorp', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '2000s A LabCorp fecal occult blood immunoassay testing kit. In June 2000, Labcorp acquired the laboratory testing business of Pathology Medical Laboratories. [1] [2] In May 2001, Labcorp acquired Path Lab Holdings, the largest regional laboratory in New England . [3] In June 2001, it acquired ViroMed, which specialized on clinical diagnostic testing in virology , molecular biology , serology , microbiology , mycology and mycobacteriology, as well as in tissue and eye bank testing. [4] In 2013, it closed the Viromed facility in Minnetonka, Minnesota and laid off 79 workers. [5] In December 2001, Labcorp became the exclusive marketer for genomics and proteomics tests for breast cancer , colon cancer , melanoma , and hypertension made by Myriad Genetics . [6] In March 2002, Roche sold its remaining interest in the company. [7] In May 2002, Labcorp acquired Dynacare , a Canadian medical laboratory services company, for $480 million. [8] [9] In January 2003, Labcorp acquired Dianon, a provider of oncology and genomic diagnostic testing services, for $598 million in cash. [10] [11] [12] In February 2005, the company acquired US Pathology Labs Inc., a provider of anatomical pathology and oncology testing services, for $155 million. [2] [13] In March 2005, Labcorp acquired Esoterix, a provider of specialty reference testing, for approximately $150 million in cash from Behrman Capital. [14] [15] In November 2006, Labcorp acquired Litholink, a kidney stone analysis laboratory. [15] In January 2008, Labcorp acquired Tandem Labs, a contract research organization specializing in advanced mass spectrometry , immunoanalytical support, pharmacokinetics , and pharmacodynamics . [16] [15] In June 2009, Labcorp acquired Monogram Biosciences , a diagnostic lab specializing in HIV resistance testing, for approximately $155 million including debt. [17] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "LABCORP ACQUIRES CALIFORNIA CLINICAL LAB" . News &amp; Record . May 4, 2000. ^ a b "LabCorp completes purchase of U', '["clm_wiki_labcorp_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
