VALUES
  ('cs_nxp-semiconductors_operations', 'org_nxp-semiconductors', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Independent company 2000s NXP was spun-off by Philips In December 2005, Philips announced its intention to spin-off Philips Semiconductors into an independent legal entity . [1] [2] In September 2006, Philips completed the sale of an 80.1 percent stake in Philips Semiconductors to a consortium of private equity investors consisting of KKR , Bain Capital , Silver Lake Partners , Apax Partners and AlpInvest Partners . [3] [4] The new company name NXP (from Next eXPerience) was announced on 31 August 2006, [5] [6] and the company was officially launched during the Internationale Funkausstellung (IFA) consumer electronics show in Berlin. The newly independent NXP was ranked as one of the world''s top 10 semiconductor companies. [7] In February 2007, NXP announced that it would acquire Silicon Laboratories ’ AeroFONE single-chip phone and power amplifier product lines to strengthen its Mobile and Personal business in exchange for $285 million in cash. [8] [9] The next year, NXP announced that it would transform its Mobile and Personal business unit into a joint venture with STMicroelectronics ; [10] in 2009, following ST''s purchase of NXP''s 20 percent stake, this business unit became ST-Ericsson , which was itself a 50/50 joint venture of Ericsson Mobile Platforms and STMicroelectronics . [11] In April 2008, NXP announced it would acquire the set-top box business of Conexant to complement its existing Home business unit. [12] [13] In September 2008, NXP announced that it would restructure its manufacturing, R&amp;D and back office operations, resulting in 4,500 job cuts worldwide. [14] In October 2009, NXP announced that it would sell its Home business unit to Trident Microsystems . [15] NXP was the co-inventor of near field communication (NFC) technology, along with Sony and Inside Secure, and had supplied NFC chip sets that enables mobile phones to be used to pay for goods, and store and exchange data securely. [16] NXP manufactures such chips for eGovernment applicatio', '["clm_wiki_nxp-semiconductors_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
