  ('cs_quest-diagnostics_leadership', 'org_quest-diagnostics', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1960–1995 Originally founded as Metropolitan Pathology Laboratory, Inc. in 1967 by Paul A. Brown, MD , the clinical laboratory underwent a variety of name changes. [1] In 1969, the company''s name changed to MetPath, Inc. [2] with headquarters in Teaneck, New Jersey . By 1982, MetPath was acquired by what was then known as Corning Glass Works [3] and was subsequently renamed Corning Clinical Laboratories. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Quest Diagnostics celebrates 50 years" . North Jersey . Retrieved October 23, 2018 . ^ "A. Raymond Bessette, 82, investment banker, built skating rink" . The Ridgefield Press . March 5, 2013. Archived from the original on October 23, 2018 . Retrieved October 23, 2018 . ^ "Corning Glass To Buy Metpath" . The New York Times . November 20, 1981 . Retrieved October 23, 2018 . ^ "History of Quest Diagnostics Inc" . FundingUniverse. Archived from the original on October 23, 2018 . Retrieved October 23, 2018 .', '["clm_wiki_quest-diagnostics_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
