  ('cs_quest-diagnostics_operations', 'org_quest-diagnostics', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '1996–2000 On December 31, 1996, Quest Diagnostics became an independent company as a spin-off from Corning . [1] [2] Kenneth W. Freeman was appointed as CEO during this transition. [3] [4] Over the next year, Quest acquired a clinical laboratory division of Branford, Connecticut –based Diagnostic Medical Laboratory, Inc. (DML). [5] Two years later in 1999, Quest added SmithKline Beecham Clinical Laboratories to their subsidiaries; [6] [7] which includes a joint venture ownership with CompuNet Clinical Laboratory. [8] The purchase of SmithKline Beecham also included the lab''s medical sample transport airline ( ICAO : LBQ , call sign : LABQUEST ) originally founded in 1988. [9] In 1997, Quest and Banner Health formed a joint venture creating the Arizona based Sonora Quest laboratory, a business unit of Laboratory Sciences of Arizona. [10] This entity represents the operations of Quest Diagnostics in the Arizona regional market. ^ Cite error: The named reference :0 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Corning to Spin Off 2 Subsidiaries to Shareholders" . The New York Times . Reuters. November 28, 1996 . Retrieved October 31, 2018 . ^ Nicolai, Kathryn (February 2018). "Kenneth W. Freeman college of management named after $25 million donation" . The Bucknellian . Retrieved October 31, 2018 . ^ "Kenneth W. Freeman Named Dean of SMG" . BU Today . Boston University . Retrieved October 31, 2018 . ^ "Quest Diagnostics Acquires Assets Of Diagnostics Medical Laboratory Inc" . Quest Diagnostics . Retrieved February 15, 2012 . ^ Nouri, Paul (February 16, 2012). "Investors Should Wait Out Quest And LabCorp" . Seeking Alpha . Retrieved October 31, 2018 . ^ "A Guide to Being Compassionate During Layoffs" . Harvard Business Review . February 25, 2016 . Retrieved October 31, 2018 . ^ "Compunet names new CEO" . Dayton Business Journal . October 20, 2014 . Retrieved October 31, 2018 . ^ Tegler, Eric (April 29, 2020). "Appearing nightly, the Quest Dia', '["clm_wiki_quest-diagnostics_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
