VALUES
  ('cs_sp-global_history', 'org_sp-global', 'overview', 'History',
   'American financial services company "McGraw-Hill, Inc." redirects here. For the education science company, see McGraw Hill Education . S&amp;P Global Inc. Headquarters at 55 Water Street Formerly McGraw–Hill, Inc. (1964–1995) The McGraw–Hill Companies, Inc. (1995–2013) McGraw Hill Financial, Inc. (2013–2016) Type Public Traded as NYSE : SPGI S&amp;P 500 component Industry Financial services Predecessor The McGraw–Hill Book/Publishing Companies (formerly ''The McGraw Publishing Company'' and ''The Hill Book Company'') Founded 1917 &#59;&#32;109 years ago ( 1917 ) Founders James H. McGraw John A. Hill Headquarters 55 Water Street, New York City , US Area served Worldwide Key people Martina Cheung ( president &amp; CEO ) Products Financial information and analytics Revenue US$ 14.2 billion (2024) Operating income US$5.58 billion (2024) Net income US$3.85 billion (2024) Total assets US$60.2 billion (2024) Total equity US$33.3 billion (2024) Number of employees 42,350 (2024) Subsidiaries S&amp;P Global Ratings S&amp;P Global Energy CRISIL S&amp;P Dow Jones Indices S&amp;P Global Market Intelligence S&amp;P Global Mobility S&amp;P Global Sustainable1 Kensho Technologies Website www /en Footnotes [1] [2] S&amp;P Global Inc. (prior to 2016, McGraw Hill Financial, Inc. , and prior to 2013, The McGraw–Hill Companies, Inc. ) is an American publicly traded corporation headquartered in Manhattan , New York. Its primary areas of business are financial information, analytics, and energy and commodities intelligence. It is the parent company of S&amp;P Global Ratings , S&amp;P Global Energy , S&amp;P Global Market Intelligence, S&amp;P Global Mobility, and the Indian credit rating agency CRISIL . It is also the majority owner of the S&amp;P Dow Jones Indices joint venture. "S&amp;P" is a shortening of " Standard and Poor''s ". ^ body:not( ):not( ) Martin, Timothy W. (July 8, 2015). "McGraw Hill Moves Downtown, Says Goodbye to Namesake Building" . The Wall Street Journal . Retrieved July 14, 2015 . ^ "SPGI 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 11, 2025.', '["clm_wiki_sp-global_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
