VALUES
  ('cs_synchrony_history', 'org_synchrony', 'overview', 'History',
   'American financial services company html body This article relies excessively on references to primary sources . Please improve this article by adding secondary or tertiary sources . Find sources: "Synchrony Financial" – news · newspapers · books · scholar · JSTOR ( February 2025 ) ( Learn how and when to remove this message ) Synchrony Financial Type Public Traded as NYSE : SYF S&amp;P 500 component Industry Financial services Founded September 12, 2003 &#59;&#32;22 years ago ( 2003-09-12 ) [1] Headquarters Draper, Utah , U.S. [2] Key people Margaret M. Keane ( Executive Chairman ) Brian Doubles ( CEO ) [3] Products Credit cards Payment systems Revenue US$ 24.17 billion (2024) [4] Net income US$3.427 billion (2024) [4] Total assets US$119.5 billion (2024) [4] Total equity US$16.58 billion (2024) [4] Number of employees 20,000 (2024) [4] Website synchrony Synchrony Financial is an American consumer financial services company with its headquarters in Draper, Utah , United States . [2] The company offers consumer financing products, including credit, promotional financing and loyalty programs, installment lending to industries and consumers through Synchrony Bank, its wholly owned online bank subsidiary. [4] [5] Brands partnered with Synchrony include Amazon , [6] Lowe''s , [7] Guitar Center , [8] Cathay Pacific , Rakuten , Verizon , Sleep Number , Walgreens , and Sam''s Club . Synchrony owns CareCredit, a credit card for medical and veterinary expenses. [9] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Synchrony Financial on the Forbes Global 2000 List" . Forbes . Retrieved October 4, 2016 . ^ a b "Synchrony Bank" . www . ^ Bishop, Sue. "Synchrony Promotes Brian Doubles To President" . PR Newswire (Press release). Synchrony . Retrieved May 21, 2019 . ^ a b c d e f "Synchrony 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. February 7, 2025 . Retrieved February 7, 2025 . ^ "Factsheet" . Sychrony . Retrieved April 16, 2019 . ^ GuruFocus. "Warren Buffett And Seth Klarman Agree On One Stock – Synchrony Financial" . Forbes . Retrieved April 24, 2020 . ^ Johnson, Andrew (March 13, 2014). "GE Plans Credit-Card IPO as Plastic Gets Popular; New Company to Be Called Synchrony Financial" . The Wall Street Journal . Dow Jones &amp; Company Inc . Retrieved June 3, 2015 . ^ Passeri, James (April 17, 2015). "GE Spinoff Synchrony Financial Is Still Trying to Stand on Its Own" . The Street . TheStreet, Inc . Retrieved June 3, 2015 . ^ Semuels, Alana (January 14, 2025). "How', '["clm_wiki_synchrony_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
