VALUES
  ('cs_te-connectivity_leadership', 'org_te-connectivity', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Products and services TE Connectivity''s product portfolio is focused on connectors and sensors [1] that are made to withstand harsh environments. [2] The company operates three primary segments. [3] Communications TE Connectivity''s communications segment supplies electronic components for home appliances, including products for washers, dryers, refrigerators, air conditioners, dishwashers, cooking appliances, water heaters, and microwaves. Transportation TE Connectivity''s transportation segment includes four business units: automotive , industrial and commercial transportation, application tooling, and sensors. TE''s products are used by the automotive industry for vehicle body and chassis systems, convenience applications, driver information, infotainment , motor and powertrain applications, and safety and security systems. Hybrid and electronic mobility include in-vehicle technologies, battery technologies, [4] and charging. In addition, TE''s products are used for on-highway vehicles, off-highway vehicles and recreational transportation, including construction, agriculture, buses, and other vehicles. [5] TE offers sensors for industries including automotive, industrial equipment, commercial transportation, medical, aerospace and defense, and consumer applications. Industrial The industrial segment supplies products for factory automation and process control systems such as industrial controls, robotics, human machine interface , industrial communication, and power distribution. TE''s building products are used to connect lighting, HVAC , elevators/escalators, and security. Its rail products are used in high-speed trains, metros, light rail vehicles, locomotives , and signaling switching equipment. [6] Also, its products are used by the solar and lighting industry. TE''s products are used by the medical industry in imaging, diagnostic, therapeutic, and surgical applications. [7] TE Connectivity provides components for the commercial aerospace industry [8] from the ini', '["clm_wiki_te-connectivity_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
