VALUES
  ('cs_trimble_leadership', 'org_trimble', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1978–1998 Trimble Inc. was founded as Trimble Navigation in November 1978 by Charles Trimble and two engineers from Hewlett-Packard . [1] The company originally operated out of Los Altos, California . [2] One of the company''s first moves was to acquire the rights to a Loran-C navigation technology that Hewlett-Packard had stopped developing. Trimble bought the technology for $50,000. [1] By 1982, Trimble was selling approximately $1 million of Loran equipment per year. [1] In the mid-1980s, Trimble began to move into the GPS technology space. For example, in 1985, the company introduced GPS tech that could be used for offshore drilling surveying as well as GPS navigation tools for aircraft. [1] In 1986, Trimble moved its headquarters from Los Altos to Sunnyvale, California . [2] Trimble held its initial public offering in 1990. [3] [4] That same year, Trimble began selling GPS-enabled personal position finders to the U.S. military. Following the Iraqi invasion of Kuwait , U.S. military demand for these finders increased significantly and Trimble''s sales revenues grew from approximately $5 million per month to $19 million per month. [1] In 1991, the company had about 750 employees. [1] In the early 1990s, Trimble began developing real-time kinematic positioning (RTK) tools for surveying. The company''s first commercially available RTK product, called the Site Surveyor System, was released in 1993. [3] The following March, Trimble released its first RTK receiver with on-the-fly capabilities. [3] In 1995, Trimble began working with Caterpillar to develop global navigation satellite system (GNSS) receivers for heavy construction vehicles. The first product of this partnership was a blade-mounted GNSS tool for bulldozers. [3] ^ a b c d e f body:not( ):not( ) Perry, Tekla S. (April 19, 2018). "Charles Trimble Bet His Company on GPS—and Won" . IEEE Spectrum . Retrieved September 2, 2025 . ^ a b Mehrtens, Savannah (October 6, 2022). "Trimble Inc. relocates headquarters to We', '["clm_wiki_trimble_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_trimble_operations', 'org_trimble', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '2019–present In October 2019, Trimble announced that Robert G. Painter would become the company''s president and CEO, effective January 4, 2020. [1] In November 2020, the firm signed an agreement with Boston Dynamics to integrate construction data collection technologies into BD''s robotic dog Spot . [2] In December 2021, Trimble purchased AgileAssets, a SaaS company helping corporate and governmental clients manage infrastructure assets. AgileAssets was absorbed into the buildings and infrastructure segment of Trimble''s business. [3] In September 2022, Trimble acquired B2W Software, a New Hampshire-based developer of software for the heavy civil construction industry. [4] The following month, Trimble announced its headquarters had relocated to Westminster, Colorado from Sunnyvale, California. [5] In December 2022, Trimble acquired the transportation management platform Transporeon in order to strengthen its existing transportation management systems offerings. [6] [7] In September 2023, AGCO announced that it would acquire an 85% stake in Trimble''s agriculture business. [8] This acquisition created a new joint venture called PTx Trimble. [9] In March 2024, Trimble joined the Alliance of OpenUSD . [10] That same month, the company announced that it would be partnering with Nvidia to provide model data for Nvidia Omniverse RTX viewers. [11] In May 2024, Trimble acquired Flashtract, a company specializing in payment, compliance, and documentation exchange. Trimble subsequently rebranded Flashtract''s technology as Trimble Pay. [12] In September 2024, Trimble announced that it would be selling its transportation telematics business to Platform Science in exchange for a 32.5% stake in Platform Science. [13] Trimble Inc. at EXCON 2025, BIEC Trimble''s construction vehicle model at EXCON 2025, BIEC ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Trimble Announces CEO Succession" . Geospatial World . October 31, 2019 . Retrieved October 31, 2019 . ^ "Trimble and Boston Dynamics form autonomous robot al', '["clm_wiki_trimble_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 852. U.S. Bancorp (slug=us, wiki='U.S. Bancorp')
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
