   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_us_history', 'org_us', 'overview', 'History',
   'American multinational banking institution "US Bank" redirects here. For other uses, see Bank of the United States . U.S. Bancorp U.S. Bancorp''s headquarters in Minneapolis Trade name U.S. Bank Type Public Traded as NYSE : USB S&amp;P 100 component S&amp;P 500 component ISIN US9029733048 Industry Financial services Founded July 13, 1863 &#59;&#32;163 years ago ( 1863-07-13 ) Headquarters U.S. Bancorp Center , Minneapolis , Minnesota, U.S. Number of locations 3,661 branches (2024) 4,771 ATMs (2024) Key people Andrew Cecere ( chairman ) Gunjan Kedia president and CEO ) Products banking asset management wealth management credit cards insurance investment management mortgage loans private equity Revenue US$ 27.46 billion (2024) Operating income US$7.84 billion (2023) Net income US$6.33 billion (2024) Total assets US$678.32 billion (2024) Total equity US$58.9 billion (2024) Number of employees 70,000+ (2024) Subsidiaries Elavon Talech Syncada Capital ratio 10.9% Tier 1 (2025) Website www /about-us-bank Footnotes [1] [2] [3] U.S. Bancorp (stylized as us bancorp ) is an American multinational banking institution headquartered in Minneapolis , Minnesota, and incorporated in Delaware . It is the 7th-largest bank in the United States as of March 2026. As the largest bank in the Midwestern United States , it is considered a domestic systemically important bank (D-SIB) by the Federal Reserve . It is the parent company of its primary operating entity, U.S. Bank National Association, which does business as U.S. Bank (stylized as us bank ). The company provides banking, investment, mortgage, trust, and payment services products to individuals, businesses, governmental entities, and other financial institutions. The firm''s early history can be traced to 1891, operating under the second-oldest banking charter granted in 1863 following the passage of the National Bank Act . Since inception, dozens of regional mergers and acquisitions throughout the Upper Midwest and Western United States led to the creation of modern U.S. Bancorp. As a diversified holding company, U.S. Bancorp has acquired multiple subsidiaries since the late 2010s. Its retail credit card offerings are provided via the Visa network in the U.S. and abroad. U.S. Bancorp''s annual revenue levels have it ranked on the Fortune 500 , with its public stock trading within both the S&amp;P 500 and S&amp;P 100 indexes. [4] [5] It was included in the 2024 Forbes Global 2000 for its sales, profitability, asset base, and', '["clm_wiki_us_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
