VALUES
  ('cs_united-rentals_operations', 'org_united-rentals', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History A Dodge Ram 1500 truck &amp; Genie SX-180 Boom lift from United Rentals. United Rentals was founded in September 1997. [1] Then-chairman and CEO Hector Salazar Jr. planned to grow the company through acquisition and consolidation, beginning in October 1997 with six small leasing companies scattered across North America. [2] In December 1997, three months after forming, United Rentals began trading on the New York Stock Exchange under the symbol URI. [2] In June 1998, it acquired U.S. Rentals, Inc., for a sum variously reported as $1.2 billion and $1.31 billion. The acquisition made United Rentals the largest equipment rental company in North America. [3] On December 26, 2006, United Rentals announced the sale of their Highway Technology division to HTS Acquisition, Inc. [4] On July 23, 2007, United Rentals announced a definitive agreement to sell itself to Cerberus Capital Management in a transaction valued at approximately $6.6 billion, including the assumption of approximately $2.6 billion in debt obligations. URI''s board of directors approved the merger agreement and recommended that stockholders do the same. [5] On November 15, 2007, the company announced that Cerberus was not prepared to proceed with the purchase on the terms set forth in its merger agreement. Cerberus confirmed that there had not been a material adverse change at United Rentals, which would have let it bow out of the deal without penalty. [6] On December 21, 2007, a Delaware Chancery Court ruling denied United Rentals'' attempt to force Cerberus to follow through on the takeover bid. However, the court did order Cerberus to pay the $100 million termination fee stipulated in the original agreement. [7] On December 16, 2011, United Rentals and RSC Holdings, Inc . announced that they had entered into a definitive merger agreement, under which United Rentals would acquire RSC in a cash-and-stock transaction. [8] The largest merger in rental equipment history was finalized on April 30, 2012,', '["clm_wiki_united-rentals_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
