  ('cs_vertex-pharmaceuticals_history', 'org_vertex-pharmaceuticals', 'overview', 'History',
   'American pharmaceutical company Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated Headquarters in Seaport District Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : VRTX Nasdaq-100 component S&amp;P 500 component Industry Pharmaceuticals Biotherapeutics Founded 1989 &#59;&#32;37 years ago ( 1989 ) Headquarters Boston , Massachusetts, U.S. Key people Reshma Kewalramani ( president and CEO ) Jeffrey Leiden ( chairman ) David Altshuler ( CSO ) Products Pharmaceuticals Revenue US$ 12.0 billion (2025) Operating income US$4.17 billion (2025) Net income US$3.95 billion (2025) Total assets US$25.6 billion (2025) Total equity US$18.7 billion (2025) Number of employees 6,400 (2025) Website vrtx Footnotes [1] [2] Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated is an American biopharmaceutical company based in Boston , Massachusetts. It was one of the first biotech firms to use an explicit strategy of rational drug design rather than combinatorial chemistry . It maintains headquarters in Boston, Massachusetts, and three research facilities, in San Diego , California, and Milton Park , Oxfordshire, England. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Vertex Pharmaceuticals Inc. 2025 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . 13 February 2026. ^ "Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated" . Hoover''s . Retrieved 24 June 2012 .', '["clm_wiki_vertex-pharmaceuticals_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
