  ('cs_w-w-grainger_leadership', 'org_w-w-grainger', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Digital operations In 1995 the grainger website was launched with an electronic catalog, later evolving to an eCommerce platform. In 2016, Grainger was named the 11th largest eCommerce retailer in North America by Internet Retailer. [1] In 2019, more than 70 percent of Grainger orders in the U.S. originated via a digital channel (including Grainger , inventory management systems, and eProcurement) and more than 85 percent of orders were shipped directly to the customer or made immediately available through onsite services. [2] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "2017 Top 500 Analysis Report" . Retrieved June 16, 2017 &#8211; via Digital Commerce 360. ^ "W.W. Grainger, Inc" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . Retrieved March 19, 2019 .', '["clm_wiki_w-w-grainger_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
