VALUES
  ('cs_williams-sonoma_history', 'org_williams-sonoma', 'overview', 'History',
   'American kitchenware and home furnishings company html body This History is missing information about the early history and the origin of the company. Please expand the History to include this information. Further details may exist on the talk page . ( January 2025 ) Williams-Sonoma, Inc. Headquarters in San Francisco Type Public Traded as NYSE : WSM S&amp;P 500 component Industry Retail [1] Founded 1956 &#59;&#32;70 years ago ( 1956 ) Headquarters 3250 Van Ness Avenue San Francisco , California, U.S. Number of locations 512 [2] (2025) Key people Laura Alber ( CEO ) [3] Jeff Howie ( CFO ) Sameer Hassan ( CTO ) [4] Brands Williams Sonoma Pottery Barn Rejuvenation West Elm Revenue US$ 7.71 billion (2024) Operating income US$1.43 billion (2024) Net income US$1.13 billion (2024) Total assets US$5.30 billion (2024) Total equity US$2.14 billion (2024) Number of employees 19,600 (2025) Website www Footnotes [2] Williams-Sonoma, Inc. , is an American publicly traded consumer retail company that sells kitchenware and home furnishings. [5] It is headquartered in San Francisco , California , United States. [6] The company has 625 brick and mortar stores and distributes to more than 60 countries, with brands including Williams Sonoma , Williams Sonoma Home, Pottery Barn , Pottery Barn Kids, PBteen, West Elm , Mark and Graham, and Rejuvenation . [7] [8] Williams-Sonoma, Inc., also operates through eight corresponding websites and a gift registry . [9] The company is one of the largest e-commerce retailers in the U.S., [5] and one of the biggest multi-channel specialty retailers in the world. [7] In 2019, Williams-Sonoma, Inc., was named as a Fortune 500 company for the first time in its history. [10] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Corporate Information -Business Profile" . Williams-Sonoma, Inc . Retrieved November 9, 2015 . ^ a b "Williams-Sonoma, Inc. 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission. March 27, 2025. ^ "Shopping catalogs making a comeback" . CBS News. March 19, 2015 . Retrieved November 9, 2015 . ^ "Executive Biographies" . Williams-Sonoma, Inc . Retrieved November 8, 2013 . ^ a b Lee, Thomas (April 3, 2015). "Williams-Sonoma is America''s best retailer — online and in store" . San Francisco Chronicle . Retrieved November 9, 2015 . ^ Flynn, Ryan (May 3, 2011). "Williams-Sonoma whips up new strategy" . Seattle Times . Retrieved November 9, 2015 . ^ a b "Laura Alber will become CEO of Williams-Sonoma in May" . Furniture Today . January 27,', '["clm_wiki_williams-sonoma_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
