   'Global insurance broking and advisory company For the Chicago skyscraper currently named after the company, see Willis Tower . Willis Towers Watson plc Principal executive offices at the Willis Building in London Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : WTW S&amp;P 500 component [1] ISIN IE00BDB6Q211 [2] Industry Human resource consulting Insurance brokerage Risk management Predecessors Willis Group Towers Watson Founded 5 January 2016 &#59;&#32;10 years ago ( 2016-01-05 ) in Ireland [3] Headquarters London, United Kingdom [3] Area served Worldwide Key people Paul Reilly ( Chairman ) [4] Carl Hess ( CEO ) [5] Services Commercial insurance broking Risk consulting Actuarial and pensions Benefits administration Human resources and rewards Investment advisory Revenue US$9.93 billion [3] (2024) Operating income US$627 million [3] (2024) Net income US$−98 million [3] (2024) Total assets US$27.68 billion [3] (2024) Total equity US$7.94 billion [3] (2024) Number of employees 48,900 [3] (2024) Website www Willis Towers Watson plc (branded as WTW) is a British-American multinational advisory, broking and solutions company. Its operations span commercial insurance brokerage and risk advisory, employee benefits and rewards consulting, retirement and actuarial services, and investment advice for pension funds and institutional investors. [3] The company is legally domiciled in Ireland and has its principal executive offices at the Willis Building in London . [3] In 2024 WTW reported revenue of US$9.93 billion and employed about 48,900 people. [3] Following completion of the Willis Group - Towers Watson merger, the company was added to the S&amp;P 500 index in January 2016. [1] WTW ranks among the largest global insurance brokers by revenue. [6] ^ a b Cite error: The named reference SP500 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference ISIN was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ a b c d e f g h i j k Cite error: The named reference 10K2024Address was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference ReillyChairPR was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference WTWLeadership was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference Reuters2025Brokers was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_willis-towers-watson_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
