VALUES
  ('cs_willis-towers-watson_operations', 'org_willis-towers-watson', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Rebranding since 2020 In November 2020 WTW acquired Acclimatise, a UK-based climate consultancy, and in November 2021 it agreed to acquire Israeli broker Leaderim as part of a broader build-out of specialty and regional broking networks. [1] [2] WTW completed the sale of its treaty reinsurance operations to Arthur J. Gallagher &amp; Co. on 1 December 2021 for an initial US$3.25 billion with a potential earn-out. [3] The company rebranded commercially as WTW in January 2022 and changed its Nasdaq ticker to WTW. [4] In March 2022 it withdrew from Russia, transferring ownership of its Russian businesses to local management. [5] In July 2022 WTW acquired Butterwire, a climate risk analytics firm, to support its advisory and software offerings. [6] In October 2024 WTW announced an agreement to sell its direct-to-consumer unit TRANZACT, completion of which was announced on 2 January 2025. [7] [8] In December 2025, it was announced WTW had reached an agreement to acquire NatWest Group ''s 85% stake in the UK-based workplace savings and pensions fintech, Cushon. The acquisition will be subject to regulatory approval. [9] In January 2026, it was announced that WTW had acquired Invoice Cover, a Québec-based specialist in trade credit insurance, with the business integrated into its Willis broking division. The acquisition, which was completed in December 2025, was intended to strengthen Willis’ presence in the Canadian trade credit market. [10] In January 2026, WTW acquired the American company Newfront in a $1.3 billion deal. [11] [12] The acquisition allowed WTW to expand its reach in the U.S. middle-market and add scale in sectors such as technology, fintech, and life sciences. [11] ^ Cite error: The named reference InsuranceBusiness2020Acclimatise was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference IJ2021Leaderim was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference IJ2021GallagherRe was invoked but never de', '["clm_wiki_willis-towers-watson_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
