VALUES
  ('cs_zebra_operations', 'org_zebra', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '21st century In 2000, Comtec Information Systems was acquired by Zebra Technologies, [1] followed in 2003 by the acquisition of Atlantek, Inc., which was a manufacturer of photo ID printers. [2] In 2004, the company expanded into RFID smart label manufacturing. [3] [4] In the following years, Zebra also acquired Swecoin, WhereNet Corp, [5] Proveo AG, [6] and Navis Holdings (later divested in 2011). [7] The company bought the Enterprise Solutions Group (ESG) in 2008 and renamed the group Zebra Enterprise Solutions in 2009. In the same year, Multispectral Solutions, Inc. was acquired. [8] In 2012, the companies LaserBand , [9] and StepOne Systems were purchased with a cash price of $1.5 million. [10] In 2013, the company acquired Hart Systems for $94 million in cash from the private equity firm Topspin Partners LBO. [11] In 2014, Zebra acquired Motorola Solutions '' Enterprise Division in a $3.45 billion transaction, providing mobile computing and advanced data capture communications technologies and services. Zebra''s acquisition of the Enterprise Division included the Symbol Technologies and Psion product lines. [11] [12] Also in 2014, Zebra provided its real-time location system (RTLS) in NFL stadiums to track players and officials and provide location-based data for the NFL''s Next Gen Stats program. [13] [14] Zebra’s partnership with the NFL extends through the 2025 football season. [15] In 2018, the company acquired Xplore Technologies , a maker of ruggedized tablets and other hard-wearing hardware. [16] In 2019, Zebra acquired Temptime Corporation, a provider of temperature monitoring devices to the healthcare industry. [17] That same year, Zebra also acquired Profitect, a retail software company that developed a product line used for tracking and identifying inventory losses. [18] [19] Zebra TC56 touchscreen handheld device configured in German In 2020, Zebra acquired Reflexis Systems, a provider of workforce scheduling and task management software to the retail,', '["clm_wiki_zebra_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 868. TD Bank, N.A. (slug=td-bank-na, wiki='TD Bank, N.A.')
