VALUES
  ('cs_santander-bank_history', 'org_santander-bank', 'overview', 'History',
   'Wholly owned subsidiary of Spanish Santander Group For the British bank with this name, see Santander UK . Santander Bank, N. A. Headquarters in Boston Formerly Sovereign Bank Type Subsidiary Industry Banking Founded 1902 &#59;&#32;124 years ago ( 1902 ) in Wyomissing, Pennsylvania (as Sovereign Bank) Headquarters 75 State Street , Boston , Massachusetts , United States Number of locations 400 (2025) [1] Key people Christiana Reilly (CEO) Tim Ryan (Chair) Revenue US$3.345 billion (2013) [2] Operating income US$1.508 billion (2013) [2] Net income US$1.042 billion (2013) [2] Number of employees 10,000 (2020) [3] [4] [5] Parent Santander Group Website santanderbank Santander Bank, N. A. ( / ˌ s ɑː n t ɑː n ˈ d ɛər / ) is an American bank operating as a wholly owned subsidiary of the Spanish Santander Group . It is based in Boston and its principal market is the northeastern United States . It has $57.5 billion in deposits , operates about 650 retail banking offices and over 2,000 ATMs , and employs approximately 9,800 people. It offers an array of financial services and products, including retail banking , mortgages , corporate banking , cash management , credit card , capital markets , trust and wealth management , and insurance . [1] Santander Bank in New York near Grand Central Station Sovereign Bank changed its name to Santander Bank on October 17, 2013; the stadium, arena, and performing arts center for which it has naming rights were also rebranded. ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "BankFind Suite: Institution Details" . fdic . Retrieved 10 August 2025 . ^ a b c "3Q Results 2013: Sovereign Bank" . Santander Group . Archived from the original on 29 October 2013 . Retrieved 13 September 2024 . ^ "About Us" . Santander Bank . Retrieved 13 September 2024 . ^ "Santander US" . Santander Bank . ^ "About Us" . Santander Bank N. A . Retrieved 6 August 2017 .', '["clm_wiki_santander-bank_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
