VALUES
  ('cs_umb-financial_history', 'org_umb-financial', 'overview', 'History',
   'American financial services and banking company UMB Financial Corporation Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : UMBF S&amp;P 400 Component Industry Banking Founded 1913 &#59;&#32;113 years ago ( 1913 ) Headquarters Kansas City, Missouri , U.S. Key people Mariner Kemper ( chairman , president &amp; CEO ) Ram Shankar ( CFO ) Jim Rine (CEO of UMB Bank) [1] Revenue US$ 1.468 billion (2022) Operating income US$433.020 million (2022) [2] Net income US$431.682 million (2022) [2] Total assets US$38.512 billion (2022) [2] Total equity US$2.667 billion (2022) [2] Number of employees 3,804 (2022) Website umb UMB Financial Corporation is an American financial services company headquartered in Kansas City, Missouri. It offers comprehensive financial services, including deposit solutions like checking and savings accounts , credit services including home mortgages , auto loans , business loans and credit cards , as well as investing and wealth management. UMB serves individuals, companies and institutions across the U.S. and in Ireland. UMB Financial is the parent company of UMB Bank , which ranks as one of America''s Best Banks by Forbes and S&amp;P Global Market Intelligence, based on eight financial measures of asset quality, capital adequacy and profitability. &#91; citation needed &#93; UMB operates banking and wealth management centers in Missouri, Arizona, California, Colorado, Illinois, Iowa, Kansas, Minnesota, Nebraska, New Mexico, Oklahoma, Texas, Utah, Wisconsin. [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Officers &amp; Directors" . UMBfinancial . Retrieved June 2, 2021 . ^ a b c d "UMB Financial Corporation - News" . ^ "BankFind Suite" . banks . Retrieved January 29, 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_umb-financial_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
