VALUES
  ('cs_united-community-bank_leadership', 'org_united-community-bank', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'History Union County Bank was founded in 1949 in Blairsville, Georgia . By 1984, the bank had grown to $42 million in assets, and that year Jimmy C. Tallent was appointed president. [1] United Community Banks, Inc was incorporated as a holding company in 1987. The following year, it acquired Union County Bank, which was later renamed United Community Bank (Georgia) in 1996. During this period, the company expanded its presence through a series of regional acquisitions. In 1990, it acquired Citizens Bank of Murphy, North Carolina, which became United Community Bank (North Carolina). Additional acquisitions included United Community Bank Towns County in 1992, White County Bank of Cleveland, Georgia, in 1995, and Rabun County Bank in 1997. United Community Bank expanded its North Carolina operations in 1995, adding branches in Andrews, Franklin and Waynesville. [2] [1] Following changes in Georgia''s banking laws, United Community Bank began opening branches in addition to making acquisitions. In 1997, the company acquired the assets of a bank in Cornelia and First Clayton Bank and Trust, further extending its footprint in northern Georgia. [1] In 1999, UCB acquired Bank of Adairsville parent Adairsville Bancshares for $7.1 million plus additional costs, along with 1st Floyd Bank. Both institutions became part of United Community Bank (Georgia) in 2001. [2] Expansions continued in 2000 with the acquisitions of North Point Bancshares Inc., Independent Bancshares Inc. and consulting firm Brintech, Inc. That same year, Lendmark Financial Services Inc. purchased the consumer finance division. [2] United Community Banks, Inc. was listed on the Nasdaq in 2002, marking a major milestone in its growth as a public company. [1] In 2003, the company acquired First Georgia Holding Inc. for approximately $42 million and added First Central Bank of Lenoir City, Tennessee to its portfolio. By 2004, as assets surpassed $5 billion, United completed additional acquisitions, including Fai', '["clm_wiki_united-community-bank_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
