VALUES
  ('cs_united-community-bank_operations', 'org_united-community-bank', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Bank holding company html body This article contains paid contributions . It may require cleanup to comply with Wikipedia''s content policies , particularly neutral point of view . Please discuss further on the talk page . ( August 2025 ) United Community Banks, Inc. United Community Headquarters in Greenville, SC Type Public Traded as NYSE : UCB S&amp;P 600 component Founded 1950 &#59;&#32;76 years ago ( 1950 ) Headquarters Greenville, South Carolina , United States Key people H. Lynn Harton ( CEO ) Total assets $27.7 billion United Community is an American bank. United is one of the largest full-service financial institutions in the Southeast, with $28.2 billion in assets and 200 offices in Alabama, Florida, Georgia, North Carolina, South Carolina and Tennessee. In addition to its presence in the Southeast, United Community is the largest bank headquartered in South Carolina by total asset size. [1] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Craver, Richard (October 1, 2021). "United Community completes $131M purchase of Aquesta" . Winston-Salem Journal .', '["clm_wiki_united-community-bank_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
