VALUES
  ('cs_slb_leadership', 'org_slb', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Corporate affairs France The company has offices in multiple cities and regions in France: Abbeville, [1] Béziers, [2] Clamart, [3] Montpellier, [4] Pau [5] and Paris. [6] [7] Such sites and entities are as well at the forefront of the SLB New Energy strategy and development. (example: Geothermal with Celsius Energy [8] and Hydrogen with Genvia [9] ) United States Schlumberger maintains a 33-acre (13 ha) campus at the northeast corner of U.S. Highway 90A and Gillingham Lane in Sugar Land, Texas ; as of 2017 Schlumberger is the third largest employer in the city. In 2015, Schlumberger announced that it was moving its U.S. corporate headquarters to the Sugar Land facility from its Houston office building. The company plans to build new buildings with a scheduled completion time of late 2017. They include a total of 250,000 square feet (23,000 m 2 ) of Class A office space and an "amenities" building with 100,000 square feet (9,300 m 2 ) of space. [10] In the 1930s, the North American headquarters were established in Houston. In the 1970s, the company''s top executives in North America were relocated to New York City . By 2006, the head office had 50 executives and support staff. By that year the company was moving that office to a building near the Houston Galleria . [11] The company moved its Houston-area offices from 5000 Gulf Freeway in Houston to the Sugar Land campus in 1995. [12] [13] [14] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "SCHLUMBERGER VECTOR SAS (ABBEVILLE) Chiffre d''affaires, résultat, bilans" . Societe . Retrieved December 19, 2022 . ^ "Etablissement SCHLUMBERGER SA à BEZIERS (34500)" . Societe . Retrieved December 19, 2022 . ^ "Etablissement ETUDES ET PRODUCTIONS SCHLUMBERGER à CLAMART (92140)" . Societe . Retrieved December 19, 2022 . ^ "Etablissement SERVICES PETROLIERS SCHLUMBERGER à MONTPELLIER (34000)" . Societe . Retrieved December 19, 2022 . ^ "Etablissement SERVICES PETROLIERS SCHLUMBERGER à PAU (64000)" . Societe . Retrieved December 19, 2022 . ^ " Europe, C.I.S', '["clm_wiki_slb_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_slb_operations', 'org_slb', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Deepwater Horizon Main articles: Deepwater Horizon explosion and Deepwater Horizon oil spill In 2010, Schlumberger was contracted to perform wireline logging on the Deepwater Horizon oil rig in the Gulf of Mexico . On the day of the explosion, the Schlumberger crew was supposed to perform a cement evaluation test, but the test was cancelled and the crew was released by BP to leave the rig on the same day. [1] [2] The cost-cutting decision to cancel the test is dramatized in the subsequent film by Peter Berg . [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Reddall, Braden (May 19, 2010). "Schlumberger says its crew left Horizon day of fire-Deep Water Horizon Accident- Schlumberger" . Reuters . Retrieved May 15, 2010 . ^ "Everyone involved with the job.. completely satisfied..." (PDF) . Deep Water: The Gulf Oil Disaster and the Future of Offshore Drilling (PDF) (Report). National Commission on the BP Deepwater Horizon Oil Spill and Offshore Drilling . January 2011. pp. 3 –4. Archived (PDF) from the original on October 9, 2024. To ensure the job did not have problems, a three-man Schlumberger team was scheduled to fly out to the rig later that day, able to perform a suite of tests to examine the well''s new bottom cement seal. [...] The decision was made to send the Schlumberger team home on the 11:00 a.m. helicopter, thus saving time and the $128,000 &#32;(equivalent to $189,000 in 2025) fee. As BP Wells Team Leader John Guide noted, "Everyone involved with the job on the rig site was completely satisfied with the [cementing] job." ^ van Oort, Eric (October 7, 2016). " ''Deepwater Horizon'' honors oil rig workers but oversimplifies the blowout" . The Conversation . Retrieved October 25, 2024 .', '["clm_wiki_slb_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
-- 914. Kodak (slug=kodak, wiki='Kodak')
