VALUES
  ('cs_wsp-global_leadership', 'org_wsp-global', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Origins of WSP William Sale Partnership was established in 1969 in England by Chris Cole, Geoffrey Williams, John Sale, and Geoffrey Middleton. [1] In 1976, it was a founding member of the Building Services Research and Information Association ( BSRIA ). It was first listed on the London Stock Exchange in 1987. [1] In the 1990s, the company expanded both domestically and internationally, forming WSP Asia in 1995, incorporating Graham Group and T P O''Sullivan and Partners in 1997, acquiring US practices Cantor Seinuk and Flack + Kurtz in 2000, as well as buying Jacobson &amp; Widmark (J&amp;W) in Sweden in 2001 (J&amp;W was founded in 1938), LT Consultants Oyj and EMP Projects Oyj in Finland in 2003 and PHB Group in the UAE in 2005. [1] ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) "Building Magazine, The Long Haul" . Retrieved 3 April 2008 .', '["clm_wiki_wsp-global_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
