  ('cs_borgwarner_history', 'org_borgwarner', 'overview', 'History',
   'American automotive supply company For the trophy, see Borg-Warner Trophy . html body This article contains paid contributions . It may require cleanup to comply with Wikipedia''s content policies , particularly neutral point of view . Please discuss further on the talk page . ( September 2023 ) BorgWarner Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : BWA S&amp;P 400 component Industry Automotive Founded 1880 &#59;&#32;146 years ago ( 1880 ) Headquarters Auburn Hills, Michigan , U.S. Number of locations 92, in 24 countries [1] Area served Worldwide Key people Joseph (Joe) F. Fadool (President and Chief Executive Officer) Revenue US$ 14.1 billion (2024) Operating income US$546 million (2024) Net income US$338 million (2024) Total assets US$14.0 billion (2024) Total equity US$5.53 billion (2024) Number of employees 38,300 (2024) Divisions Air management, E-propulsion &amp; Drivetrain Website borgwarner Footnotes [2] BorgWarner Inc. is an American automotive and e-mobility supplier headquartered in Auburn Hills, Michigan . As of 2023, the company maintains production facilities and sites at 92 locations in 24 countries, [1] and generates revenues of US$14.2 billion, while employing around 39,900 people. [3] The company is one of the 25 largest automotive suppliers in the world . [4] Since February 2025, Joseph F. Fadool has been CEO of BorgWarner Inc. [5] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "BorgWarner announces $42.7M investment to expand Oconee County operations" . Upstate Business Journal . April 19, 2023 . Retrieved July 7, 2023 . ^ "Borgwarner Inc. 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 6, 2025 . Retrieved February 6, 2025 . ^ "Borgwarner Inc. 2022 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . February 9, 2023 . Retrieved July 7, 2023 . ^ Prawitz, Sven (June 7, 2022). "Das sind die 100 größten Automobilzulieferer 2021" . Automobil Industrie (in German) . Retrieved July 10, 2023 . ^ "Leadership" . www . Retrieved July 17, 2025 .', '["clm_wiki_borgwarner_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
