  ('cs_kellanova_leadership', 'org_kellanova', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Operations The Trafford Park factory in Greater Manchester , England—Kellogg''s European base since 1938. [1] The factory produces more Corn Flakes than any other Kellogg''s factory in the world. [2] Australia: Pagewood [3] Charmhaven (snack and cereal plant closed in 2014.) [4] Belgium: Zaventem &amp; Mechelen plant Brazil: São Paulo Colombia: Bogotá Canada: Mississauga , Ontario – Canadian head office Anjou, Quebec – Eastern Canada sales office Calgary , Alberta – Western Canada sales office London, Ontario – manufacturers and distributes cereals (including corn flakes) in Canada. Closed at end of 2014, [5] Belleville, Ontario – cereal production plant opened 2009 and upgraded 2011; took over some operations from London after 2014 China: Shanghai – Joint venture with agribusiness and food company Yihai Kerry Ecuador: Guayaquil France: Noisy-le-Grand , Paris [6] Germany: Hamburg (sales and marketing for Germany, Austria, Switzerland, and Scandinavia; production in Germany shut down in 2018) [7] India: Mumbai Republic of Ireland: European Head Office – Kellogg Europe Trading, Swords, County Dublin [8] Italy: Milan Japan: Shinjuku, Tokyo [9] Malaysia: Bandar Enstek , Negeri Sembilan [10] [11] Mexico: Querétaro Middle East [12] Bahrain: Manama Egypt: Giza Iran: Tehran Israel: Lod Jordan: Amman Kuwait: Kuwait City Lebanon: Beirut Libya: Tripoli Oman: Azaiba, Muscat Qatar: Doha Saudi Arabia: Jeddah Syria: Damascus UAE: Dubai Netherlands: Den Bosch [13] [14] Philippines: Bonifacio Global City Poland: Kutno [15] Portugal: Lisbon Russia: Kellogg Rus LLC [8] (Sold to the Russian company Chernogolovka in July 2023) [16] South Africa: Springs [17] South Korea: Seoul Spain: Valls (cereal production plant) and Alcobendas (Spanish head office) [8] Sri Lanka: Colombo ; Sri Jayawardenapura Kotte Thailand: Bangkok , Rayong (snacks and cereals) United Kingdom: England: Manchester [8] Scotland: Portable Foods Manufacturing Livingston [8] Wales: Wrexham including Portable Foods Manufact', '["clm_wiki_kellanova_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
