VALUES
  ('cs_precision-castparts_history', 'org_precision-castparts', 'overview', 'History',
   'American manufacturing company 45°29′21″N 122°40′22″W &#xfeff; / &#xfeff; 45.4891271°N 122.6728299°W &#xfeff; / 45.4891271; -122.6728299 Precision Castparts Corp. Type Subsidiary Industry Aerospace and defense Founded April 1, 1953 &#59;&#32;73 years ago ( 1953-04-01 ) in Portland, Oregon , U.S. Headquarters Portland, Oregon , U.S. Key people Mark Donegan ( Chairman &amp; CEO ) Products Investment castings, forged products, fasteners Revenue US$ 9.6 billion (FY 2014) [1] Operating income US$2.6 billion (FY 2014) [1] Net income US$1.7 billion (FY 2014) [1] Total assets US$18.5 billion (FY 2014) [1] Total equity US$11.4 billion (FY 2014) [1] Owner Berkshire Hathaway (since 2016) [2] Number of employees 30,100 (March 2015) [2] Divisions PCC Airfoils, PCC Structurals, PCC Energy Group, PCC Fasteners, PCC Aerostructures Subsidiaries Wyman-Gordon , Special Metals Corporation , Titanium Metals Corporation , Texas Honing Inc. Website www Precision Castparts Corp. is an American industrial goods and metal fabrication company that manufactures investment castings, forged components, and airfoil castings for use in the aerospace , industrial gas turbine, and defense industries. In 2009, it ranked 362nd on the Fortune 500 list, and 11th in the aerospace and defense industry. [3] In 2015, it ranked 322nd overall and 9th in the aerospace and defense industry. [4] In 2014, it ranked 133rd on the S&amp;P 500 based on market capitalization. [5] In January 2016, the company became a wholly owned subsidiary of Berkshire Hathaway . [2] [6] Before that event, it used to be one of the three Fortune 500 companies headquartered in Oregon . ^ a b c d e body:not( ):not( ) "Precision Castparts 2012 Annual Report, Form 10-K, Filing Date May 31, 2012" (PDF) . secdatabase . Retrieved June 8, 2012 . ^ a b c Rogoway, Mike (January 30, 2016) [first published online January 29]. "Precision Castparts'' $37B sale finalized" . The Oregonian . p. C8 . Retrieved February 2, 2016 . ^ Precision Castparts. &#91; dead link &#93; Fortune 500: 2009. CNNMoney . Retrieved on April 20, 2009. ^ Brett Krasnove (June 3, 2015). "Fortune 500" . Fortune . Retrieved April 16, 2016 . ^ Dividend Channel (September 8, 2014). "Precision Castparts Takes Over #133 Spot From Kraft Foods Group" . Forbes . ^ F., Bruner; Jake, Dubois. "Warren E. Buffett, 2015" . SSRN 2974596 .', '["clm_wiki_precision-castparts_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
