  ('cs_precision-castparts_leadership', 'org_precision-castparts', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '20th century Precision Castparts (PCC) was founded by Joseph Buford Cox on April 1, 1953. [1] Cox was owner of Oregon Saw Chain and in 1949 had started a casting operation to make saw teeth with assistant general manager Ed Cooley also working on the project. In 1953 Cox separated the two companies and PCC was formed, moving into a new larger facility in 1955, and incorporating the following year with Ed Cooley as one of the owners. [1] ^ a b History. Deprecated link archived March 11, 2002, at archive Precision Castparts. Retrieved on February 28, 2008.', '["clm_wiki_precision-castparts_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
