  ('cs_agco_history', 'org_agco', 'overview', 'History',
   'American agricultural machinery manufacturer For the Ontario government commission, see Alcohol and Gaming Commission of Ontario . AGCO Corporation Formerly Gleaner-Allis Corporation Allis-Gleaner Corporation Type Public Traded as NYSE : AGCO S&amp;P 400 component Industry Agricultural machinery Predecessor Allis-Chalmers (1909–1985) Deutz-Allis (1985–1990) Founded 1990 &#59;&#32;36 years ago ( 1990 ) Headquarters Duluth, Georgia , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Eric Hansotia ( chairman , president , CEO ) Damon Audia ( senior vice president , CFO ) Products Tractors , Combines , Hay tools, Foragers , Seeding &amp; Tillage equipment, Self-propelled sprayers , Smart Farming Technology, Diesel engines and generators Brands Challenger , Fendt , Gleaner , GSI, Massey Ferguson , RoGator, TerraGator, Sunflower Manufacturing, Valtra , White Farm Equipment , JCA Technologies Services Parts, service, finance Revenue US$ 14.41 billion (2023) Net income US$1.17 billion (2023) Total assets US$11.42 billion (2023) [1] Total equity US$4.66 billion (2023) [1] Number of employees 27,900 (2023) Website agcocorp AGCO Corporation is an American agricultural machinery manufacturer headquartered in Duluth, Georgia , United States. It was founded in 1990. AGCO designs, produces and sells tractors , combines , foragers , hay tools, self-propelled sprayers , smart farming technologies, seeding equipment, and tillage equipment. ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "US SEC: Form 10-K AGCO Corporation for fiscal year ending December 31, 2023" . United States Securities and Exchange Commission . Archived from the original on May 22, 2024 . Retrieved September 5, 2024 .', '["clm_wiki_agco_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
