  ('cs_tenneco_leadership', 'org_tenneco', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Federal Mogul and Öhlins acquisitions On October 1, 2018, Tenneco completed its acquisition of Federal-Mogul , a large global supplier to original equipment manufacturers and the aftermarket. [1] The following month, Tenneco bought a majority stake in Öhlins for $160 million. [2] In February 2019, Tenneco announced that it would spin off its automotive aftermarket suspension components into DRiV Incorporated. [3] In October 2024, Tenneco agreed to sell Öhlins to Brembo for $405 million. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Tenneco Announces Close Of Federal-Mogul Acquisition" (Press release). ^ "Tenneco to buy Öhlins Racing for $160M" . November 16, 2018. Archived from the original on October 2, 2020 . Retrieved August 10, 2020 . ^ "DRiV Incorporated to Spin From Tenneco Later This Year" . Business Wire (Press release). February 14, 2019 . Retrieved November 11, 2019 . ^ "Brembo buys suspension maker Ohlins Racing for $405 million" . Reuters . Retrieved October 11, 2024 .', '["clm_wiki_tenneco_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
