VALUES
  ('cs_red-hat_history', 'org_red-hat', 'overview', 'History',
   'American open source software company This article is about the company. For other uses, see Red Hat (disambiguation) . Red Hat, LLC Red Hat Tower , the company''s headquarters in Raleigh Type Subsidiary (Independent) Industry Computer software Predecessor Container Linux Cygnus Solutions Founded March 1993 &#59;&#32;33 years ago ( 1993-03 ) Founder Bob Young Marc Ewing Headquarters Raleigh, North Carolina , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Matt Hicks ( President and CEO ) [1] Paul Cormier ( Chairman ) [2] Products List Red Hat Enterprise Linux Red Hat Directory Server Satellite Red Hat Enterprise Virtualization Red Hat Storage Server JBoss EAP Red Hat Single Sign On Ansible CloudForms OpenShift Red Hat Hyperconverged Infrastructure for Virtualization Red Hat Certificate System Red Hat AMQ Red Hat Insights [3] Number of employees 19,000 [4] Parent IBM (2019–present) Subsidiaries § Red Hat Czech § Red Hat India Website redhat Red Hat, LLC (formerly Red Hat Software, Inc. and then Red Hat, Inc. ) is an American software company that provides open source software products to enterprises and is a subsidiary of IBM . [5] Founded in 1993, Red Hat has its corporate headquarters in Raleigh, North Carolina , with other offices worldwide. Red Hat has become associated to a large extent with its enterprise operating system Red Hat Enterprise Linux (RHEL). Having grown significantly beyond just Linux, it also includes the OpenShift Container Platform, Ansible Automation Platform, and Red Hat AI. Red Hat had acquired the open-source enterprise middleware vendor JBoss. Red Hat now offers OpenShift Virtualization, which replaces the long retired product Red Hat Virtualization (RHV), an enterprise virtualization product. Red Hat provides operating system platforms, middleware, applications, management products, support, training, and consulting services . Red Hat creates, maintains, and contributes to many free software projects. It has acquired the codebases of several proprietary software products through corporate mergers and acquisitions , and has released such software under open source licenses . As of June 2026 &#91;update&#93; , Red Hat is the fourth largest corporate contributor to the Linux kernel after Intel , Meta, and Google. [6] On October 28, 2018, IBM announced its intent to acquire Red Hat for $34 billion. [7] [8] [9] The acquisition closed on July 9, 2019, and it now operates as an independent subsidiary. [10] [11] [10] On January 12, 2026, Red Hat c', '["clm_wiki_red-hat_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_red-hat_leadership', 'org_red-hat', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'IBM subsidiary On October 28, 2018, IBM announced its intent to acquire Red Hat for US$34 billion, in one of its largest-ever acquisitions. The company will operate out of IBM''s Hybrid Cloud division. [1] [2] Microsoft , Amazon , and Google reportedly also considered buying Red Hat. [3] Six months later, on May 3, 2019, the US Department of Justice concluded its review of IBM''s proposed Red Hat acquisition, [4] and according to Steven J. Vaughan-Nichols "essentially approved the IBM/Red Hat deal". [5] The acquisition was closed on July 9, 2019. [6] On January 12, 2026, Red Hat converted from a corporation to a limited liability company. &#91; citation needed &#93; ^ body:not( ):not( ) Liptak, Andrew (October 28, 2018). "IBM will acquire open-source cloud software company Red Hat" . The Verge . Retrieved October 28, 2018 . ^ Kolodny, Lora; Sherman, Alex (October 28, 2018). "IBM to acquire Red Hat in deal valued at $34 billion" . CNBC . Retrieved October 28, 2018 . ^ Peterson, Becky (December 16, 2018). "IBM''s $34 billion Red Hat acquisition came after deal talks with Microsoft, Google, and Amazon, sources say" . Business Insider . Retrieved May 22, 2025 . ^ United States Securities and Exchange Commission. "International Business Machines Corporation" . Form 8-K Current Report Pursuant to Section 13 or 15 (d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 . Archived from the original on June 3, 2019 . Retrieved June 3, 2019 . ^ Vaughan-Nichols, Steven J. "IBM''s Red Hat acquisition moves forward" . ZDNet . Retrieved June 3, 2019 . ^ "IBM Closes Landmark Acquisition of Red Hat for $34 Billion; Defines Open, Hybrid Cloud Future" (Press release). Red Hat. July 9, 2019 . Retrieved July 9, 2019 .', '["clm_wiki_red-hat_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
