VALUES
  ('cs_avaya_leadership', 'org_avaya', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisitions and partnerships Since 2001, Avaya has sold and acquired several companies. [1] Through Nortel''s bankruptcy proceedings, assets related to their Enterprise Voice and Data business units were auctioned. Avaya placed a $900 million bid, and was announced as the winner of the assets on September 14, 2009. [2] [3] In 1985, Performance Engineering Corporation (later PEC Solutions) was formed to offer technology services to government customers. [4] On June 6, 2005, Nortel acquired PEC Solutions to form Nortel PEC Solutions. [5] [6] On January 18, 2006, Nortel PEC Solutions was renamed Nortel Government Solutions. [7] On December 21, 2009, Avaya acquired Nortel''s government business as part of the company''s assets sale. [8] [9] In October 2019, Avaya entered into a strategic partnership with RingCentral and together, introduced a new unified communications as a service solution called Avaya Cloud Office ("ACO"). RingCentral also contributed $500 million to be the exclusive provider of the new Avaya UCaaS offering. [10] Avaya''s headquarters are at 350 Mt. Kemble Avenue, Morristown, New Jersey 07960 US. [11] Avaya sponsors the IAUG users'' group [12] and training programs for IT professional certification in the use of Avaya''s products. [13] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Avaya Acquisitions" . avaya . Retrieved January 22, 2015 . ^ Sean Michael Kerner (September 14, 2009). "Avaya Closes Nortel Enterprise Deal for $900M" . internetnews . Retrieved February 16, 2010 . ^ "Nortel Networks, Form 8-K, Current Report, Filing Date Sep 14, 2009" (PDF) . secdatabase . Retrieved January 19, 2013 . ^ "PEC Solutions Inc" . Washington Post 200PEC Solutions Inc. 2005 . Retrieved April 1, 2011 . ^ "Nortel Completes Acquisition of PEC Solutions, Inc" . Business Wire. June 7, 2005 . Retrieved April 1, 2011 . ^ Witte, Griff (April 27, 2005). "Nortel to Buy PEC Solutions For $448 Million" . The Washington Post . ^ "Nortel PEC Solutions Renamed Nortel Government Solutions" . Nortel. January ', '["clm_wiki_avaya_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
