   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_enviri_operations', 'org_enviri', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History Harsco rail equipment seen in Bradford, Ontario, May 2015. Harsco was founded in 1853 as The Harrisburg Car Manufacturing Company and became the Harrisburg Steel Corporation in 1935. Following a series of acquisitions, the company became Harsco Corporation in 1956, forming three divisions: Metals &amp; Minerals (Now Harsco Environmental), Rail, and Industrial. By the early 1990s, Harsco products and services covered defense, industrial, commercial, and construction applications, with over 250 manufacturing, reclamation, distribution, and service facilities across 14 countries. [1] In 2018, Harsco acquired Altek, [2] a UK producer of aluminum processing equipment. In 2019, Harsco Metals &amp; Minerals rebranded to Harsco Environmental, and acquired Clean Earth, a U.S. provider of services for specialty waste streams. [3] In April 2020, Harsco Corporation acquired the Environmental Solutions business (ESOL) from Stericycle, Inc. [4] The company finally rebranded as Enviri in 2023. [5] Enviri operates as the mother company with its three main divisions Clean Earth, Harsco Environmental and Harsco Rail. Additional subsidiary companies include Altek, SteelPhalt, and Black Beauty Abrasives. ^ body:not( ):not( ) Kepos, Paula; Derdak, Thomas (1988). International Directory of Company Histories . St. James Press. p. 245. ISBN 155862323X . ^ "£45m deal agreed to acquire manufacturer" . ^ Corporation, Harsco (2019-05-09). "Harsco Enters Into Definitive Agreement to Acquire Clean Earth, Accelerating its Transformation to a Global Market Leader of Environmental Solutions" . GlobeNewswire News Room (Press release) . Retrieved 2023-02-03 . ^ "Harsco Acquires Stericycle''s Environmental Solutions Business" . finance . 2020-04-07 . Retrieved 2020-04-07 . ^ Cite error: The named reference :0 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ).', '["clm_wiki_enviri_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
