VALUES
  ('cs_pall_operations', 'org_pall', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Achievements 1990 : Dr. Pall is awarded the National Medal of Technology for patenting and commercializing over 100 filtration and other fluid clarification products beneficial to society and for building Pall Corporation into a global company. [1] 2008 : Dr. Pall is posthumously inducted into the National Inventors Hall of Fame for his invention of the leukoreduction filter. [2] 2009 : Pall Corporation is named one of the greenest companies in America in Newsweek ’s September 28 issue. The company was ranked second in the industrial goods sector and 47th among America''s largest companies. [3] [4] 2011 : Pall Corporation is awarded the Engineering Materials Achievement Award (EMAA) by ASM International . The company was recognized for its porous iron aluminide technology. [5] 2011 : Pall Corporation is named a top green company in Newsweek ''s third annual Green Rankings. The company was ranked fifth in the capital goods sector and 69th among the U.S. 500 list. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "The National Medal of Technology and Innovation Recipients, 1990 Laureates" . United States Patent and Trademark Office . Retrieved 12 September 2011 . ^ "David Boris Pall" . National Inventors Hall of Fame. Archived from the original on 5 August 2011 . Retrieved 12 September 2011 . ^ "Pall Corporation Named a Top Green Company by Newsweek" . Machinery Lubrication . Retrieved 12 September 2011 . ^ "Pall in Russia" . Retrieved 2013-07-19 . ^ "Pall wins Engineering Materials Achievement Award for 2011" . Filtration + Separation. 14 September 2010 . Retrieved 12 September 2011 . ^ "Pall Corporation Named A Top Green Company By Newsweek" . Pharmaceutical Online. 1 November 2011. Archived from the original on 15 September 2012 . Retrieved 9 November 2011 . : CS1 maint: deprecated archival service ( link )', '["clm_wiki_pall_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
