  ('cs_teradata_overview', 'org_teradata', 'overview', 'Overview',
   'Teradata Corporation is an American software company that provides cloud database and analytics-related software, products, and services. The company was formed in 1979 in Brentwood, California, as a collaboration between researchers at Caltech and Citibank''s advanced technology group.', '["clm_wiki_teradata_overview"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   10, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_teradata_history', 'org_teradata', 'overview', 'History',
   'Overview Teradata is an enterprise software company that develops and sells database analytics software. [1] [2] [3] [4] The company provides three main services: business analytics, cloud products, and consulting. [5] It operates in North and Latin America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia. [6] Teradata is headquartered in San Diego , California, and has additional major U.S. locations in Atlanta and San Francisco , where its data center research and development is housed. [3] It is publicly traded on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE) under the stock symbol TDC. [7] Steve McMillan has served as the company''s president and chief executive officer since 2020. [8] [9] [10] The company reported $1.836 billion in revenue, a net income of $129 million, and 8,535 employees globally, as of February 9, 2020. [11] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Teradata Express &#124; Download Free Trial" . ^ Abrar, Peerzada (November 23, 2017). "Teradata to help Rajasthan Govt. on citizen services" . The Hindu . ISSN 0971-751X . OCLC 13119119 . Retrieved December 7, 2017 . ^ a b Freeman, Mike (July 14, 2017). "San Diego data center tech start-up StackIQ acquired by Teradata" . The San Diego Union-Tribune . Tronc . Retrieved December 7, 2017 . ^ Macaulay, Tom (October 24, 2017). "How Teradata aims to unify customers'' analytics under new data platform" . Computerworld . Retrieved December 7, 2017 . ^ Backaitis, Virginia (September 13, 2016). "Teradata Promises to Better Serve its Customers #TDPARTNERS16" . CMS Wire . Archived from the original on December 22, 2017 . Retrieved December 7, 2017 . ^ "The World''s Biggest Public Companies: #1,982 Teradata" . Forbes . Retrieved December 7, 2017 . ^ "NCR Completes Teradata Spin Off" (Press release). NCR. October 1, 2007. Archived from the original on October 18, 2007. ^ Condon, Stephanie (7 May 2020). "Teradata names Steve McMillan as new CEO" . ZDNET . Retrieved 2026-03-03 . ^ Navera, Tristan (November 17, 2016). "Teradata execs: New strategy to mean ''double digit'' growth" . Dayton Business Journal . Retrieved December 7, 2017 . ^ "SD500 2022: Steve McMillan" . San Diego Business Journal . 2023-01-19 . Retrieved 2026-03-03 . ^ "For 10-K: Annual Report for the Fiscal Year Ending December 31, 2019" . February 28, 2020. Archived from the original on November 15, 2021 . Retrieved August 10, 2020 .', '["clm_wiki_teradata_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_teradata_leadership', 'org_teradata', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'History The concept of Teradata grew from research at the California Institute of Technology and from the discussions of Citibank ''s advanced technology group in the 1970s. [1] In 1979, the company was incorporated in Brentwood, California , by Jack E. Shemer, Philip M. Neches, Walter E. Muir, Jerold R. Modes, William P. Worth, Carroll Reed and David Hartke. Teradata released its DBC/1012 database machine in 1984, [2] [3] with Citibank as an early customer. [4] In 1990, the company acquired Sharebase, originally named Britton Lee , [5] another early database machine vendor that, unlike Teradata''s IBM mainframe focus, primarily served midrange systems . [4] In September 1991, AT&amp;T Corporation acquired NCR Corporation , [6] which announced the acquisition of Teradata for about $250 million in December. Teradata built the first system over 1 terabyte for Wal-Mart in 1992. [7] NCR acquired Strategic Technologies &amp; Systems in 1999 and appointed Stephen Brobst as chief technology officer of Teradata Solutions Group. In 2000, NCR acquired Ceres Integrated Solutions and its customer relationship management software for $90 million, [8] as well as Stirling Douglas Group and its demand chain management software. [9] Teradata acquired financial management software from DecisionPoint in 2005. [10] In January 2007, NCR announced Teradata would become an independent public company, led by Michael F. Koehler . [11] [12] The new company''s shares started trading in October. [13] In April 2016, a hardware product line called IntelliFlex was announced. [14] Victor L. Lund became the chief executive on May 5, 2016. [15] [16] In October 2018, Teradata started promoting its cloud analytics software called Vantage (which evolved from the Teradata Database). [17] On May 7, 2020, Teradata announced the appointment of Steve McMillan as president and chief executive officer, effective June 8, 2020. [18] In December 2024, Teradata successfully appealed a California federal judge''s deci', '["clm_wiki_teradata_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_teradata_operations', 'org_teradata', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisitions and divestitures Teradata has acquired several companies since becoming an independent public company in 2008. In March 2008, Teradata acquired professional services company Claraview, which previously had spun out software provider Clarabridge . [1] Teradata acquired column-oriented DBMS vendor Kickfire in August 2010, [2] [3] followed by the marketing software company Aprimo for about $550 million in December. [4] [5] In March 2011, the company acquired Aster Data Systems for about $263 million. [6] [7] Teradata acquired Software-as-a-service digital marketing company eCircle in May 2012, which was merged into the Aprimo business. [8] In 2014, Teradata acquired the assets of Revelytix, a provider of information management products and for a reported $50 million. [9] [10] [11] [12] In September, Teradata acquired Hadoop service firm Think Big Analytics. [12] In December, Teradata acquired RainStor , a company specializing in online data archiving on Hadoop. [13] Teradata acquired Appoxxee, a mobile marketing software as a service provider, for about $20 million in January 2015, [14] followed by the Netherlands-based digital marketing company FLXone in September. That same year Teradata acquired a small Business Intelligence firm, MiaPearl. [15] In July 2016, the marketing applications division, using the Aprimo brand, was sold to private equity firm Marlin Equity Partners for about $90 million [16] [17] with Aprimo under CEO John Stammen moving its headquarters to Chicago. [18] while absorbing Revenew Inc. that Marlin had also bought. [19] Teradata acquired Big Data Partnership, a service company based in the UK, on July 21, 2016. [20] In July 2017, Teradata acquired StackIQ, maker of the Stacki cluster manager software. [21] In 2023, Teradata acquired Stemma, a data catalog software provider. [22] [23] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Grimes, Seth (March 20, 2008). "Teradata has Acquired BI/DW Firm Claraview" . InformationWeek . Archived from the original on Octo', '["clm_wiki_teradata_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
