  ('cs_wixcom_operations', 'org_wixcom', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Corporate affairs Wix was founded in 2006 by Israeli developers Avishai Abrahami , Nadav Abrahami, and Giora Kaplan. [1] With its main offices in Tel Aviv , Wix was backed by investors Insight Venture Partners , Mangrove Capital Partners, Bessemer Venture Partners , DAG Ventures , and Benchmark Capital . [2] By April 2010, Wix had 3.5 million users and raised US$10 million in Series C funding provided by Benchmark Capital and existing investors Bessemer Venture Partners and Mangrove Capital Partners. [3] In March 2011, Wix had 8.5 million users and raised US$40 million in Series D funding, bringing its total funding to that date to US$61 million. [4] By August 2013, the Wix platform had more than 34 million registered users. [5] On 5 November 2013, Wix had an initial public offering on NASDAQ , raising about US$127 million for the company and some shareholders. [6] In 2016, Mark Tluszcz became the chair of the board of directors. In 2020, Wix''s revenue increased to $989 million, a 30% rise year-on-year, primarily due to the shift of businesses online during the coronavirus pandemic . The company added over 31 million new registered users in 2020, reaching a total of 196.7 million by year''s end. Wix added approximately 1 million net new premium subscriptions in 2020, surpassing $1 billion in annual collections for the first time. By the end of the year, there were 5.5 million premium subscriptions, a 22% increase compared to the end of 2019. [7] As of its most recent reporting in June 2024, Wix has over 260 million users worldwide. [8] In May 2026, Wix announced layoffs affecting approximately 1,000 employees, or 20% of its workforce. CEO Avishai Abrahami cited two factors: the need to restructure around artificial intelligence and the appreciation of the Israeli shekel against the US dollar , which increased the cost of its Israel-based workforce relative to its dollar-denominated revenue. [9] [10] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Tress, Luke (23 February 2017). "Wix acquires o', '["clm_wiki_wixcom_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
