  ('cs_plains-all-american-pipeline_history', 'org_plains-all-american-pipeline', 'overview', 'History',
   'Midstream oil and gas company Plains All American Pipeline, L.P. Type Public Traded as Nasdaq : PAA Nasdaq : PAGP Industry Petroleum industry Founded 1981 &#59;&#32;45 years ago ( 1981 ) Headquarters Houston, Texas , United States Key people Willie Chiang ( chairman and CEO ) Services Pipeline transport Oil terminal Revenue $57.342 billion (2022) Net income $1,037 billion (2022) Total assets $23.892 billion (2022) Total equity $13.325 billion (2022) Website www Footnotes [1] Plains (also known as " Plains All American Pipeline, L.P." and " Plains GP Holdings ") is a master limited partnership engaged in pipeline transport , marketing, and storage of liquefied petroleum gas and petroleum in the United States and Canada . [2] [3] Plains owns interests in 18,370 miles (29,560 km) of pipelines, storage capacity for about 75 million barrels of crude oil, 28 million barrels of NGLs, 68 billion cubic feet of natural gas , and 5 natural gas processing plants. The company is headquartered in the Allen Center in Downtown Houston , Texas . [1] Plains (NASDAQ: PAA) is a publicly traded Master limited partnership . PAA owns an extensive network of pipeline transportation, terminalling, storage and gathering assets in key crude oil and NGL producing basins and transportation corridors at major market hubs in the United States and Canada. [4] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "Plains All American Pipeline, L.P. 2022 Form 10-K Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . ^ "Who We Are" . Plains All American Pipeline . Retrieved 2025-12-22 . ^ "Plains GP Holdings" . Fortune . Retrieved 2025-12-22 . ^ "About Us" . Plains . Retrieved July 30, 2023 .', '["clm_wiki_plains-all-american-pipeline_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
