  ('cs_fti-consulting_leadership', 'org_fti-consulting', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Criticism and controversies In 2020, the New York Times reported on FTI consulting''s work for the fossil fuel industry. Reporting found that FTI had helped to design, staff and run organizations and websites funded by energy companies that were made to appear to represent grass-roots support for fossil-fuel initiatives. [1] [2] [3] [4] [5] [6] [7] [8] In 2023, the company was hired by Johnny &amp; Associates to manage a press conference addressing sexual abuse by its late founder Johnny Kitagawa . The Japanese public broadcaster NHK reported that the consulting firm had a ''blacklist'' of journalists to avoid calling on during the event. [9] [10] FTI admitted the existence of the ''blacklist'' as well as a list of reporters who should preferably be given a chance to ask a question. [11] [12] The firm also admitted the lists were given to the conference modulator. [12] Their concern about some reporters who would spend long periods talking about their own opinions or ask thoughtless questions (or remarks) that could be unnecessarily stressful and painful to the victims watching the press conference was given as a reason to prepare the list. [12] FTI told the press that their press conference policy was confirmed with the talent agency. [12] On whether it is a good system to prepare such lists, Akihiro Nojiri, Senior Managing Director of Strategic Communications at FTI Consulting Japan Office, said, "Well, I don''t think I am in a position to judge whether it is good or not." [13] ^ Cite error: The named reference NYTimes_20201111 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference FT_20201116 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference FT_20201122 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference House_Committee_20220817 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference DeSmog_20220826 was invoked but never defined (see the he', '["clm_wiki_fti-consulting_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
