VALUES
  ('cs_groupon_leadership', 'org_groupon', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Initial public offering On June 2, 2011, Groupon filed to go public under the ticker symbol GRPN. [1] The company went public on November 4, 2011, with its shares listed on Nasdaq . [2] It was the biggest IPO by an Internet company since Google in 2004. [3] The IPO was handled by Morgan Stanley , Goldman Sachs Group and Credit Suisse Group . [4] On August 10, 2011, Groupon updated its IPO filing, after facing scrutiny from regulators and analysts over its use of a non-standard accounting metric called Adjusted Consolidated Segment Operating Income . Critics argued that ACSOI was used by Groupon to present a misleading metric of profitability. Groupon''s original IPO filing with ACSOI accounting showed a positive operating income of $60.6 million for 2010; after replacing the ACSOI metric with standard accounting metrics, Groupon''s IPO filing reported an operating loss of $420 million for 2010. [5] Prior to the IPO, some analysts criticized Groupon''s decision to pay out over $940 million of the $1.12 billion in venture capital Groupon had raised before the IPO – over 84% of its venture capital raised – as cash payouts to its 3 founders and early backers, rather than into the company. [6] The large cash payout also made Groupon technically insolvent when it filed for its IPO. [7] In 2012, it was noted that Groupon had lost 80% of its value since its initial public offering the previous year. [8] The stock had since rebounded and was trading around $8 in Q1 2015 before plunging as low as $2.15 in early 2016. [9] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Groupon files for a $750-million IPO" . LA Times Blogs – Technology . June 2, 2011 . Retrieved September 24, 2019 . ^ Pepitone, Julianne. "Groupon spikes 31% in IPO" . CNN . Archived from the original on November 7, 2011 . Retrieved September 24, 2019 . ^ "Groupon''s IPO biggest by U.S. Web company since Google" . Reuters . November 4, 2011 . Retrieved April 11, 2016 . ^ "Groupon''s IPO biggest by U.S. Web company since Google" . Reuters . No', '["clm_wiki_groupon_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
