   'American semiconductor manufacturer Wolfspeed, Inc. Formerly Cree, Inc. (1999–2021) Type Public Traded as NYSE : WOLF Nasdaq : CREE (1993–2021 Industry Electronics Founded 1987 &#59;&#32;39 years ago ( 1987 ) Headquarters Research Triangle Park , North Carolina, US Products Wide-bandgap semiconductors Revenue US$ 807 million (2024) Operating income US$–445 million (2024) Net income US$–864 million (2024) Total assets US$7.98 billion (2024) Total equity US$882 million (2024) Number of employees 5,013 (2024) Website wolfspeed Footnotes [1] Wolfspeed, Inc. is an American developer and manufacturer of wide-bandgap semiconductors , focused on silicon carbide materials and devices for power applications such as transportation, power supplies, power inverters , and wireless systems. The company was formerly named Cree, Inc. [1] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "Wolfspeed, Inc. FY 2024 Annual Report (Form 10-K)" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . August 22, 2024.', '["clm_wiki_wolfspeed_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
