VALUES
  ('cs_scripps-networks-interactive_leadership', 'org_scripps-networks-interactive', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Acquisition by Discovery On July 31, 2017, Discovery Communications announced that it would acquire Scripps Networks Interactive for $14.6 billion in a cash and stock deal. [1] Discovery will establish an operational hub in Knoxville, but the company also announced plans to relocate its worldwide headquarters from Silver Spring, Maryland to New York City in 2019. [2] On February 6, 2018, the European Commission approved the deal. Since Liberty Global , which operates pay television services in Poland under the UPC Polska brand, is a major shareholder in Discovery Communications, the EU required that Discovery ensure the continued availability of TVN24 and TVN24 BiS to third-party television providers. [3] [4] The purchase was approved by the U.S. Department of Justice on February 27, 2018, [5] and was completed on March 6, 2018; at that time, the company also changed its name to Discovery, Inc. [6] SNI''s chief programmer Kathleen Finch was retained as Discovery''s Chief Lifestyle Brands Officer, overseeing the former SNI channels, as well as Discovery lifestyle networks such as TLC . [7] In turn, Discovery, Inc. merged with WarnerMedia in April 2022 to form Warner Bros. Discovery ; Finch was subsequently promoted to head of U.S. Networks, overseeing all non-premium cable networks run by Warner Bros. Discovery (besides Magnolia Network , which reports to HBO head Casey Bloys). [8] [9] [10] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Szalai, Georg (July 31, 2017). "Discovery to Acquire Scripps Networks for $14.6 Billion" . The Hollywood Reporter . Retrieved July 31, 2017 . ^ Steinberg, Brian (January 9, 2018). "Discovery Communications to Shift Headquarters to New York City" . Variety . Retrieved January 9, 2018 . ^ "Case M.8665 – Discovery / Scripps" (PDF) . European Commission. February 6, 2018. Archived (PDF) from the original on March 7, 2018 . Retrieved March 6, 2018 . ^ "European Commission Clears Discovery Deal to Buy Scripps" . The Hollywood Reporter . Retrieved March 7, 2018 . ^ "Di', '["clm_wiki_scripps-networks-interactive_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
