VALUES
  ('cs_unity_operations', 'org_unity', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'New platforms and expansion (2009–2019) The technology was developed for different platforms. [1] By 2018, Unity was used to make games and other experiences for more than 25 platforms, including mobile, desktop, consoles, and virtual reality. [2] [3] Unity games can also be deployed on the Web. [3] [2] The Unity Asset Store launched in November 2010 as an online marketplace for Unity users to sell project assets (artwork, code systems, audio, etc.) to each other. [4] In April 2012, Unity reportedly had 1 million registered developers, 300,000 of whom used Unity on a monthly basis. [5] In May of the same year, a survey by Game Developer revealed that approximately 53% of mobile game developers were using Unity. [6] By 2016, the company reported more than 5.5 million registered users. [7] Part of Unity''s appeal is that it allows people who lack the technical knowledge to program games from scratch to create games and other simulations. [1] Facebook integrated a software development kit for games using the Unity game engine in 2013. [8] The kit featured tools that allowed tracking advertising campaigns and deep linking , where users were directly linked from social media posts to specific portions within games, and in-game-image sharing. [8] Unity acquired Applifier, a Helsinki-based mobile service provider, in March 2014. Applifier''s game replay sharing and community service was initially called Everyplay, and became known as Unity Everyplay. The acquisition also meant that Applifier''s mobile video ad network, GameAds, became Unity Ads. [9] Two more acquisitions followed later in 2014: Playnomics, a data analysis platform for developers (now Unity Analytics), and Tsugi, whose continuous integration service became known as Unity Cloud Build. [10] [11] In October 2014, Helgason announced in a blog post that he would be stepping down as CEO with John Riccitiello , the former CEO of game company Electronic Arts , replacing him. Helgason remained with the company as execu', '["clm_wiki_unity_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
