  ('cs_element-solutions_operations', 'org_element-solutions', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'History The corporation was founded in 2013 by Martin E. Franklin , with financial backing from Bill Ackman . [1] In July, 2018, United Phosphorus Limited announced the acquisition of Arysta Life Sciences, the Crop business of Platform Specialty Chemicals for a total sum of $4.2 billion, with the latter exiting the crop business entirely. [2] In 2019, the company changed its name to Element Solutions Inc. from Platform Specialty Chemicals. [3] It is now listed as ESI on the New York Stock Exchange. [4] [5] In March 2025, Element Solutions was added to the S&amp;P SmallCap 600 Index. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Raice, Shayndi; Walker, Ian (July 13, 2015). "Martin Franklin Expands Chemicals Empire With $2.1 Billion U.K. deal: Acquisition is latest in deal-making spree by founder of Jarden and Nomad groups" . The Wall Street Journal . Retrieved October 31, 2015 . ^ "UPL completes acquisition of Arysta LifeScience for $4.2 billion" . The Economic Times . 2019-02-04 . Retrieved 2019-06-03 . ^ "Platform Specialty Products launches as Element Solutions" . Chemical &amp; Engineering News . Retrieved 2019-06-03 . ^ Cite error: The named reference hammond was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Cite error: The named reference cnbc was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Indices, S&amp;P Dow Jones. "DoorDash, TKO Group Holdings, Williams-Sonoma and Expand Energy Set to Join S&amp;P 500; Others to Join S&amp;P 100, S&amp;P MidCap 400 and S&amp;P SmallCap 600" . www . Retrieved 2025-06-02 .', '["clm_wiki_element-solutions_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
