VALUES
  ('cs_amylin-pharmaceuticals_leadership', 'org_amylin-pharmaceuticals', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   '1992–1998: Invention of Pramlintide and partnership with Johnson &amp; Johnson Amylin, in its natural form, is sticky, clumping on needles and forming little rocks &#91; clarification needed &#93; in the pancreas . To create a synthetic version that was more reliable and easy to work with, researchers at Amylin Pharmaceuticals altered amino acids in the molecule. The result was a new drug named pramlintide . [1] In 1995, Amylin Pharmactietucals signed an agreement with Johnson &amp; Johnson ''s LifeScan division to further develop pramlintide. [2] A Phase II study made public in January 1997 showed that pramlintide was safe to mix with leading short-acting and intermediate-acting commercial insulin products, with preliminary results suggesting it might improve glycemic control . [3] Initial Phase III trial results released in August 1997 demonstrated statistically significant results for type 1 (juvenile-onset) diabetes , helping modestly to improve glucose control without increasing the risk of hypoglycemia (low blood sugar) while also improving weight and cholesterol levels. In patients with adult-onset type 2 diabetes , pramlintide showed significant benefits at six months but not after 12 months. [4] In 1998, Johnson &amp; Johnson terminated its partnership with Amylin. [5] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Chartrand, Sabra (1997-11-17). "Patents; Presenting amylin, which is being called the first new diabetes drug since the discovery of insulin" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Retrieved 2017-05-26 . ^ Fisher, Lawrence M. (1995-06-22). "Amylin Gets Johnson Deal And Ends One With Glaxo" . The New York Times . ISSN 0362-4331 . Retrieved 2017-05-26 . ^ Moukheiber, Zina (2000-07-24). "Roller Coasting" . Forbes . Retrieved 2017-05-26 . ^ "The Motley Fool, 3/20/98: The Daily Trouble" . www . Archived from the original on 2006-03-08 . Retrieved 2017-05-26 . ^ Gellene, Denise (September 21, 2002). "Eli Lilly to Join Forces With Amylin" . Los Angeles Times . Retrieved June 3, ', '["clm_wiki_amylin-pharmaceuticals_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
