  ('cs_getty-images_history', 'org_getty-images', 'overview', 'History',
   'American visual media company "Wire Image" redirects here. For the method of transmitting images through telephone lines, see wirephoto . For the concept in computer networking, see wire data . "Via Getty" redirects here. For the American Capitol rioter misidentified as "Via Getty", see Adam Christian Johnson . Not to be confused with Getty designs . Getty Images Holdings, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : GETY Industry Publishing media web design Genre Stock photography Predecessors Getty Communications PhotoDisc Founded 14 March 1995 &#59;&#32;31 years ago ( 1995-03-14 ) (as Getty Investments, LLC.) [1] Founders Mark Getty [1] Jonathan Klein [1] Headquarters Seattle , Washington , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Mark Getty ( chairman ) Craig Peters ( CEO ) Jennifer Leyden ( CFO ) [2] Products Digital images audio video Services Rights-managed and royalty-free images, audio, and video Revenue US$ 917 million (2023) [3] Operating income US$128 million (2023) [3] Net income US$19.6 million (2023) [3] Total assets US$2.60 billion (2023) [3] Total equity US$681 million (2023) [3] Owner Getty family (36.7%) [4] Number of employees c. &#8201;~1,700 (2023) [3] Divisions Getty Productions Subsidiaries iStock Unsplash Photos Website gettyimages Getty Images Holdings, Inc. (stylized as gettyimages ) is an American visual media company and supplier of stock images , editorial photography, video, and music for businesses and consumers, with a library of over 477 million assets. It targets three markets— creative professionals (advertising and graphic design), the media (print and online publishing), and corporate (in-house design, marketing and communication departments). Getty Images has distribution offices around the world and capitalizes on the Internet for distribution with over 2.3 billion searches annually on its sites. As Getty Images has acquired other older photo agencies and archives, it has digitized their collections, enabling online distribution. Getty Images operates a large commercial website that clients use to search and browse for images, purchase usage rights, and download images. Image prices vary according to resolution and type of rights. The company also offers custom photo services for corporate clients. In January 2025, it was announced that the company would be merging with Shutterstock . [5] ^ a b c body:not( ):not( ) Roberts, Paul (1 December 2019). "It''s crunch time for Seattle-based photo giant Getty Images, and for photographers"', '["clm_wiki_getty-images_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
