VALUES
  ('cs_getty-images_operations', 'org_getty-images', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Corporate ownership and management In February 2008, it was announced that Getty Images would be acquired by the private equity firm Hellman &amp; Friedman in a transaction valued at an estimated US$2.4 billion. [1] On 2 July 2008, Getty Images announced the completion of its acquisition. Getty Images common stock ceased trading on the New York Stock Exchange at the close of the acquisition and was delisted from the NYSE. [2] In 2012, H&amp;F engaged investment bankers to sell the company. While a price of $4 billion was initially discussed, in August, when the private equity firm Carlyle Group emerged as the likely acquirer, the price under consideration was said to be $3.3–3.4 billion. CVC Capital Partners Ltd. was also said to have been bidding but had yet to top Carlyle''s price. [3] The sale to Carlyle thereafter was announced at $3.3 billion, with co-founders Getty and Klein and the Getty family all carrying their investments over into the new ownership structure. Getty continues to serve as chairman and Klein as chief executive. [4] In September 2018, the Getty family announced it would acquire a majority stake in the company from The Carlyle Group . [5] In July 2022, the company went public again. [6] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Getty Images Press Release" (Press release). 25 February 2008. Archived from the original on 29 February 2008. ^ "Getty Images Announces Completion of Acquisition by Hellman &amp; Friedman" (Press release). 2 July 2008. Archived from the original on 30 June 2011 . Retrieved 9 October 2010 . ^ Alesci, Cristina, and Jeffrey McCracken, "Carlyle Group Said to Be Leading Bidder for Getty Images" Archived 16 August 2012 at the Wayback Machine , Bloomberg , 14 August 2012. Retrieved 14 August 2012. ^ Cite error: The named reference NYT01 was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ "Getty family to buy majority stake in Getty Images from Carlyle" . Reuters . 4 September 2018. Archived from the original on 4 September 2018 . Retrieved 4 Se', '["clm_wiki_getty-images_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
