VALUES
  ('cs_thq_operations', 'org_thq', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Company growth and acquisitions (2000–2009) In February 2000, THQ faced a class action lawsuit over a violation of federal security laws due to nondisclosure of material information. [1] In September of the same year, the company expanded its internal product development capabilities with the acquisition of Volition located in Champaign, Illinois . [2] Since then, THQ''s internal studio system grew to eleven studios across the globe with distinct capabilities across all viable gaming platforms. Some of these studios, such as Relic Entertainment , Vigil Games , Blue Tongue Entertainment , Juice Games, Kaos Studios and Volition , worked on games for next generation consoles as well as PCs. THQ went on to acquire Vigil Games in 2006. [3] In 2000, THQ signed a deal with Fox Interactive to bring five of the titles to the Game Boy Color market, such as the Croc franchise. [4] In April 2000, THQ announced an agreement with Warner Bros. Interactive Entertainment to publish video games based on the Scooby-Doo franchise. [5] In October 2000, THQ acquired the rights to publish Tetris games in a licensing agreement with The Tetris Company . [6] In 2001, THQ obtained an extended agreement with Nickelodeon to produce video games based on its franchises, as well as computer game rights to Rugrats , SpongeBob SquarePants and Rocket Power and console and computer rights to other Nickelodeon shows like Jimmy Neutron: Boy Genius and The Wild Thornberrys . [7] [8] The agreement also covered games based on original intellectual properties, such as Tak and the Power of Juju , with the potential that THQ would release a game first, followed by an animated cartoon on Nickelodeon. [9] In 2002, THQ signed a deal with Disney Interactive and Pixar to publish video games based on Pixar films. [10] [11] In 2004, THQ signed an agreement with MGA Entertainment to publish video games based on the Bratz fashion doll line. [12] Also in 2004, THQ''s deal with Nickelodeon was extended. [13] In 2008, THQ ', '["clm_wiki_thq_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
