VALUES
  ('cs_zynga_leadership', 'org_zynga', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Funding In its first round of funding in January 2008, Zynga received US$10 million. [1] In July of the same year, Zynga received US$29 million in venture finance from several firms. [2] During its first four years of operation Zynga raised a total of $854 million in three rounds of fund raising. The last round, in February 2011, raised $490 million. [3] Public offering On July 1, 2011, the company filed its Form S-1 registration statement with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC). [4] Zynga was priced at $10 per share and began trading on NASDAQ under ZNGA on December 16, 2011. The stock closed down 5% on its first day, [5] then climbed 26% to $13.39 per share after Facebook''s IPO filing on February 1, 2012 (Facebook had reported that 12% of its revenue comes from Zynga). [6] In March 2012 ZNGA was trading at $14.50. [7] For several years the stock performed poorly, but in 2017 the price hit a three-year high. By the end of 2017 Zynga''s shares were trading at $4.00, a 56% gain for the year. [8] ^ body:not( ):not( ) Stone, Brad (January 15, 2008). "More Than Games, a Net to Snare Social Networkers" . The New York Times . Archived from the original on August 11, 2021 . Retrieved February 28, 2017 . ^ "Zynga Completes $29 Million Round Led by Kleiner Perkins and IVP" . Foundry Group . July 23, 2008. Archived from the original on February 24, 2022 . Retrieved February 19, 2018 . ^ "Zynga has raised $845M in three rounds over four years | GamesBeat" . venturebeat . July 2011. Archived from the original on February 24, 2022 . Retrieved February 19, 2018 . ^ Don Reisinger, CNET. " Zynga files for IPO Archived 2023-02-27 at the Wayback Machine ." July 1, 2011. Retrieved July 1, 2011. ^ Cite error: The named reference Forbes IPO was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ Douglas MacMillan - 2012-02-03T21:14:47Z (February 3, 2012). "Zynga Surges for Second Day After Facebook IPO Filing: San Francisco Mover" . Bloomberg. Archived from the original on A', '["clm_wiki_zynga_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
