VALUES
  ('cs_sturm-ruger_history', 'org_sturm-ruger', 'overview', 'History',
   'American firearm manufacturing company "Ruger" redirects here, and thus, for technical reasons , "Ruger #1" and "Ruger #3" also redirect here. For the rifles, see Ruger No. 1 and Ruger No. 3 . For other uses, see Ruger (disambiguation) . Sturm, Ruger &amp; Company, Inc. Type Public Traded as NYSE : RGR Industry Firearms Founded 1949 &#59;&#32;77 years ago ( 1949 ) Founders William B. Ruger , Alexander McCormick Sturm Headquarters Mayodan, North Carolina [1] , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Ronald C. Whitaker ( Chairman ) [2] Christopher J. Killoy ( President and CEO ) [3] Products Revolvers , pistols , rifles , shotguns Revenue $664 million [4] (2016) Operating income $596 million (2022) Net income $88 million [4] (2016) Owner Beretta Holding (9.95%) [5] Number of employees 2,120 [4] (2016) Subsidiaries Marlin Firearms Website www Sturm, Ruger &amp; Company, Inc. , better known by the shortened name Ruger , is an American firearm manufacturing company based in Mayodan, North Carolina , with production facilities also in Newport, New Hampshire ; Mayodan, North Carolina ; Hebron, Kentucky and Prescott, Arizona . The company was founded in 1949 by Alexander McCormick Sturm and William B. Ruger and has been publicly traded since 1969. Ruger produces bolt-action , semi-automatic , and single-shot rifles , semi-automatic pistols , and single- and double-action revolvers . [6] According to the ATF statistics for 2022, [7] Ruger is the largest firearm manufacturer [8] in the United States, surpassing Smith &amp; Wesson . ^ body:not( ):not( ) Schott, Paul (May 11, 2026). "Gun manufacturer Sturm Ruger moves HQ from Connecticut to North Carolina" . CT Insider . Retrieved July 27, 2026 . ^ Ruger. "Board of Directors - Ruger" . Retrieved June 20, 2019 . ^ Ruger. "Corporate Officers - Ruger" . Retrieved June 20, 2019 . ^ a b c "Corporate Report" (PDF) . February 22, 2017. &#91; dead link &#93; ^ [1] &#91; dead link &#93; ^ "BATFE Annual Firearms Manufacturing And Export Report" . Gunreports . 2006. ^ BATFE Annual Firearms Manufacturing And Export Report 2022, Atf ^ "Top 30 Largest Firearm Manufacturers" . Orchidadvisors . Retrieved March 22, 2024 .', '["clm_wiki_sturm-ruger_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   20, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
