  ('cs_sturm-ruger_leadership', 'org_sturm-ruger', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Statistics Ruger was ranked the number one U.S. firearms manufacturer from 2008 to 2011. In 2011, Ruger manufactured 1,114,687 firearms, as their promotion, the "Million Gun Challenge to Benefit the NRA", played a significant role in the company maintaining its top U.S. manufacturer status. [1] The company has set a new goal of 2 million firearms produced per year. [2] From 2009 to 2012, Ruger was the top-seller of handguns . [3] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "US Firearms Industry Today" . Shooting Industry . 2013. ^ "The Ruger 2 Million Gun Challenge" . Ruger . Retrieved July 12, 2018 . ^ "US Firearms Industry Today" . Shooting Industry . 2012.', '["clm_wiki_sturm-ruger_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
