  ('cs_exar_history', 'org_exar', 'overview', 'History',
   'American semiconductor manufacturer (1971–2017) Exar Trade name Exar Corporation Type Subsidiary Traded as NYSE : EXAR [1] Industry Electronics Semiconductor Founded 1971 &#59;&#32;55 years ago ( 1971 ) in California, United States Defunct 2017 ( 2017 ) Fate Acquired by MaxLinear Headquarters United States Number of employees 269 [2] (2016) Parent Rohm (1971–1990) Website exar at the Wayback Machine &#32;(archived 2016-02-29) Function generator integrated circuit XR-2206 by Exar Exar Corporation was an American semiconductor manufacturer active from 1971 to 2017 as a subsidiary of the Japanese firm Rohm . It was acquired by MaxLinear in May 2017 and maintained as a wholly owned subsidiary for a short while. ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Exar Corporation (EXAR) Admitted to Trading on the NYSE" . 29 July 2013. ^ "Form 10K: Annual Report for the fiscal year ended March 27, 2016" . United States Securities and Exchange Commission. May 25, 2016 . Retrieved September 2, 2016 .', '["clm_wiki_exar_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
