  ('cs_stantec_operations', 'org_stantec', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Acquisitions Stantec has acquired over 130 firms since 1994. [1] Acquisitions include MWH Global, Inc. , [2] KBR, Inc. Infrastructure Americas Division, [3] Dessau engineering , Fay, Spofford &amp; Thorndike , Sparling, [4] [5] Traffic Design Group , [6] Cardno, [7] ZETCON Engineering, [8] and Hydrock. [9] In August 2025, the company completed the acquisition of Page, an American architecture firm. [10] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Acquisition History - Stantec" . www . Retrieved 2019-03-21 . ^ Cite error: The named reference engineering hub was invoked but never defined (see the help page ). ^ "Stantec to Acquire KBR''s Infrastructure Americas Division" . Marketwired L.P. Marketwired. 5 November 2015 . Retrieved 19 May 2016 . ^ "Sparling is part of a team" . Sparling . Retrieved 19 May 2016 . ^ Morgan, Geoffrey. "Stantec continues to buy up engineering firms in fractured U.S. market with acquisition of Massachusetts company" . National Post - Financial Post . Postmedia Network Inc . Retrieved 19 May 2016 . ^ "Stantec acquires TDG" . ^ "Stantec completes acquisition of select Cardno businesses to grow Environmental Services and Infrastructure footprint" . www . Retrieved 2026-01-16 . ^ "Stantec to acquire ZETCON Engineering, a leading German infrastructure firm" . Financial Post . Nov 14, 2023. ^ Rogers, Dave (1 May 2024). "Canadian engineer buys Hydrock" . Building . Retrieved 2 May 2024 . ^ Flatman, Ben. "Stantec acquisition of Page makes it second largest US architecture firm" . Building Design . Retrieved 2026-05-27 .', '["clm_wiki_stantec_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
