  ('cs_burns-mcdonnell_operations', 'org_burns-mcdonnell', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Armco Steel In 1971, the firm was bought by Armco Steel , based in Ohio . [1] As Armco prepared to sell Burns &amp; McDonnell in the early 1980s, its employees opted to buy the company themselves and took on a loan to finance a buyout in 1985. [1] The loan was provided by the United Missouri Bank . [2] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) Eaton, Collin (2016-11-04). "At Burns &amp; McDonnell, employees feel like owners -- because they are" . Chron . Retrieved 2022-06-20 . ^ Dahl, Darren. "How Do You Build Companies That Last Hundreds Of Years? Make Them Employee-Owned" . Forbes . Retrieved 2022-06-20 .', '["clm_wiki_burns-mcdonnell_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
