  ('cs_dell_history', 'org_dell', 'overview', 'History',
   'American multinational technology company This article is about the company formed after the merger of Dell and EMC Corporation (now Dell EMC). For other uses, see Dell (disambiguation) . Dell Technologies Inc. Headquarters in Round Rock, Texas Type Public Traded as NYSE : DELL ( Class C ) S&amp;P 500 component Industry Information technology Predecessors Dell EMC Corporation Founded September 7, 2016 &#59;&#32;9 years ago ( 2016-09-07 ) as a merger of EMC Corporation and Dell Inc. Founder Michael Dell Headquarters Round Rock, Texas , U.S. Area served Worldwide Key people Michael Dell (chairman and CEO) Jeff Clarke (vice chairman and COO) Products Computer hardware Consumer electronics Software development Cloud computing Corporate venture capital Revenue US$ 113.5 billion (2026) Operating income US$8.149 billion (2026) Net income US$5.936 billion (2026) Total assets US$101.3 billion (2026) Total equity US$–2.47 billion (2026) Owner Michael Dell (58.9%) [1] Number of employees c. &#8201;97,000 (2026) Divisions Client Solutions Group Infrastructure Solutions Group Subsidiaries Alienware Virtustream Website dell Footnotes Financials as of January 30,&#32;2026 &#91;update&#93; . [2] Dell Technologies Inc. is an American multinational technology company that has been headquartered in Round Rock, Texas , since 1994. [3] It was formed as a result of the September 2016 merger of Dell and EMC Corporation . [4] Dell Technologies ranked 48th on the 2024 Fortune 500 rankings of the largest United States corporations based on its 2023 revenue; [5] its products include personal computers, servers , monitors, computer software, computer security and network security , as well as information security services. [4] ^ body:not( ):not( ) "DELL MICHAEL S - DELL / Dell Technologies Inc. / DELL MICHAEL S Passive Investment - SC 13G/A - February 13, 2024" . Archived from the original on February 12, 2025 . Retrieved July 21, 2026 . ^ "Dell Technologies Inc. FY 2026 Form 10-K Annual Report" . U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission . March 16, 2026. ^ "An Economic Powerhouse: How Dell Technologies helped change the direction of Round Rock''s future" . Round Rock . February 21, 2020 . Retrieved June 24, 2025 . ^ a b Shah, Agam (September 7, 2016). "The new Dell Technologies: 6 things you need to know" . PC World . Retrieved August 10, 2026 . ^ "Fortune 500: Dell Technologies" . Fortune . Retrieved September 6, 2024 .', '["clm_wiki_dell_history"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
