   'Early years Hard Drives International was founded in 1988 by Eric and Tim Crown. Initially a mail order business selling computer storage, the company expanded into a storefront when credit card companies declined service. In 1991, the company changed its name to Insight Enterprises, and distribution included a full line of computers and accessories. [1] The company held its initial public offering in January 1995. [2] [3] Insight became an international company when it acquired TC Computers, based in Montreal , Canada , in 1997. In April 1998, Insight signed an agreement to acquire Choice Peripherals Ltd. and Plusnet Technologies Ltd., an Internet service provider and website hosting and development company operating as Force 9. [4] The acquisition expanded Insight''s operations to Europe. [1] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) William P. Barrett (24 August 1998). "The Internet doesn''t know borders" . Forbes . Retrieved 18 April 2016 . ^ "Insight Enterprises Inc. reports earnings for 4th qtr to Jun 30" . The New York Times . 19 August 1995 . Retrieved 18 April 2016 . ^ "Offerings This Week" . The New York Times . 23 January 1995 . Retrieved 18 April 2016 . ^ "Insight Acquires Choice Peripherals in U.K." internetnews . 1998-04-07 . Retrieved 2015-08-06 .', '["clm_wiki_insight_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
