VALUES
  ('cs_insight_operations', 'org_insight', 'overview', 'Operations',
   '2000–2010 Insight acquired Action Computer Supplies Holdings PLC, a U.K.-based direct marketer, in October 2001 for approximately $150 million in stock. [1] [2] In April 2002, the company acquired Comark for $150 million, increasing Insight''s ability to work with clients of all sizes, including the public sector. [1] In July 2006, Insight entered an agreement to purchase Software Spectrum , a company which focused on software and mobility products for medium and large companies, from Level 3 Communications for $287 million. [3] Calence LLC, a technology company focused on Cisco networking and advanced communications, was acquired by Insight in April 2008 for $125 million. [4] Insight acquired U.K.-based Minx Ltd., a European network integrator with Cisco Gold Partner accreditation, in July 2008 for $1.5 million and the assumption of $4.6 million of existing debt. [5] [6] ^ a b body:not( ):not( ) "Insight Acquires Comark for $150 Million" . crn . 2002-04-25 . Retrieved 2015-08-06 . ^ "Company News; Insight Enterprises to Add Action Computer" . The New York Times . 1999-05-11 . Retrieved 2015-08-06 . ^ Scott Campbell (2006-07-20). "Insight Enterprises To Acquire Software Spectrum From Level 3" . Crn . p. 1 . Retrieved 2015-06-04 . ^ "Insight Enterprises completes $125M acquisition of Calence LLC" . Bizjournals . 2008-04-01 . Retrieved 2015-06-04 . ^ "Insight Enterprises (NSIT) Acquires MINX Limited" . Street Insider. 10 July 2008 . Retrieved 18 April 2016 . ^ Scott Campbell (11 July 2008). "Insight Buys U.K.-Based Network Integrator" . CRN . Retrieved 18 April 2016 .', '["clm_wiki_insight_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
