  ('cs_trane_leadership', 'org_trane', 'overview', 'Leadership',
   'Brands and subsidiaries The company''s brands and subsidiaries [1] include: Trane – subsidiary brand manufacturing heating, ventilation, and air conditioning (HVAC) equipment American Standard Heating &amp; Air Conditioning – HVAC equipment brand Ameristar – Value HVAC equipment brand of American Standard Oxbox – Value HVAC equipment brand RunTru – Value HVAC equipment brand Thermocold – European HVAC equipment brand AL-KO – European manufacturer of air handling units Thermo King – subsidiary brand manufacturing refrigeration units for transport industry, HVAC units for buses and trains Frigoblock – European refrigeration unit brand ICS Cool Energy – Refrigeration and HVAC equipment for European industrial customers MTA-IT – HVAC equipment for European customers Nuvolo – cloud-based connected workplace solutions for digital advancements in heating and cooling BrainBox AI – Driving artificial intelligence and innovation across the built environment, including the Trane Technologies AI Lab Life Science Solutions – Provide precision-temperature controlled solutions for health and life sciences customers Farrar Scientific – Life sciences refrigeration brand Helmer Scientific – Life sciences refrigeration brand Diversified Laboratory Repair (DLR) - maintenance and repair services of laboratory equipment Data Center Solutions – Advancing smarter data center cooling Trane - Provides thermal management strategy [2] for hyperscale data centers Stellar Energy – innovator of data center cooling solutions in modular data centers Liquid Stack – liquid cooling technology for high-density AI-scale workloads ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Our Brands | Sustainable Solutions" . www . Retrieved 23 March 2026 . ^ "Improving how data centers are developed, designed and operated" . www . Retrieved 23 March 2026 .', '["clm_wiki_trane_leadership"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   30, 1, 1, unixepoch());
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO content_section
  (id, entity_id, section_type, heading, body_markdown, claim_ids, source_ids,
   reading_level, language, author_type, generator_version, editorial_status,
   version, created_at, updated_at, display_order, claim_count, source_count, last_verified_at)
VALUES
  ('cs_trane_operations', 'org_trane', 'overview', 'Operations',
   'Sustainability and Innovation Trane Technologies embeds sustainability across its products, operations and long-term strategy. The company has key sustainability related commitments, which include: Gigaton Challenge , their goal to reduce one billion metric tons, or a gigaton, of greenhouse gas emissions (CO2e) from customer''s carbon footprints by 2030. Leading by Example , their commitment to have a restorative impact on the environment through their own supply chain and operations with decarbonization strategies and the 2050 Net-Zero roadmap, as outlined in their Climate Transition Plan [1] . Opportunity for All , a component of the workforce culture at Trane Technologies [2] where their employees are part of an uplifting culture focused on broadening access to education and skill development, purpose-driven careers with growth opportunities and career pathways in the company. Trane Technologies has expanded its digital and AI-enabled solutions through strategic acquisitions focused on building automation, data-driven energy optimization and advanced thermal management technologies. Brainbox AI : Trane Technologies announced the acquisition of BrainBox AI [3] , a developer of autonomous building management and AI‑driven HVAC optimization technology, on December 18, 2024 , and completed the acquisition on January 3, 2025 . Stellar Energy: The company completed the acquisition of the digital business of Stellar Energy [4] Americas, Inc. on February 17, 2026 , expanding its capabilities in energy systems analytics and performance optimization. LiquidStack: Trane Technologies announced its acquisition of LiquidStack [5] , a leader in advanced liquid cooling technologies for data centers and electronics, on February 10, 2026 , and completed the transaction on March 3, 2026 . ^ body:not( ):not( ) "Trane Technologies Climate Transition Plan" (PDF) . ^ "Careers at Trane Technologies | Trane Technologies jobs" . Trane Technologies . Retrieved 23 March 2026 . ^ "Trane Techn', '["clm_wiki_trane_operations"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
   'general', 'en', 'assisted', 'orgs_sections_v1', 'auto_approved', 1, unixepoch(), unixepoch(),
   40, 1, 1, unixepoch());
