  ('cs_snap-on_overview', 'org_snap-on', 'overview', 'Overview',
   'Snap-on Incorporated is a United States designer, manufacturer, and marketer of high-end tools and equipment for professional use in the transportation industry, including the automotive, heavy duty, equipment, marine, aviation, and railroad industries. Headquartered in Kenosha, Wisconsin, since 1930, Snap-on also distributes lower-end tools under the brand name Blue-Point. Their primary competitors include Matco, Mac Tools, and Cornwell Tools.', '["clm_wiki_snap-on_overview"]', '["src_en_wikipedia"]',
